{
	file.0000000000000001.title: "Warbucks Chemistry: The Demigod's Codex"
	chapter_group.2DCF10F76EBF2A74.title: "The Demigod's Path"
	chapter_group.3B51167C89EBE873.title: "Chemistry Lab"
	chapter_group.4801EE691EF63116.title: "Engineering"
	chapter_group.517E2EE5EE2E76FF.title: "Magic and Relics"
	chapter_group.4045A6EE7751118B.title: "Exploration"
	chapter_group.37409AEB3F7AB09E.title: "Farming and Food"
	chapter_group.71650C5783BBAA4C.title: "Collections"
	chapter.4335527ACA7CF750.title: "Welcome"
	chapter.4335527ACA7CF750.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Read this first: who you are, how this world works, and how to use this book."
	]
	quest.54E4F62471779F14.title: "Welcome, Demigod"
	quest.54E4F62471779F14.quest_subtitle: "Your first page of the Demigod's Codex"
	quest.54E4F62471779F14.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember light pouring from your hands. Now there is only dirt under your nails.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Welcome to Warbucks Chemistry. You're a demigod who has lost your power, and you'll win it back by mastering chemistry: taking matter apart into its elements and building it back up."
		"&eHow:&r Follow the lines from quest to quest. Each one tells you what to do and how to do it. Click the checkmark to collect your first reward."
		"&eTip:&r The sleeping bag skips the night without moving your spawn point."
	]
	quest.14851AEFE672966D.title: "Who You Were"
	quest.14851AEFE672966D.quest_subtitle: "A god's memory, and a chemist's method"
	quest.14851AEFE672966D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Some things you still know without being taught: that water is two parts hydrogen to one of oxygen, that fire is a reaction, not a spirit.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Your power returns as you rebuild your understanding of matter. Every chapter of this book is one more piece of what you once were."
		"&eChemistry:&r All matter is made of about 90 naturally occurring elements. Rearrange their atoms and you change what a thing is. That's the whole game."
		"&eHow:&r Click the checkmark to continue."
	]
	quest.022F679599389147.title: "How Progression Works"
	quest.022F679599389147.quest_subtitle: "Eight tiers, each opened by chemistry"
	quest.022F679599389147.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r The pack has 8 tiers. Each one is unlocked by a chemistry milestone, not just more metal."
		"&eHow:&r Fire and bronze → coke and steel → hydrogen and flight → electricity → acids → oil and plastics → silicon, PVC and the atom → antimatter."
		"Modern Industrialization's voltage tiers (LV, MV, HV, EV) are the spine. Other mods (Mekanism, AE2, Powah and more) unlock alongside them."
		"&eTip:&r If a recipe looks different from what you remember, it's been gated on purpose. JEI always shows the real recipe."
	]
	quest.745DBEEE9AE746C7.title: "Your Toolkit"
	quest.745DBEEE9AE746C7.quest_subtitle: "The keys you'll press a thousand times"
	quest.745DBEEE9AE746C7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A few mods make everything easier. Learn their keys now."
		"&eHow:&r &eR&r / &eU&r over an item: recipes / uses (JEI). &eM&r: map and chunk claiming (FTB Chunks)."
		"Hold &e`&r while mining to vein mine (FTB Ultimine). Look at a block and Jade shows what it is and what it's doing."
		"&eTip:&r Inventory sorting, crafting-grid tweaks and the trash slot are in your inventory screen; check Controls for their keys."
	]
	quest.268396713B9B58E9.title: "Reading This Book"
	quest.268396713B9B58E9.quest_subtitle: "Sections, side quests and gold lines"
	quest.268396713B9B58E9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Every quest is written the same way, so you always know where to look."
		"&eHow:&r &eWhat&r says what the thing is, &eChemistry&r gives the real science, &eHow&r gives the steps, and &eTip&r saves you time."
		"Quests marked &eoptional&r sit above or below the main line. They give bonus tokens but never block progress."
		"&eTip:&r Gold lines are your memories returning. They mark the start of each chapter and its big milestones."
	]
	quest.32306651C1085697.title: "Demigod Tokens"
	quest.32306651C1085697.quest_subtitle: "Quest rewards you can spend"
	quest.32306651C1085697.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Most quests give &eDemigod Tokens&r. Spend them on convenience items by crafting: torches, food, XP, iron, coke, rubber, osmium, backpack upgrades and a Warp Stone."
		"&eHow:&r Search &eDemigod Token&r in JEI and press U to see the whole shop."
		"&eTip:&r Bigger milestones pay more tokens, and later tiers pay more than early ones. Optional quests pay too."
	]
	quest.19F5D52D281D058B.title: "Playing Together"
	quest.19F5D52D281D058B.quest_subtitle: "Share quests and land with friends"
	quest.19F5D52D281D058B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r On a server, make a team so you share quest progress and claimed land."
		"&eHow:&r &e/ftbteams party create <name>&r, then invite friends with &e/ftbteams party invite <player>&r."
		"&eTip:&r Split the work: one player on ore processing, one on power, one exploring. Chemistry rewards a production line."
	]
	quest.006E1D3530E698E7.title: "Give the Game Room"
	quest.006E1D3530E698E7.quest_subtitle: "Memory settings for a big pack"
	quest.006E1D3530E698E7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r This is a large pack. Too little memory means stutters; too much can cause long pauses."
		"&eHow:&r In Prism, open the instance settings and allocate about 8-10 GB. The pack's docs/README.md has the recommended Java arguments."
		"&eTip:&r If the game hitches every few seconds, check the memory bar in F3 before blaming a mod."
	]
	quest.61103C80A99526F9.title: "Begin"
	quest.61103C80A99526F9.quest_subtitle: "Open Getting Started"
	quest.61103C80A99526F9.quest_desc: [
		"&6The world is waiting to be taken apart and put back together.&r"
		"&eHow:&r That's everything. Open &eGetting Started&r and take your first step."
		"&eTip:&r You can come back to this chapter any time from the chapter list."
	]
	quest.5F462A144226867C.title: "The Periodic Table"
	quest.5F462A144226867C.quest_subtitle: "Fun fact: 118 known elements"
	quest.5F462A144226867C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Chemists know 118 elements. Each one is defined by its number of protons, its &eatomic number&r."
		"&eChemistry:&r Dmitri Mendeleev arranged the table in 1869 by repeating properties, and left gaps for elements nobody had found yet. Gallium and germanium later filled them almost exactly as he predicted."
		"&eTip:&r The Periodic Table chapter tracks every element you collect."
	]
	quest.5EFC77C0525603E5.title: "Nothing Is Lost"
	quest.5EFC77C0525603E5.quest_subtitle: "Fun fact: conservation of mass"
	quest.5EFC77C0525603E5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Antoine Lavoisier showed in the 1780s that in a closed system, mass before a reaction equals mass after it."
		"&eChemistry:&r Atoms are rearranged, never created or destroyed in a chemical reaction. That's why every equation balances."
		"&eTip:&r The Dissolver and Combiner follow the same rule: what you take apart, you can build back."
	]
	chapter.1CE4EAE5C8575E5D.title: "Getting Started"
	chapter.1CE4EAE5C8575E5D.chapter_subtitle: [
		"You wake in a world you didn't make, with a god's patience and none of a god's power."
		"These first steps get you fed, armed, rested and ready for chemistry."
	]
	quest.4D8BFEB75E87D5CA.title: "The Awakening"
	quest.4D8BFEB75E87D5CA.quest_subtitle: "Everything is made of elements"
	quest.4D8BFEB75E87D5CA.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember being more than this.&r The memory is fading, but one idea stays clear: everything is made of elements, and elements can be taken apart and put back together."
		"&eWhat:&r This book walks you from your first log to antimatter. Follow the lines: each quest unlocks the next."
		"&eHow:&r Click the checkmark on the right to begin."
	]
	quest.61A00C75298573F8.title: "Tip: Recipes (JEI)"
	quest.61A00C75298573F8.quest_subtitle: "R for recipes, U for uses"
	quest.61A00C75298573F8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r JEI shows every recipe in the pack, including the ones changed for progression."
		"&eHow:&r Press &eR&r over any item to see how it's made, or &eU&r to see what it's used in. Try it on a quest icon, then click the checkmark."
		"&eTip:&r Type &e@modname&r in the JEI search bar to list everything one mod adds."
	]
	quest.2F1CA29E2D318F95.title: "Tip: What Am I Looking At?"
	quest.2F1CA29E2D318F95.quest_subtitle: "Jade names every block"
	quest.2F1CA29E2D318F95.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Jade shows a small panel at the top of the screen for whatever block you're looking at."
		"&eHow:&r Look at any block or machine. Jade shows its name, its mod, and for machines their progress, energy and fluids."
		"&eTip:&r When a machine isn't working, look at it first. Jade usually tells you why."
	]
	quest.310586A0CE86D7B4.title: "Wood and a Workbench"
	quest.310586A0CE86D7B4.quest_subtitle: "Logs, planks, and your first table"
	quest.310586A0CE86D7B4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Every tool starts at a crafting table."
		"&eChemistry:&r Wood is mostly cellulose, (C₆H₁₀O₅)ₙ: long chains of sugar molecules. Later you'll take it apart atom by atom."
		"&eHow:&r Punch a tree for logs, turn them into planks, and put 4 planks in a 2x2 grid. Any wood works."
	]
	quest.056B70005B9D0DDB.title: "A Wooden Pick"
	quest.056B70005B9D0DDB.quest_subtitle: "Just enough to break stone"
	quest.056B70005B9D0DDB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A wooden pickaxe is weak, but it can mine stone, and stone is your next step."
		"&eHow:&r Craft sticks from planks, then 3 planks and 2 sticks in the pickaxe shape."
		"&eTip:&r Don't bother upgrading it. Stone is minutes away."
	]
	quest.1E339D434FEA09CE.title: "Stone Age"
	quest.1E339D434FEA09CE.quest_subtitle: "Cobblestone tools"
	quest.1E339D434FEA09CE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Stone tools last longer and can mine iron ore."
		"&eHow:&r Mine some cobblestone with the wooden pickaxe, then craft a stone pickaxe."
		"&eTip:&r FTB Ultimine mines a whole vein at once. Hold the &e`&r key (grave/tilde) while breaking blocks."
	]
	quest.2181236B6834BFDF.title: "Something to Eat"
	quest.2181236B6834BFDF.quest_subtitle: "Wheat, bread, and a full belly"
	quest.2181236B6834BFDF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Gods don't need to eat. You do, for now."
		"&eChemistry:&r Baking turns starch and protein into new compounds. The brown crust comes from the &eMaillard reaction&r between sugars and amino acids."
		"&eHow:&r Break grass for seeds, farm wheat, and craft bread from 3 wheat."
		"&eTip:&r AppleSkin shows how much hunger and saturation each food restores."
	]
	quest.168A3AC3F1C50464.title: "Rest Anywhere"
	quest.168A3AC3F1C50464.quest_subtitle: "Skip the night, keep your spawn"
	quest.168A3AC3F1C50464.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A &esleeping bag&r skips the night without moving your spawn point, so it's great while exploring."
		"&eHow:&r Craft it from wool. Any colour works for the recipe; this quest wants a white one."
		"&eTip:&r Hammocks skip the day instead."
	]
	quest.1010A20D70EB78BD.title: "A Roof Overhead"
	quest.1010A20D70EB78BD.quest_subtitle: "Walls, a door, and light"
	quest.1010A20D70EB78BD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Monsters spawn in the dark. A small, lit, enclosed room keeps you safe while you work."
		"&eHow:&r Build four walls and a roof, add a door, and light the inside with torches. Click the checkmark when you're done."
		"&eTip:&r Leave room to grow. Your steam machines in Chapter I need floor space."
	]
	quest.490B2EFFC87D0F70.title: "Somewhere to Put Things"
	quest.490B2EFFC87D0F70.quest_subtitle: "Two chests for your first stockpile"
	quest.490B2EFFC87D0F70.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r You'll collect far more than you can carry. Chests hold 27 stacks each, and two side by side make a double chest."
		"&eHow:&r 8 planks in a ring make a chest."
		"&eTip:&r Inventory sorting works in chests too. Check Controls for the sort key."
	]
	quest.4A91AD1D881ECA8C.title: "Coal"
	quest.4A91AD1D881ECA8C.quest_subtitle: "Ancient carbon from the ground"
	quest.4A91AD1D881ECA8C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Coal fuels furnaces now, and becomes coke and steel in Chapter II."
		"&eChemistry:&r Coal is plant matter buried for millions of years. Heat and pressure drove off most of its hydrogen and oxygen and left mostly carbon."
		"&eHow:&r Coal ore is the black-speckled stone common in exposed cliffs and mountains. Mine it with any pickaxe."
		"&eTip:&r Save extra coal. The Coke Oven eats a lot of it."
	]
	quest.38196E0094811FC0.title: "Light in the Dark"
	quest.38196E0094811FC0.quest_subtitle: "Combustion you can carry"
	quest.38196E0094811FC0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Torches stop monsters spawning and light up caves."
		"&eChemistry:&r A torch is &ecombustion&r: carbon reacting with oxygen, C + O₂ → CO₂, releasing heat and light."
		"&eHow:&r One coal or charcoal on top of one stick makes 4 torches."
	]
	quest.324A651EE9DDF0ED.title: "Fire"
	quest.324A651EE9DDF0ED.quest_subtitle: "Your first chemistry tool"
	quest.324A651EE9DDF0ED.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Fire is your first chemistry tool. Cooking logs in a furnace makes &echarcoal&r (more on why in Chapter I)."
		"&eChemistry:&r A furnace drives reactions with heat: it cooks food, reduces ores to metal and chars wood into carbon."
		"&eHow:&r 8 cobblestone in a ring make a furnace. Smelt a log, using a log or planks as fuel."
	]
	quest.1C5E43BCEDA7593F.title: "Iron"
	quest.1C5E43BCEDA7593F.quest_subtitle: "Ore, heat, and carbon make metal"
	quest.1C5E43BCEDA7593F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Iron is the metal of your first real tools, buckets and armour."
		"&eChemistry:&r Iron ore is iron oxide. In the furnace, carbon pulls the oxygen away: Fe₂O₃ + 3C → 2Fe + 3CO. That's &ereduction&r."
		"&eHow:&r Mine iron ore (it's common around Y 16 and in mountains) and smelt it."
		"&eTip:&r Iron Furnaces (see the Storage and Logistics chapter) smelt faster once you have spare iron."
	]
	quest.7A1D323C6D2FA6FE.title: "Iron Pickaxe"
	quest.7A1D323C6D2FA6FE.quest_subtitle: "Diamonds, gold and redstone open up"
	quest.7A1D323C6D2FA6FE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Needed for diamonds, redstone and gold, and to start the journey to the Nether."
		"&eChemistry:&r Iron is harder than stone because its atoms sit in a regular metal lattice held by metallic bonds, which bend rather than shatter."
		"&eHow:&r 3 iron ingots and 2 sticks."
	]
	quest.0A8F569FBAF9D8B1.title: "Shield"
	quest.0A8F569FBAF9D8B1.quest_subtitle: "Block the arrows"
	quest.0A8F569FBAF9D8B1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A shield blocks arrows, melee hits and creeper blasts while you hold right-click."
		"&eHow:&r 1 iron ingot and 6 planks (check JEI for the shape)."
		"&eTip:&r Hold it in your off-hand so you can block and swing at the same time."
	]
	quest.78AB87381549A629.title: "Iron Armour"
	quest.78AB87381549A629.quest_subtitle: "A full set before you dig deep"
	quest.78AB87381549A629.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A full set of iron armour makes caves and the night survivable."
		"&eHow:&r Helmet, chestplate, leggings and boots take 24 iron ingots in total."
		"&eTip:&r Ultimine through an iron vein and you'll have this set in minutes."
	]
	quest.6939E4AEBA9EF3ED.title: "Water"
	quest.6939E4AEBA9EF3ED.quest_subtitle: "The most important chemical in the pack"
	quest.6939E4AEBA9EF3ED.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Water is the most important chemical in this pack: steam, electrolysis and acids all start with it."
		"&eChemistry:&r H₂O is a small, polar molecule. That polarity lets it dissolve salts and acids, which is why chemists call it the universal solvent."
		"&eHow:&r 3 iron ingots make a bucket. Fill it at any water source."
	]
	quest.30347A69744DE975.title: "A Backpack"
	quest.30347A69744DE975.quest_subtitle: "More pockets, upgradeable later"
	quest.30347A69744DE975.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r More inventory, and it can be upgraded later (pickup, magnet, feeding and more)."
		"&eHow:&r Craft it from leather, string and a chest (check JEI). Wear it in the chest slot or keep it in your inventory."
		"&eTip:&r Backpack upgrades are in the Demigod Token shop."
	]
	quest.78540BFEDFE5CCD4.title: "Claim Your Land"
	quest.78540BFEDFE5CCD4.quest_subtitle: "Protect your base with FTB Chunks"
	quest.78540BFEDFE5CCD4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r FTB Chunks protects your base and can keep it loaded while you're away."
		"&eHow:&r Press &eM&r to open the map, then drag over chunks to claim them. Click the checkmark when done."
		"&eTip:&r Right-click a claimed chunk to force-load it. You'll need that for the flight pylon later."
	]
	quest.4081488F0A14597A.title: "The Paxel"
	quest.4081488F0A14597A.quest_subtitle: "Pickaxe, axe and shovel in one"
	quest.4081488F0A14597A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A &epaxel&r is a pickaxe, axe and shovel in one tool. Mekanism Tools adds them for every material, from wood to refined obsidian."
		"&eHow:&r Craft an iron pickaxe, axe and shovel together with 2 sticks (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r One tool slot instead of three leaves more room for ore."
	]
	quest.384F1C4A2EF051A0.title: "Tools from Parts"
	quest.384F1C4A2EF051A0.quest_subtitle: "Silent Gear: stats come from materials"
	quest.384F1C4A2EF051A0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Silent Gear builds tools from parts. Each part's stats come from its &ematerial&r, so better chemistry means better tools."
		"&eHow:&r Make Blueprint Paper, craft a Pickaxe Blueprint, then craft a pickaxe head and rod."
		"&eTip:&r The Tools and Comfort chapter goes deeper."
	]
	quest.14F9F46803366AD8.title: "Ready for Chemistry"
	quest.14F9F46803366AD8.quest_subtitle: "Fed, armed, sheltered"
	quest.14F9F46803366AD8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fed, armed, sheltered.&r Now the real work begins: fire, ore, alloys, and the slow road back to divinity."
		"&eHow:&r Click to open Chapter I. The copper and tin in the reward are a head start on your first alloy."
		"&eTip:&r Bring spare coal and iron. Chapter I eats both."
	]
	quest.5D6A23FA8DF41833.title: "Rock Collector"
	quest.5D6A23FA8DF41833.quest_subtitle: "One of every vanilla ore drop"
	quest.5D6A23FA8DF41833.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Collect one drop from every vanilla ore. Emeralds only generate in mountain biomes."
		"&eChemistry:&r Real ores are minerals: iron comes from oxides like hematite (Fe₂O₃), copper often from sulfides like chalcopyrite (CuFeS₂), and diamond is pure carbon."
		"&eTip:&r Every one of these can go into the Dissolver later. Keep spares."
	]
	quest.421D29C6B470FAC0.title: "Kitchen Chemistry"
	quest.421D29C6B470FAC0.quest_subtitle: "Farmer's Delight: a proper meal"
	quest.421D29C6B470FAC0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Farmer's Delight meals restore more hunger and give the Nourishment and Comfort effects."
		"&eChemistry:&r Stewing denatures proteins: heat unfolds them, which is why meat turns firm and tender."
		"&eHow:&r Craft a Cooking Pot (iron, bricks, a water bucket and a wooden shovel), set it over a campfire or stove, and cook raw beef, a carrot and a potato."
		"&eTip:&r Check JEI for the Cooking Pot's other recipes."
	]
	quest.51F87365154D80E8.title: "A Closer Look"
	quest.51F87365154D80E8.quest_subtitle: "Copper and amethyst"
	quest.51F87365154D80E8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A spyglass lets you scout terrain and spot ore in cliff faces from far away."
		"&eChemistry:&r Amethyst is quartz (SiO₂). Its purple colour comes from traces of iron in the crystal."
		"&eHow:&r 2 copper ingots and 1 amethyst shard. Amethyst geodes sit underground, ringed with smooth basalt."
	]
	quest.34A2F932F17C9F0D.title: "Paxel Collector"
	quest.34A2F932F17C9F0D.quest_subtitle: "Wood, stone, gold and diamond"
	quest.34A2F932F17C9F0D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Craft the early paxels you skipped, plus a diamond one for the long haul."
		"&eChemistry:&r Gold is soft because its atoms slide past each other easily. Diamond is the hardest natural material because every carbon atom is locked to four neighbours."
		"&eHow:&r Same recipe as the iron paxel: pickaxe, axe and shovel of one material, plus 2 sticks."
	]
	chapter.48AF3DD6C95E2CE8.title: "I. Fire and Bronze"
	chapter.48AF3DD6C95E2CE8.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Heat drives chemistry: reduce ore with carbon, mix metals into alloys, and let steam do the work."
	]
	quest.79F4E5BCC7D2EFBF.title: "Pyrolysis"
	quest.79F4E5BCC7D2EFBF.quest_subtitle: "Wood, heat, and no air"
	quest.79F4E5BCC7D2EFBF.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember the first fire you ever tamed. It was smaller than this, and it frightened you more.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r &eCharcoal&r is almost pure carbon: fuel, and the reducing agent that turns ore into metal."
		"&eChemistry:&r Heat wood without enough oxygen to burn and the volatile compounds escape as smoke, tar, methanol and acetic acid. What's left is carbon. This is &epyrolysis&r."
		"&eHow:&r Smelt logs in a furnace."
		"&eTip:&r A tree farm now saves hours later. Charcoal fuels everything until you have coke."
	]
	quest.139143689A0FF7FD.title: "Copper"
	quest.139143689A0FF7FD.quest_subtitle: "The first metal humans smelted"
	quest.139143689A0FF7FD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Copper is three quarters of bronze, and MI uses it for rotors, gears and wires."
		"&eChemistry:&r Smelting is &ereduction&r: carbon pulls oxygen away from the metal oxide and leaves metal behind, CuO + C → Cu + CO."
		"&eHow:&r Copper ore is common near the surface, especially in dripstone caves. Smelt the raw copper."
	]
	quest.30FB6A2D6AE22741.title: "Tin"
	quest.30FB6A2D6AE22741.quest_subtitle: "The other quarter of bronze"
	quest.30FB6A2D6AE22741.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Tin is soft on its own, but a little of it makes copper much harder."
		"&eChemistry:&r Real tin comes from cassiterite, SnO₂. Carbon reduces it the same way: SnO₂ + 2C → Sn + 2CO."
		"&eHow:&r Tin ore here comes from Modern Industrialization (MI). It's grey with pale specks and fairly common underground. Mine it and smelt the raw tin."
	]
	quest.622967087A4B1D2B.title: "The MI Guidebook"
	quest.622967087A4B1D2B.quest_subtitle: "Every machine and multiblock, explained"
	quest.622967087A4B1D2B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Modern Industrialization's own manual. It explains each machine and shows multiblock layouts."
		"&eHow:&r 8 copper nuggets around a book. Break a copper ingot into nuggets first."
		"&eTip:&r JEI (R/U) also shows multiblock shapes in 3D."
	]
	quest.1DD1902EBDA6FD91.title: "The Forge Hammer"
	quest.1DD1902EBDA6FD91.quest_subtitle: "Your first workstation"
	quest.1DD1902EBDA6FD91.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI's first workstation. It crushes ore and ingots into dust and hammers ingots into plates, rods and bolts."
		"&eHow:&r 3 heavy weighted pressure plates over 4 iron ingots. Place it and right-click to use."
		"&eTip:&r Ores give at most &e2x&r here. Bigger yields come later from &eacids&r, not bigger hammers."
	]
	quest.1638082093BAC031.title: "Metal Dust"
	quest.1638082093BAC031.quest_subtitle: "Crush ingots so they can mix"
	quest.1638082093BAC031.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Solid ingots can't blend. Powders can."
		"&eChemistry:&r Grinding a metal to powder gives it a huge surface area, so the two metals mix evenly when they melt together."
		"&eHow:&r Put copper and tin ingots in the Forge Hammer: 1 ingot makes 1 dust."
	]
	quest.7164771969B473AD.title: "Mixing Bronze"
	quest.7164771969B473AD.quest_subtitle: "3 copper + 1 tin"
	quest.7164771969B473AD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Bronze dust is the blended alloy, ready to melt into ingots."
		"&eChemistry:&r Traditional bronze is about 88% copper and 12% tin by mass. Tin atoms jam the copper crystal so its layers can't slide, which makes it harder."
		"&eHow:&r Craft 3 copper dust with 1 tin dust to get 3 bronze dust."
		"&eTip:&r The Steam Mixer later turns the same inputs into 4 bronze dust instead of 3."
	]
	quest.6EB1CA116210134C.title: "The First Alloy"
	quest.6EB1CA116210134C.quest_subtitle: "Humanity's first engineered material"
	quest.6EB1CA116210134C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Metal that never existed until a mind decided it should. You remember the feeling.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r &eBronze&r is harder than either copper or tin alone, and it's the frame of your whole steam age."
		"&eChemistry:&r An &ealloy&r is a mixture of metals. Its properties can beat its ingredients because the mixed atoms resist being pushed out of line."
		"&eHow:&r Smelt bronze dust in any furnace."
	]
	quest.0FF0E23A8B2B7B70.title: "Bronze Plates"
	quest.0FF0E23A8B2B7B70.quest_subtitle: "The sheet metal of the steam age"
	quest.0FF0E23A8B2B7B70.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Almost every steam machine is built from plates."
		"&eHow:&r Hammer bronze ingots in the Forge Hammer. Without a hammer tool, 2 ingots make 1 plate."
		"&eTip:&r With an Iron Hammer in the tool slot it's 1 ingot per plate, and the Steam Compressor later does it 1:1 for free."
	]
	quest.18FE9304A0173084.title: "Rods, Bolts and Rings"
	quest.18FE9304A0173084.quest_subtitle: "Small parts for bigger parts"
	quest.18FE9304A0173084.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Gears need bolts and a ring; rings need rods and bolts."
		"&eHow:&r In the Forge Hammer, 1 bronze ingot makes 1 rod or 2 bolts. Craft rods and bolts into rings (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r Make a few extra of each. Every gear takes 4 bolts and a ring."
	]
	quest.6132BB59977148BB.title: "Bronze Gears"
	quest.6132BB59977148BB.quest_subtitle: "The heart of every machine casing"
	quest.6132BB59977148BB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Each machine casing needs a gear at its centre."
		"&eHow:&r 4 bronze plates, 4 bolts and 1 ring (check JEI for the shape)."
		"&eTip:&r Make extra rings and bolts while you're at it. You'll need several casings."
	]
	quest.697156ADC0ABAEB8.title: "Bronze Machine Casing"
	quest.697156ADC0ABAEB8.quest_subtitle: "The block every steam machine is built around"
	quest.697156ADC0ABAEB8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r The core of every steam machine. You'll also need one for the Dissolver in Chapter II."
		"&eHow:&r 8 bronze plates around 1 bronze gear."
		"&eTip:&r Multiblock hatches each need a casing too. Make a few."
	]
	quest.2574A917B43992A6.title: "Large Iron Plates"
	quest.2574A917B43992A6.quest_subtitle: "20 iron plates, pressed in fours"
	quest.2574A917B43992A6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r The head of the Iron Hammer is made of large plates."
		"&eHow:&r Hammer iron ingots into plates (2 ingots per plate), then craft 4 plates into 1 large plate. That's about 40 iron in total."
		"&eTip:&r Ultimine an iron vein first. This is the hungriest step of the chapter."
	]
	quest.0653BB5BC79C83EC.title: "The Iron Hammer"
	quest.0653BB5BC79C83EC.quest_subtitle: "A tool for the Forge Hammer"
	quest.0653BB5BC79C83EC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Put it in the Forge Hammer's tool slot to unlock better recipes: 1 ingot per plate, and crushing bricks into dust."
		"&eHow:&r 5 large iron plates and 2 sticks (check JEI). The tool loses durability with each use."
		"&eTip:&r Only use the tool slot when you need it. Plain recipes don't wear it down."
	]
	quest.17CFDD38CE2280C0.title: "Brick Dust"
	quest.17CFDD38CE2280C0.quest_subtitle: "Crushed, already-fired clay"
	quest.17CFDD38CE2280C0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Brick dust is half of fire clay."
		"&eChemistry:&r Potters call crushed fired clay &egrog&r. It has already shrunk in the kiln, so mixing it into raw clay stops the new brick cracking when heated."
		"&eHow:&r Smelt clay balls into bricks, then hammer bricks in the Forge Hammer with the Iron Hammer in the tool slot."
	]
	quest.4BC4D530815158F0.title: "Fire Clay"
	quest.4BC4D530815158F0.quest_subtitle: "Clay that survives the furnace"
	quest.4BC4D530815158F0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Fire clay is a &erefractory&r: a material that stays solid at temperatures that would ruin ordinary brick."
		"&eChemistry:&r Refractory clays are rich in alumina (Al₂O₃) and silica (SiO₂), which melt far above a fire's temperature."
		"&eHow:&r Craft 2 clay balls with 2 brick dust to make 3 fire clay dust."
	]
	quest.604936958718809F.title: "Fire Clay Bricks"
	quest.604936958718809F.quest_subtitle: "Fired once, hard forever"
	quest.604936958718809F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Single fire bricks, ready to stack into blocks."
		"&eChemistry:&r Firing drives the bound water out of clay minerals and fuses the grains together. That change can't be undone."
		"&eHow:&r Smelt fire clay dust in a furnace."
	]
	quest.34418487854EFB2D.title: "Firebrick Blocks"
	quest.34418487854EFB2D.quest_subtitle: "The boiler's firebox"
	quest.34418487854EFB2D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r The bronze boiler sits on a row of 3 fire clay brick blocks."
		"&eHow:&r 4 fire clay bricks in a 2x2 make 1 block."
		"&eTip:&r Chapter II's Steam Blast Furnace is built from dozens of these. Start stockpiling clay."
	]
	quest.1A507DB4026F531C.title: "Bronze Tank"
	quest.1A507DB4026F531C.quest_subtitle: "Holds the boiler's water"
	quest.1A507DB4026F531C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A bronze tank stores fluid, and the boiler needs one to hold its water."
		"&eChemistry:&r Bronze resists corrosion from water, which is why it was used for ship fittings for centuries."
		"&eHow:&r 8 bronze plates around 1 glass block."
	]
	quest.696474FC1863B20C.title: "Steam Power"
	quest.696474FC1863B20C.quest_subtitle: "Fire boils water, steam does work"
	quest.696474FC1863B20C.quest_desc: [
		"&6The engines remember you even if the world doesn't. Pressure, heat, motion: old friends.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Burn fuel, boil water, and the expanding steam does work. Welcome to the industrial revolution."
		"&eChemistry:&r Water expands more than 1,600 times in volume when it boils into steam. That pressure is what drives the machines."
		"&eHow:&r Craft it from bronze plates, a bronze tank, a furnace and 3 fire clay brick blocks. Give it water and fuel (coal or charcoal), and place steam machines next to it."
		"&eTip:&r Steam flows into adjacent machines, or through MI fluid pipes once you have them."
	]
	quest.1B20E348E02AE451.title: "Steam Furnace"
	quest.1B20E348E02AE451.quest_subtitle: "Smelting without fuel"
	quest.1B20E348E02AE451.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Smelts with steam instead of fuel. Your first automated machine."
		"&eHow:&r Place it touching the boiler, or pipe steam to it later."
		"&eTip:&r It smelts the same things as a vanilla furnace, so dust and raw ore can go straight in."
	]
	quest.1FCCFB27D4E61D8B.title: "Steam Macerator"
	quest.1FCCFB27D4E61D8B.quest_subtitle: "Ore and ingots into dust"
	quest.1FCCFB27D4E61D8B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Grinds ore and items into dust without wearing out a tool."
		"&eHow:&r 1 ore makes 2 raw ore here (capped at 2x until acids)."
		"&eTip:&r It also grinds bricks into brick dust, so your Iron Hammer can rest."
	]
	quest.0DCF15D0DDB80EE0.title: "Steam Compressor"
	quest.0DCF15D0DDB80EE0.quest_subtitle: "Plates at 1 ingot each"
	quest.0DCF15D0DDB80EE0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Presses ingots into plates 1:1, and plates into curved plates."
		"&eHow:&r Place it touching the boiler and put ingots in. Curved plates come from plates you put back in."
		"&eTip:&r Machines need lots of plates. Keep this one fed."
	]
	quest.319D2A4BD36DBDCD.title: "Steam Mixer"
	quest.319D2A4BD36DBDCD.quest_subtitle: "Better alloy ratios"
	quest.319D2A4BD36DBDCD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mixes dusts (like copper and tin into bronze) and fluids."
		"&eChemistry:&r Same copper and tin, less loss: a good process wastes less of its inputs. That's called &eyield&r."
		"&eHow:&r 3 copper dust + 1 tin dust makes 4 bronze dust here, one more than by hand."
	]
	quest.5FA030B61A0C335C.title: "Steam Cutting Machine"
	quest.5FA030B61A0C335C.quest_subtitle: "Rods, bolts and planks"
	quest.5FA030B61A0C335C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Cuts ingots into 2 rods, rods into bolts, and logs into 6 planks."
		"&eHow:&r It needs &elubricant&r as a cutting fluid. You'll make lubricant from creosote and redstone in Chapter II, so build it now and run it then."
		"&eTip:&r Until then, the Forge Hammer makes rods and bolts."
	]
	quest.296A19C3A1BFE619.title: "Curved Plates"
	quest.296A19C3A1BFE619.quest_subtitle: "The walls of a pipe"
	quest.296A19C3A1BFE619.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Pipes are made from curved bronze plates."
		"&eHow:&r Put bronze plates in the Steam Compressor, or hammer 2 ingots into 1 curved plate."
		"&eTip:&r You need 6 per batch of 16 pipes. Make 12 to have pipes to spare."
	]
	quest.229F63ADEA222BD4.title: "Copper Rotors"
	quest.229F63ADEA222BD4.quest_subtitle: "Blades, a ring and bolts"
	quest.229F63ADEA222BD4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Rotors push fluid through pipes and pumps."
		"&eHow:&r 4 copper blades, 1 copper ring and 4 copper bolts. Blades are curved copper plates on a copper rod (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r Every part comes from the Forge Hammer or the Steam Compressor."
	]
	quest.0DB20A7152AEF87F.title: "Fluid Pipes"
	quest.0DB20A7152AEF87F.quest_subtitle: "Carry water and steam anywhere"
	quest.0DB20A7152AEF87F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI fluid pipes carry water, steam and later every chemical in the pack."
		"&eHow:&r 6 bronze curved plates, 2 copper rotors and a glass pane make 16 pipes."
		"&eTip:&r Right-click a pipe end with an empty hand to set it to insert or extract. Item pipes need steel gears, so they wait for Chapter II."
	]
	quest.15BEE6A43E8C4B6E.title: "Endless Water"
	quest.15BEE6A43E8C4B6E.quest_subtitle: "A boiler that never runs dry"
	quest.15BEE6A43E8C4B6E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fire, water, metal, motion. The pieces of a world are coming back to you.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r A steam-powered pump that pulls water from the ground, so your boiler never runs dry."
		"&eHow:&r Copper rotors, copper gears, a bronze tank, a machine casing and fluid pipes (check JEI). Place it next to the boiler, or pipe its water into it."
		"&eTip:&r Next stop: coke and steel in Chapter II."
	]
	quest.5D9DA66BCD1F549C.title: "Bronze Age Hoard"
	quest.5D9DA66BCD1F549C.quest_subtitle: "Four blocks of bronze"
	quest.5D9DA66BCD1F549C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 36 ingots of bronze, stored as blocks."
		"&eChemistry:&r Bronze resists corrosion: its surface forms a thin layer of copper compounds that protects the metal underneath. Bronze statues can last thousands of years."
		"&eHow:&r 9 bronze ingots make 1 block."
	]
	quest.4C3565E3456D5AE4.title: "Bronze Paxel"
	quest.4C3565E3456D5AE4.quest_subtitle: "Your alloy, as a tool"
	quest.4C3565E3456D5AE4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism Tools makes paxels from bronze too."
		"&eChemistry:&r Ancient bronze tools replaced stone ones because bronze can be cast, sharpened and repaired. Stone can only be chipped."
		"&eHow:&r Craft a bronze pickaxe, axe and shovel, then combine them with 2 sticks."
	]
	quest.6D6DC704E6FBCF0F.title: "The Wrench"
	quest.6D6DC704E6FBCF0F.quest_subtitle: "Handle MI machines with care"
	quest.6D6DC704E6FBCF0F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI's wrench rotates MI machines, sets which face they output from, and picks them up quickly."
		"&eHow:&r 5 bronze plates in a wrench shape (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r Handy when you rearrange your steam setup for the Coke Oven in Chapter II."
	]
	quest.3257C24FD424AE58.title: "Steam Mining Drill"
	quest.3257C24FD424AE58.quest_subtitle: "A drill that burns fuel"
	quest.3257C24FD424AE58.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A fuel-burning mining tool that digs a 3x3 area and can give an easy Silk Touch."
		"&eHow:&r Furnaces, diamonds, large iron plates, a copper drill head and a bucket (check JEI). Read its tooltip for fuel and mode controls."
		"&eTip:&r Diamonds are the hard part. Mine deep, around Y -59."
	]
	quest.1AF0C99AB1B7CD3F.title: "Efficient Alloying"
	quest.1AF0C99AB1B7CD3F.quest_subtitle: "Let the mixer earn its keep"
	quest.1AF0C99AB1B7CD3F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mix 32 bronze dust in the Steam Mixer."
		"&eChemistry:&r In real metallurgy, alloy ratios are measured by mass or by number of atoms. Getting the ratio right matters more than the amount."
		"&eTip:&r Pipe the macerator's dust straight into the mixer and you'll never mix by hand again."
	]
	chapter.598D356C3B16EC05.title: "II. Steam and Steel"
	chapter.598D356C3B16EC05.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Destructive distillation turns coal into coke, and coke turns iron into steel."
		"At the end of this chapter, matter itself opens up to you."
	]
	quest.1EDDC44EC9C4E742.title: "A Kiln's Worth of Bricks"
	quest.1EDDC44EC9C4E742.quest_subtitle: "The Coke Oven's shell"
	quest.1EDDC44EC9C4E742.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember smoke rising from a hill of earth, and what came out of it burning hotter than anything before.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r The Coke Oven is built from ordinary brick blocks: one ring of 8 for the controller, and more for its walls."
		"&eChemistry:&r Firing clay drives out the water bound in its minerals and fuses the grains, turning soft mud into ceramic."
		"&eHow:&r Smelt clay balls into bricks, then craft 4 bricks into a brick block."
		"&eTip:&r Rivers and swamps are full of clay. Ultimine a clay patch."
	]
	quest.1F11787528A18CB9.title: "The Coke Oven"
	quest.1F11787528A18CB9.quest_subtitle: "The controller block"
	quest.1F11787528A18CB9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r The controller of a small multiblock that bakes coal into coke."
		"&eChemistry:&r Coal is carbon mixed with many other compounds. Bake it without air and those volatiles are driven off. This is &edestructive distillation&r."
		"&eHow:&r 8 brick blocks around a furnace."
	]
	quest.3E0966482A811593.title: "Hatches"
	quest.3E0966482A811593.quest_subtitle: "How things get in and out of a multiblock"
	quest.3E0966482A811593.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI multiblocks have no inventory of their own. Hatches built into the walls take items and steam in and push products out."
		"&eHow:&r An item hatch is a hopper on a bronze machine casing; a fluid hatch is a bronze tank on a casing (check JEI for the output versions)."
		"&eTip:&r While you hold a hatch, MI can highlight the spots where it fits (a client option in MI's config)."
	]
	quest.4952190F5A9DACFA.title: "Build the Coke Oven"
	quest.4952190F5A9DACFA.quest_subtitle: "A 3x3x3 brick cube with hatches"
	quest.4952190F5A9DACFA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Put the shell together and the controller comes to life."
		"&eHow:&r Press R on the Coke Oven in JEI or open the MI guidebook to see the 3D layout: a 3x3x3 cube of brick blocks with the controller in one face. Swap wall bricks for hatches: item in, item out, steam in, and a fluid output for creosote."
		"&eTip:&r Pipe steam from your boiler into the fluid input hatch. Click the checkmark once the controller shows it's formed."
	]
	quest.2E90112C74807A32.title: "Coke"
	quest.2E90112C74807A32.quest_subtitle: "Nearly pure carbon, burns hotter than coal"
	quest.2E90112C74807A32.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Coke is exactly what a blast furnace needs: strong, porous, nearly pure carbon."
		"&eChemistry:&r With the hydrogen, sulfur and tars baked out, what's left is a carbon skeleton that burns hot and clean."
		"&eHow:&r Feed coal into the item input hatch. Each coal becomes 1 coke in 30 seconds."
		"&eTip:&r Coal dust works too and comes out as coke dust, which saves a grinding step later."
	]
	quest.4E8A54354F577B14.title: "Byproduct: Creosote"
	quest.4E8A54354F577B14.quest_subtitle: "The tar driven out of coal"
	quest.4E8A54354F577B14.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Half the time, coking a coal also yields 500 mB of &ecreosote&r. Nothing is wasted in chemistry: creosote is a boiler fuel."
		"&eChemistry:&r Coal-tar creosote is a mix of phenols, cresols and ring-shaped hydrocarbons, the same family of compounds that makes tar smell the way it does."
		"&eHow:&r Pipe it out of the fluid output hatch into a tank, or straight into a boiler."
	]
	quest.6788BDC814345011.title: "Lubricant"
	quest.6788BDC814345011.quest_subtitle: "Creosote + redstone"
	quest.6788BDC814345011.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r The Steam Cutting Machine needs lubricant as cutting fluid. Now you can finally run it."
		"&eHow:&r In the Steam Mixer, 500 mB of creosote and 1 redstone make 500 mB of lubricant."
		"&eTip:&r Each cut uses only 1 mB, so one bucket lasts a very long time."
	]
	quest.01D936F8C9EF70C6.title: "Coke Dust"
	quest.01D936F8C9EF70C6.quest_subtitle: "Carbon, powdered"
	quest.01D936F8C9EF70C6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Steel is mixed as dust, so the carbon has to be a powder too."
		"&eChemistry:&r Coke is the reducing agent in a real blast furnace: it pulls oxygen out of iron ore and supplies the carbon that becomes steel."
		"&eHow:&r Grind coke in the Steam Macerator, or coke coal dust directly in the Coke Oven."
	]
	quest.6DFD06FF06C7F3C4.title: "Iron Dust"
	quest.6DFD06FF06C7F3C4.quest_subtitle: "Seven parts of the recipe"
	quest.6DFD06FF06C7F3C4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r The other ingredient of steel."
		"&eHow:&r Grind iron ingots in the Steam Macerator or the Forge Hammer (1 ingot makes 1 dust)."
		"&eTip:&r Macerating iron ore gives 2 raw iron per ore, which smelts into more ingots than mining alone."
	]
	quest.4991EED8B0E223D1.title: "Uncooked Steel"
	quest.4991EED8B0E223D1.quest_subtitle: "7 iron dust + 2 coke dust"
	quest.4991EED8B0E223D1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A blend of iron and carbon, ready for the blast furnace."
		"&eChemistry:&r Real steel holds far less carbon than this mix suggests, but the idea is right: carbon is the ingredient that turns soft iron into steel."
		"&eHow:&r Craft 7 iron dust with 2 coke dust to get 7 uncooked steel dust."
	]
	quest.2F826829D36DA434.title: "Blast Furnace Materials"
	quest.2F826829D36DA434.quest_subtitle: "Dozens of firebricks and a blast furnace"
	quest.2F826829D36DA434.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r The Steam Blast Furnace is a tower of fire clay bricks, hotter than anything you've built."
		"&eHow:&r Make fire clay bricks as in Chapter I (the Steam Macerator grinds bricks into brick dust now). A vanilla blast furnace is 5 iron, a furnace and 3 smooth stone."
		"&eTip:&r Automate it: macerator → crafting → steam furnace. You'll want a lot of these."
	]
	quest.09118CFFDCA49A2D.title: "The Steam Blast Furnace"
	quest.09118CFFDCA49A2D.quest_subtitle: "Hot enough to dissolve carbon in iron"
	quest.09118CFFDCA49A2D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A multiblock that gets hot enough to melt iron and dissolve carbon into it."
		"&eHow:&r Craft the controller from 8 fire clay brick blocks around a blast furnace. Check the structure in JEI: a 3x3 tower, four blocks tall, with bronze hatches for items and steam."
		"&eTip:&r Some later recipes in this furnace need a steel hatch. Steel itself only needs bronze ones."
	]
	quest.506EB945C083CC2E.title: "Steel"
	quest.506EB945C083CC2E.quest_subtitle: "Iron and carbon in the right ratio"
	quest.506EB945C083CC2E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Iron that bends without breaking. You remember forging weapons for gods out of something very like this.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Iron with a small, controlled amount of carbon (about 0.2-2%) is &esteel&r: strong, tough, and the backbone of every machine to come."
		"&eChemistry:&r Carbon atoms sit in the gaps between iron atoms and stop the layers sliding. Too much carbon and you get brittle cast iron. Chemistry is about the right ratio."
		"&eHow:&r Put uncooked steel dust in the blast furnace's item input hatch. Each dust becomes 1 steel ingot in 30 seconds."
	]
	quest.5FC7A4838C153DB0.title: "Steel Paxel"
	quest.5FC7A4838C153DB0.quest_subtitle: "A sturdier all-in-one tool"
	quest.5FC7A4838C153DB0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A sturdier paxel for the long mining trips ahead."
		"&eHow:&r A steel pickaxe, axe and shovel with 2 sticks (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r Steel tools last much longer than iron ones. Good for clearing ground for the factory ahead."
	]
	quest.750EFDC1E2DC1879.title: "Steel Boiler"
	quest.750EFDC1E2DC1879.quest_subtitle: "More steam per tick"
	quest.750EFDC1E2DC1879.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r More steam per tick than the bronze boiler."
		"&eHow:&r Steel plates, a steel tank, a furnace and 3 fire clay brick blocks (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r Steel versions of the steam machines (macerator, compressor and others) run faster too."
	]
	quest.1622F5994D7D8D48.title: "Steel Plates"
	quest.1622F5994D7D8D48.quest_subtitle: "For gears, pipes and Alchemistry"
	quest.1622F5994D7D8D48.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r The Dissolver and Combiner are framed in steel plates, and steel gears need them too."
		"&eHow:&r The Steam Compressor presses 1 steel ingot into 1 plate."
		"&eTip:&r You need at least 8 for the Dissolver and Combiner, plus more for gears. Keep the compressor busy."
	]
	quest.7C26AEBE7939F360.title: "Steel Gears"
	quest.7C26AEBE7939F360.quest_subtitle: "Plates, bolts and a ring, in steel"
	quest.7C26AEBE7939F360.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Item pipes and steel machine casings need steel gears."
		"&eHow:&r Same pattern as bronze: 4 steel plates, 4 steel bolts and 1 steel ring (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r Steel rods, bolts and rings come from the Forge Hammer, or from the Cutting Machine now that you have lubricant."
	]
	quest.287260F7D5158B76.title: "Item Pipes"
	quest.287260F7D5158B76.quest_subtitle: "Automate the item flow"
	quest.287260F7D5158B76.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI item pipes move items between machines, so dust, ingots and coke flow on their own."
		"&eHow:&r 6 bronze curved plates and 2 steel gears make 16 pipes."
		"&eTip:&r Right-click a pipe end with an empty hand to switch it between insert and extract."
	]
	quest.3D9A8C810E3CC81C.title: "A Simple Generator"
	quest.3D9A8C810E3CC81C.quest_subtitle: "Burn fuel, make Forge Energy"
	quest.3D9A8C810E3CC81C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Generator Galore's Copper Generator burns solid fuel into FE (Forge Energy) and pushes it into machines it touches."
		"&eChemistry:&r Burning releases the chemical energy stored in carbon bonds as heat; the generator turns that heat into electricity."
		"&eHow:&r Copper ingots around a furnace, with a block of redstone (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.54E6526368208022.title: "Forge Energy"
	quest.54E6526368208022.quest_subtitle: "Enough FE to run the Dissolver"
	quest.54E6526368208022.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Some machines run on &eFE&r instead of steam. You'll need it for the Dissolver."
		"&eHow:&r Upgrade the Copper Generator: surround it with iron ingots and a block of redstone to make the Iron Generator."
		"&eTip:&r A Mekanism Heat Generator or Powah Furnator also works. Burn coke for long runs."
	]
	quest.4EF4EA98C358B2AE.title: "Heat and Pressure"
	quest.4EF4EA98C358B2AE.quest_subtitle: "Magma and pistons for the Dissolver"
	quest.4EF4EA98C358B2AE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Besides steel plates and a bronze machine casing, the Dissolver needs 2 magma blocks and 2 pistons."
		"&eChemistry:&r Magma blocks are rock hot enough to glow, a fitting heat source for a machine that tears compounds apart."
		"&eHow:&r Magma blocks generate in underwater ravines and caves, or can be crafted from 4 magma cream. Pistons need iron, redstone, cobblestone and planks."
	]
	quest.7B8C9B9BAD74D427.title: "Pressure and Precision"
	quest.7B8C9B9BAD74D427.quest_subtitle: "A diamond and obsidian for the Combiner"
	quest.7B8C9B9BAD74D427.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r The Combiner needs a diamond, 2 obsidian and a piston, plus steel plates and a casing."
		"&eChemistry:&r Obsidian is volcanic glass: lava that cooled too fast for crystals to form."
		"&eHow:&r Pour water onto a lava source to make obsidian, and mine it with a diamond pickaxe. Diamonds are most common near the bottom of the world."
	]
	quest.7E15308871B090AE.title: "The Dissolver"
	quest.7E15308871B090AE.quest_subtitle: "Break anything into its elements"
	quest.7E15308871B090AE.quest_desc: [
		"&6Your first divine gift returns.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r The Dissolver breaks any item into the &eelements and compounds&r it's made of."
		"&eHow:&r Steel plates, pistons, magma blocks and a Bronze Machine Casing (check JEI). Power it with FE, insert anything, and collect the elements."
		"&eTip:&r Some things dissolve into compounds first. Put those back in to break them down further."
	]
	quest.29BEA270C571B58C.title: "The Combiner"
	quest.29BEA270C571B58C.quest_subtitle: "Build items back up from elements"
	quest.29BEA270C571B58C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r The reverse: arrange elements and the Combiner builds them back into items and blocks."
		"&eHow:&r Steel plates, a diamond, obsidian, a piston and a Bronze Machine Casing (check JEI). It runs on FE too."
		"&eTip:&r Taking the world apart and rebuilding it to your design is what this pack is about."
	]
	quest.6482D732148C9CAB.title: "Wood, Undone"
	quest.6482D732148C9CAB.quest_subtitle: "Logs dissolve into cellulose"
	quest.6482D732148C9CAB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Your first compound out of the Dissolver."
		"&eChemistry:&r Cellulose is a chain of glucose units, (C₆H₁₀O₅)ₙ. It's the most common organic compound on Earth and gives wood its strength."
		"&eHow:&r Dissolve logs: each log gives 1 cellulose. Dissolve the cellulose again to get 6 carbon, 10 hydrogen and 5 oxygen."
	]
	quest.7A840CDAA02E6E54.title: "Graphite"
	quest.7A840CDAA02E6E54.quest_subtitle: "Coal and charcoal, sorted"
	quest.7A840CDAA02E6E54.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Coal and charcoal dissolve into graphite, a pure form of carbon."
		"&eChemistry:&r In graphite, carbon atoms form flat sheets of hexagons that slide over each other. That's why pencil 'lead' leaves a mark."
		"&eHow:&r Dissolve coal or charcoal: each gives 2 graphite. Each graphite dissolves into 4 carbon."
	]
	quest.2C209AB4708A194F.title: "First Entries in the Periodic Table"
	quest.2C209AB4708A194F.quest_subtitle: "H, C, O and Fe"
	quest.2C209AB4708A194F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Dissolve whatever you have lying around and collect your first elements: &eH&r (1), &eC&r (6), &eO&r (8), &eFe&r (26)."
		"&eChemistry:&r The number is the &eatomic number&r: how many protons are in the nucleus. Change it and you have a different element."
		"&eHow:&r Cellulose gives carbon, hydrogen and oxygen; graphite gives carbon. Each iron ingot gives 16 iron."
		"&eTip:&r The Periodic Table chapter tracks every element from here on."
	]
	quest.3D16D152C8C89059.title: "Your First Synthesis"
	quest.3D16D152C8C89059.quest_subtitle: "2 H + 1 O → H₂O"
	quest.3D16D152C8C89059.quest_desc: [
		"&6Two hydrogen, one oxygen, and a world's worth of oceans. You remember making the first ones.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Build water from its elements in the Combiner. It's a trivial compound, but you made it from scratch. That's the point."
		"&eChemistry:&r 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O. Hydrogen and oxygen share electrons in covalent bonds, and the bent shape of the molecule makes it polar."
		"&eHow:&r Pick water as the target in the Combiner's GUI, then supply 2 hydrogen and 1 oxygen per water."
	]
	quest.4E77936288D67925.title: "Fuel Reserve"
	quest.4E77936288D67925.quest_subtitle: "Four blocks of coke"
	quest.4E77936288D67925.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A stockpile of coke for boilers, generators and future steel."
		"&eChemistry:&r Coke is porous. Air flows through it, which is why it burns so hot and steadily in a furnace."
		"&eTip:&r A full Coke Oven running overnight fills these quickly."
	]
	quest.786BB9183811C265.title: "Steel Upgrades"
	quest.786BB9183811C265.quest_subtitle: "Faster steam machines"
	quest.786BB9183811C265.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A Steel Upgrade turns a bronze steam machine into its faster steel version."
		"&eHow:&r Craft Steel Upgrades from a steel machine casing, bronze parts, fluid pipes and fire clay bricks (check JEI), then combine one with the Bronze Macerator."
		"&eTip:&r Upgrade the machines that bottleneck you first, usually the macerator."
	]
	quest.34238F774A63B533.title: "Proof of Composition"
	quest.34238F774A63B533.quest_subtitle: "Copper and tin, as elements"
	quest.34238F774A63B533.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Dissolve a copper ingot and a tin ingot to see the two elements that make bronze."
		"&eChemistry:&r Copper is element 29 and tin is element 50. Every bronze ingot you made in Chapter I was these two, mixed."
		"&eHow:&r Each copper or tin ingot dissolves into 16 of its element."
	]
	quest.0227C974352048DA.title: "Sweet Chemistry"
	quest.0227C974352048DA.quest_subtitle: "Sugar is C₁₂H₂₂O₁₁"
	quest.0227C974352048DA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Dissolve sugar into sucrose, then sucrose into its elements."
		"&eChemistry:&r Sucrose is glucose and fructose joined together. Dissolved, it gives 12 carbon, 22 hydrogen and 11 oxygen."
		"&eHow:&r Sugar cane makes sugar; the Dissolver turns 1 sugar into 1 sucrose."
	]
	quest.5228E072334D75AA.title: "Carbon Is Carbon"
	quest.5228E072334D75AA.quest_subtitle: "Dissolve a diamond"
	quest.5228E072334D75AA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A diamond dissolves into 128 graphite. Expensive, but it proves a point."
		"&eChemistry:&r Diamond and graphite are both pure carbon, called &eallotropes&r. In diamond every atom bonds to four neighbours in 3D; in graphite, to three in flat sheets."
		"&eTip:&r Don't dissolve your last diamond. You'll need them for machines."
	]
	chapter.33108756735886F7.title: "III. Divine Ascent"
	chapter.33108756735886F7.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Walk through fire, brew in the dark, and take back the sky."
		"Flight needs the Nether and your first Alchemistry machine: fire and chemistry together."
	]
	quest.206E95EBFA840B9D.title: "A Door of Fire"
	quest.206E95EBFA840B9D.quest_subtitle: "Ten blocks of obsidian and a spark"
	quest.206E95EBFA840B9D.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember the sky. Not looking up at it: standing in it.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a Nether portal is a 4x5 frame of obsidian (corners optional), lit with flint and steel."
		"&eChemistry:&r obsidian is volcanic glass. Lava cooled so fast its atoms never had time to form crystals."
		"&eHow:&r mine obsidian with a diamond pickaxe, or pour water over still lava to make it in place."
		"&eTip:&r a bucket of water and a bucket of lava let you cast the frame block by block."
	]
	quest.04B2CA0DEFD9BEA6.title: "Into the Fire"
	quest.04B2CA0DEFD9BEA6.quest_subtitle: "A dimension of quartz, fire and soul sand"
	quest.04B2CA0DEFD9BEA6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Nether is a chemistry lab: quartz (SiO₂), blaze powder and nether wart all come from here."
		"&eHow:&r bring food, armour, blocks and a way home. NetherPortalFix keeps portals linked properly."
		"&eTip:&r water evaporates instantly here and beds explode. Bring a respawn plan, not a bed."
	]
	quest.324D521459A0712A.title: "Blaze Rods"
	quest.324D521459A0712A.quest_subtitle: "Fuel for the brewing stand"
	quest.324D521459A0712A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r blaze rods craft the brewing stand, and blaze powder fuels it."
		"&eHow:&r blazes spawn around spawners in Nether Fortresses. Explorer's Compass can point you to one."
		"&eTip:&r snowballs hurt blazes, and fire resistance makes the fight easy."
	]
	quest.7C9C1346FF3451C6.title: "Nether Wart"
	quest.7C9C1346FF3451C6.quest_subtitle: "The base of almost every potion"
	quest.7C9C1346FF3451C6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the base reagent for almost every potion."
		"&eHow:&r it grows on soul sand in fortress stairwells. Bring some soul sand home and replant it; it grows in the Overworld too."
		"&eTip:&r one stack of wart grown at home covers every brew in this chapter."
	]
	quest.75644D12ABEA0664.title: "Nether Quartz"
	quest.75644D12ABEA0664.quest_subtitle: "Silicon dioxide, straight from the rock"
	quest.75644D12ABEA0664.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Nether quartz ore is everywhere in Nether netherrack. The Infusion Pylon needs it."
		"&eChemistry:&r quartz is silicon dioxide, SiO₂. Much later you'll reduce it with carbon to get pure silicon for circuits."
		"&eTip:&r keep a spare stack. Quartz dust plus coke becomes silicon in Chapter V."
	]
	quest.069E15B497A964D9.title: "Blackstone"
	quest.069E15B497A964D9.quest_subtitle: "Dark volcanic stone for the pylon"
	quest.069E15B497A964D9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Infusion Pylon is framed in blackstone."
		"&eChemistry:&r blackstone is a basalt-like volcanic rock, rich in dark iron and magnesium minerals."
		"&eHow:&r it fills basalt deltas and bastion remnants. Any pickaxe mines it."
	]
	quest.7271A237054B8116.title: "The Brewer's Art"
	quest.7271A237054B8116.quest_subtitle: "Applied chemistry, the old-fashioned way"
	quest.7271A237054B8116.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a brewing stand turns water bottles into potions, one ingredient at a time."
		"&eChemistry:&r brewing is extraction and reaction: each ingredient changes what's dissolved in the bottle."
		"&eHow:&r 1 blaze rod + 3 cobblestone. Blaze powder in the top-left slot fuels 20 brews."
		"&eTip:&r look up &ePotion of Flying&r in JEI (from Apothic Attributes). The next quests walk the whole chain."
	]
	quest.74482F0ACB9A447C.title: "The Awkward Potion"
	quest.74482F0ACB9A447C.quest_subtitle: "Water bottle + nether wart"
	quest.74482F0ACB9A447C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Awkward Potion does nothing by itself, but almost every potion starts from it."
		"&eHow:&r fill glass bottles with water, put three in the stand, add nether wart on top."
		"&eTip:&r brew three at a time. Every ingredient affects all three bottles at once."
	]
	quest.5BCAB5B85016C31D.title: "Slow Falling"
	quest.5BCAB5B85016C31D.quest_subtitle: "Awkward + phantom membrane"
	quest.5BCAB5B85016C31D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r step 1 toward flight. Awkward Potion + phantom membrane = Potion of Slow Falling."
		"&eHow:&r phantoms appear at night when someone in the world hasn't slept for three or more days. Fight them on a roof."
		"&eTip:&r one membrane brews three bottles, so four membranes go a long way."
	]
	quest.51616CABAD571846.title: "Levitation"
	quest.51616CABAD571846.quest_subtitle: "Slow Falling + fermented spider eye"
	quest.51616CABAD571846.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r step 2. Slow Falling + fermented spider eye = Potion of Levitation (Apothic Attributes)."
		"&eChemistry:&r fermentation is yeast turning sugar into alcohol and acids. Here it 'corrupts' the effect into its opposite."
		"&eHow:&r fermented spider eye = spider eye + sugar + brown mushroom (shapeless)."
	]
	quest.0860B82960107DA5.title: "Lifting Gas"
	quest.0860B82960107DA5.quest_subtitle: "Levitation + hydrogen = Flying"
	quest.0860B82960107DA5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r step 3. In this pack, Flying is made with &ehydrogen&r instead of End chorus fruit, so you can fly before the End."
		"&eChemistry:&r hydrogen (H₂) is the lightest gas there is, about 14 times lighter than air. It lifted the first passenger balloons in 1783."
		"&eHow:&r get hydrogen from the Alchemistry Dissolver (dissolve water or plants). You need 2 per Flying potion."
		"&eTip:&r the brewing-stand route (popped chorus fruit) still works too, once you reach the End."
	]
	quest.6C6CE3E3BD959A45.title: "Potion of Flying"
	quest.6C6CE3E3BD959A45.quest_subtitle: "8 minutes of flight in a bottle"
	quest.6C6CE3E3BD959A45.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Potion of Flying gives creative-style flight for 8 minutes."
		"&eHow:&r in a crafting grid: 1 Potion of Levitation + 2 hydrogen (check JEI). Tick this when you've made one."
		"&eTip:&r don't drink it yet. The next step makes it last far longer."
	]
	quest.025AF6A3C6CE7426.title: "Extended Flight"
	quest.025AF6A3C6CE7426.quest_subtitle: "Redstone, twice: 15 minutes, then 30"
	quest.025AF6A3C6CE7426.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r redstone stretches a potion's duration. Flying + redstone = Long Flying (15 min). Add redstone again for Extra Long Flying (30 min)."
		"&eHow:&r brew redstone into your Flying potions, then into the Long ones."
		"&eTip:&r a Potion Filter needs a full hour, which is just &etwo Extra Long&r potions. Brew at least two."
	]
	quest.06C7CB442A50E345.title: "Potion Filter"
	quest.06C7CB442A50E345.quest_subtitle: "Store an effect in a filter"
	quest.06C7CB442A50E345.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Potion Filter holds a potion effect for the Infusion Pylon."
		"&eHow:&r drink a potion, then right-click the filter to store the effect. It activates once it holds &e1 hour&r of that effect."
		"&eTip:&r combine two filters with the same effect by holding one in each hand and right-clicking."
	]
	quest.73D202B5B6CBA404.title: "A Full Hour"
	quest.73D202B5B6CBA404.quest_subtitle: "Charge the filter to one hour"
	quest.73D202B5B6CBA404.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the filter shows how much effect time it holds. It needs 60 minutes of Flying to work in a pylon."
		"&eHow:&r two Extra Long Flying (30 min each), four Long Flying (15 min), or about eight regular potions."
		"&eTip:&r drink and load one potion at a time, so none of the effect runs out first."
	]
	quest.7033201713D3AEDC.title: "Lighter than Air"
	quest.7033201713D3AEDC.quest_subtitle: "The lightest element, from your Dissolver"
	quest.7033201713D3AEDC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r your flight pylon needs hydrogen, and only the &eDissolver&r can pull it out of matter as an item."
		"&eChemistry:&r H is element 1: one proton, one electron. Hydrogen balloons carried people aloft in 1783."
		"&eHow:&r dissolve water, plants or wood and collect the hydrogen."
		"&eTip:&r feed the Dissolver from a hopper and it runs while you're in the Nether."
	]
	quest.2EE32733B83E0FCA.title: "Wings of a God"
	quest.2EE32733B83E0FCA.quest_subtitle: "Permanent flight, built from fire and hydrogen"
	quest.2EE32733B83E0FCA.quest_desc: [
		"&6The sky is yours again. You had forgotten how small the world looks from here.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the &eInfusion Pylon&r applies a filter's effect to you anywhere. With a Flying filter, that's creative-style flight."
		"&eHow:&r craft it from Nether quartz, blackstone and &ehydrogen&r from your Dissolver (see JEI), place it, and put the full filter inside."
		"&eTip:&r the pylon only works while its chunk is loaded. Force-load it (see the next quest)."
	]
	quest.165366B8F8450DF0.title: "Keep It Running"
	quest.165366B8F8450DF0.quest_subtitle: "Force-load the pylon's chunk"
	quest.165366B8F8450DF0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r if the pylon's chunk unloads, your flight stops. Over a long trip that means a long fall."
		"&eHow:&r open the FTB Chunks map (press M), claim the chunk with the pylon, then right-click it again to force-load it."
		"&eTip:&r force-load your Dissolver and brewing setup too, so they keep working while you travel."
	]
	quest.7543D8AB321711BF.title: "Fortress Found"
	quest.7543D8AB321711BF.quest_subtitle: "Bring home a piece of a fortress"
	quest.7543D8AB321711BF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Nether Fortresses hold blazes, wither skeletons and nether wart."
		"&eHow:&r Explorer's Compass points to structures. Mine nether bricks from the fortress walls."
		"&eTip:&r build a small portal near the fortress and your next trip is much shorter."
	]
	quest.2BF8FDA92111B602.title: "Fire Resistance"
	quest.2BF8FDA92111B602.quest_subtitle: "Awkward + magma cream"
	quest.2BF8FDA92111B602.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Fire Resistance makes lava and blaze fire harmless. Swimming in lava becomes a shortcut."
		"&eHow:&r magma cubes drop magma cream in basalt deltas, or craft it from blaze powder + slimeball. Brew it into an Awkward Potion."
		"&eTip:&r add redstone for an 8-minute version before any lava-heavy trip."
	]
	quest.2A7CD7184FBD641A.title: "Ghast Tears"
	quest.2A7CD7184FBD641A.quest_subtitle: "Regeneration, from a crying ghast"
	quest.2A7CD7184FBD641A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ghast tears brew Regeneration and drop rarely, since the ghast must die over solid ground."
		"&eHow:&r reflect a fireball back with a punch or arrow, then catch the tear before it burns in lava."
		"&eTip:&r a bow and patience beat chasing ghasts across lava lakes."
	]
	quest.5162E347921E0863.title: "Ancient Debris"
	quest.5162E347921E0863.quest_subtitle: "The rarest ore in the Nether"
	quest.5162E347921E0863.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ancient debris smelts into netherite scrap, the base of netherite gear."
		"&eHow:&r it hides deep in the Nether (around Y 8-22) and resists explosions, so bed or TNT mining works."
		"&eTip:&r try the Dissolver on a scrap later and see what this 'element' really is."
	]
	quest.32E9236C34FD4F59.title: "Fire into Source"
	quest.32E9236C34FD4F59.quest_subtitle: "Burn fuel to make magical Source"
	quest.32E9236C34FD4F59.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Volcanic Sourcelink turns burning fuel into Source, the energy behind Ars Nouveau."
		"&eHow:&r craft it from source gems, gold and a lava bucket, place it near a Source Jar and give it fuel. The Worn Notebook explains the details."
		"&eTip:&r it suits a Nether-themed base: blaze rods and lava-adjacent fuels keep it going."
	]
	quest.7FC86D79A91A5FFB.title: "Archwood"
	quest.7FC86D79A91A5FFB.quest_subtitle: "Magic trees in the archwood forests"
	quest.7FC86D79A91A5FFB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r archwood is Ars Nouveau's magic wood, used for its jars, tables and rituals."
		"&eHow:&r look for brightly coloured trees in archwood forests; any colour works, but this quest wants blue."
		"&eTip:&r archwood saplings grow at home, so a few logs become a farm."
	]
	quest.04AB64EC70146236.title: "Whispers of Magic"
	quest.04AB64EC70146236.quest_subtitle: "Light magic suits a demigod"
	quest.04AB64EC70146236.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Worn Notebook teaches Ars Nouveau spellcrafting. Source gems are its basic magical material."
		"&eHow:&r the notebook is a book + lapis lazuli (shapeless). Source gems come from the Imbuement Chamber (lapis or amethyst + Source)."
		"&eTip:&r its Ritual of Flight is a second way to fly near your base. See the Ars Nouveau page (Magic and Relics)."
	]
	chapter.00581FF47AFBFC11.title: "IV. The Electric Age"
	chapter.00581FF47AFBFC11.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Electricity is the tool that splits compounds apart. First you have to make it, and build the circuits that use it."
	]
	quest.06244939DFC248C8.title: "Rubber"
	quest.06244939DFC248C8.quest_subtitle: "Insulation, so current goes where you want"
	quest.06244939DFC248C8.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember lightning answering when you called it. Now you'll have to build it a road.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r rubber sheets insulate cables and form circuit boards."
		"&eChemistry:&r natural rubber is polyisoprene, (C₅H₈)ₙ: long chains that don't let electrons through."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI (press R on Rubber Sheet) for MI's rubber recipes, from plant matter or, later, synthetic rubber."
	]
	quest.57D063A8E142DE9D.title: "Wires and Cables"
	quest.57D063A8E142DE9D.quest_subtitle: "Copper conducts; rubber makes it a cable"
	quest.57D063A8E142DE9D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r copper wire goes into every component. Tin cable carries LV power between machines."
		"&eChemistry:&r copper's single outer electron moves freely between atoms, which is why it conducts so well."
		"&eHow:&r the Steel Wiremill pulls plates into wire. Cables combine wire with rubber sheets."
		"&eTip:&r tin cable is rated for LV (32 EU/t). Higher tiers need better cable."
	]
	quest.03F683AA3BD598A6.title: "Battery Alloy"
	quest.03F683AA3BD598A6.quest_subtitle: "Lead and antimony, as in a car battery"
	quest.03F683AA3BD598A6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r battery alloy makes the casing and grids of redstone batteries."
		"&eChemistry:&r lead hardened with antimony is the grid metal of real lead-acid batteries. Pure lead is too soft."
		"&eHow:&r mix lead and antimony dust (check JEI), then smelt. Lead deposits sit around Y -24 to 16."
	]
	quest.66D90743DD8F6EC0.title: "Analog Circuit Board"
	quest.66D90743DD8F6EC0.quest_subtitle: "Rubber, copper, rubber"
	quest.66D90743DD8F6EC0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the base every analog circuit is soldered onto."
		"&eHow:&r rubber sheet, copper plate, rubber sheet stacked in a column."
		"&eTip:&r once you have an Assembler, it makes these automatically."
	]
	quest.28A08814D26B46D9.title: "Capacitor"
	quest.28A08814D26B46D9.quest_subtitle: "Stores charge between two plates"
	quest.28A08814D26B46D9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r capacitors store a small charge and smooth out the current."
		"&eChemistry:&r two conductors (gold plates) separated by an insulator (rubber): charge builds up on each side."
		"&eHow:&r gold plates, copper wire and a rubber sheet (see JEI)."
	]
	quest.4D4359831AE16AE9.title: "Resistor"
	quest.4D4359831AE16AE9.quest_subtitle: "Limits the current through a circuit"
	quest.4D4359831AE16AE9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r resistors limit current so the rest of the circuit doesn't burn out."
		"&eChemistry:&r carbon conducts, but poorly. A pinch of coal dust between fine copper wires makes a carbon resistor."
		"&eHow:&r paper, copper fine wire and coal dust. One craft gives three."
	]
	quest.3562EE0D06376879.title: "Inductor"
	quest.3562EE0D06376879.quest_subtitle: "A coil that resists change"
	quest.3562EE0D06376879.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r inductors resist sudden changes in current. The Polarizer also needs them."
		"&eChemistry:&r current through a coil makes a magnetic field; changing the current fights that field."
		"&eHow:&r copper wire wound around a steel rod."
	]
	quest.2BF86ECE9691E81C.title: "Redstone Battery"
	quest.2BF86ECE9691E81C.quest_subtitle: "The LV hull needs two"
	quest.2BF86ECE9691E81C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a simple rechargeable battery. Every LV hull holds two."
		"&eHow:&r battery alloy plate and curved plates, tin cable and redstone (see JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the LV Storage Unit is built from six of these, so make spares."
	]
	quest.55AF98DD41956199.title: "Analog Circuit"
	quest.55AF98DD41956199.quest_subtitle: "Your first circuit"
	quest.55AF98DD41956199.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the LV circuit. Mekanism's Basic Control Circuit also needs one, so MI and Mekanism advance together."
		"&eHow:&r 2 resistors, 1 inductor, 2 capacitors, the board, and 3 copper wire (see JEI for the layout)."
		"&eTip:&r make four or five now. The hull, turbine and each machine all eat them."
	]
	quest.0E122D2C0AEFAF5E.title: "Steel Machine Casing"
	quest.0E122D2C0AEFAF5E.quest_subtitle: "The frame inside every LV machine"
	quest.0E122D2C0AEFAF5E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a steel frame. The LV hull is built around it."
		"&eHow:&r steel plates (see JEI). You've made the bronze one already; this is the steel upgrade."
		"&eTip:&r the LV hull uses one casing each, and every LV machine needs a hull. Make a few."
	]
	quest.392A7909301184E2.title: "LV Machine Hull"
	quest.392A7909301184E2.quest_subtitle: "The heart of every LV machine"
	quest.392A7909301184E2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Your hands remember wiring this. Your mind is still catching up.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r &eLV&r (Low Voltage) is the first electric tier. Every LV machine is built on this hull."
		"&eHow:&r steel machine casing + analog circuit + 2 redstone batteries + 3 tin cable."
	]
	quest.1295A863E0D4A446.title: "Magnetic Steel Rod"
	quest.1295A863E0D4A446.quest_subtitle: "A steel rod surrounded by redstone"
	quest.1295A863E0D4A446.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the core of an electric motor."
		"&eChemistry:&r iron-based alloys hold magnetism because their electron spins line up in domains."
		"&eHow:&r a steel rod ringed by redstone. Later the Polarizer magnetises rods with electricity."
	]
	quest.2082C655C0D3F03A.title: "Electric Motor"
	quest.2082C655C0D3F03A.quest_subtitle: "Electricity in, rotation out"
	quest.2082C655C0D3F03A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r motors drive turbines, pistons, conveyors and robot arms. Nearly every LV machine needs one."
		"&eChemistry:&r current in a coil next to a magnet creates a force; that's the motor effect. Run it backwards and it's a generator."
		"&eHow:&r magnetic steel rod, steel rods, copper wire and tin cable (see JEI)."
	]
	quest.2535BA17FB64FACE.title: "Steam to Electricity"
	quest.2535BA17FB64FACE.quest_subtitle: "Your boilers become a power plant"
	quest.2535BA17FB64FACE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a turbine turns your boiler's steam into &eEU&r, MI's electricity."
		"&eHow:&r pipe steam in, and run tin cable from the turbine to your machines."
		"&eTip:&r watch the turbine's steam input. If machines stall, add boilers before adding turbines."
	]
	quest.18D25C63CA285B54.title: "Piston"
	quest.18D25C63CA285B54.quest_subtitle: "A motor that pushes"
	quest.18D25C63CA285B54.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI's piston component, used in the macerator, compressor and robot arm."
		"&eHow:&r steel plates, steel rods, steel gear, tin cable and a motor."
		"&eTip:&r the Electric Macerator and Electric Compressor each need pistons, so make four."
	]
	quest.5E348DAE3EAE594E.title: "Conveyor"
	quest.5E348DAE3EAE594E.quest_subtitle: "A rubber belt on two motors"
	quest.5E348DAE3EAE594E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r conveyors move items inside machines. The Assembler, Packer and Cutting Machine need them."
		"&eHow:&r rubber sheets, two motors and tin cable."
		"&eTip:&r motors are the bottleneck here. Keep a few spare."
	]
	quest.2F67A54D1D634F0A.title: "Electric Compressor"
	quest.2F67A54D1D634F0A.quest_subtitle: "Plates, faster and without steam"
	quest.2F67A54D1D634F0A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r plates, curved plates and rings for every part you'll build next."
		"&eHow:&r LV hull, two pistons, analog circuits and tin cable."
		"&eTip:&r it doubles as a second plate source while the steam compressor keeps running."
	]
	quest.0E77517E4651B27A.title: "Electric Wiremill"
	quest.0E77517E4651B27A.quest_subtitle: "Wire, faster"
	quest.0E77517E4651B27A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r copper wire and fine wire in bulk. Circuits use a lot of it."
		"&eHow:&r LV hull, motors and analog circuits (see JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r feed it from your compressor's plate output."
	]
	quest.2EF4BB510E2F28AC.title: "Polarizer"
	quest.2EF4BB510E2F28AC.quest_subtitle: "Magnetises rods and wires"
	quest.2EF4BB510E2F28AC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r magnetic steel rods for motors, and &emagnetic cupronickel wire&r for heating coils."
		"&eChemistry:&r a strong field lines up the magnetic domains in the metal, and they stay lined up."
		"&eHow:&r LV hull, inductors, tin wire and tin cable."
	]
	quest.48A4FFD83AE8AD44.title: "Electric Mixer"
	quest.48A4FFD83AE8AD44.quest_subtitle: "Alloy dusts and chemical mixes"
	quest.48A4FFD83AE8AD44.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r mixing dusts into alloys (bronze, invar, cupronickel, battery alloy) and fluids into mixtures."
		"&eHow:&r LV hull, motor, tin rotor, glass, a fluid pipe and analog circuits."
		"&eTip:&r you'll need it for cupronickel (copper + nickel) and invar (iron + nickel) right away."
	]
	quest.541A010A43E31E95.title: "Electric Macerator"
	quest.541A010A43E31E95.quest_subtitle: "Grinding, now electric"
	quest.541A010A43E31E95.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ore to crushed dust, ingots back to dust. Still capped at 2x per ore until acids."
		"&eHow:&r needs an &einvar rotary blade&r (invar gear + diamond dust). Invar is iron + nickel; mix the dusts."
		"&eTip:&r the hull quest reward included one. Build a second for throughput."
	]
	quest.435D6984CDDF47E1.title: "Electric Furnace"
	quest.435D6984CDDF47E1.quest_subtitle: "Smelting with heat from a wire coil"
	quest.435D6984CDDF47E1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fast, fuel-free smelting."
		"&eChemistry:&r current through a resistive wire turns into heat (Joule heating), the same idea as a toaster."
		"&eHow:&r LV hull wrapped in magnetic cupronickel wire, with analog circuits."
	]
	quest.23F83FE4BAEF4BD9.title: "Robot Arm"
	quest.23F83FE4BAEF4BD9.quest_subtitle: "Motors, a piston and a circuit"
	quest.23F83FE4BAEF4BD9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r robot arms move parts inside the Assembler and Packer."
		"&eHow:&r two motors, a piston, steel rods, tin cable and an analog circuit."
		"&eTip:&r the Assembler takes two and the Packer two more."
	]
	quest.7364759091BAA54E.title: "Cutting Machine"
	quest.7364759091BAA54E.quest_subtitle: "Rods, bolts and planks"
	quest.7364759091BAA54E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r cutting ingots into rods and bolts, and logs into more planks."
		"&eHow:&r it uses an invar rotary blade, motors and a conveyor. Its cuts use a little lubricant (check JEI for where to get it)."
		"&eTip:&r logs give six planks here instead of four."
	]
	quest.0DFEE581F10201B2.title: "Magnetic Cupronickel Wire"
	quest.0DFEE581F10201B2.quest_subtitle: "Copper-nickel wire for heating coils"
	quest.0DFEE581F10201B2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the heating wire for the Electric Furnace and Electric Blast Furnace."
		"&eChemistry:&r cupronickel (copper + nickel) resists current more than copper and survives heat. Coins and ship pipes use it too."
		"&eHow:&r mix copper and nickel dust, smelt, draw into wire, then magnetise it in the Polarizer."
	]
	quest.290BB135DCEA6DC7.title: "Assembler"
	quest.290BB135DCEA6DC7.quest_subtitle: "Where MI automation really starts"
	quest.290BB135DCEA6DC7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r circuits and machine parts, automatically, from a stocked input."
		"&eHow:&r LV hull, two robot arms, two conveyors and two analog circuits."
		"&eTip:&r MI shows every assembler recipe in JEI. Feed it sheets, wire and plates and leave it running."
	]
	quest.6D28244E306FB852.title: "Packer"
	quest.6D28244E306FB852.quest_subtitle: "Blocks, double ingots and more"
	quest.6D28244E306FB852.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r compacting ingots into blocks and double ingots, and assembling a few parts. You'll want bauxite blocks next chapter."
		"&eHow:&r robot arms, conveyors, analog circuits and tin cable on an LV hull."
		"&eTip:&r unpacking is a separate machine, the Unpacker. Build one if you store metal as blocks."
	]
	quest.0213687BA73A9908.title: "Electric Blast Furnace"
	quest.0213687BA73A9908.quest_subtitle: "The furnace that makes aluminum"
	quest.0213687BA73A9908.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fire you can measure in volts. You used to do this without the volts.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r MI's big furnace multiblock. With cupronickel coils it reaches the heat for &ealuminum&r and &esilicon&r."
		"&eHow:&r the controller is an LV hull wrapped in magnetic cupronickel wire. Check the structure in JEI or the MI guidebook, then add an LV energy input hatch and item hatches."
		"&eTip:&r hold a hatch or wrench near the controller to see the valid positions highlighted."
	]
	quest.474137432EABE206.title: "Osmium"
	quest.474137432EABE206.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism's blue-grey metal"
	quest.474137432EABE206.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism builds almost everything from osmium: its infuser, casings and circuits."
		"&eChemistry:&r real osmium is the densest natural element, 22.6 g/cm³. A litre of it weighs about as much as a big dog."
		"&eHow:&r osmium ore is common in small veins underground. Smelt the raw osmium into ingots."
	]
	quest.42B76D3BDE21F0DC.title: "Mekanism: Metallurgic Infuser"
	quest.42B76D3BDE21F0DC.quest_subtitle: "Infuse metals with carbon, redstone and more"
	quest.42B76D3BDE21F0DC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism's entry machine. It infuses metals with other materials."
		"&eHow:&r iron ingots, redstone, an osmium ingot and two furnaces."
		"&eTip:&r it runs on FE. Your Chapter II generator works, or a Mekanism Heat Generator (Power chapter)."
	]
	quest.354E125FC5D3BB01.title: "Infused Alloy"
	quest.354E125FC5D3BB01.quest_subtitle: "Copper infused with redstone"
	quest.354E125FC5D3BB01.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism's basic alloy. The Enrichment Chamber and many basic machines need it."
		"&eChemistry:&r a real alloy mixes metals at the atomic level. Here redstone plays the part of the second element."
		"&eHow:&r put redstone in the infuser's left slot (it becomes an infusion buffer), then feed copper ingots."
	]
	quest.480FB3C55927F1A1.title: "Mekanism Circuits"
	quest.480FB3C55927F1A1.quest_subtitle: "MI's analog circuit, in Mekanism form"
	quest.480FB3C55927F1A1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r in this pack, a Basic Control Circuit is &eMI Analog Circuit + osmium&r. Each Mekanism circuit tier needs the matching MI circuit."
		"&eHow:&r the Steel Casing (steel, glass and osmium) is the frame for most Mekanism machines."
		"&eTip:&r make several casings at once. Every Mekanism machine in the next chapter needs one."
	]
	quest.3A2454B103645938.title: "Enrichment Chamber"
	quest.3A2454B103645938.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism's 2x ore processing"
	quest.3A2454B103645938.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ore → 2 dust. It also turns dirty dust into clean dust in the higher-tier lines."
		"&eHow:&r steel casing, infused alloy, iron and a basic control circuit."
		"&eTip:&r 3x, 4x and 5x need gases and acids: that's the next chapter."
	]
	quest.6BB487593411143E.title: "Crusher"
	quest.6BB487593411143E.quest_subtitle: "Clumps into dirty dust"
	quest.6BB487593411143E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r crushes ingots to dust and, later, ore clumps into dirty dust in the 3x+ lines."
		"&eHow:&r steel casing, basic control circuits, redstone and lava buckets."
		"&eTip:&r it also turns ingots back into dust, handy for alloy recipes."
	]
	quest.0FC4E1E093B6BE04.title: "The Wrench"
	quest.0FC4E1E093B6BE04.quest_subtitle: "Rotate machines, see multiblock spots"
	quest.0FC4E1E093B6BE04.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI's wrench adjusts machines and pipes. Read its tooltip for the controls."
		"&eHow:&r bronze plates (see JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r holding it near a multiblock controller highlights where the hatches can go."
	]
	quest.715BC066754DE9B0.title: "Pipe Config Card"
	quest.715BC066754DE9B0.quest_subtitle: "Copy one pipe's settings to another"
	quest.715BC066754DE9B0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r saves an item or fluid pipe connection's settings and pastes them onto other connections."
		"&eHow:&r sneak + use on a configured pipe connection to save; use on another connection to apply. Sneak + use on air clears it."
		"&eTip:&r it can also camouflage pipes as any block. The card's tooltip explains how."
	]
	quest.58932C2263D38534.title: "LV Storage Unit"
	quest.58932C2263D38534.quest_subtitle: "A buffer for your power grid"
	quest.58932C2263D38534.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r stores EU, so machines keep running when the turbine can't keep up for a moment."
		"&eHow:&r six redstone batteries, battery alloy plates and an LV hull."
		"&eTip:&r put it between turbine and machines so short dips don't stop anything."
	]
	quest.7DE855B5084E6181.title: "Electric Water Pump"
	quest.7DE855B5084E6181.quest_subtitle: "Endless water for boilers"
	quest.7DE855B5084E6181.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r pumps water from nothing but power, for boilers and (soon) electrolysis."
		"&eHow:&r an LV hull with a pump, tin rotor, pipes and an analog circuit."
		"&eTip:&r next chapter, water becomes hydrogen and oxygen. You'll want lots of it."
	]
	quest.4C7AA8620B6D2885.title: "The Spectrometer"
	quest.4C7AA8620B6D2885.quest_subtitle: "Every element sings its own colour"
	quest.4C7AA8620B6D2885.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember seeing the colours inside things, the light every element gives off.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a hand-held scanner (Warbucks Core, made for this pack). Right-click to read the ore signal in the loaded chunks around you."
		"&eChemistry:&r heated atoms give off light only at certain wavelengths, an emission spectrum unique to each element. That's how helium was found in the Sun before anyone found it on Earth."
		"&eHow:&r amethyst prism, steel plates, copper wire and an analog circuit (check JEI). It lists each element with its strength, direction, distance and depth."
		"&eTip:&r a \"strong\" signal is usually a rich deposit. Walk towards it and scan again."
	]
	quest.70A17E4532B8DA8B.title: "A Rich Lead Deposit"
	quest.70A17E4532B8DA8B.quest_subtitle: "Find a chunk full of lead"
	quest.70A17E4532B8DA8B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r rich ore deposits hold hundreds of ores in one chunk, at a metal-specific depth. Lead's sits around Y -24 to 16."
		"&eHow:&r strip-mine at that depth and check ore with Jade. FTB Ultimine clears a vein in one go."
		"&eTip:&r galena (lead sulfide, PbS) is the world's main lead ore, and it often carries silver."
	]
	quest.6A50FF652B6B5624.title: "Osmium Hoard"
	quest.6A50FF652B6B5624.quest_subtitle: "Stockpile for the Mekanism build-out"
	quest.6A50FF652B6B5624.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every Mekanism machine, casing and circuit costs osmium. A stockpile saves trips."
		"&eHow:&r smelt or enrich raw osmium into ingots."
		"&eTip:&r the Enrichment Chamber doubles osmium ore, so process it there once it's built."
	]
	chapter.6549651AA2526584.title: "V. Electrochemistry and Acids"
	chapter.6549651AA2526584.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Electricity splits compounds into elements. Acids dissolve what fire can't."
		"Ore processing becomes chemistry."
	]
	quest.0D7390621F3F2B9F.title: "Mekanism Gases"
	quest.0D7390621F3F2B9F.quest_subtitle: "Split water into hydrogen and oxygen"
	quest.0D7390621F3F2B9F.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember pulling water apart with a word. A machine and a cable will have to do.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Electrolytic Separator makes hydrogen and oxygen as gases you can pipe and store."
		"&eChemistry:&r 2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂. Current drives the reaction backwards from burning hydrogen."
		"&eHow:&r feed it water and FE. Gases leave from the coloured sides (configure them with the Configurator)."
	]
	quest.326FC7460262152E.title: "Pressurized Tubes"
	quest.326FC7460262152E.quest_subtitle: "Pipes for gases"
	quest.326FC7460262152E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r gases need sealed tubes. Item pipes and fluid pipes won't carry them."
		"&eHow:&r craft basic pressurized tubes (see JEI) and run them from the separator's outputs."
		"&eTip:&r vent what you don't need yet. A full output tank stops the whole separator."
	]
	quest.5FB4044A1D311473.title: "A Source of Sulfur"
	quest.5FB4044A1D311473.quest_subtitle: "Yellow brimstone for the contact process"
	quest.5FB4044A1D311473.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r sulfur is where sulfuric acid starts."
		"&eChemistry:&r S is element 16. Volcanoes and fossil fuels are full of it; most industrial sulfur is stripped out of oil and gas."
		"&eHow:&r macerate crushed lignite coal (about half the time you get sulfur dust), or centrifuge lava later. Press U on Sulfur Dust in JEI for all sources."
	]
	quest.4B75115FF988850B.title: "Contact Process 1: SO₂"
	quest.4B75115FF988850B.quest_subtitle: "Burn sulfur into sulfur dioxide"
	quest.4B75115FF988850B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Chemical Oxidizer turns a solid into a gas. Sulfur dust becomes sulfur dioxide."
		"&eChemistry:&r S + O₂ → SO₂. It's the sharp smell of a struck match."
		"&eHow:&r one sulfur dust gives 100 mB of SO₂. Pipe it out with pressurized tubes."
	]
	quest.25824A2CB3B866D5.title: "Contact Process 2: SO₃"
	quest.25824A2CB3B866D5.quest_subtitle: "Sulfur dioxide + oxygen"
	quest.25824A2CB3B866D5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Chemical Infuser combines two gases. SO₂ plus oxygen from your separator gives sulfur trioxide."
		"&eChemistry:&r 2SO₂ + O₂ → 2SO₃. Real plants pass the gases over a vanadium oxide (V₂O₅) catalyst at about 450 °C: the 'contact' in the name."
		"&eHow:&r SO₂ in one side, O₂ in the other."
	]
	quest.4630AF08524F8BB3.title: "Water Vapor"
	quest.4630AF08524F8BB3.quest_subtitle: "Turn water into a gas Mekanism can use"
	quest.4630AF08524F8BB3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Rotary Condensentrator converts fluids to gases and back. It turns water into water vapor."
		"&eHow:&r set it to gas mode (the toggle in its GUI), pipe water in and pressurized tube out."
		"&eTip:&r it also turns Mekanism gases into buckets, which is handy for storage and trading."
	]
	quest.7C9F89951691CE8C.title: "Contact Process 3: H₂SO₄"
	quest.7C9F89951691CE8C.quest_subtitle: "SO₃ + water vapor in a second infuser"
	quest.7C9F89951691CE8C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a second Chemical Infuser combines SO₃ with water vapor into sulfuric acid gas. Tick this when acid is flowing."
		"&eChemistry:&r SO₃ + H₂O → H₂SO₄. Real plants dissolve SO₃ in existing acid first (oleum), because SO₃ and water alone make a corrosive mist."
		"&eTip:&r store the acid in a chemical tank. The 5x ore line drinks it."
	]
	quest.4015B208E94DAE2D.title: "Salt"
	quest.4015B208E94DAE2D.quest_subtitle: "Sodium chloride, NaCl"
	quest.4015B208E94DAE2D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r salt is the start of the chlor-alkali industry: chlorine, sodium and everything made from them."
		"&eChemistry:&r NaCl is an ionic crystal: Na⁺ and Cl⁻ held together by charge. Split it and you get a soft, reactive metal and a toxic green gas."
		"&eHow:&r MI salt ore is found underground and drops salt dust."
	]
	quest.1CA114894501491D.title: "Brine"
	quest.1CA114894501491D.quest_subtitle: "Salt dissolved in water"
	quest.1CA114894501491D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r brine is salty water, and Mekanism splits it into chlorine. Tick this when you have brine."
		"&eHow:&r put salt dust in a Chemical Oxidizer (15 mB brine per dust), or build a Thermal Evaporation Plant (see the side quest)."
		"&eTip:&r a second oxidizer just for salt saves you from swapping inputs."
	]
	quest.573EAFB3E7A17498.title: "Chlorine"
	quest.573EAFB3E7A17498.quest_subtitle: "Electrolyse brine into Cl₂ and sodium"
	quest.573EAFB3E7A17498.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Electrolytic Separator also takes brine. Out come chlorine and sodium. Tick this when chlorine is flowing."
		"&eChemistry:&r real brine electrolysis gives Cl₂ at one electrode and H₂ + NaOH at the other. Mekanism simplifies it to sodium + chlorine."
		"&eTip:&r use a second separator so your hydrogen and oxygen line keeps running."
	]
	quest.649A4F33DE9E7A82.title: "Hydrogen Chloride"
	quest.649A4F33DE9E7A82.quest_subtitle: "H₂ + Cl₂ in a Chemical Infuser"
	quest.649A4F33DE9E7A82.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r hydrogen chloride drives the 4x ore line. Tick this when HCl is flowing."
		"&eChemistry:&r H₂ + Cl₂ → 2HCl. Dissolved in water it's hydrochloric acid, the same acid in your stomach."
		"&eHow:&r hydrogen in one side of a Chemical Infuser, chlorine in the other."
	]
	quest.613C5C713C056E03.title: "3x Ore: Oxygen"
	quest.613C5C713C056E03.quest_subtitle: "Purification Chamber + oxygen"
	quest.613C5C713C056E03.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r before acids, every route caps at &e2x&r per ore. Purifying ore with oxygen gives &e3x&r."
		"&eHow:&r ore + O₂ → 3 clumps. Crusher: clumps → dirty dust. Enrichment Chamber: dirty dust → dust."
		"&eTip:&r Mekanism shows each step in JEI. Chain them with pipes and side configuration."
	]
	quest.5DC82018A921CB16.title: "4x Ore: Hydrogen Chloride"
	quest.5DC82018A921CB16.quest_subtitle: "Chemical Injection Chamber + HCl"
	quest.5DC82018A921CB16.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r injecting hydrogen chloride splits ore into shards: &e4x&r."
		"&eHow:&r ore + HCl → 4 shards. Purification Chamber: shards → clumps, then on through your 3x line."
		"&eTip:&r your 3x machines are now the back half of the 4x line. Nothing is wasted."
	]
	quest.1F8977634DAF6D2D.title: "Dissolving Ore"
	quest.1F8977634DAF6D2D.quest_subtitle: "Ore + sulfuric acid → dirty slurry"
	quest.1F8977634DAF6D2D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Dissolution Chamber dissolves ore in sulfuric acid, giving a dirty slurry."
		"&eChemistry:&r acid leaching: H₂SO₄ turns metal minerals into soluble sulfates, leaving the rock behind."
		"&eHow:&r feed it ore and sulfuric acid gas. The slurry comes out as a chemical."
	]
	quest.6D834765E3A2FDF2.title: "Washing Slurry"
	quest.6D834765E3A2FDF2.quest_subtitle: "Dirty slurry + water → clean slurry"
	quest.6D834765E3A2FDF2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Chemical Washer rinses impurities out of the slurry."
		"&eChemistry:&r washing removes the dissolved gangue (waste rock) so only the metal salt is left to crystallise."
		"&eHow:&r slurry in, water in, clean slurry out. An MI electric water pump keeps the water coming."
	]
	quest.79928EE6B7E8E534.title: "5x Ore: Dissolution"
	quest.79928EE6B7E8E534.quest_subtitle: "Crystallise the slurry: five from one"
	quest.79928EE6B7E8E534.quest_desc: [
		"&6Five from one. You used to call that a small miracle. Now you call it hydrometallurgy.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Chemical Crystallizer turns clean slurry into crystals: &e5x&r per ore."
		"&eChemistry:&r this is &ehydrometallurgy&r, the way most of the world's copper is really refined."
		"&eHow:&r crystals → Injection Chamber (shards) → Purification Chamber (clumps) → Crusher → Enrichment Chamber."
	]
	quest.5610598250CF6B1D.title: "Ore Byproducts"
	quest.5610598250CF6B1D.quest_subtitle: "Dirty dust through a centrifuge"
	quest.5610598250CF6B1D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r real ores are never pure. Send Mekanism's &edirty dust&r through MI's &eCentrifuge&r instead of the Enrichment Chamber for the same dust plus a chance at a bonus metal."
		"&eChemistry:&r iron → nickel, copper → gold, gold → silver, &elead → silver&r (galena), tin → tungsten, osmium → iridium, uranium → lead (decay)."
		"&eHow:&r the Centrifuge needs an electronic circuit. Route dirty dust to it, and rare metals arrive as a bonus."
	]
	quest.543D2B2404F95AAA.title: "Bauxite"
	quest.543D2B2404F95AAA.quest_subtitle: "The ore aluminum hides in"
	quest.543D2B2404F95AAA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r bauxite is the only practical aluminum ore. MI bauxite ore drops bauxite dust."
		"&eChemistry:&r bauxite is mostly aluminium hydroxides, Al(OH)₃ and AlO(OH), stained red by iron oxide."
		"&eHow:&r rich bauxite deposits sit around Y -16 to 24. Pack 9 dust into a bauxite block (Packer or crafting grid)."
	]
	quest.4718BEF4ACA3AAE9.title: "Aluminum"
	quest.4718BEF4ACA3AAE9.quest_subtitle: "Bauxite block → aluminum ingot in the EBF"
	quest.4718BEF4ACA3AAE9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r aluminum is the metal of the MV tier: boards, rotors, casings."
		"&eChemistry:&r aluminium is the most common metal in the crust but clings to oxygen. It only got cheap after 1886, when Hall and Héroult electrolysed molten alumina."
		"&eHow:&r Electric Blast Furnace with cupronickel coils: 1 bauxite block → 1 aluminum ingot."
		"&eTip:&r once you have an Electrolyzer, 10 bauxite dust → 4 aluminum dust + titanium. Much better yield."
	]
	quest.628A267853F0DE86.title: "Electrum"
	quest.628A267853F0DE86.quest_subtitle: "Gold and silver, the ancient alloy"
	quest.628A267853F0DE86.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r electrum cable and fine wire go into every MV component."
		"&eChemistry:&r electrum is a natural gold-silver alloy. The first coins, in Lydia around 600 BC, were struck from it."
		"&eHow:&r mix gold and silver dust, then smelt. Check JEI (press R on Silver Dust) for silver ore in this pack."
	]
	quest.26C82AE08878EB74.title: "Silicon"
	quest.26C82AE08878EB74.quest_subtitle: "Quartz + carbon in the EBF"
	quest.26C82AE08878EB74.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r silicon is the semiconductor every transistor and diode is built on."
		"&eChemistry:&r SiO₂ + 2C → Si + 2CO. Carbon pulls the oxygen off quartz at furnace heat: carbothermic reduction."
		"&eHow:&r macerate quartz into dust, then EBF: quartz dust + coke dust → silicon dust. Smelt it into ingots."
	]
	quest.28A4F44C2FBD94F2.title: "Electronic Circuit Board"
	quest.28A4F44C2FBD94F2.quest_subtitle: "Aluminum, electrum and a battery"
	quest.28A4F44C2FBD94F2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the base for MV circuits."
		"&eHow:&r an analog circuit board with aluminum plates, electrum cable and a redstone battery (see JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the Assembler can make these too, once you stock it."
	]
	quest.714E6088B9678A36.title: "Transistors and Diodes"
	quest.714E6088B9678A36.quest_subtitle: "Semiconductors, finally"
	quest.714E6088B9678A36.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r diodes let current flow one way; transistors are switches controlled by current."
		"&eChemistry:&r a pure silicon crystal barely conducts. Tiny amounts of other elements ('doping') make it conduct in controllable ways."
		"&eHow:&r silicon plates, steel plates and electrum fine wire (diodes add glass)."
	]
	quest.6C18ADE33F69C1A9.title: "Electronic Circuit"
	quest.6C18ADE33F69C1A9.quest_subtitle: "The MV circuit"
	quest.6C18ADE33F69C1A9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the MV circuit. The Electrolyzer, Chemical Reactor and Centrifuge all need it, even though they sit on an LV hull."
		"&eHow:&r electronic circuit board, 4 analog circuits, 2 diodes and 2 transistors."
		"&eTip:&r set an Assembler to make these. You'll need dozens."
	]
	quest.6913B96166CC25DA.title: "Electrolysis"
	quest.6913B96166CC25DA.quest_subtitle: "MI's electrolysis machine"
	quest.6913B96166CC25DA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r pass current through a compound and it splits. This is &eelectrochemistry&r."
		"&eChemistry:&r water → H₂ + O₂ (3000 mB water → 2000 mB H₂ + 1000 mB O₂). Salt → sodium + chlorine. Bauxite → aluminum + titanium."
		"&eHow:&r magnetic cupronickel wire, aluminum rods, an LV hull, an electronic circuit and a large pump."
	]
	quest.256D9F2CFA36ADE2.title: "The Chemical Reactor"
	quest.256D9F2CFA36ADE2.quest_subtitle: "MI's general-purpose reaction vessel"
	quest.256D9F2CFA36ADE2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r combines items and fluids into new compounds. You'll use it constantly from here to the end."
		"&eHow:&r glass, a large pump, aluminum rotors, an LV hull, electronic circuits and electrum cable."
		"&eTip:&r MI fluids go in through pipes. A Configurable Tank holds spare H₂ and O₂."
	]
	quest.73B0B0B23BDA8732.title: "Sodium"
	quest.73B0B0B23BDA8732.quest_subtitle: "Electrolyse salt: sodium + chlorine"
	quest.73B0B0B23BDA8732.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r sodium goes into the HV tier's sodium battery. The chlorine is a bonus."
		"&eChemistry:&r 2NaCl → 2Na + Cl₂. Real sodium is made this way from molten salt (the Downs cell). It reacts violently with water."
		"&eHow:&r Electrolyzer: 2 salt dust → 1 sodium dust + 125 mB chlorine."
	]
	quest.4377040E34093CBC.title: "Sulfuric Acid"
	quest.4377040E34093CBC.quest_subtitle: "The most-produced chemical on Earth"
	quest.4377040E34093CBC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Acid opens what fire cannot. You remember that lesson; you remember learning it the hard way.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r sulfuric acid, as an MI fluid you can bucket. The Undergarden portal and many MI recipes need it."
		"&eChemistry:&r S + O₂ + H₂O → &eH₂SO₄&r, the whole contact process in one vessel. Industry makes more of it than any other chemical."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: 1 sulfur dust + 200 mB O₂ + 200 mB water → 500 mB sulfuric acid."
	]
	quest.5869888A4C20B8A7.title: "Silicon Battery"
	quest.5869888A4C20B8A7.quest_subtitle: "The MV hull needs two"
	quest.5869888A4C20B8A7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the MV battery. Every MV hull holds two."
		"&eHow:&r battery alloy plates, electrum cable and silicon dust."
		"&eTip:&r make four. The Advanced (MV) hull uses two, and you'll want a second hull soon."
	]
	quest.17832D4C895DEFF7.title: "MV: Aluminum"
	quest.17832D4C895DEFF7.quest_subtitle: "Medium Voltage: the MV machine hull"
	quest.17832D4C895DEFF7.quest_desc: [
		"&6The circuits are getting smaller and the power larger. So are you.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the &eMV hull&r is the base for every MV machine, and Powah, Hostile Neural Networks and Extended Crafting all want MV circuits."
		"&eHow:&r advanced machine casing (an LV hull wrapped in aluminum plates) + electronic circuit + 2 silicon batteries + electrum cable."
	]
	quest.758A1909AD8F6980.title: "Uranium"
	quest.758A1909AD8F6980.quest_subtitle: "Deep, heavy and faintly warm"
	quest.758A1909AD8F6980.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r uranium is the fuel of Powah's reactors and, much later, fission."
		"&eChemistry:&r U is element 92, the heaviest element found in quantity in nature. It slowly decays into lead."
		"&eHow:&r rich uranium deposits sit deep, around Y -56 to -24. Macerate the ore into dust."
	]
	quest.4F41C5095B66BC1F.title: "Uranium Dioxide"
	quest.4F41C5095B66BC1F.quest_subtitle: "Oxidise uranium in the Chemical Reactor"
	quest.4F41C5095B66BC1F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r uraninite fuels Powah's reactors. Powah's Energizing Orb needs an MV circuit."
		"&eChemistry:&r uraninite is UO₂, the main ore of uranium in nature. Here you make it: U + O₂ → UO₂."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: uranium dust + 500 mB oxygen → uraninite. Powah's own uraninite ore is turned off."
	]
	quest.6CD23CD722EC696F.title: "The Undergarden"
	quest.6CD23CD722EC696F.quest_subtitle: "A realm beneath the world"
	quest.6CD23CD722EC696F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a strange underground dimension. Its portal catalyst needs a bucket of MI sulfuric acid."
		"&eHow:&r build a stone-brick portal frame and right-click it with the catalyst."
		"&eTip:&r bring torches and food. It is dark down there."
	]
	quest.00FA8DB26B0899BD.title: "Thermal Evaporation"
	quest.00FA8DB26B0899BD.quest_subtitle: "Sun and heat turn water into brine"
	quest.00FA8DB26B0899BD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a tall multiblock that boils water down into brine, and brine down into lithium."
		"&eChemistry:&r evaporation concentrates dissolved salts. Salt flats and lithium ponds in Chile work the same way."
		"&eHow:&r see Just Enough Mekanism Multiblocks in JEI for the layout. Taller towers run faster; heat speeds it up."
	]
	quest.750A6D2490DE7F3E.title: "Bottled Gases"
	quest.750A6D2490DE7F3E.quest_subtitle: "Keep a tank of H₂, O₂ and Cl₂"
	quest.750A6D2490DE7F3E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r chemical tanks store gases and keep them when broken, so you can carry them around."
		"&eHow:&r fill one tank each with hydrogen, oxygen and chlorine."
		"&eTip:&r a tank of hydrogen also fuels the Gas-Burning Generator (Power chapter)."
	]
	quest.0524143B8E8534E6.title: "Fun Fact: Oleum"
	quest.0524143B8E8534E6.quest_subtitle: "How industry really makes H₂SO₄"
	quest.0524143B8E8534E6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r SO₃ hitting water directly forms a fine acid mist that's hard to capture."
		"&eChemistry:&r plants absorb SO₃ into concentrated H₂SO₄ to make oleum (H₂S₂O₇), then dilute: H₂S₂O₇ + H₂O → 2H₂SO₄."
		"&eTip:&r you've now run, in miniature, a process that makes over 250 million tonnes a year."
	]
	quest.6BB95E31DBD366B3.title: "Five for Everything"
	quest.6BB95E31DBD366B3.quest_subtitle: "Run iron, copper, gold, tin and osmium at 5x"
	quest.6BB95E31DBD366B3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a challenge: put at least five different ores through the full 5x line."
		"&eHow:&r one Dissolution Chamber handles every metal, but each slurry needs its own washer and crystallizer pass. Tick this when five ores are done."
		"&eTip:&r Mekanism factories (upgraded machines) run several ores at once."
	]
	quest.55F835AE318C2487.title: "A Red Mountain"
	quest.55F835AE318C2487.quest_subtitle: "Mine a rich bauxite deposit"
	quest.55F835AE318C2487.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r rich deposits hold hundreds of ores in one chunk. Find bauxite's and the MV tier stops feeling slow."
		"&eHow:&r strip-mine around Y -16 to 24 and look for red ore with Jade. FTB Ultimine helps a lot."
		"&eTip:&r Fortune works on bauxite ore, since it drops dust."
	]
	quest.21C7F639DD99DD59.title: "A Hint of Titanium"
	quest.21C7F639DD99DD59.quest_subtitle: "Bauxite electrolysis leaves titanium"
	quest.21C7F639DD99DD59.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r electrolysing bauxite dust gives aluminum dust plus a little titanium. Save it for much later."
		"&eChemistry:&r bauxite carries titanium dioxide (TiO₂) as an impurity. Real refineries leave it in 'red mud'."
		"&eHow:&r Electrolyzer: 10 bauxite dust → 4 aluminum dust + 3 tiny titanium dust."
	]
	quest.2D7E142062D6BFB0.title: "Hydrochloric Acid, MI Style"
	quest.2D7E142062D6BFB0.quest_subtitle: "H₂ + Cl₂ in the Chemical Reactor"
	quest.2D7E142062D6BFB0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI makes hydrochloric acid as a fluid, the alternative to Mekanism's HCl gas."
		"&eChemistry:&r H₂ + Cl₂ → 2HCl. 1000 mB of each gas gives 2000 mB of acid."
		"&eHow:&r chlorine from salt electrolysis, hydrogen from water electrolysis, both into the Chemical Reactor."
	]
	quest.5736D9E48B04A7B0.title: "Lye"
	quest.5736D9E48B04A7B0.quest_subtitle: "Sodium hydroxide, the strong base"
	quest.5736D9E48B04A7B0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r sodium hydroxide (NaOH, lye) is the strong base to sulfuric acid's strong acid. Soap is made with it."
		"&eChemistry:&r acid + base → salt + water. H₂SO₄ + 2NaOH → Na₂SO₄ + 2H₂O."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: sodium dust + 1000 mB oxygen + 1000 mB hydrogen → 2000 mB sodium hydroxide."
	]
	chapter.2059D0F0735E71DD.title: "VI. Petrochemistry"
	chapter.2059D0F0735E71DD.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Crude oil is a mixture. Separate it by boiling point, then build polymers from the pieces."
	]
	quest.3975D5E5733B2029.title: "Black Gold"
	quest.3975D5E5733B2029.quest_subtitle: "Millions of years of sunlight, stored underground"
	quest.3975D5E5733B2029.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember the world before people: forests that grew, died and sank, pressed into oil over ages you once watched pass.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r crude oil is a soup of hydrocarbons, from tiny gas molecules to long waxy chains."
		"&eChemistry:&r hydrocarbons are just carbon and hydrogen (CₙH₂ₙ₊₂ and friends). Chain length decides whether one is a gas, a fuel or a tar."
		"&eHow:&r put the Oil Drilling Rig in an MI Quarry over an oil-rich area (check JEI). It slowly wears out aluminum drills."
		"&eTip:&r pipe the crude straight into a tank. You'll need a lot of it."
	]
	quest.077B8D568A0E67A4.title: "Fractional Distillation"
	quest.077B8D568A0E67A4.quest_subtitle: "The refinery of the pack"
	quest.077B8D568A0E67A4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Distillation Tower is a multiblock that splits one fluid into several fractions at once."
		"&eChemistry:&r heat the crude and each fraction boils off at its own temperature. Light molecules rise to the top, heavy ones stay low."
		"&eHow:&r the 3D layout is in JEI and the MI guidebook. Each extra layer adds one more output."
		"&eTip:&r every other mod gets its fuel and plastic from here, so build it with room to grow."
	]
	quest.5C73D62A251E158E.title: "Sour Fractions"
	quest.5C73D62A251E158E.quest_subtitle: "Three cuts of crude, all still full of sulfur"
	quest.5C73D62A251E158E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 1000 mB of crude gives 500 light fuel, 200 heavy fuel and 300 naphtha, but all three are 'sour'."
		"&eChemistry:&r natural oil carries sulfur compounds. Burn them and you get SO₂, the gas behind acid rain."
		"&eHow:&r run crude through the Distillation Tower and catch each output in its own tank or bucket."
	]
	quest.41CD2A6115484870.title: "Sweetening the Oil"
	quest.41CD2A6115484870.quest_subtitle: "Hydrogen pulls the sulfur out"
	quest.41CD2A6115484870.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r hydrotreating removes the sulfur and gives clean light fuel, heavy fuel and naphtha."
		"&eChemistry:&r hydrogen reacts with sulfur compounds to form H₂S. Real refineries turn that into sulfur and then acid; MI hands you sulfuric acid directly."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: 12 B of a sour fraction + 2 B hydrogen → 12 B clean fraction + 2 B H₂SO₄."
		"&eTip:&r feed the acid back into your ore line. Nothing is wasted."
	]
	quest.7CB7FF40BB33AD8F.title: "Diesel Power"
	quest.7CB7FF40BB33AD8F.quest_subtitle: "Blend two fuels into one"
	quest.7CB7FF40BB33AD8F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r diesel runs MI generators, tools and, later, your rockets (Ad Astra burns MI diesel)."
		"&eChemistry:&r diesel is a blend of C₁₀ to C₂₀ hydrocarbons: mostly light fuel, with heavy fuel for energy density."
		"&eHow:&r Mixer: 5 B light fuel + 1 B heavy fuel → 6 B diesel."
		"&eTip:&r a Large Diesel Generator is far more efficient than a row of small ones."
	]
	quest.63562E7CFD3869A1.title: "Steam Cracking"
	quest.63562E7CFD3869A1.quest_subtitle: "Break big molecules into useful small ones"
	quest.63562E7CFD3869A1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r naphtha is too big to make plastic from. Cracking breaks it into the small building blocks chemists actually want."
		"&eChemistry:&r at high temperature with steam, long chains snap apart into short, reactive molecules with double bonds (alkenes)."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: 1000 mB naphtha + 100 mB steam → 1000 mB steam-cracked naphtha."
	]
	quest.2B7050355105A3E8.title: "Ethylene"
	quest.2B7050355105A3E8.quest_subtitle: "C₂H₄, the most important molecule in plastics"
	quest.2B7050355105A3E8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r distilling cracked naphtha gives eight products: methane, acetylene, &eethylene&r, propene, butadiene, benzene, toluene and ethylbenzene."
		"&eChemistry:&r ethylene's C=C double bond can open up and link to its neighbours. That is how plastics are born."
		"&eHow:&r send steam-cracked naphtha through the Distillation Tower (more layers give more outputs; all eight need the full tower)."
		"&eTip:&r store every fraction. Each one has a use later in this chapter."
	]
	quest.76071A1B98D9CFD3.title: "Polymerisation"
	quest.76071A1B98D9CFD3.quest_subtitle: "Thousands of ethylenes, one long chain"
	quest.76071A1B98D9CFD3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r polyethylene, (C₂H₄)ₙ, is the plastic in bags and bottles, and the laminate on HV circuit boards."
		"&eChemistry:&r a metal catalyst opens each double bond so the molecules join head to tail. Real plants use chromium (Phillips) or titanium catalysts."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: 500 mB ethylene + 4 tiny lead or chromium dust → 300 mB polyethylene."
	]
	quest.4B32EEF0B09F51CB.title: "HDPE"
	quest.4B32EEF0B09F51CB.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism's plastic, from your ethylene"
	quest.4B32EEF0B09F51CB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r high-density polyethylene pellets become Mekanism's plastic sheets, rods and later the MekaSuit."
		"&eChemistry:&r HDPE has straight chains that pack tightly, so it's stiffer than ordinary polyethylene."
		"&eHow:&r Pressurized Reaction Chamber with ethylene, water and substrate (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.1A986E281B98DA89.title: "Chromium and Manganese"
	quest.1A986E281B98DA89.quest_subtitle: "The metals that keep steel from rusting"
	quest.1A986E281B98DA89.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r stainless steel needs chromium, nickel and manganese on top of iron."
		"&eChemistry:&r chromium is leached with acid: crushed chromium + HCl → chromium chloride solution, then electrolysis splits out the metal plus H₂ and Cl₂."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor (chromium crushed dust + 9 B HCl), then Electrolyzer. Check JEI for manganese."
	]
	quest.4083455951FE50A4.title: "Stainless Steel Dust"
	quest.4083455951FE50A4.quest_subtitle: "Six parts iron, one each of Cr, Ni and Mn"
	quest.4083455951FE50A4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the mixed powder that becomes stainless steel."
		"&eChemistry:&r at 10.5% chromium or more, the surface forms an invisible Cr₂O₃ film that stops rust spreading."
		"&eHow:&r Mixer: 6 iron dust + 1 chromium + 1 nickel + 1 manganese → 9 stainless steel dust."
	]
	quest.589F846BD366467D.title: "Hot Ingots"
	quest.589F846BD366467D.quest_subtitle: "Too hot to handle, until you freeze it"
	quest.589F846BD366467D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Electric Blast Furnace melts the dust into a &ehot ingot&r that must be cooled before use."
		"&eHow:&r EBF turns 1 stainless steel dust into 1 hot ingot. Build the Vacuum Freezer multiblock (layout in JEI) to cool it."
		"&eTip:&r later, the Heat Exchanger cools hot ingots too and gives argon and helium back."
	]
	quest.5534AEA7CF93C53D.title: "Stainless Steel"
	quest.5534AEA7CF93C53D.quest_subtitle: "The metal that survives acid"
	quest.5534AEA7CF93C53D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r stainless steel resists corrosion, so it can hold acids and hot fluids."
		"&eChemistry:&r if the surface is scratched, chromium re-forms the oxide film at once. The steel heals itself."
		"&eHow:&r cool hot ingots in the Vacuum Freezer. HV circuit boards need 4 stainless plates each."
		"&eTip:&r automate the whole line: mixer → EBF → freezer → compressor."
	]
	quest.6630705D72AEB78D.title: "Digital Circuit Board"
	quest.6630705D72AEB78D.quest_subtitle: "Plastic, steel and silicon in one board"
	quest.6630705D72AEB78D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the base of every HV circuit."
		"&eChemistry:&r polyethylene is an excellent insulator, so it separates the copper layers of the board."
		"&eHow:&r Assembler: electronic circuit board + 4 stainless steel plates + silicon battery + 6 aluminum cable + 750 mB polyethylene."
	]
	quest.494A81F2F340497C.title: "Sodium Battery"
	quest.494A81F2F340497C.quest_subtitle: "Table salt becomes a battery"
	quest.494A81F2F340497C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the HV hull needs two sodium batteries."
		"&eChemistry:&r electrolysis splits salt: 2NaCl → 2Na + Cl₂. Sodium metal is so reactive it fizzes in water, which is what makes it a good battery material."
		"&eHow:&r Electrolyzer: 2 salt dust → 1 sodium dust + chlorine. Then craft the battery (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep the chlorine. It's needed for HCl and, next chapter, PVC."
	]
	quest.6D18179563EC6FB4.title: "HV: Digital Circuits"
	quest.6D18179563EC6FB4.quest_subtitle: "High Voltage, built on plastic"
	quest.6D18179563EC6FB4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Logic gates, clicking into place. You used to think this fast.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r digital circuits unlock HV machines, AE2, the Angel Ring and elite jetpack coils."
		"&eHow:&r Assembler: digital circuit board + 4 electronic circuits + AND, OR and NOT gates. The &eTurbo hull&r adds 2 sodium batteries and aluminum cable."
		"&eTip:&r set up a dedicated assembler for circuits. You'll make hundreds."
	]
	quest.0977A230BB3A6718.title: "Fallen Stars"
	quest.0977A230BB3A6718.quest_subtitle: "Meteorites hide the presses AE2 needs"
	quest.0977A230BB3A6718.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r AE2's inscriber presses are only found in the core of meteorites."
		"&eHow:&r craft a Meteorite Compass, follow it, and dig to the centre of the sky stone crater. Each meteorite's mysterious cube holds one press."
		"&eTip:&r once you have one press, the Inscriber can copy it with an iron block."
	]
	quest.61C8ED46F157C456.title: "Fluix"
	quest.61C8ED46F157C456.quest_subtitle: "Charged quartz for the network"
	quest.61C8ED46F157C456.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fluix crystals carry the ME network's signal. The ME Controller needs them."
		"&eHow:&r charge certus quartz in the Charger, then drop charged certus, redstone and Nether quartz in water together (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r budding certus quartz grows new crystals, so certus is renewable once you find some."
	]
	quest.6C079DD7BD5DC36A.title: "The Inscriber"
	quest.6C079DD7BD5DC36A.quest_subtitle: "Printing circuits onto silicon"
	quest.6C079DD7BD5DC36A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every AE2 processor is printed in the Inscriber. In this pack it's built on a Turbo hull."
		"&eChemistry:&r engineering processors print a circuit onto silicon, the same element your HV boards depend on."
		"&eHow:&r press a diamond into a printed engineering circuit, silicon into printed silicon, then combine them with redstone."
	]
	quest.45849083414E98A3.title: "The God's Archive"
	quest.45849083414E98A3.quest_subtitle: "Your memory, rebuilt as a network"
	quest.45849083414E98A3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Everything you ever owned, known at once. You remember having a mind like that.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Applied Energistics 2 stores items as data and crafts on demand."
		"&eHow:&r the ME Controller needs a digital circuit, an engineering processor, fluix and smooth sky stone."
		"&eTip:&r Tom's Simple Storage was your early network. AE2 takes over from here (see the Applied Energistics page in Engineering)."
	]
	quest.40E5C8E7AFD9DCDB.title: "First Storage Cells"
	quest.40E5C8E7AFD9DCDB.quest_subtitle: "Where the archive keeps its memories"
	quest.40E5C8E7AFD9DCDB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r storage cells go into an ME Drive. Fluid cells hold your acids and fuels as data too."
		"&eHow:&r a 1k cell component needs a logic processor (gold + logic press). Check JEI for the housing."
		"&eTip:&r a few fluid cells beat a wall of tanks for small stocks of rare chemicals."
	]
	quest.4B6B18DEE9511230.title: "The Twilight Forest"
	quest.4B6B18DEE9511230.quest_subtitle: "A realm of permanent dusk"
	quest.4B6B18DEE9511230.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a dimension of bosses, strange woods and unique metals (see the Twilight Forest page in Exploration)."
		"&eHow:&r dig a 2x2 pool of water ringed with flowers, stand in it, and throw in a diamond."
		"&eTip:&r set a waystone near the portal before you explore."
	]
	quest.66878B009C6ABC9F.title: "Benzene Rings"
	quest.66878B009C6ABC9F.quest_subtitle: "The hexagon at the heart of organic chemistry"
	quest.66878B009C6ABC9F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r benzene (C₆H₆) and toluene (C₇H₈) come out of the cracked-naphtha distillation."
		"&eChemistry:&r benzene is a flat ring of six carbons whose electrons are shared around the whole ring. That makes it unusually stable."
		"&eHow:&r collect them from the Distillation Tower's benzene and toluene outputs."
		"&eTip:&r benzene also makes dyes and, via caprolactam, nylon."
	]
	quest.5529968E112BBA9E.title: "Styrene"
	quest.5529968E112BBA9E.quest_subtitle: "Add ethylene, then strip off hydrogen"
	quest.5529968E112BBA9E.quest_desc: [
		"&eChemistry:&r benzene + ethylene → ethylbenzene (acid catalyst). Steam over iron then pulls off H₂ to give styrene, C₈H₈, exactly as in real plants."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: benzene + ethylene + a little HCl → ethylbenzene. Then ethylbenzene + steam + iron dust → styrene + hydrogen."
		"&eTip:&r the hydrogen by-product can go straight back into hydrotreating."
	]
	quest.11E3CE994DD5E91B.title: "Synthetic Rubber"
	quest.11E3CE994DD5E91B.quest_subtitle: "Car-tyre rubber, made from oil"
	quest.11E3CE994DD5E91B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r styrene-butadiene rubber (SBR) is the rubber in most tyres. Here it makes rubber sheets by the stack."
		"&eChemistry:&r styrene and butadiene polymerise together into one chain (a copolymer): stiff styrene parts, springy butadiene parts."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: styrene + butadiene → styrene-butadiene, then polymerise with tiny lead or chromium dust. The Vacuum Freezer turns 200 mB into 64 rubber sheets."
		"&eTip:&r this replaces plant rubber for good and feeds the better cable recipes."
	]
	quest.7A05E39EE109E1CA.title: "Diesel Toys"
	quest.7A05E39EE109E1CA.quest_subtitle: "Optional: fuel-powered tools"
	quest.7A05E39EE109E1CA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI's diesel drill and jetpack run on the fuel you just learned to blend."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for both recipes, then fill them from a tank."
		"&eTip:&r the jetpack is loud and thirsty, but it flies. Real flight comes later."
	]
	quest.697083271627CD0D.title: "Fuel from Plants"
	quest.697083271627CD0D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: diesel without drilling"
	quest.697083271627CD0D.quest_desc: [
		"&eChemistry:&r transesterification: plant oil + ethanol, with NaOH as catalyst, swaps the oil's glycerol backbone for ethyl groups. The result burns like diesel."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: plant oil + ethanol + sodium hydroxide → raw biodiesel, then wash it with steam (check JEI for plant oil)."
		"&eTip:&r Ad Astra rockets accept biodiesel too."
	]
	quest.1AAB2F81853CDE86.title: "Acrylic Glue"
	quest.1AAB2F81853CDE86.quest_subtitle: "Optional: slime from propene"
	quest.1AAB2F81853CDE86.quest_desc: [
		"&eChemistry:&r propene + oxygen → acrylic acid + water. Polymerised, it becomes a sticky acrylic: the same family as superabsorbent polymers."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor for the acid, then polymerise with tiny lead or chromium dust."
		"&eTip:&r the Chemical Reactor can turn acrylic glue into slime balls. No more slime farms."
	]
	quest.6879CF7353CD336E.title: "Nylon"
	quest.6879CF7353CD336E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: string from benzene"
	quest.6879CF7353CD336E.quest_desc: [
		"&eChemistry:&r benzene + hydrogen over nickel leads to caprolactam, a ring that opens up and polymerises into nylon-6."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: benzene + hydrogen + tiny nickel dust → caprolactam, then polymerise it."
		"&eTip:&r 20 mB of nylon makes one string in the Chemical Reactor."
	]
	quest.66000D449A417BFA.title: "A Mountain of Rubber"
	quest.66000D449A417BFA.quest_subtitle: "Optional: stockpile challenge"
	quest.66000D449A417BFA.quest_desc: [
		"&eHow:&r keep the SBR line and Vacuum Freezer running until you have 256 sheets."
		"&eWhat:&r four full stacks of rubber sheets, made the modern way."
		"&eTip:&r one bucket of SBR is five freezer runs, so a single bucket gets you there."
	]
	chapter.12C105E0A9C3B5B2.title: "VII. Materials and Nuclear"
	chapter.12C105E0A9C3B5B2.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Purity and precision: semiconductors, PVC, isotopes."
		"Then transmutation: any element from any other."
	]
	quest.7EFA01609EB9CAE8.title: "Argon from Air"
	quest.7EFA01609EB9CAE8.quest_subtitle: "The lazy gas that protects hot silicon"
	quest.7EFA01609EB9CAE8.quest_desc: [
		"&6You once stirred the sky. Now you pour it, liquid, into a tank.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r argon is an inert blanket gas. Growing a silicon crystal in air would ruin it."
		"&eChemistry:&r air is 78% N₂, 21% O₂ and about 0.9% argon. Cool it until it liquefies, then separate the parts."
		"&eHow:&r the Vacuum Freezer (or Pressurizer) with an Air Intake makes liquid air. The Centrifuge splits it into oxygen, nitrogen and a little argon."
		"&eTip:&r the Heat Exchanger gives far more argon while it cools hot ingots."
	]
	quest.5487AC6E80EEFF90.title: "Semiconductor Silicon"
	quest.5487AC6E80EEFF90.quest_subtitle: "One perfect crystal, sliced thin"
	quest.5487AC6E80EEFF90.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r computer chips need silicon purer than 99.9999999%, grown as one single crystal."
		"&eChemistry:&r a seed crystal is pulled slowly out of molten silicon (the Czochralski process). Every atom lines up with the one below it."
		"&eHow:&r EBF: 32 silicon dust + 1 tiny iridium dust + argon → monocrystalline silicon. Cut it into wafers with lubricant."
		"&eTip:&r iridium comes from osmium byproducts or the platinum line's residue (below)."
	]
	quest.7F783CDF991DA3CA.title: "Chips"
	quest.7F783CDF991DA3CA.quest_subtitle: "Memory, logic and control on silicon"
	quest.7F783CDF991DA3CA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a processing unit needs RAM, an ALU and an MMU."
		"&eChemistry:&r a pinch of aluminum (p-type) or phosphorus (n-type) in silicon changes how it carries current. That's 'doping', the basis of every transistor."
		"&eHow:&r Assembler. The ALU uses a diamond plate and logic gates, the MMU silicon wafers and platinum fine wire. Check JEI for RAM."
	]
	quest.1CA61C282BFA56F8.title: "Acetylene"
	quest.1CA61C282BFA56F8.quest_subtitle: "The welding gas, from methane"
	quest.1CA61C282BFA56F8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r acetylene (C₂H₂) has a triple bond, which makes it very reactive."
		"&eChemistry:&r heat methane hard enough and pairs of molecules lose hydrogen and join: 2CH₄ → C₂H₂ + 3H₂."
		"&eHow:&r Electric Blast Furnace: 200 mB methane → 200 mB acetylene. Cracked naphtha also gives a little."
	]
	quest.7ADCA113114E63A0.title: "Vinyl Chloride"
	quest.7ADCA113114E63A0.quest_subtitle: "Acetylene meets hydrochloric acid"
	quest.7ADCA113114E63A0.quest_desc: [
		"&eChemistry:&r C₂H₂ + HCl → C₂H₃Cl. HCl adds across the triple bond. This was the original industrial route to PVC."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: 1 B acetylene + 1 B hydrochloric acid → 1 B vinyl chloride."
		"&eTip:&r your salt line's chlorine and hydrogen make the HCl."
	]
	quest.56149E13A2EFBE0C.title: "PVC"
	quest.56149E13A2EFBE0C.quest_subtitle: "Petrochemistry meets chlor-alkali"
	quest.56149E13A2EFBE0C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r polyvinyl chloride, (C₂H₃Cl)ₙ, is tough, fire-resistant and insulates EV circuit boards."
		"&eChemistry:&r just like polyethylene, but every other carbon carries a chlorine atom. That's why PVC doesn't burn easily."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: 500 mB vinyl chloride + 4 tiny lead or chromium dust → 300 mB PVC."
	]
	quest.336CD4DE5D9F2FAF.title: "Cadmium Battery"
	quest.336CD4DE5D9F2FAF.quest_subtitle: "Nickel-cadmium cells for the EV hull"
	quest.336CD4DE5D9F2FAF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the EV hull and processing unit board each need 2 cadmium batteries."
		"&eChemistry:&r a NiCd cell runs Cd + 2NiO(OH) + 2H₂O → Cd(OH)₂ + 2Ni(OH)₂, and it can be recharged by running it backwards."
		"&eHow:&r MI centrifuges monazite dust into cadmium (in reality, it's mostly a by-product of zinc refining). Then craft the battery with annealed copper cable."
		"&eTip:&r cadmium is toxic in real life. Here it just needs a lot of monazite."
	]
	quest.4226F3C3C6AF3441.title: "Processing Unit Board"
	quest.4226F3C3C6AF3441.quest_subtitle: "PVC, platinum and cadmium in one board"
	quest.4226F3C3C6AF3441.quest_desc: [
		"&eHow:&r Assembler: digital circuit board + 4 platinum plates + 2 cadmium batteries + 8 annealed copper cable + 1500 mB PVC."
		"&eChemistry:&r platinum never corrodes, so it makes contacts that last forever."
		"&eTip:&r platinum comes from MI's ore processing or the Platinum Line below (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.009FBA775299B910.title: "EV: Processing Units"
	quest.009FBA775299B910.quest_subtitle: "Extreme Voltage, built on purity"
	quest.009FBA775299B910.quest_desc: [
		"&6A mind of silicon, insulated in salt and oil. It thinks the way you used to.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r processing units unlock EV machines, the NASA Workbench, Flux Networks and Alchemistry's chambers."
		"&eHow:&r Assembler: processing unit board + 4 digital circuits + 2 RAM + ALU + MMU. The &eEV hull&r adds 2 cadmium batteries."
	]
	quest.515EABDC83B26416.title: "Yellowcake"
	quest.515EABDC83B26416.quest_subtitle: "The first step from ore to fuel"
	quest.515EABDC83B26416.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r yellowcake is concentrated uranium oxide powder, the raw material of nuclear fuel."
		"&eChemistry:&r natural uranium is only 0.72% U-235, the isotope that splits. The rest is U-238."
		"&eHow:&r Enrichment Chamber: 1 uranium ingot → 2 yellowcake. Then the Chemical Oxidizer turns it into uranium oxide gas."
		"&eTip:&r a Geiger counter tells you when you're standing too close to anything radioactive."
	]
	quest.6DA3A8FA4B30A712.title: "Hydrofluoric Acid"
	quest.6DA3A8FA4B30A712.quest_subtitle: "The acid that eats glass"
	quest.6DA3A8FA4B30A712.quest_desc: [
		"&eChemistry:&r CaF₂ + H₂SO₄ → CaSO₄ + 2HF. Hydrogen fluoride dissolves glass and is one of the most dangerous acids there is."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Dissolution Chamber: fluorite + sulfuric acid → hydrofluoric acid gas."
		"&eTip:&r fluorite ore sits deep. Mystical Agriculture and Occultism can't make it in this pack."
	]
	quest.2393C134BD200793.title: "Uranium Hexafluoride"
	quest.2393C134BD200793.quest_subtitle: "Turn uranium into a gas"
	quest.2393C134BD200793.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r UF₆ is the only uranium compound that becomes a gas at low temperature (it sublimes at 56 °C), so it can be spun."
		"&eChemistry:&r real plants go UO₂ → UF₄ → UF₆ with HF and then fluorine. Mekanism combines the steps."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Infuser: uranium oxide + hydrofluoric acid → uranium hexafluoride."
	]
	quest.5CE57DF0EEA3E9C2.title: "Isotope Separation"
	quest.5CE57DF0EEA3E9C2.quest_subtitle: "Only mass tells U-235 and U-238 apart"
	quest.5CE57DF0EEA3E9C2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the two isotopes behave identically in every reaction, so chemistry can't separate them."
		"&eChemistry:&r U-235 is about 1% lighter. Spin UF₆ fast enough and the heavier molecules drift outward."
		"&eHow:&r Isotopic Centrifuge: uranium hexafluoride → fissile fuel."
	]
	quest.1CFE682A19E514A6.title: "Reactor Parts"
	quest.1CFE682A19E514A6.quest_subtitle: "Fuel, control rods and ports"
	quest.1CFE682A19E514A6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fuel assemblies hold the fuel, control rods absorb neutrons, and ports move fuel, coolant and waste."
		"&eChemistry:&r each split releases 2 to 3 neutrons. Absorb too few and the chain reaction runs away."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for each part. Plan for water or sodium coolant and somewhere for the steam to go."
	]
	quest.79D73BB7E003DB38.title: "Fission"
	quest.79D73BB7E003DB38.quest_subtitle: "Split the atom"
	quest.79D73BB7E003DB38.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r split heavy nuclei and release enormous energy. Mind the temperature, and the waste."
		"&eChemistry:&r U-235 + n → two lighter nuclei + 2-3 n + about 200 MeV, millions of times more than any chemical bond."
		"&eHow:&r Just Enough Mekanism Multiblocks shows the layout in JEI. Pair it with a turbine (see Power)."
		"&eTip:&r wire a Logic Adapter to SCRAM the reactor if it overheats."
	]
	quest.170C5FC9F9808944.title: "Plutonium"
	quest.170C5FC9F9808944.quest_subtitle: "An element made by neutrons"
	quest.170C5FC9F9808944.quest_desc: [
		"&eChemistry:&r U-238 captures a neutron and beta-decays twice into Pu-239, which is itself fissile."
		"&eHow:&r Isotopic Centrifuge: 10 nuclear waste → 1 plutonium. Pressurized Reaction Chamber: plutonium + fluorite dust + water → pellet."
		"&eTip:&r the pellet reaction also gives spent nuclear waste. Store it in a Radioactive Waste Barrel."
	]
	quest.1615290C8FEE0C7C.title: "Polonium"
	quest.1615290C8FEE0C7C.quest_subtitle: "The element Marie Curie named for Poland"
	quest.1615290C8FEE0C7C.quest_desc: [
		"&eChemistry:&r polonium-210 is made by neutron capture; it is intensely radioactive and gives off heat on its own."
		"&eHow:&r Solar Neutron Activator (needs open sky and daylight): 10 nuclear waste → 1 polonium. Pellets come from the Pressurized Reaction Chamber, as with plutonium."
		"&eTip:&r polonium is the input for the SPS and for Energy Cores."
	]
	quest.69D67DF12EE0C400.title: "Transmutation by Neutron"
	quest.69D67DF12EE0C400.quest_subtitle: "Lead to gold was never the hard part"
	quest.69D67DF12EE0C400.quest_desc: [
		"&6The old alchemists wanted to change one element into another. You do it before breakfast.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r reprocessing nuclear waste gives &eplutonium&r and &epolonium&r, two elements that barely exist in nature."
		"&eHow:&r keep both pellet lines running. Plutonium feeds the quantum tier; polonium feeds antimatter."
		"&eTip:&r spent waste still goes in a Radioactive Waste Barrel. Never dump it."
	]
	quest.0485E912DC2B316F.title: "Chamber Frame"
	quest.0485E912DC2B316F.quest_subtitle: "The shell around an element reactor"
	quest.0485E912DC2B316F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Alchemistry's fission and fusion chambers share the same casing, energy, input and output blocks."
		"&eHow:&r craft the frame blocks (check JEI) and build the chamber around its controller. The controllers themselves are crafted with a reactor casing."
		"&eTip:&r build both chambers side by side so one can feed the other."
	]
	quest.606688FB50C32212.title: "Element Transmutation"
	quest.606688FB50C32212.quest_subtitle: "Split or merge any element"
	quest.606688FB50C32212.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the fission chamber splits one element into two lighter ones; the fusion chamber merges two into a heavier one."
		"&eChemistry:&r atomic numbers simply add or divide: fuse sodium (11) with chlorine (17) and you get nickel (28)."
		"&eHow:&r both controllers need a processing unit; fusion also needs a Nether Star."
		"&eTip:&r with both, &eevery element&r is within reach."
	]
	quest.6C2882437A5C659C.title: "The Complete Periodic Table"
	quest.6C2882437A5C659C.quest_subtitle: "Element 118"
	quest.6C2882437A5C659C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Oganesson. It barely exists in reality, but you made one.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the heaviest element on the table, made by fusing lighter ones."
		"&eChemistry:&r real oganesson has been made only a handful of times, and each atom lasted under a millisecond."
		"&eHow:&r fuse your way up in the Fusion Chamber (check JEI for which pairs reach 118)."
		"&6Every block in this world can now be built from chemicals. You're close to what you once were.&r"
	]
	quest.3720EEA89BCDC92F.title: "Wireless Power"
	quest.3720EEA89BCDC92F.quest_subtitle: "Energy without cables"
	quest.3720EEA89BCDC92F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Flux Networks moves energy anywhere in a dimension, or across them."
		"&eHow:&r the Flux Core needs a processing unit in this pack. Add plugs at sources and points at machines."
		"&eTip:&r set a password on your network if you share a server."
	]
	quest.1D1660D4E4098CF6.title: "Haber-Bosch"
	quest.1D1660D4E4098CF6.quest_subtitle: "Bread from air"
	quest.1D1660D4E4098CF6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Feeding a world used to take a harvest god. Now it takes a reactor and some hydrogen.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r ammonia is the root of fertiliser, nitric acid and ammonium salts."
		"&eChemistry:&r N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃. Breaking nitrogen's triple bond is hard; this process feeds about half the world through fertiliser."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: 1 B nitrogen + 3 B hydrogen → 2 B ammonia. Fill a bucket from the output tank."
	]
	quest.703A5F9E92E332B9.title: "Ostwald Process"
	quest.703A5F9E92E332B9.quest_subtitle: "Burn ammonia, catch nitric acid"
	quest.703A5F9E92E332B9.quest_desc: [
		"&eChemistry:&r NH₃ + 2O₂ → HNO₃ + H₂O. Real plants burn ammonia over a platinum gauze, the very metal you're about to extract with it."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: 1 B ammonia + 2 B oxygen → 1 B nitric acid + 1 B water."
		"&eTip:&r the water by-product can go back into your electrolysis line."
	]
	quest.1BC8628F6F7EC4AF.title: "Anode Sludge"
	quest.1BC8628F6F7EC4AF.quest_subtitle: "Treasure in the electrolyzer's leftovers"
	quest.1BC8628F6F7EC4AF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r refining nickel and copper electrically leaves a sludge rich in platinum-group metals."
		"&eChemistry:&r noble metals don't dissolve at the anode, so they fall to the bottom of the cell."
		"&eHow:&r Electrolyzer: 4 nickel or copper dust → 4 dust back + PGM sludge (25% chance)."
		"&eTip:&r it costs you nothing but power. Leave it running."
	]
	quest.0B9EEBE52756E0D9.title: "Ammonium Chloride"
	quest.0B9EEBE52756E0D9.quest_subtitle: "Two gases make a white powder"
	quest.0B9EEBE52756E0D9.quest_desc: [
		"&eChemistry:&r NH₃ + HCl → NH₄Cl. Open bottles of each near one another and a white smoke of this salt forms in the air."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: 1 B ammonia + 1 B hydrochloric acid → 1 ammonium chloride."
		"&eTip:&r you need 2 per precipitation, so make plenty."
	]
	quest.20C5260FC05F87BA.title: "Aqua Regia"
	quest.20C5260FC05F87BA.quest_subtitle: "Royal water dissolves the noble metals"
	quest.20C5260FC05F87BA.quest_desc: [
		"&eChemistry:&r 3 HCl : 1 HNO₃. Nitric acid oxidises the platinum and chloride grabs the ions, forming chloroplatinic acid, H₂PtCl₆."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: 4 PGM sludge + 3 B HCl + 1 B nitric acid → 2 chloroplatinic acid + 1 PGM residue."
		"&eTip:&r iridium, osmium, rhodium and ruthenium don't dissolve. Keep the residue."
	]
	quest.051D638F5846BAE0.title: "Precipitation"
	quest.051D638F5846BAE0.quest_subtitle: "Pull platinum out of solution as a salt"
	quest.051D638F5846BAE0.quest_desc: [
		"&eChemistry:&r ammonium chloride makes the platinum fall out as yellow ammonium hexachloroplatinate, (NH₄)₂PtCl₆."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: 1 chloroplatinic acid + 2 ammonium chloride → 1 ammonium hexachloroplatinate."
		"&eTip:&r this step is why real platinum refining needs both the Haber-Bosch and Ostwald plants."
	]
	quest.45087080B517BD44.title: "The Platinum Line"
	quest.45087080B517BD44.quest_subtitle: "Calcine the salt, keep the metal"
	quest.45087080B517BD44.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember metals that never tarnish. Now you know why: they refuse to react.&r"
		"&eChemistry:&r heating (calcining) drives off ammonia and HCl and leaves pure platinum metal."
		"&eHow:&r Electric Blast Furnace: 2 ammonium hexachloroplatinate → 1 platinum dust."
		"&eTip:&r processing unit boards need 4 platinum plates each. Automate this line."
	]
	quest.2C530BDB9215DABC.title: "The Rare Four"
	quest.2C530BDB9215DABC.quest_subtitle: "Iridium, osmium, rhodium, ruthenium"
	quest.2C530BDB9215DABC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the insoluble residue holds the rarest metals on Earth."
		"&eChemistry:&r osmium is the densest element known, and iridium the most corrosion-resistant metal."
		"&eHow:&r Centrifuge the PGM residue. Each output is a chance, so run plenty."
		"&eTip:&r iridium is needed for monocrystalline silicon and, later, quantum circuit boards."
	]
	quest.5A912483315D29F6.title: "Dress for the Job"
	quest.5A912483315D29F6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: radiation safety"
	quest.5A912483315D29F6.quest_desc: [
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for each piece."
		"&eWhat:&r a full hazmat suit blocks radiation; the Geiger counter shows how much is around you."
		"&eTip:&r a leaking waste pipe can make an area dangerous for a long time. Check before you build."
	]
	quest.479B3AFD6DB059F7.title: "Closing the Fuel Cycle"
	quest.479B3AFD6DB059F7.quest_subtitle: "Optional: burn plutonium as fuel"
	quest.479B3AFD6DB059F7.quest_desc: [
		"&eChemistry:&r plutonium-239 is fissile, so spent fuel can be recycled into new fuel, as some real reactors do."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Injection Chamber: plutonium pellet + hydrogen chloride → 4 fragments. Oxidize them into fissile fuel."
		"&eTip:&r it means less waste and more fuel from every uranium ingot."
	]
	quest.74E8AAEEA075991E.title: "The Unstable Ones"
	quest.74E8AAEEA075991E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: elements with no stable form"
	quest.74E8AAEEA075991E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r four elements that real chemists almost never get to hold."
		"&eChemistry:&r technetium (43) and promethium (61) are the only light elements with no stable isotope. Astatine and francium are the rarest natural elements: grams exist in the whole crust."
		"&eHow:&r fuse or split your way to each atomic number (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.218AA021BA449275.title: "Platinum Reserve"
	quest.218AA021BA449275.quest_subtitle: "Optional: stockpile challenge"
	quest.218AA021BA449275.quest_desc: [
		"&eHow:&r keep the Platinum Line running, then smelt the dust."
		"&eWhat:&r half a stack of platinum ingots, all pulled out of sludge."
		"&eTip:&r every processing unit board eats 4 platinum plates. You'll be glad of the reserve."
	]
	chapter.45FF88D8CD5549A4.title: "VIII. Creation"
	chapter.45FF88D8CD5549A4.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Leave the cradle. Make matter from energy. Seed a new world."
	]
	quest.7F5D0246011FE307.title: "Leaving the Cradle"
	quest.7F5D0246011FE307.quest_subtitle: "Every rocket starts on this bench"
	quest.7F5D0246011FE307.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember the stars up close. Time to stop looking at them from the ground.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the NASA Workbench assembles every Ad Astra rocket."
		"&eHow:&r in this pack it needs an EV (Highly Advanced) hull, so processing units come first."
	]
	quest.2D71A1E8E2859236.title: "Rocket Parts"
	quest.2D71A1E8E2859236.quest_subtitle: "Nose cone, fins, tanks and an engine"
	quest.2D71A1E8E2859236.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Tier 1 rocket needs a nose cone, 4 fins, 2 steel tanks, a steel engine and 6 steel blocks."
		"&eChemistry:&r a rocket carries its own oxidiser as well as fuel: there's no air to burn in once you're up."
		"&eHow:&r all parts are crafted from steel plates and rods (check JEI). The nose cone uses a lightning rod."
	]
	quest.06F69B817832C614.title: "Breathe"
	quest.06F69B817832C614.quest_subtitle: "Space has no air"
	quest.06F69B817832C614.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Oxygen Loader fills your space suit's tank."
		"&eChemistry:&r it accepts plain water, but 100 mB of water gives only 4 mB of oxygen. Pure O₂ from your electrolysis line (2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂) goes in 1:1."
		"&eHow:&r pipe MI or Mekanism oxygen into the loader, power it, and put the suit in the slot."
	]
	quest.494D2FBE3172520A.title: "The Full Suit"
	quest.494D2FBE3172520A.quest_subtitle: "Helmet alone won't do"
	quest.494D2FBE3172520A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the full set keeps you alive in vacuum and in the cold of the Moon."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for each piece. Wear all four before launch."
		"&eTip:&r the chest piece holds the oxygen. Watch the gauge on your HUD."
	]
	quest.6DDB2C2ACDAA5443.title: "Launch Pad"
	quest.6DDB2C2ACDAA5443.quest_subtitle: "Somewhere to stand the rocket"
	quest.6DDB2C2ACDAA5443.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r rockets are placed on a launch pad, not on the bare ground."
		"&eHow:&r craft it (check JEI) and place it in the open, with clear sky above."
		"&eTip:&r build a pad on each world you visit so you always have somewhere to land and relaunch."
	]
	quest.44A4B4888AF3AF27.title: "Rocket Fuel"
	quest.44A4B4888AF3AF27.quest_subtitle: "Ad Astra burns your diesel"
	quest.44A4B4888AF3AF27.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r in this pack rockets run on MI diesel (biodiesel works too). Ad Astra's own oil refining is removed."
		"&eChemistry:&r a kilogram of diesel releases about 45 MJ when it burns: more than ten times a good battery."
		"&eHow:&r fill the rocket from buckets or pipes (check its GUI for how much it holds)."
		"&eTip:&r bring spare fuel for the trip home."
	]
	quest.0C1DD95BA033EAB3.title: "One Small Step"
	quest.0C1DD95BA033EAB3.quest_subtitle: "Reach the Moon"
	quest.0C1DD95BA033EAB3.quest_desc: [
		"&6The Moon looks smaller than you remember. Or perhaps you were larger.&r"
		"&eHow:&r build the rocket in the NASA Workbench, place it on the pad, fuel it, climb in and launch. Pick the Moon on the planet screen."
		"&eTip:&r place a bed or waystone near your landing site before exploring."
	]
	quest.1B2FF1921BFAFACF.title: "Desh"
	quest.1B2FF1921BFAFACF.quest_subtitle: "The Moon's own metal"
	quest.1B2FF1921BFAFACF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r desh is Ad Astra's lunar metal, needed for the Tier 2 rocket and oxygen equipment."
		"&eHow:&r mine desh ore on the Moon, smelt it, and press the ingots into plates in Ad Astra's Compressor."
		"&eTip:&r the Moon also has cheese ore. Really."
	]
	quest.17759B5826DD9CB6.title: "A Breathable Room"
	quest.17759B5826DD9CB6.quest_subtitle: "Bring an atmosphere with you"
	quest.17759B5826DD9CB6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Oxygen Distributor fills a sealed room with air, so you can take off your helmet."
		"&eHow:&r built from an Oxygen Loader, a large gas tank, fans, an oxygen gear and desh plates. Feed it oxygen and power."
		"&eTip:&r any gap in the walls lets the air out. Seal the room completely, doors included."
	]
	quest.243C3A96FE99DD8D.title: "Supercritical Phase Shifter"
	quest.243C3A96FE99DD8D.quest_subtitle: "A multiblock that turns polonium into antimatter"
	quest.243C3A96FE99DD8D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the SPS is Mekanism's largest machine. It needs huge amounts of power."
		"&eHow:&r Just Enough Mekanism Multiblocks shows the full layout in JEI. Ports feed polonium in and power the supercharged coil."
		"&eTip:&r feed it from a fission reactor and turbine, or several Flux Networks plugs."
	]
	quest.1CB50F40C6DA26D6.title: "Bottling Antimatter"
	quest.1CB50F40C6DA26D6.quest_subtitle: "Antimatter gas becomes a pellet"
	quest.1CB50F40C6DA26D6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the SPS outputs antimatter as a gas. The Chemical Crystallizer packs 1000 mB of it into one pellet."
		"&eHow:&r pipe antimatter from the SPS output port into the crystallizer."
		"&eTip:&r pipe the SPS straight into the crystallizer so the antimatter never sits in a tank."
	]
	quest.1E6BA9227B6B280F.title: "Antimatter"
	quest.1E6BA9227B6B280F.quest_subtitle: "Matter with every charge reversed"
	quest.1E6BA9227B6B280F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Matter from nothing but energy. This is the first thing you've made that you once made too.&r"
		"&eChemistry:&r when matter meets antimatter both vanish into pure energy, E = mc². One gram of each releases about 1.8 × 10¹⁴ J."
		"&eHow:&r SPS → antimatter gas → Chemical Crystallizer → antimatter pellet."
		"&eTip:&r it's the most energy-dense substance there is. Antimatter Cores need four pellets each."
	]
	quest.25E45CBEE34D9D34.title: "Empty Energy Core"
	quest.25E45CBEE34D9D34.quest_subtitle: "A stainless shell around polonium"
	quest.25E45CBEE34D9D34.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the vessel for the most concentrated energy you can hold."
		"&eChemistry:&r polonium gives off so much heat by decay that a gram of it glows. Here it seeds the core."
		"&eHow:&r craft: 4 stainless steel plates + 4 polonium pellets + a processing unit in the centre."
		"&eTip:&r the Complete Periodic Table quest rewards one empty core."
	]
	quest.4EF6FFBCA6DD55AD.title: "Charge the Core"
	quest.4EF6FFBCA6DD55AD.quest_subtitle: "About three million EU, poured into one item"
	quest.4EF6FFBCA6DD55AD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an empty core holds nothing until you charge it with raw electrical energy."
		"&eHow:&r MI Assembler at 512 EU/t for 6000 ticks: about 3 million EU per core."
		"&eTip:&r give it its own power line. A charging core will starve every other machine on the network."
	]
	quest.39868F66D40B59DD.title: "Antimatter Core"
	quest.39868F66D40B59DD.quest_subtitle: "The heart of the Seed"
	quest.39868F66D40B59DD.quest_desc: [
		"&6You feel it humming in your hand. You remember being this.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a charged core, upgraded with antimatter and a quantum circuit."
		"&eHow:&r MI Assembler at 2048 EU/t for 6000 ticks: charged Energy Core + 4 antimatter pellets + 1 quantum circuit."
		"&eTip:&r the Seed needs eight. Start a production line, not a one-off."
	]
	quest.37BAEF06294D5602.title: "Made of Cheese"
	quest.37BAEF06294D5602.quest_subtitle: "Optional: test an old rumour"
	quest.37BAEF06294D5602.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the old rumour is partly true: the Moon has cheese ore."
		"&eHow:&r mine moon cheese ore and smelt it (or macerate it in MI)."
		"&eTip:&r it's food. Lunar picnic, anyone?"
	]
	quest.17ABF0CEA1A27F7B.title: "Low Earth Orbit"
	quest.17ABF0CEA1A27F7B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: look down on home"
	quest.17ABF0CEA1A27F7B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every planet has an orbit dimension above it, a good place for a space station."
		"&eHow:&r pick Earth Orbit on the rocket's planet screen."
		"&eTip:&r bring building blocks and a way home."
	]
	quest.3AC9108E8851EEA2.title: "Grand Tour"
	quest.3AC9108E8851EEA2.quest_subtitle: "Optional: visit every planet"
	quest.3AC9108E8851EEA2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Moon (Tier 1 rocket), Mars (Tier 2), Venus and Mercury (Tier 3) and Glacio (Tier 4)."
		"&eHow:&r a dimension task completes on arrival. Plan fuel and oxygen for each trip."
		"&eTip:&r Venus and Mercury are hot enough to cook an ordinary space suit. Bring the netherite one."
	]
	quest.2DD64AE9BEF9A844.title: "Heat-Proof Suit"
	quest.2DD64AE9BEF9A844.quest_subtitle: "Optional: armour for hot planets"
	quest.2DD64AE9BEF9A844.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the netherite space suit survives the heat of Venus and Mercury."
		"&eWhat:&r the netherite space suit survives the heat of Venus and Mercury."
		"&eHow:&r the chest piece is a netherite chestplate with ostrum plates (from Mars), gas tanks and an oxygen gear. Check JEI for the rest."
	]
	quest.5F38F7B1EF8C809A.title: "Glacio"
	quest.5F38F7B1EF8C809A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the frozen planet in another system"
	quest.5F38F7B1EF8C809A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Glacio orbits another star and needs a Tier 4 rocket built from calorite."
		"&eHow:&r calorite comes from Venus. The tanks, engine and blocks are all calorite (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r it's the only planet outside our solar system. Take a look at the sky."
	]
	quest.4E04F8FE399BBE55.title: "Antiprotonic Nucleosynthesizer"
	quest.4E04F8FE399BBE55.quest_subtitle: "Optional: transmute items with antimatter"
	quest.4E04F8FE399BBE55.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism's late-game machine uses antimatter to rebuild one item into another."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the recipe and for what it can transmute."
		"&eTip:&r it uses antimatter as fuel, so it needs your SPS running."
	]
	chapter.232C6148722A8576.title: "The Seed of a New World"
	chapter.232C6148722A8576.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Every tier in one 9x9 grid. The act of making a world."
	]
	quest.27A09B9B53019B2A.title: "The Last Recipe"
	quest.27A09B9B53019B2A.quest_subtitle: "One grid, thirteen ingredients"
	quest.27A09B9B53019B2A.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember now what all of this was for. Not machines. A world.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Seed of a New World is the pack's final craft: a 9x9 Ultimate Table recipe that uses something from every tier you've climbed."
		"&eHow:&r each line on this page gathers one ingredient. The checklist quests next to the centre hold the exact counts."
		"&eTip:&r you can start the cheap lines (coke, water, acid, plastic) right away. The Antimatter Cores at the bottom take the longest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eThe full recipe:&r 4 coke, 8 ChemLib water, 4 ChemLib hydrogen, 8 sulfuric acid buckets, 16 polyethylene buckets, 8 processing units, 4 stainless steel plates, 8 oganesson, 4 plutonium pellets, 4 polonium pellets, 4 Nether Stars, 8 Antimatter Cores and 1 Dragon Egg. 81 slots, every one filled."
		"&eWhy these:&r read them in order and they retell the climb: fire (coke), the elements (water, hydrogen), the Acid Age, the Oil Age, the machine ages, the atomic age, and the energy you learned to bottle at the end."
		"&eWhere:&r the Extended Crafting Ultimate Table (9x9). JEI shows the layout; press U on the Seed."
	]
	quest.6D36DDBCE1D2EF87.title: "Coke"
	quest.6D36DDBCE1D2EF87.quest_subtitle: "The fuel that started your steel"
	quest.6D36DDBCE1D2EF87.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the four corners of the Seed are coke, the first thing your coke oven ever made."
		"&eChemistry:&r coke is coal baked without air. Heat drives off water, tar and coal gas, leaving a hard, porous lump that is mostly carbon."
		"&eHow:&r any coke oven or MI Coke Oven. Four pieces."
		"&eTip:&r it's fitting that the last recipe starts with the first fuel."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: why coke, not coal?&r"
		"Raw coal is full of volatile hydrocarbons and sulfur. In a blast furnace they would boil off, foul the iron and choke the burden."
		"Coking (about 1000 °C, no oxygen) cooks them out. What's left is strong enough to carry the weight of ore above it and burns hot and clean."
		"In the furnace, coke does two jobs: it burns for heat, and its carbon monoxide strips oxygen from iron oxide: Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂."
	]
	quest.226A4C5E8144864D.title: "Hydrogen, Element 1"
	quest.226A4C5E8144864D.quest_subtitle: "The simplest atom there is"
	quest.226A4C5E8144864D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Seed needs 4 hydrogen on its own, and 8 water needs 16 more hydrogen to build. Start with a dozen and keep the Dissolver running."
		"&eChemistry:&r one proton and one electron. Hydrogen makes up about three quarters of all the ordinary matter in the universe by mass."
		"&eHow:&r the Alchemistry Dissolver breaks ChemLib water into 2 hydrogen + 1 oxygen. Other compounds give hydrogen too (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r it's the same element you used for the Potion of Flying back in Chapter II."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: the first element&r"
		"Almost all the hydrogen in existence was made in the first few minutes after the Big Bang. Every other element was built from it later, inside stars."
		"Stars fuse hydrogen into helium. Bigger stars go on to carbon, oxygen and up to iron. Heavier elements need supernovae and neutron-star collisions."
		"So hydrogen is the right place to start a new world: it's where the old one started too."
	]
	quest.5B4E365A4D8B860A.title: "Synthesized Water"
	quest.5B4E365A4D8B860A.quest_subtitle: "H₂O, built one molecule at a time"
	quest.5B4E365A4D8B860A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 8 ChemLib water, made from elements rather than scooped from a lake."
		"&eChemistry:&r 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O. The reaction releases a lot of energy: it's what powers a hydrogen fuel cell."
		"&eHow:&r Alchemistry Combiner: 2 hydrogen + 1 oxygen → 1 water."
		"&eTip:&r the Dissolver gives you the oxygen along with the hydrogen, so nothing is wasted."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: why build water at all?&r"
		"You could pour a bucket. The point of the Seed is that every part of a world can be made from its elements, and water is the most important compound of all."
		"Water's bent shape (104.5° between the two O-H bonds) makes it polar. That polarity is why it dissolves salts, why ice floats, and why it holds so much heat."
		"No water, no life. It's on the Seed eight times."
	]
	quest.3B78A43C636B517A.title: "Sulfur"
	quest.3B78A43C636B517A.quest_subtitle: "Brimstone, in quantity"
	quest.3B78A43C636B517A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r eight buckets of acid need 16 sulfur dust."
		"&eChemistry:&r sulfur is a yellow non-metal. Most of the world's supply comes from scrubbing it out of oil and gas, much as you do in petrochemistry."
		"&eHow:&r sulfuric purification of crude oil and fuels in the MI Chemical Reactor, or from ore processing byproducts (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.3295CA3D2D55ACB5.title: "The King of Chemicals"
	quest.3295CA3D2D55ACB5.quest_subtitle: "Sulfuric acid, one more time"
	quest.3295CA3D2D55ACB5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the acid that unlocked 5x ore processing. The Seed needs eight buckets."
		"&eChemistry:&r S + O₂ → SO₂, then 2SO₂ + O₂ → 2SO₃, then SO₃ + H₂O → H₂SO₄. MI's Chemical Reactor does it in one step from sulfur, oxygen and water."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: 1 sulfur dust + 200 mB oxygen + 200 mB water → 500 mB sulfuric acid."
		"&eTip:&r one reactor makes the full 8000 mB in a few minutes."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: the Contact Process&r"
		"Industry makes sulfuric acid by the contact process. Burning sulfur gives SO₂; a vanadium(V) oxide catalyst at about 450 °C turns it into SO₃."
		"SO₃ isn't simply added to water: the reaction is so violent it makes a mist of acid. It's absorbed into concentrated acid first (making oleum, H₂S₂O₇), then diluted."
		"More sulfuric acid is made than any other chemical. A country's output of it was once used as a measure of its industrial strength."
	]
	quest.0CEF6566B979F348.title: "Ethylene"
	quest.0CEF6566B979F348.quest_subtitle: "C₂H₄, the plastic monomer"
	quest.0CEF6566B979F348.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the feedstock for polyethylene. 16 buckets of plastic need about 11.5 buckets of ethylene."
		"&eChemistry:&r ethylene has a carbon-carbon double bond. That bond is what lets thousands of molecules link into a chain."
		"&eHow:&r steam-crack naphtha or light fuel and distil the result, or dehydrate ethanol in the Chemical Reactor (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.7518F6AC8A7D7AA9.title: "Polymerise"
	quest.7518F6AC8A7D7AA9.quest_subtitle: "Many small molecules, one long chain"
	quest.7518F6AC8A7D7AA9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Seed uses 16 buckets of polyethylene, more than any other ingredient."
		"&eChemistry:&r n C₂H₄ → (–CH₂–CH₂–)ₙ. The double bond opens and each monomer joins the next."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor: 500 mB ethylene + a tiny pile of chromium (or lead) dust → 700 mB polyethylene."
		"&eTip:&r the chromium is a catalyst in real life too (see the next page)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: catalysts that make plastic&r"
		"Most of the world's high-density polyethylene is made with chromium catalysts (the Phillips process) or titanium-aluminium ones (Ziegler-Natta)."
		"The metal centre grabs an ethylene molecule and slots it into the growing chain, again and again. The result is a long, straight chain that packs tightly: strong, stiff plastic."
		"Without a catalyst you need huge pressures and get a branched, softer plastic (LDPE). Same formula, different shape, different material."
	]
	quest.16A26034057BB6C8.title: "Eight Processing Units"
	quest.16A26034057BB6C8.quest_subtitle: "The EV brain, eight times over"
	quest.16A26034057BB6C8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r processing units are MI's EV circuits. The Seed takes eight, and each Energy Core needs one more."
		"&eChemistry:&r they're built on PVC boards. PVC is polyethylene with a chlorine atom on every other carbon, which makes it harder and flame-resistant."
		"&eHow:&r MI Assembler (check JEI). Queue sixteen: eight for the Seed and eight for the cores."
		"&eTip:&r processing units are slow. Start them first and let them run while you do the other lines."
	]
	quest.2AC1B7061B4071EE.title: "Stainless Steel"
	quest.2AC1B7061B4071EE.quest_subtitle: "Steel that guards itself"
	quest.2AC1B7061B4071EE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 4 plates for the Seed itself and 4 for each of the 8 Energy Core shells: 36 in all."
		"&eChemistry:&r stainless steel is iron with at least 10.5% chromium, often with nickel. The chromium forms a thin Cr₂O₃ film that heals itself when scratched."
		"&eHow:&r plates from stainless steel ingots in the Compressor. Ingots from the Electric Blast Furnace (check JEI)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: passivation&r"
		"Ordinary iron rusts because its oxide flakes off and exposes fresh metal. Chromium oxide does the opposite: it's a dense layer a few nanometres thick that sticks."
		"Scratch it and the exposed chromium reacts with oxygen in the air and seals the gap within moments. That's why stainless steel stays shiny."
		"Nickel keeps the steel in its austenite form at room temperature: tough, non-magnetic and easy to work."
	]
	quest.0EC50EEC62D9F3F6.title: "Oganesson ×8"
	quest.0EC50EEC62D9F3F6.quest_subtitle: "Element 118, eight times"
	quest.0EC50EEC62D9F3F6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the last element on the periodic table. You made one to finish the table; the Seed wants eight."
		"&eChemistry:&r oganesson-294 has a half-life of under a millisecond. Only a handful of atoms have ever been made."
		"&eHow:&r Alchemistry Fusion Chamber: fuse two elements whose atomic numbers add up to 118 (check JEI for the pairs)."
		"&eTip:&r automate the inputs. Eight by hand is a long afternoon."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: making element 118&r"
		"In 2002 a team in Dubna, Russia fired calcium-48 ions (20 protons) at a californium-249 target (98 protons). 20 + 98 = 118."
		"Over months of beam time they saw about three atoms. Each decayed by alpha emission within a millisecond, into livermorium (116)."
		"It sits in the noble gas column, but it may not behave like one: its electrons move so fast that relativity smears out its shells. Your Fusion Chamber does the same addition, rather more reliably."
	]
	quest.1CCD67EEFD869A89.title: "Plutonium Pellets"
	quest.1CCD67EEFD869A89.quest_subtitle: "Element 94, from your reactor's waste"
	quest.1CCD67EEFD869A89.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r four plutonium pellets for the Seed."
		"&eChemistry:&r uranium-238 in a reactor captures a neutron and decays twice: U-238 → U-239 → Np-239 → Pu-239."
		"&eHow:&r Mekanism: nuclear waste → Isotopic Centrifuge → plutonium → Chemical Crystallizer → pellet."
		"&eTip:&r a running fission reactor makes waste whether you want it or not. This is a good use for it."
	]
	quest.6C44C6845C242921.title: "Polonium Pellets"
	quest.6C44C6845C242921.quest_subtitle: "Element 84, in bulk"
	quest.6C44C6845C242921.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 4 pellets for the Seed and 4 for each of the 8 Energy Core shells: 36 in all. Polonium also feeds the SPS that makes antimatter."
		"&eChemistry:&r Marie and Pierre Curie found polonium in 1898 and named it after Poland. Po-210 is so radioactive that a gram of it glows from its own heat."
		"&eHow:&r Mekanism: nuclear waste → Solar Neutron Activator → polonium → Chemical Crystallizer → pellet."
		"&eTip:&r activators only work in daylight. Build a row of them, not one."
	]
	quest.5C3E6875CBAE0E55.title: "The Wither"
	quest.5C3E6875CBAE0E55.quest_subtitle: "Four stars means four fights"
	quest.5C3E6875CBAE0E55.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every Nether Star comes from a Wither. The Seed needs four."
		"&eHow:&r soul sand T-shape, three wither skeleton skulls on top. Fight it somewhere you don't mind losing."
		"&eTip:&r fight it underground or in a sealed box so it can't fly off, and bring milk for the wither effect."
	]
	quest.2DF7AB2F8A372D6E.title: "The Dragon"
	quest.2DF7AB2F8A372D6E.quest_subtitle: "The egg sits at the very centre"
	quest.2DF7AB2F8A372D6E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Dragon Egg is the Seed's centre slot."
		"&eHow:&r kill the Ender Dragon. The egg appears on top of the exit portal. Push it off with a piston or knock it onto a torch; clicking it makes it teleport."
		"&eTip:&r if someone on the server already took the egg, there's another way. Look into the Antiprotonic Nucleosynthesizer."
	]
	quest.0571A0A13F5FE83E.title: "Thirty-Two Antimatter Pellets"
	quest.0571A0A13F5FE83E.quest_subtitle: "The bulk of the work"
	quest.0571A0A13F5FE83E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each Antimatter Core takes 4 antimatter pellets, so eight cores need 32."
		"&eChemistry:&r an antiproton has the proton's mass and the opposite charge. When one meets a proton both vanish into energy (and a spray of lighter particles)."
		"&eHow:&r SPS → antimatter gas → Chemical Crystallizer. Keep both running non-stop."
		"&eTip:&r a second SPS halves the wait, if you can feed it the polonium and the power."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: how much energy?&r"
		"E = mc². Annihilating 1 gram of antimatter with 1 gram of matter releases about 1.8 × 10¹⁴ J, roughly the energy of a 43-kiloton explosion."
		"Real labs (CERN's Antiproton Decelerator) have made only nanograms in decades, and keep them for minutes at most in magnetic traps."
		"Your SPS is far kinder than physics, but it still asks for a lot of power. That's the price of reversing every charge in an atom."
	]
	quest.028FCEE75EB61B76.title: "Eight Quantum Circuits"
	quest.028FCEE75EB61B76.quest_subtitle: "One for every core"
	quest.028FCEE75EB61B76.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI's top circuit. Each Antimatter Core needs one."
		"&eHow:&r MI Assembler (check JEI). Quantum circuit boards come first."
		"&eTip:&r quantum circuits also build the fusion reactor and the quantum armour in the Creation chapter. Make spares."
	]
	quest.25D884DA0739E05F.title: "Two Cores"
	quest.25D884DA0739E05F.quest_subtitle: "A production line, not a one-off"
	quest.25D884DA0739E05F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r you've made one Antimatter Core. Make it two."
		"&eHow:&r Empty Energy Core (4 stainless plates, 4 polonium pellets, 1 processing unit) → MI Assembler at 512 EU/t to charge it → MI Assembler at 2048 EU/t with 4 antimatter pellets and 1 quantum circuit."
		"&eTip:&r two assemblers, one for each step, let the cores flow without you."
	]
	quest.5F8D7BB001543AF8.title: "Four Cores"
	quest.5F8D7BB001543AF8.quest_subtitle: "Halfway to eight"
	quest.5F8D7BB001543AF8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r four Antimatter Cores. The Seed's diamond of power is half built."
		"&eHow:&r keep the line running. Each core is about 3 million EU to charge and 12 million more to upgrade."
		"&eTip:&r if your network sags while the assemblers run, give them their own generator."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: the energy budget&r"
		"Charging: 512 EU/t × 6000 ticks = about 3.1 million EU. Upgrading: 2048 EU/t × 6000 ticks = about 12.3 million EU."
		"That's about 15 million EU per core, or about 123 million EU for all eight, before counting the SPS that makes the antimatter."
		"A fission reactor with a turbine, or a Mekanism fusion reactor, makes this a matter of hours. A wall of solar panels makes it a matter of weeks."
	]
	quest.4148D8D889253331.title: "Fire, Water, Hydrogen"
	quest.4148D8D889253331.quest_subtitle: "Seed checklist: where it all began"
	quest.4148D8D889253331.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Seed's corners and edges hold the first things you learned: coke from your coke oven, and water and hydrogen synthesized as chemicals."
		"&eHow:&r 4 coke, 8 ChemLib water and 4 ChemLib hydrogen, all held at once."
		"&eTip:&r all three are cheap now. Make spares."
	]
	quest.73A2968AB5DB56B3.title: "Eight Buckets of Acid"
	quest.73A2968AB5DB56B3.quest_subtitle: "Seed checklist: the Acid Age"
	quest.73A2968AB5DB56B3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 8 buckets of sulfuric acid, the chemical that unlocked 5x ore processing."
		"&eHow:&r fill buckets from your sulfuric acid tanks."
		"&eTip:&r buckets don't stack. Clear inventory space first, or keep them in a backpack."
	]
	quest.737B13A3F051EBCE.title: "Sixteen Buckets of Plastic"
	quest.737B13A3F051EBCE.quest_subtitle: "Seed checklist: the Oil Age"
	quest.737B13A3F051EBCE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 16 buckets of polyethylene, the most of any ingredient."
		"&eHow:&r polymerise ethylene in the Chemical Reactor, as in Petrochemistry."
		"&eTip:&r fill them straight from your polymerisation reactor's output."
	]
	quest.4B92489590061799.title: "Circuits and Steel"
	quest.4B92489590061799.quest_subtitle: "Seed checklist: the machine ages"
	quest.4B92489590061799.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 8 processing units and 4 stainless steel plates."
		"&eHow:&r both come from lines you already run. Keep these apart from the ones meant for Energy Cores."
		"&eTip:&r processing units are slow to make, so start these early."
	]
	quest.4C94606E9E477108.title: "Heavy Elements"
	quest.4C94606E9E477108.quest_subtitle: "Seed checklist: the atomic age"
	quest.4C94606E9E477108.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 8 oganesson, 4 plutonium pellets and 4 polonium pellets."
		"&eHow:&r oganesson from the Fusion Chamber; pellets from your reactor's waste."
		"&eTip:&r keep 4 polonium pellets aside. The core shells will happily eat them all."
	]
	quest.6C1F822313ECDE4A.title: "Stars and an Egg"
	quest.6C1F822313ECDE4A.quest_subtitle: "Seed checklist: trophies of the old world"
	quest.6C1F822313ECDE4A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 4 Nether Stars, and the Dragon Egg at the very centre."
		"&eHow:&r defeat the Wither four times; kill the Ender Dragon for the egg."
		"&eTip:&r on a server, agree who crafts the Seed before anyone grabs the egg."
	]
	quest.13530533FFB056A9.title: "Eight Antimatter Cores"
	quest.13530533FFB056A9.quest_subtitle: "Seed checklist: the hardest part"
	quest.13530533FFB056A9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r eight Antimatter Cores ring the centre of the recipe."
		"&eHow:&r that's 32 antimatter pellets, 32 polonium pellets, 32 stainless plates, 8 processing units and 8 quantum circuits in total."
		"&6Eight suns in your pack. You remember carrying more.&r"
	]
	quest.3A6618C9323E34D8.title: "Seed of a New World"
	quest.3A6618C9323E34D8.quest_subtitle: "The endgame goal"
	quest.3A6618C9323E34D8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Every lesson, in one 9x9 grid. You hold it, and it holds a world.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a recipe on the Ultimate Table that needs something from every tier."
		"&eHow:&r 4 coke, 8 water, 4 hydrogen, 8 sulfuric acid, 16 polyethylene, 8 processing units, 4 stainless plates, 8 oganesson, 4 plutonium, 4 polonium, 4 Nether Stars, 8 Antimatter Cores, and the Dragon Egg at the centre."
		"&eTip:&r check JEI for the exact layout before you fill the table. One wrong slot and nothing happens."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: reading the grid&r"
		"The pattern is symmetrical in every direction. Coke holds the four corners. Water and acid line the outer ring. Plastic forms crosses on all four sides."
		"Stainless steel and processing units make an inner square. Oganesson, plutonium and Nether Stars sit closer in. Eight Antimatter Cores form a diamond around the centre."
		"And in the middle, one Dragon Egg: the only thing in the old world that was already a seed of something new."
	]
	quest.4EDA4951BC73B125.title: "Ultimate Auto Table"
	quest.4EDA4951BC73B125.quest_subtitle: "Optional: let the table fill itself"
	quest.4EDA4951BC73B125.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an auto-crafting version of the Ultimate Table. Set the recipe once, then pipe the ingredients in."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the recipe. It needs power to craft."
		"&eTip:&r useful if your team wants a second Seed, or for the other 9x9 recipes in the pack."
	]
	quest.670A449A96D33FEA.title: "The Bill of Materials"
	quest.670A449A96D33FEA.quest_subtitle: "Optional: everything, counted from scratch"
	quest.670A449A96D33FEA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a shopping list for the whole Seed, Energy Cores included."
		"&eHow:&r read the next page, then tick this quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eSeed only:&r 4 coke, 8 water, 4 hydrogen, 8 acid buckets, 16 polyethylene buckets, 8 processing units, 4 stainless plates, 8 oganesson, 4 plutonium pellets, 4 polonium pellets, 4 Nether Stars, 1 Dragon Egg."
		"&eEight cores:&r 32 stainless plates, 32 polonium pellets, 8 processing units, 32 antimatter pellets, 8 quantum circuits, about 123 million EU."
		"&eGrand total:&r 36 stainless plates, 36 polonium pellets, 16 processing units, 32 antimatter pellets, 8 quantum circuits, plus everything above."
		"&eIn raw terms:&r 16 sulfur dust for the acid, 16 hydrogen and 8 oxygen for the water (plus 4 hydrogen), about 11.5 buckets of ethylene."
	]
	quest.540E985F5EBBBAA4.title: "Four Withers"
	quest.540E985F5EBBBAA4.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one for every star"
	quest.540E985F5EBBBAA4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r kill the Wither four times, once for each Nether Star in the Seed."
		"&eHow:&r a wither skeleton farm makes the skulls easy. Fight in a sealed bunker each time."
		"&eTip:&r Looting on your sword raises the skull drop chance from wither skeletons."
	]
	quest.13E910EB9FC8D13F.title: "A Second Egg"
	quest.13E910EB9FC8D13F.quest_subtitle: "Secret: a chicken egg, rewritten"
	quest.13E910EB9FC8D13F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r you found it: the Antiprotonic Nucleosynthesizer turns an ordinary egg into a Dragon Egg with a little antimatter."
		"&eChemistry:&r nucleosynthesis means building heavier nuclei from lighter ones. Stars do it slowly. Mekanism does it with an egg and 4 mB of antimatter."
		"&eTip:&r now every player on the server can have a Seed of their own."
	]
	chapter.5AFB176150767B83.title: "Creation"
	chapter.5AFB176150767B83.chapter_subtitle: [
		"The Seed is planted. Now shape what grows."
	]
	quest.699C8548A909219F.title: "A New World"
	quest.699C8548A909219F.quest_subtitle: "The demigod, restored"
	quest.699C8548A909219F.quest_desc: [
		"&6You took the world apart, element by element, and learned to build it again.&r"
		"Fire, steel, acid, oil, silicon, the atom, antimatter. Every tier was a lesson in chemistry, and you mastered them all."
		"&6The worlds out there are blank canvases now. Go make them yours.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eWhat now:&r this chapter is for after the Seed. Nothing here gates anything; it's what a demigod does with full power."
		"&eTo the right:&r making matter. Rewrite nuclei with antimatter, compress a singularity, build armour from a collapsed star."
		"&eTo the left:&r walking the worlds you can now reach, and holding the rarest parts of the periodic table in your hand."
	]
	quest.246A11D921704D57.title: "A Sample of Somewhere"
	quest.246A11D921704D57.quest_subtitle: "Bottle a biome"
	quest.246A11D921704D57.quest_desc: [
		"&6Every world you have walked through, you can carry with you.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a Biome Capsule records the biome you stand in (sneak + right-click). It tells the Terraformer what to grow."
		"&eHow:&r glass bottle, rubber sheet and any sapling. Travel to the biome you want, then record it."
		"&eTip:&r capsules stack until filled; each one holds one biome."
	]
	quest.6DC38F2552EAF71E.title: "The Terraformer"
	quest.6DC38F2552EAF71E.quest_subtitle: "The Seed, planted"
	quest.6DC38F2552EAF71E.quest_desc: [
		"&6The Seed was never meant to stay in your pocket.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Terraformer (Warbucks Core) rewrites the biome around it, nearest chunks first, out to a 9x9 chunk area."
		"&eHow:&r craft it from the Seed of a New World, processing units, stainless plates and energy cores. Right-click it with a filled Biome Capsule, then with Charged Energy Cores (each powers 9 chunks; sneak to insert a stack). Right-click empty-handed for status."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eWhat changes:&r grass and leaf colours, weather (rain or snow), and which mobs spawn, just like vanilla /fillbiome. Blocks you placed stay as they are."
		"&eTip:&r you can change it again later: a new capsule restarts the spread with the new biome."
	]
	quest.2BA7DDC2C439E998.title: "A World You Chose"
	quest.2BA7DDC2C439E998.quest_subtitle: "All 81 chunks"
	quest.2BA7DDC2C439E998.quest_desc: [
		"&6This is what the power was for.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r let a Terraformer finish its whole area (status shows 81 / 81), then tick this off."
		"&eTip:&r 9 Charged Energy Cores finish one Terraformer."
	]
	quest.2BE57BED6090B129.title: "Nucleosynthesis"
	quest.2BE57BED6090B129.quest_subtitle: "Turn one thing into another with antimatter"
	quest.2BE57BED6090B129.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember making things out of nothing. This is close.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism's Antiprotonic Nucleosynthesizer feeds a few millibuckets of antimatter into an item and rebuilds it as something rarer."
		"&eChemistry:&r nucleosynthesis is how stars make elements: lighter nuclei fuse into heavier ones. This machine borrows the idea."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the recipe and the full list of transmutations. Pipe antimatter in from your SPS."
		"&eTip:&r it works slowly. Give it its own antimatter tank."
	]
	quest.4B42E676B0625A61.title: "Hearts of the Sea"
	quest.4B42E676B0625A61.quest_subtitle: "A Nether Star, rewritten"
	quest.4B42E676B0625A61.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r four Hearts of the Sea, each nucleosynthesized from a Nether Star with 5 mB of antimatter."
		"&eHow:&r Nether Star in, antimatter in, wait about a minute."
		"&eTip:&r a Heart of the Sea plus nautilus shells makes a Conduit: permanent water breathing and night vision around an ocean base."
	]
	quest.2B7A00AD7F472C4C.title: "Skulls on Demand"
	quest.2B7A00AD7F472C4C.quest_subtitle: "Two Withers' worth, no fortress"
	quest.2B7A00AD7F472C4C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r six wither skeleton skulls, made from ordinary skeleton skulls with 5 mB of antimatter each."
		"&eHow:&r skeleton skulls drop when a charged creeper kills a skeleton, or from other sources (check JEI). Feed them to the Nucleosynthesizer."
		"&eTip:&r that's enough for two more Withers, and two more Nether Stars for a second Seed."
	]
	quest.0B60041E38BE73BA.title: "Echoes"
	quest.0B60041E38BE73BA.quest_subtitle: "Amethyst in, Ancient City loot out"
	quest.0B60041E38BE73BA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 32 echo shards, rebuilt from amethyst shards with 2 mB of antimatter each."
		"&eChemistry:&r real amethyst is quartz (SiO₂) coloured purple by traces of iron and natural radiation. Here it becomes something no chemist could make."
		"&eHow:&r amethyst shards from geodes or a budding amethyst farm. Nucleosynthesizer, 2 mB antimatter each."
		"&eTip:&r echo shards make Recovery Compasses, which point to where you last died."
	]
	quest.5980CE602A035671.title: "Sixty-Four Nukes"
	quest.5980CE602A035671.quest_subtitle: "Not for throwing"
	quest.5980CE602A035671.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI's Nuke block. Sixty-four of them are crushed together to make a singularity."
		"&eChemistry:&r a nuke combines fission (plutonium) and fusion fuel (deuterium and tritium, the heavy isotopes of hydrogen) around industrial TNT."
		"&eHow:&r MI Assembler: 6 industrial TNT, 4 plutonium ingots, 2 processing units, 4 nuclear alloy plates, 100 mB deuterium, 50 mB tritium → 2 nukes."
		"&eTip:&r that's 32 crafts, 64 processing units and 128 plutonium ingots. Automate it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: two kinds of nuclear energy&r"
		"Fission splits heavy nuclei like Pu-239 into lighter ones. Fusion joins light nuclei like deuterium (²H) and tritium (³H) into helium."
		"Both release energy because the products are more tightly bound than the inputs. Iron-56 sits at the bottom of that curve: nothing is gained by splitting it or fusing it."
		"Real thermonuclear weapons use a fission stage to compress and heat a fusion stage. MI's recipe follows the same idea."
	]
	quest.0F393E87019D7242.title: "A Singularity"
	quest.0F393E87019D7242.quest_subtitle: "Sixty-four nukes, one point"
	quest.0F393E87019D7242.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI's Singularity: an ultradense metal ball collapsed by 64 nukes in the Implosion Compressor."
		"&eHow:&r ultradense metal ball (tungsten large plates, lead plates and an iridium plate, check JEI) + 64 nukes → Implosion Compressor."
		"&eTip:&r it's never used up in the Electrolyzer: it slowly bleeds out UU-matter, 1 mB every 2500 ticks. Build several Electrolyzers and several singularities."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: collapse&r"
		"A real singularity is the centre of a black hole, where matter is crushed past every limit we know. Stars more than about 20 times the Sun's mass end this way."
		"Before that, there's neutron-star matter: electrons are pushed into protons until only neutrons remain. A teaspoon would weigh about a billion tonnes."
		"MI's singularity is a game item, not physics. But the idea, matter compressed until it becomes a source of something new, fits a demigod well."
	]
	quest.5CF14C9A3DB9276D.title: "Quantum Upgrade"
	quest.5CF14C9A3DB9276D.quest_subtitle: "UU-matter, circuits and a singularity"
	quest.5CF14C9A3DB9276D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the part that turns netherite armour into MI quantum armour."
		"&eHow:&r MI Assembler: 32 highly advanced upgrades, 8 quantum circuits, 1 singularity, 1 quantum circuit board, 50 mB UU-matter."
		"&eTip:&r 50 mB of UU-matter takes one Electrolyzer and singularity about 1.7 hours (1 mB per 2500 ticks). More singularities, more Electrolyzers."
	]
	quest.73FDE51567B46CCC.title: "Quantum Armour"
	quest.73FDE51567B46CCC.quest_subtitle: "Armour fit for a god"
	quest.73FDE51567B46CCC.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember not needing armour. This is the next best thing.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r MI's quantum armour: a full set, each piece a netherite piece plus a quantum upgrade."
		"&eHow:&r MI Packer: netherite armour piece + 1 quantum upgrade, 200 ticks at 1,000,000 EU/t. Four upgrades for four pieces."
		"&eTip:&r that draw is far above a plain Packer's limit. Check JEI and the MI guidebook for how machine upgrades raise it."
	]
	quest.2E4322C04DA4BF91.title: "Replicator"
	quest.2E4322C04DA4BF91.quest_subtitle: "Optional: copy anything with UU-matter"
	quest.2E4322C04DA4BF91.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI's Replicator copies items using UU-matter."
		"&eHow:&r MI Assembler: quantum machine hull, 2 quantum upgrades, 4 quantum circuits, 500 mB UU-matter. Check JEI for what it can copy."
		"&eTip:&r 500 mB is about 17 hours for one Electrolyzer. A long-term goal for a server, not a weekend."
	]
	quest.01EEDEE42183D76A.title: "A Star in a Box"
	quest.01EEDEE42183D76A.quest_subtitle: "MI's fusion reactor and plasma turbine"
	quest.01EEDEE42183D76A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI's fusion reactor makes helium plasma; the plasma turbine turns it into a flood of EU."
		"&eChemistry:&r D + T → ⁴He + n. MI's reactor turns 1000 mB each of deuterium and tritium into helium plasma and hydrogen."
		"&eHow:&r fusion reactor: 6 fusion chambers, a quantum machine hull and 2 quantum circuits in the MI Assembler. The multiblock layout is in JEI and the MI guidebook."
		"&eTip:&r deuterium-deuterium and helium-3 routes exist too (check JEI under the fusion reactor)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: why fusion is hard&r"
		"Nuclei are positively charged and repel each other. To fuse, they need temperatures over 100 million °C, hotter than the Sun's core."
		"The Sun manages at 15 million °C only because of its crushing gravity and its sheer size. On Earth we use magnetic bottles (tokamaks) or lasers instead."
		"In 2022 the US National Ignition Facility got more energy out of a fusion shot than its lasers put in, for the first time."
	]
	quest.5EFEE568ABAE16CE.title: "Sixty-Four Superconductors"
	quest.5EFEE568ABAE16CE.quest_subtitle: "Wire with no resistance at all"
	quest.5EFEE568ABAE16CE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a stack of MI superconductor ingots, the material of MI's best cables and coils."
		"&eChemistry:&r below a critical temperature, a superconductor carries current with zero resistance. Real high-temperature ones, like YBa₂Cu₃O₇, are copper oxides with yttrium and rare earths."
		"&eHow:&r Mixer: iridium, annealed copper, yttrium and neodymium dusts → superconductor dust. Electric Blast Furnace → hot ingot → Vacuum Freezer."
		"&eTip:&r 64 ingots need 64 EBF runs at 128 EU/t. Run several furnaces."
	]
	quest.4885EA03F81450DB.title: "Shining Alloy"
	quest.4885EA03F81450DB.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism Extras' antimatter alloy"
	quest.4885EA03F81450DB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism Extras' alloys go beyond atomic: radiance → thermonuclear → shining → spectrum. Shining is the first that needs antimatter."
		"&eHow:&r enriched thermonuclear material + antimatter in the Nucleosynthesizer gives enriched shining. Turn it into shining infusion and infuse a thermonuclear alloy (check JEI for each step)."
		"&eTip:&r these alloys build Mekanism Extras' higher tiers of factories, cables and energy cubes."
	]
	quest.60D90CB55CC28586.title: "A Stack of Atomic Alloy"
	quest.60D90CB55CC28586.quest_subtitle: "Quantity is its own kind of power"
	quest.60D90CB55CC28586.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 64 atomic alloys, Mekanism's top standard alloy."
		"&eHow:&r Metallurgic Infuser: reinforced alloy + refined obsidian dust (check JEI). Each step up uses the alloy before it."
		"&eTip:&r a Metallurgic Infusing Factory makes this a matter of minutes."
	]
	quest.4DED552C15CC21B1.title: "Quantum Compressor"
	quest.4DED552C15CC21B1.quest_subtitle: "Ten thousand of anything, made one"
	quest.4DED552C15CC21B1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Extended Crafting's Quantum Compressor squeezes huge amounts of one material into a singularity."
		"&eHow:&r crafting table: black iron ingots, a black iron slate, 2 elite components, 2 elite catalysts and a frame (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r it uses 5,000 FE/t and holds 10 million FE. Power it well."
	]
	quest.27F6CADD94271013.title: "Your First Singularity"
	quest.27F6CADD94271013.quest_subtitle: "Ten thousand ingots in one item"
	quest.27F6CADD94271013.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r any Extended Crafting singularity: iron, copper, gold, steel, aluminium, platinum and more."
		"&eHow:&r insert 10,000 of one material into the Quantum Compressor, plus 5 million FE. Check JEI for the full list."
		"&eTip:&r iron or copper is the easiest first pick: your ore lines make thousands an hour."
	]
	quest.57580059AE02623F.title: "Ultimate Singularity"
	quest.57580059AE02623F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: every singularity, in one"
	quest.57580059AE02623F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one of every singularity, combined on the Ultimate Table."
		"&eHow:&r there are 19 singularities in this pack (check JEI for the list). That's about 190,000 items in total."
		"&eTip:&r this is a server project. Split the materials between players."
	]
	quest.78E502B19DD89147.title: "Worlds Within Worlds"
	quest.78E502B19DD89147.quest_subtitle: "A demigod should have rooms to spare"
	quest.78E502B19DD89147.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Compact Machines are small rooms in their own dimension. You've made a new world; now make a few small ones."
		"&eHow:&r 64 machine walls, then step inside any of your machines with the Personal Shrinking Device."
		"&eTip:&r one room per production line keeps your main base clean and your server's tick time low."
	]
	quest.72095611C2C91CF1.title: "Rare Ground"
	quest.72095611C2C91CF1.quest_subtitle: "The Overworld's rarest places"
	quest.72095611C2C91CF1.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember these places from above. Walk them this time.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r visit a Mushroom Fields island, an Ice Spikes plain and a Cherry Grove."
		"&eHow:&r Explorer's Compass or Nature's Compass (if you have one) finds biomes; otherwise fly and look. Each completes on arrival."
		"&eTip:&r Mushroom Fields never spawn hostile mobs. A good place for a quiet base."
	]
	quest.23B71F2FEF5E96E0.title: "Under Everything"
	quest.23B71F2FEF5E96E0.quest_subtitle: "Deep Dark, the Otherside, the Undergarden"
	quest.23B71F2FEF5E96E0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Deep Dark, the Otherside's Echoing Forest, and the Undergarden's Frostfields."
		"&eHow:&r the Deep Dark is under mountains in the Overworld; the Echoing Forest is in Deeper and Darker's Otherside; the Frostfields are in the Undergarden."
		"&eTip:&r the Warden still doesn't care how powerful you are. Sneak."
	]
	quest.6D98BE12A9AAC748.title: "Fire Below"
	quest.6D98BE12A9AAC748.quest_subtitle: "The Nether's strangest corners"
	quest.6D98BE12A9AAC748.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Soul Sand Valley and two of Biomes O' Plenty's rarer Nether biomes: the Crystalline Chasm and the Withered Abyss."
		"&eChemistry:&r soul sand and soul soil burn with a blue flame. Real blue flames mean complete combustion; these are just strange."
		"&eTip:&r the Withered Abyss has bottomless drops. Bring a way to fly."
	]
	quest.40787344DD5655A1.title: "Twilight Wanderer"
	quest.40787344DD5655A1.quest_subtitle: "Deep into the Twilight Forest"
	quest.40787344DD5655A1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Enchanted Forest, the Glacier and the Highlands of the Twilight Forest."
		"&eHow:&r the Glacier and Highlands are locked behind Twilight bosses. If a biome hurts you, you haven't beaten the boss that guards it yet."
		"&eTip:&r the Enchanted Forest is small and rare. The Magic Map shows biomes as you explore."
	]
	quest.1BE80DCE67BFB851.title: "Gardens of the End"
	quest.1BE80DCE67BFB851.quest_subtitle: "The outer End islands"
	quest.1BE80DCE67BFB851.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the End Highlands and three Biomes O' Plenty End biomes: the Wilds, the Reef and the Corruption."
		"&eHow:&r take an End Gateway out past the main island. The BOP biomes are scattered among the outer islands."
		"&eTip:&r End Cities in the Highlands hold Elytra and shulker shells."
	]
	quest.6778022C45172E21.title: "Other Skies"
	quest.6778022C45172E21.quest_subtitle: "Four planets, four strange landscapes"
	quest.6778022C45172E21.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mars's polar caps, Venus's infernal barrens, Mercury's deltas and Glacio's ice peaks."
		"&eChemistry:&r Mars's polar caps are water ice under a layer of frozen CO₂ (dry ice). Venus's air is 96% CO₂ at 90 times Earth's pressure."
		"&eHow:&r Tier 2 rocket for Mars, Tier 3 for Venus and Mercury, Tier 4 for Glacio. Netherite space suit for the hot ones."
		"&eTip:&r set up a launch pad on each planet before you go exploring."
	]
	quest.66C984FCB0A4C541.title: "A Breath of Noble Gas"
	quest.66C984FCB0A4C541.quest_subtitle: "64 of helium, neon, argon, krypton, xenon or radon"
	quest.66C984FCB0A4C541.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r any 64 noble gas items from ChemLib, in any mix."
		"&eChemistry:&r noble gases have full outer electron shells, so they almost never react. Neon glows red in a discharge tube; xenon glows blue; radon is radioactive."
		"&eHow:&r Alchemistry Dissolver on air-rich or gas-bearing items, or the Fusion Chamber (check JEI for which inputs give which gas)."
		"&eTip:&r helium is the lightest: fuse two hydrogen and you're there."
	]
	quest.323139D4D25E743E.title: "The Rare Earths"
	quest.323139D4D25E743E.quest_subtitle: "64 of any lanthanide, element 57 to 71"
	quest.323139D4D25E743E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r any 64 lanthanide items from ChemLib: lanthanum through lutetium."
		"&eChemistry:&r the lanthanides fill the 4f electron shell, which sits deep inside the atom. That's why they're so alike and so hard to separate."
		"&eHow:&r Fusion Chamber (pairs that add up to 57-71) or the Dissolver on rare-earth-bearing items (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r neodymium makes the strongest permanent magnets; europium makes red phosphors in screens."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: why 'rare' earths?&r"
		"They aren't rare. Cerium is about as common as copper in the Earth's crust. They're 'rare' because they never form rich deposits on their own."
		"Separating them took chemists over a century. Their outer electrons are nearly the same, so their chemistry is nearly the same; only the slow shrinking of the atoms across the row (the lanthanide contraction) tells them apart."
		"Industry separates them by solvent extraction, hundreds of stages long. Your Fusion Chamber skips all that."
	]
	quest.4D22FC631684D41C.title: "Island of Stability"
	quest.4D22FC631684D41C.quest_subtitle: "64 superheavy atoms, elements 113 to 118"
	quest.4D22FC631684D41C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r any 64 of the six newest elements: nihonium, flerovium, moscovium, livermorium, tennessine and oganesson."
		"&eChemistry:&r all six were made in the last 25 years, a few atoms at a time, and decay within seconds or less."
		"&eHow:&r Alchemistry Fusion Chamber. Automate the inputs and let it run."
		"&eTip:&r physicists predict an 'island of stability' near 114 protons and 184 neutrons, where superheavy nuclei might last much longer. No one has reached it yet."
	]
	quest.192E6C7744B27AF1.title: "Demigod"
	quest.192E6C7744B27AF1.quest_subtitle: "Nothing left to remember"
	quest.192E6C7744B27AF1.quest_desc: [
		"&6You don't remember being this any more. You simply are.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r you've walked every world, built armour from a collapsed star, and held the whole periodic table."
		"&eNow:&r build. A city, a garden on Mars, a pocket world for every friend on the server. The tools are yours."
		"&6The new world is waiting. It's whatever you make it.&r"
	]
	quest.591A55827650C75D.title: "Pressure Not Required"
	quest.591A55827650C75D.quest_subtitle: "Secret: coal, rewritten into diamond"
	quest.591A55827650C75D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Nucleosynthesizer turns coal into diamond with 4 mB of antimatter. You found it."
		"&eChemistry:&r both are carbon. Graphite and diamond differ only in how the atoms bond: sheets of rings versus a rigid 3D lattice. Nature needs about 50,000 atmospheres to make the change."
		"&eTip:&r 64 diamonds from 64 coal. Your younger self, swinging an iron pickaxe, would be furious."
	]
	quest.3783C72768169901.title: "Where It Began"
	quest.3783C72768169901.quest_subtitle: "Secret: the oldest-looking valley"
	quest.3783C72768169901.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Biomes O' Plenty's Origin Valley, built to look like the very first versions of Minecraft."
		"&6Bright grass, roses, plain old trees. You remember a world this simple. It was the first one you made.&r"
		"&eTip:&r it's rare. If you found it by chance, consider it a gift."
	]
	chapter.4077DB038B5ACC44.title: "The Periodic Table"
	chapter.4077DB038B5ACC44.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Rebuild the table, group by group. Each column shares a chemistry, because each shares an outer-electron arrangement."
	]
	quest.66353CA51BFD14BF.title: "Reading the Table"
	quest.66353CA51BFD14BF.quest_subtitle: "Rows, columns, and why they matter"
	quest.66353CA51BFD14BF.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember this chart. You used to know every box by heart.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the periodic table orders the elements by proton number. Rows are periods; columns are groups."
		"&eChemistry:&r elements in the same group have the same number of outer (valence) electrons, so they react alike."
		"&eHow:&r press &eU&r on any element in JEI to see which blocks the Dissolver turns into it."
		"&eTip:&r this chapter is a side path. Nothing in the main story waits on it, but it pays well."
	]
	quest.65BFE56092A18CC6.title: "Alkali Metals"
	quest.65BFE56092A18CC6.quest_subtitle: "Group 1: one electron to give away"
	quest.65BFE56092A18CC6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r lithium, sodium and potassium, the softest and most reactive metals."
		"&eChemistry:&r one valence electron, easily lost. Sodium fizzes on water (2Na + 2H₂O → 2NaOH + H₂); potassium burns lilac."
		"&eHow:&r end stone gives lithium; lapis lazuli gives sodium (the mineral lazurite is a sodium aluminosilicate). Plants give potassium."
		"&eTip:&r check JEI with &eU&r on each element. Many common blocks hide small amounts."
	]
	quest.7C336C41BCCDBBD5.title: "Alkaline Earth Metals"
	quest.7C336C41BCCDBBD5.quest_subtitle: "Group 2: two electrons, still eager"
	quest.7C336C41BCCDBBD5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r beryllium, magnesium and calcium: lighter structural metals and the stuff of bones and limestone."
		"&eChemistry:&r two valence electrons, so they form 2+ ions. Calcium carbonate (CaCO₃) is limestone; magnesium burns blinding white."
		"&eHow:&r andesite and bone give calcium (bone via hydroxylapatite, the mineral in teeth). Beryllium and magnesium come out of their compounds: check JEI."
	]
	quest.25099A06619CE537.title: "Transition Metals"
	quest.25099A06619CE537.quest_subtitle: "The wide middle block"
	quest.25099A06619CE537.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the hard, conductive metals behind every machine you've built."
		"&eChemistry:&r their d-orbitals fill across the row. That's why they form coloured compounds and make good catalysts."
		"&eHow:&r dissolve ingots, nuggets or dusts of each metal."
		"&eTip:&r ore you already process gives nuggets and dust. Dissolve the spares, not your ingots."
	]
	quest.0710D708F34467AF.title: "Post-Transition Metals"
	quest.0710D708F34467AF.quest_subtitle: "Soft metals on the metal side of the line"
	quest.0710D708F34467AF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r aluminum, tin, lead and indium: softer, lower-melting metals just right of the transition block."
		"&eChemistry:&r indium tin oxide is the clear conductor in every touchscreen. Lead is dense enough to stop X-rays."
		"&eHow:&r diorite dissolves into tin and indium. Aluminum and lead come from their ingots, dusts and minerals (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.109F6CDEEFC90F6D.title: "Liquid Metals"
	quest.109F6CDEEFC90F6D.quest_subtitle: "Metals that melt in your hand"
	quest.109F6CDEEFC90F6D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r mercury and gallium, the two metals you can pour (almost) at room temperature."
		"&eChemistry:&r mercury melts at −38.8 °C; gallium at 29.8 °C, below body temperature."
		"&eHow:&r ender pearls and end stone dissolve into mercury. Cobblestone gives a little gallium."
	]
	quest.38880DD5F24455C0.title: "Challenge: The First Twenty"
	quest.38880DD5F24455C0.quest_subtitle: "Hydrogen to calcium, one of each"
	quest.38880DD5F24455C0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one of each of elements 1 to 20, the four shortest rows of the table."
		"&eChemistry:&r these twenty make up almost all of your body, the oceans and the air."
		"&eHow:&r most come from the groups in this chapter. Boron and the noble gases need the Fusion Chamber (boron is 5: try H + Be)."
		"&eTip:&r an optional collection. Keep one of each in a chest as you go."
	]
	quest.5A6D643C9FD789DE.title: "The Coinage Metals"
	quest.5A6D643C9FD789DE.quest_subtitle: "Group 11: copper, silver, gold"
	quest.5A6D643C9FD789DE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the three metals humans have minted into money for thousands of years."
		"&eChemistry:&r they're unreactive enough to keep their shine. Silver is the best electrical conductor of any element."
		"&eHow:&r deepslate dissolves into a little silver. Check JEI for richer sources."
	]
	quest.6D2ACD876F2DB46F.title: "Metalloids"
	quest.6D2ACD876F2DB46F.quest_subtitle: "Half metal, half non-metal"
	quest.6D2ACD876F2DB46F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r germanium, silicon and arsenic sit on the staircase between metals and non-metals."
		"&eChemistry:&r silicon conducts a little, and a trace of arsenic (doping) controls how much. The first transistor (1947) was germanium."
		"&eHow:&r sand dissolves into silicon dioxide, which dissolves again into silicon and oxygen. Blaze powder and Nether bricks give germanium."
		"&eTip:&r you'll need a lot of silicon later, for circuits and AE2."
	]
	quest.50A543F5038B63D3.title: "Non-Metals"
	quest.50A543F5038B63D3.quest_subtitle: "Fertilisers, matches and acids"
	quest.50A543F5038B63D3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r nitrogen, phosphorus and sulfur. Life and industry both run on them."
		"&eChemistry:&r nitrogen and phosphorus feed every crop; sulfur becomes sulfuric acid, the most-made chemical on Earth."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI with &eU&r. Nether blocks are a good place to look for sulfur."
	]
	quest.2357AF880243FC07.title: "Chalcogens"
	quest.2357AF880243FC07.quest_subtitle: "Group 16: the ore-formers"
	quest.2357AF880243FC07.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r oxygen, sulfur and selenium. 'Chalcogen' means 'ore-former'."
		"&eChemistry:&r two electrons short of a full shell, so they grab metals: most ores are oxides or sulfides (Fe₂O₃, ZnS, PbS)."
		"&eHow:&r fish and crimson fungus dissolve into selenium. Oxygen comes from nearly everything."
		"&eTip:&r selenium is a trace nutrient: you need a little, and too much is poisonous."
	]
	quest.58998E87C50508C4.title: "Halogens"
	quest.58998E87C50508C4.quest_subtitle: "Group 17: the salt-makers"
	quest.58998E87C50508C4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fluorine, chlorine, bromine and iodine, the most reactive non-metals."
		"&eChemistry:&r one electron short of full. 'Halogen' means 'salt-maker': Na + Cl → NaCl, table salt."
		"&eHow:&r magma blocks give fluorine and bromine. Horn coral gives iodine (via lead iodide). Chlorine comes out of salts: check JEI."
	]
	quest.67AFDB4F1145AF74.title: "Noble Gases"
	quest.67AFDB4F1145AF74.quest_subtitle: "Group 18: the full shell"
	quest.67AFDB4F1145AF74.quest_desc: [
		"&6Two halves of the table, joined. More of the old knowledge settles into place.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r helium, neon and argon, the gases that refuse to react."
		"&eChemistry:&r a full outer shell means nothing to gain or lose. Argon shields welds from air; neon glows red in a discharge tube."
		"&eHow:&r nothing dissolves into them, so build them: the Alchemistry Fusion Chamber (EV) adds proton numbers, so H + H → He. Check JEI for neon and argon."
		"&eTip:&r real stars fuse hydrogen into helium too, though it takes them four protons, not two."
	]
	quest.2FCFC5332C725FC5.title: "Heavy Noble Gases"
	quest.2FCFC5332C725FC5.quest_subtitle: "Even the 'inert' ones have limits"
	quest.2FCFC5332C725FC5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r xenon and radon, the heaviest natural noble gases."
		"&eChemistry:&r in 1962 xenon was made to react (with platinum hexafluoride), ending the idea that noble gases never react. Radon is radioactive."
		"&eHow:&r dragon's breath dissolves into both. That means a trip to the End."
	]
	quest.4FDD1C7682843FC7.title: "Rare Earths"
	quest.4FDD1C7682843FC7.quest_subtitle: "Not rare, just hard to separate"
	quest.4FDD1C7682843FC7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the lanthanides: lanthanum, cerium, neodymium and their near-identical neighbours."
		"&eChemistry:&r they differ only in an inner (4f) shell, so their chemistry is almost the same. Neodymium makes the strongest permanent magnets."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for sources. The Alchemistry Fusion Chamber can also build them from lighter elements."
	]
	quest.28B0DD716F969942.title: "Actinides"
	quest.28B0DD716F969942.quest_subtitle: "Every one of them radioactive"
	quest.28B0DD716F969942.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r thorium, uranium and plutonium, the fuels of the nuclear age."
		"&eChemistry:&r every actinide is radioactive. Plutonium barely exists in nature: you made it by firing neutrons at uranium."
		"&eHow:&r dissolve uranium and thorium materials. Plutonium comes from your fission reactor's waste."
	]
	quest.37629D084F46D2D3.title: "Isotopes: Heavy Water"
	quest.37629D084F46D2D3.quest_subtitle: "Same element, different weight"
	quest.37629D084F46D2D3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r heavy water, D₂O: water made with deuterium, hydrogen with an extra neutron."
		"&eChemistry:&r isotopes have the same protons (so the same chemistry) but different neutrons. About 1 in 6,400 hydrogen atoms is deuterium."
		"&eHow:&r put a Filter Upgrade in a Mekanism Electric Pump and pump from water. It pulls out heavy water instead."
		"&eTip:&r deuterium is half of fusion fuel. You'll want this again in the Power chapter."
	]
	quest.6092229653F9D8E1.title: "Superheavy Elements"
	quest.6092229653F9D8E1.quest_subtitle: "Element 117, built by fusion"
	quest.6092229653F9D8E1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tennessine, element 117. Nothing in the world dissolves into it; you have to build it."
		"&eChemistry:&r real labs make superheavy elements by smashing nuclei together; only a handful of atoms have ever existed."
		"&eHow:&r the Alchemistry Fusion Chamber joins two elements, adding their proton numbers. Check JEI for the pairs that reach 117."
		"&eTip:&r one more step after this: add hydrogen (1) to tennessine (117) and you get 118."
	]
	quest.1488AD40E664A1B0.title: "Element 118"
	quest.1488AD40E664A1B0.quest_subtitle: "The last box on the table"
	quest.1488AD40E664A1B0.quest_desc: [
		"&6The last box on the table. You remember now: you once named these.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r oganesson, the heaviest element ever made."
		"&eChemistry:&r in reality it lasts under a millisecond. Here it sits in your inventory, which is the kind of thing demigods can do."
		"&eHow:&r fuse tennessine with hydrogen (or any pair adding to 118) in the Fusion Chamber."
	]
	quest.6FD07C82DBE5D22F.title: "Covalent Bonds: CO₂"
	quest.6FD07C82DBE5D22F.quest_subtitle: "Non-metals share electrons"
	quest.6FD07C82DBE5D22F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r carbon dioxide, your first compound in this chapter."
		"&eChemistry:&r C + O₂ → CO₂. Non-metals don't hand electrons over; they share them in covalent bonds (O=C=O)."
		"&eHow:&r in the Combiner, pick Carbon Dioxide and supply 1 carbon + 2 oxygen."
		"&eTip:&r the Combiner GUI shows each recipe once you select its output."
	]
	quest.37C4E268B693B12C.title: "Hydrocarbons"
	quest.37C4E268B693B12C.quest_subtitle: "Carbon chains and hydrogen"
	quest.37C4E268B693B12C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r methane (natural gas) and ethylene (the building block of polyethylene)."
		"&eChemistry:&r CH₄ has four single bonds. C₂H₄ has a C=C double bond, which is what lets it link into plastic chains."
		"&eHow:&r Combiner: methane = 1 C + 4 H; ethylene = 2 C + 4 H."
	]
	quest.60B403CE02523A26.title: "Ammonia"
	quest.60B403CE02523A26.quest_subtitle: "Nitrogen made useful"
	quest.60B403CE02523A26.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ammonia, NH₃, the base of nearly all fertiliser."
		"&eChemistry:&r N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃. Breaking nitrogen's triple bond is hard; the Haber-Bosch process needs heat, pressure and an iron catalyst."
		"&eHow:&r Combiner: 1 nitrogen + 3 hydrogen. Later you'll run real Haber-Bosch in an MI machine."
	]
	quest.5C85F46DBAFB7975.title: "Ionic Bonds: Salt"
	quest.5C85F46DBAFB7975.quest_subtitle: "A metal gives, a non-metal takes"
	quest.5C85F46DBAFB7975.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r sodium chloride, NaCl: table salt."
		"&eChemistry:&r sodium gives its one electron to chlorine. Na⁺ and Cl⁻ then hold together in a cubic crystal: an ionic bond."
		"&eHow:&r Combiner: 1 sodium + 1 chlorine."
		"&eTip:&r a reactive metal plus a poisonous gas makes something you sprinkle on food. Chemistry is strange."
	]
	quest.0432714741764BB2.title: "Strong Acids"
	quest.0432714741764BB2.quest_subtitle: "Hydrochloric and nitric acid"
	quest.0432714741764BB2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r hydrochloric acid (HCl) and nitric acid (HNO₃)."
		"&eChemistry:&r acids give up H⁺ ions in water. Mixed 3:1, HCl and HNO₃ make aqua regia, which dissolves gold and platinum."
		"&eHow:&r Combiner: HCl = 1 H + 1 Cl; HNO₃ = 1 H + 1 N + 3 O."
	]
	quest.6C1BC2C1F5E838C9.title: "King of Chemicals"
	quest.6C1BC2C1F5E838C9.quest_subtitle: "H₂SO₄ from its elements"
	quest.6C1BC2C1F5E838C9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Built atom by atom. The old craft is coming back faster now.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r sulfuric acid, H₂SO₄, built straight from elements."
		"&eChemistry:&r industry makes it by the contact process: S → SO₂ → SO₃ → H₂SO₄. Here you skip the plant and place the atoms yourself."
		"&eHow:&r Combiner: 2 hydrogen + 1 sulfur + 4 oxygen."
	]
	quest.5A7E7E44590CC88A.title: "Sugar and Wood"
	quest.5A7E7E44590CC88A.quest_subtitle: "Carbohydrates from scratch"
	quest.5A7E7E44590CC88A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r sucrose (table sugar) and cellulose (what wood and paper are made of)."
		"&eChemistry:&r plants make both from CO₂ and water using sunlight. Cellulose is a chain of glucose rings: C₆H₁₀O₅ per unit."
		"&eHow:&r Combiner: sucrose = 12 C + 22 H + 11 O; cellulose = 6 C + 10 H + 5 O."
		"&eTip:&r that's a lot of atoms. Stock up on carbon, hydrogen and oxygen first."
	]
	quest.62A5D4682F28805B.title: "Alcohol"
	quest.62A5D4682F28805B.quest_subtitle: "Add an OH group"
	quest.62A5D4682F28805B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ethanol, C₂H₅OH, made by attaching a hydroxide (OH) group to a two-carbon chain."
		"&eChemistry:&r the -OH group is what makes it an alcohol and lets it mix with water."
		"&eHow:&r Combiner: hydroxide = 1 O + 1 H, then ethanol = 2 C + 5 H + 1 hydroxide."
	]
	quest.4E03509D055DE107.title: "Lye"
	quest.4E03509D055DE107.quest_subtitle: "The base that balances the acid"
	quest.4E03509D055DE107.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r sodium hydroxide, NaOH: lye, a strong base."
		"&eChemistry:&r industry makes it by electrolysing salt water: 2NaCl + 2H₂O → 2NaOH + Cl₂ + H₂. Acid + base → salt + water."
		"&eHow:&r Combiner: 1 sodium + 1 hydroxide (make hydroxide from 1 O + 1 H)."
	]
	quest.22EF02A8E3C647BA.title: "Rust"
	quest.22EF02A8E3C647BA.quest_subtitle: "Iron, slowly returning to ore"
	quest.22EF02A8E3C647BA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r iron(III) oxide, Fe₂O₃: rust, and also hematite, the most common iron ore."
		"&eChemistry:&r 4Fe + 3O₂ → 2Fe₂O₃. A blast furnace runs this backwards, using carbon to pull the oxygen off."
		"&eHow:&r Combiner: 2 iron + 3 oxygen."
	]
	quest.588B21981793812F.title: "Group 1, Complete"
	quest.588B21981793812F.quest_subtitle: "Every alkali metal, lithium to francium"
	quest.588B21981793812F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r all six alkali metals: Li, Na, K, Rb, Cs and Fr."
		"&eChemistry:&r reactivity climbs down the group: the outer electron sits further from the nucleus and is lost more easily. Caesium explodes in water."
		"&eHow:&r press &eU&r on rubidium and caesium in JEI for Dissolver sources. Francium is rare in both reality and here; the Fusion Chamber can build it."
		"&eTip:&r real francium has a half-life of about 22 minutes. Yours keeps."
	]
	quest.4D4D8F69EA0E51DA.title: "Group 2, Complete"
	quest.4D4D8F69EA0E51DA.quest_subtitle: "Beryllium to radium"
	quest.4D4D8F69EA0E51DA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r all six alkaline earth metals: Be, Mg, Ca, Sr, Ba and Ra."
		"&eChemistry:&r strontium salts burn red and barium salts green: that's how fireworks get their colours. Radium glows from its own radioactivity."
		"&eHow:&r JEI (&eU&r) shows Dissolver sources for strontium, barium and radium; the Fusion Chamber fills any gaps."
	]
	quest.7A6D3E363800E95F.title: "The Boron Group"
	quest.7A6D3E363800E95F.quest_subtitle: "Group 13: three valence electrons"
	quest.7A6D3E363800E95F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r boron, aluminum, gallium, indium and thallium."
		"&eChemistry:&r boron is a metalloid; the rest are metals. Borosilicate glass (with B₂O₃) survives sudden heat, which is why lab glassware uses it."
		"&eHow:&r boron needs the Fusion Chamber (5 = 1 + 4: hydrogen + beryllium). Check JEI for thallium."
		"&eTip:&r thallium is very toxic in reality. In a chest it's harmless."
	]
	quest.5A3D23B90C25591B.title: "The Carbon Group"
	quest.5A3D23B90C25591B.quest_subtitle: "Group 14: from diamond to lead"
	quest.5A3D23B90C25591B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r carbon, silicon, germanium, tin and lead, all with four valence electrons."
		"&eChemistry:&r the group runs from a non-metal (carbon) through metalloids (Si, Ge) to metals (Sn, Pb). Same outer shell, very different behaviour."
		"&eHow:&r all five come from the Dissolver: coal or graphite, sand, Nether bricks, diorite and lead ingots (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.78A106BCA05B94C4.title: "The Pnictogens"
	quest.78A106BCA05B94C4.quest_subtitle: "Group 15: nitrogen to bismuth"
	quest.78A106BCA05B94C4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r nitrogen, phosphorus, arsenic, antimony and bismuth."
		"&eChemistry:&r five valence electrons, so they often form three bonds (NH₃, PH₃). Bismuth crystals grow in stepped 'hopper' shapes with a rainbow oxide film."
		"&eHow:&r JEI (&eU&r) shows Dissolver sources for antimony and bismuth."
	]
	quest.1475430F54A37D4C.title: "Group 17, Complete"
	quest.1475430F54A37D4C.quest_subtitle: "All five halogens, astatine included"
	quest.1475430F54A37D4C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the four common halogens plus astatine, one of the rarest natural elements on Earth."
		"&eChemistry:&r down the group the halogens go from gas (F₂, Cl₂) to liquid (Br₂) to solid (I₂): bigger molecules attract each other more strongly."
		"&eHow:&r astatine has a few Dissolver sources (press &eU&r in JEI), or build it in the Fusion Chamber."
	]
	quest.237F3EB96853A0D3.title: "Group 18, Complete"
	quest.237F3EB96853A0D3.quest_subtitle: "Every natural noble gas"
	quest.237F3EB96853A0D3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r helium through radon, the whole right-hand column."
		"&eChemistry:&r from 1960 to 1983 the metre was defined by the orange light of krypton-86. Xenon lights car headlamps and drives ion engines in spacecraft."
		"&eHow:&r nothing dissolves into the light ones: fuse them in the Fusion Chamber (krypton is 36: try neon + iron). Xenon and radon come from dragon's breath."
	]
	quest.74C0A65252881167.title: "All Fifteen Lanthanides"
	quest.74C0A65252881167.quest_subtitle: "Lanthanum to lutetium"
	quest.74C0A65252881167.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the full lanthanide row, the first line of the f-block."
		"&eChemistry:&r europium makes the red in old TV screens and the anti-forgery glow in euro notes. Promethium has no stable isotope at all."
		"&eHow:&r a few have Dissolver sources (press &eU&r); the Fusion Chamber builds the rest by adding proton numbers."
		"&eTip:&r a challenge, not a requirement. Work through them as spare elements pile up."
	]
	quest.6C84E4F71745246F.title: "All Fifteen Actinides"
	quest.6C84E4F71745246F.quest_subtitle: "Actinium to lawrencium"
	quest.6C84E4F71745246F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the full actinide row. Everything past uranium is man-made."
		"&eChemistry:&r einsteinium and fermium were first found in the debris of the first hydrogen bomb test in 1952. Americium sits in household smoke detectors."
		"&eHow:&r the Fusion Chamber: gold (79) plus a light element reaches actinium and beyond (check JEI for the pairs)."
	]
	quest.22D0F58DF7F25E10.title: "Limestone"
	quest.22D0F58DF7F25E10.quest_subtitle: "CaCO₃: shells, chalk and marble"
	quest.22D0F58DF7F25E10.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r calcium carbonate, the mineral in limestone, chalk, marble and seashells."
		"&eChemistry:&r heat it and it splits: CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂. That quicklime is the start of cement and mortar."
		"&eHow:&r Combiner: first carbonate (1 carbon + 3 oxygen), then 1 calcium + 1 carbonate."
	]
	quest.5AC83B5A60A95BA7.title: "Saltpeter"
	quest.5AC83B5A60A95BA7.quest_subtitle: "KNO₃: fertiliser and black powder"
	quest.5AC83B5A60A95BA7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r potassium nitrate, the oxidiser in gunpowder and a classic fertiliser."
		"&eChemistry:&r black powder is roughly 75% KNO₃, 15% charcoal and 10% sulfur. The nitrate brings its own oxygen, so it burns without air."
		"&eHow:&r Combiner: nitrate (1 nitrogen + 3 oxygen), then 1 potassium + 1 nitrate."
		"&eTip:&r the Combiner also turns potassium nitrate, sulfur and graphite into gunpowder (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.2E9EA30781616E79.title: "Aspirin"
	quest.2E9EA30781616E79.quest_subtitle: "C₉H₈O₄, from willow bark to pill"
	quest.2E9EA30781616E79.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r acetylsalicylic acid, the world's best-known painkiller."
		"&eChemistry:&r willow bark contains salicin, used against pain for thousands of years. Adding an acetyl group (1897) made it gentler on the stomach."
		"&eHow:&r Combiner: 9 carbon + 8 hydrogen + 4 oxygen."
	]
	quest.7BCDFE7974554AE4.title: "Permanganate"
	quest.7BCDFE7974554AE4.quest_subtitle: "KMnO₄: the purple oxidiser"
	quest.7BCDFE7974554AE4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r potassium permanganate, deep purple crystals and a strong oxidiser."
		"&eChemistry:&r manganese here is in its +7 oxidation state and eager to take electrons back. The purple fades as it reacts, so chemists use it as its own indicator."
		"&eHow:&r Combiner: 1 potassium + 1 manganese + 4 oxygen."
	]
	quest.13136D8964D60149.title: "Morning Coffee"
	quest.13136D8964D60149.quest_subtitle: "Secret: C₈H₁₀N₄O₂"
	quest.13136D8964D60149.quest_desc: [
		"&6Even a demigod likes a cup in the morning. You remember that much without trying.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r caffeine, built atom by atom: 8 carbon, 10 hydrogen, 4 nitrogen, 2 oxygen."
		"&eChemistry:&r it blocks adenosine receptors in the brain, the signal that tells you you're tired."
		"&eTip:&r plants make caffeine as an insecticide. You drink it on purpose."
	]
	quest.1ED913270D2A436D.title: "Han Purple"
	quest.1ED913270D2A436D.quest_subtitle: "Secret: an ancient synthetic pigment"
	quest.1ED913270D2A436D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r han purple, BaCuSi₂O₆, a barium copper silicate."
		"&eChemistry:&r Chinese artisans made it more than 2,000 years ago by firing barium, copper and silica minerals together. It colours figures in the Terracotta Army."
		"&eHow:&r Combiner: 1 barium + 1 copper + 2 silicon + 6 oxygen."
		"&eTip:&r one of the first synthetic pigments in history. You just repeated an ancient experiment."
	]
	chapter.3FC1F772A8F79D5D.title: "Lab Notebook"
	chapter.3FC1F772A8F79D5D.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Why it works: the real chemistry behind every machine in the pack."
	]
	quest.54D480148A428377.title: "Note: Why Alloys Are Harder"
	quest.54D480148A428377.quest_subtitle: "Bronze and the sliding-layer problem"
	quest.54D480148A428377.quest_desc: [
		"&6You open a notebook in your own handwriting. The first page is about bronze.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a pure metal is soft because its atoms sit in neat layers that slide past each other."
		"&eChemistry:&r add a few bigger or smaller atoms (tin in copper) and the layers jam. Bronze is about 88% Cu, 12% Sn."
		"&eTip:&r tick this when you've read both pages. Lab notes never block the main path."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive:&r metals are a lattice of positive ions in a 'sea' of shared electrons (metallic bonding). The electrons hold the ions together but let whole planes of atoms shift: that's why metals bend instead of shattering."
		"&eSolid solutions:&r in bronze, tin atoms replace some copper atoms in the lattice. Tin atoms are larger, so they distort the planes around them and pin them in place. Harder, stronger, still workable."
		"&eIn the pack:&r 3 copper dust + 1 tin dust → 3 bronze dust (a 3:1 ratio by count, close to the historical recipe). Every later alloy follows the same idea with different partners."
	]
	quest.3BC13BCE2A947A64.title: "Note: Steel and Carbon"
	quest.3BC13BCE2A947A64.quest_subtitle: "A pinch of carbon changes everything"
	quest.3BC13BCE2A947A64.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r steel is iron with up to about 2% carbon. Most structural steel has well under 1%."
		"&eChemistry:&r tiny carbon atoms fit into the gaps between iron atoms (an interstitial alloy) and lock the layers."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eFrom ore to iron:&r a real blast furnace burns coke to carbon monoxide, which strips oxygen from iron ore: Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂."
		"&eToo much carbon:&r furnace iron ('pig iron') has about 4% carbon and is brittle. Steelmaking blows oxygen through it to burn the excess off as CO and CO₂ (the basic oxygen process)."
		"&eIn the pack:&r MI skips the ore step: iron dust + coke dust → uncooked steel, baked in the Steam Blast Furnace. The coke you made is the carbon source."
	]
	quest.2141C053422A6B2D.title: "Note: Invar, the Metal That Won't Grow"
	quest.2141C053422A6B2D.quest_subtitle: "Iron + nickel with almost no thermal expansion"
	quest.2141C053422A6B2D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r invar is about 64% iron and 36% nickel. MI uses it for rotary blades and gears."
		"&eChemistry:&r most metals expand when heated. Invar barely does, which keeps precision parts precise."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eWhy:&r in this exact mix, a magnetic effect inside the crystal shrinks the lattice as it warms, cancelling the normal expansion (the 'Invar effect')."
		"&eHistory:&r Charles-Édouard Guillaume found it in 1896 and won the 1920 Nobel Prize in Physics. It went into clocks, measuring tapes and later the shadow masks of colour TVs."
		"&eIn the pack:&r mix iron and nickel dust in the Mixer (check JEI for the ratio). Cupronickel (copper + nickel) is its cousin, used for heating coils because it resists current steadily."
	]
	quest.7CBC658F33E8B7F7.title: "Note: Electrum, a Natural Alloy"
	quest.7CBC658F33E8B7F7.quest_subtitle: "Gold and silver that nature mixed first"
	quest.7CBC658F33E8B7F7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r electrum is gold alloyed with silver. It's found that way in rivers, already mixed."
		"&eChemistry:&r gold and silver atoms are almost the same size and both form the same crystal, so they mix in any proportion."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eComplete solubility:&r when two metals have similar atomic radius, the same crystal structure and similar electronegativity, they can blend smoothly from 0% to 100% (the Hume-Rothery rules). Gold-silver and copper-nickel are classic examples."
		"&eWhy MI wants it:&r both metals conduct electricity superbly and resist corrosion, ideal for circuit boards."
		"&eIn the pack:&r gold ore often gives silver as a byproduct in the Centrifuge for exactly this reason: native gold is usually electrum."
	]
	quest.7F6A8CAA886F253C.title: "Note: Stainless Steel"
	quest.7F6A8CAA886F253C.quest_subtitle: "Steel that heals its own skin"
	quest.7F6A8CAA886F253C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r steel with at least 10.5% chromium (plus nickel and manganese) that doesn't rust."
		"&eChemistry:&r chromium reacts with air to form a thin Cr₂O₃ film only a few atoms thick. It seals the surface."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&ePassivation:&r ordinary rust (hydrated iron oxide) is flaky, so it falls off and exposes fresh iron: 4Fe + 3O₂ + 2xH₂O → 2Fe₂O₃·xH₂O. Chromium oxide is dense and sticks, so oxygen can't get through."
		"&eSelf-repair:&r scratch the surface and the exposed chromium reacts with oxygen again within moments, rebuilding the film."
		"&eIn the pack:&r 6 iron + 1 chromium + 1 nickel + 1 manganese dust → 9 stainless dust. It melts so hot that it leaves the EBF as a hot ingot and must be cooled in the Vacuum Freezer."
	]
	quest.423D337BE9E0D3BA.title: "Note: Coking Coal"
	quest.423D337BE9E0D3BA.quest_subtitle: "Baking coal without air"
	quest.423D337BE9E0D3BA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r coke is coal heated in an oven with no air, leaving almost pure carbon."
		"&eChemistry:&r without oxygen the coal can't burn. Instead its volatile parts (tars, gases, water) boil away. This is pyrolysis."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eWhat leaves:&r coal tar and creosote (heavy aromatic oils), coal gas (mostly H₂ and CH₄), ammonia and sulfur compounds. Old gasworks sold all of them."
		"&eWhat stays:&r a hard, porous carbon skeleton. It's strong enough to carry the weight of ore in a blast furnace and burns hotter than coal."
		"&eIn the pack:&r the Coke Oven turns coal into coke and sometimes creosote. Charcoal from wood is the same idea on a smaller scale."
	]
	quest.42F1B1EE7E035990.title: "Note: Taking Things Apart"
	quest.42F1B1EE7E035990.quest_subtitle: "The Dissolver, and what real chemists do"
	quest.42F1B1EE7E035990.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Dissolver turns any block into the elements and compounds it's made of."
		"&eChemistry:&r every substance is built from about 90 natural elements. Analysing what's inside is called elemental analysis."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eThe real thing:&r chemists can't dissolve a block of wood into a pile of carbon, but they can measure it. Burn a sample in oxygen and weigh the CO₂ and H₂O formed: that gives the carbon and hydrogen content (combustion analysis). A mass spectrometer reads atoms by their mass."
		"&eConservation of mass:&r atoms are never created or destroyed in a chemical change, only rearranged (Lavoisier, 1789). The Dissolver is a game version of that law: everything you put in comes out as atoms."
		"&eIn the pack:&r many outputs are chance-based (JEI shows the odds). Some items give compounds first; dissolve those again for pure elements."
	]
	quest.5EBB0B1FD1ED63A6.title: "Note: Fixed Recipes"
	quest.5EBB0B1FD1ED63A6.quest_subtitle: "Why water is always H₂O"
	quest.5EBB0B1FD1ED63A6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Combiner always needs the same numbers of each element for a compound."
		"&eChemistry:&r that's the law of definite proportions: a pure compound always has the same elements in the same ratio."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eProust's law (1794):&r water from a river, a glacier or a test tube is always 2 H for every 1 O, which is 11.2% hydrogen by mass. Compounds aren't mixtures; they have a formula."
		"&eBalanced equations:&r because atoms are conserved, both sides of a reaction must hold the same atoms: 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O has 4 H and 2 O on each side. The Combiner's recipes are balanced equations made of items."
		"&eIn the pack:&r compare a Combiner recipe in JEI with the formula on the compound's tooltip; the counts match."
	]
	quest.4D1154B739B71329.title: "Note: Isotopes"
	quest.4D1154B739B71329.quest_subtitle: "Same element, different weight"
	quest.4D1154B739B71329.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r isotopes are atoms of one element with different numbers of neutrons."
		"&eChemistry:&r chemistry is decided by electrons, and isotopes have the same electrons, so they react identically. Only their mass differs."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eHydrogen's three:&r ¹H (no neutron), deuterium ²H (one) and tritium ³H (two). Deuterium is stable and found in heavy water, D₂O; tritium is radioactive and is bred from lithium. Both feed the fusion reactor."
		"&eUranium's two:&r natural uranium is 99.3% U-238 and only 0.72% U-235, the isotope that splits easily. Reactors need it enriched to roughly 3 to 5%."
		"&eHow enrichment works:&r turn uranium into UF₆, a gas, then spin it. Molecules with U-238 are about 1% heavier and drift outward. Thousands of centrifuges in a row (a cascade) multiply that tiny difference. The Isotopic Centrifuge is one stage of that."
	]
	quest.6B270AB61C2A38E4.title: "Note: Making Elements"
	quest.6B270AB61C2A38E4.quest_subtitle: "Where the elements really come from"
	quest.6B270AB61C2A38E4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Alchemistry's fission and fusion chambers split or join nuclei to change one element into another."
		"&eChemistry:&r an element is defined by its proton count (atomic number). Change the nucleus and you change the element. That's nuclear physics, not chemistry."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eIn stars:&r stars fuse hydrogen into helium, then helium into carbon and oxygen, and so on up to iron. Fusing past iron costs energy instead of releasing it."
		"&eHeavier than iron:&r most heavy elements form when nuclei capture neutrons, slowly in old giant stars (the s-process) or in a flash during neutron-star mergers and supernovae (the r-process). Your gold was forged in a cosmic collision."
		"&eOganesson (118):&r made in 2002 by firing calcium-48 (Z = 20) at californium-249 (Z = 98): 20 + 98 = 118. Only a handful of atoms have ever existed, each lasting under a millisecond. The chambers add atomic numbers the same way."
	]
	quest.16413D21780D1807.title: "Fool's Gold"
	quest.16413D21780D1807.quest_subtitle: "Not everything that glitters"
	quest.16413D21780D1807.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember laughing at prospectors. Then you remember being one.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r you synthesised iron disulfide, FeS₂: pyrite, better known as fool's gold."
		"&eChemistry:&r brassy and cubic, it fooled miners for centuries. Strike it on steel and it sparks; the name comes from the Greek for fire."
		"&eTip:&r roasting pyrite was once a major source of SO₂ for sulfuric acid: 4FeS₂ + 11O₂ → 2Fe₂O₃ + 8SO₂."
	]
	quest.7E828052210346C3.title: "Note: Why Crushing Doubles Ore"
	quest.7E828052210346C3.quest_subtitle: "Ore, gangue and the 2x rule"
	quest.7E828052210346C3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r in this pack, every route caps at &e2x&r per ore block (1.5x per raw ore) until you have acids."
		"&eChemistry:&r real ore is a little metal mineral locked in a lot of worthless rock (gangue). Grinding frees the mineral so it can be separated."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eBeneficiation:&r mines crush ore to powder, then concentrate it. Dense minerals sink in water (gravity separation), magnetic ones stick to magnets, and sulfide minerals cling to air bubbles in froth flotation while the rock sinks."
		"&eSmelting the concentrate:&r only then is the metal freed by heat and chemistry, for example 2PbS + 3O₂ → 2PbO + 2SO₂, then PbO + C → Pb + CO."
		"&eThe game rule:&r crushing recovers more of the metal than tossing raw chunks in a furnace, so dust gives more ingots. The 2x cap is a balance choice; the next notes explain how acids push past it."
	]
	quest.7FFCA794F7A0681A.title: "Note: 3x, 4x, 5x"
	quest.7FFCA794F7A0681A.quest_subtitle: "Oxygen, chloride and acid leaching"
	quest.7FFCA794F7A0681A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism's ore chain adds a chemical step per tier: O₂ (3x), HCl (4x), H₂SO₄ (5x)."
		"&eChemistry:&r each step mirrors a real way of pulling metal out of rock: roasting, chlorination and leaching."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&e3x, oxygen:&r roasting sulfide ore in air turns it into an oxide that is easier to reduce: 2ZnS + 3O₂ → 2ZnO + 2SO₂."
		"&e4x, chloride:&r metal chlorides are often volatile or soluble, so chlorination separates metals cleanly. Titanium is refined this way (the Kroll process goes through TiCl₄)."
		"&e5x, leaching:&r sulfuric acid dissolves the metal out as a sulfate slurry, e.g. CuO + H₂SO₄ → CuSO₄ + H₂O. Wash it, crystallise it, and almost nothing is left behind. This hydrometallurgy is how much of the world's copper is made today."
	]
	quest.1090A28FC3203361.title: "Note: Ores Come in Families"
	quest.1090A28FC3203361.quest_subtitle: "Why the Centrifuge finds a second metal"
	quest.1090A28FC3203361.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r centrifuging Mekanism dirty dust gives the main metal plus a chance at a second one."
		"&eChemistry:&r metals with similar chemistry crystallise together in the same rocks, so real refineries recover them as byproducts."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eThe pairs in this pack:&r iron → nickel (iron-nickel ores), copper → gold (recovered when copper is refined), gold → silver (native gold is electrum), lead → silver (galena, PbS, is the main silver source), tin → tungsten (cassiterite sits with wolframite), osmium → iridium (osmiridium), uranium → lead (uranium decays into lead over billions of years)."
		"&eWhy it matters:&r many rare metals have no mines of their own. Most of the world's indium, gallium and germanium comes out of zinc and aluminum refining."
	]
	quest.628CDE2D665A1E45.title: "Note: Refining Platinum"
	quest.628CDE2D665A1E45.quest_subtitle: "Aqua regia and a careful precipitation"
	quest.628CDE2D665A1E45.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the platinum line turns anode sludge into pure platinum and four rarer metals."
		"&eChemistry:&r platinum resists almost every acid, but aqua regia (3 HCl : 1 HNO₃) dissolves it. Then a salt pulls it back out alone."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eStep 1, dissolve:&r nitric acid oxidises the metal and chloride holds it in solution: Pt + 4HNO₃ + 6HCl → H₂PtCl₆ + 4NO₂ + 4H₂O."
		"&eStep 2, precipitate:&r ammonium chloride forms a yellow salt that barely dissolves: H₂PtCl₆ + 2NH₄Cl → (NH₄)₂PtCl₆ + 2HCl."
		"&eStep 3, calcine:&r heat drives everything else off as gas: 3(NH₄)₂PtCl₆ → 3Pt + 2NH₄Cl + 16HCl + 2N₂."
		"&eThe residue:&r iridium, osmium, rhodium and ruthenium don't dissolve in aqua regia, so they stay behind and are separated later (the Centrifuge in this pack)."
	]
	quest.569F76BBACC216C2.title: "Coffee Break"
	quest.569F76BBACC216C2.quest_subtitle: "Every lab runs on it"
	quest.569F76BBACC216C2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Even a demigod needs a coffee before the long reactions.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r you synthesised caffeine, C₈H₁₀N₄O₂, from its elements."
		"&eChemistry:&r caffeine fits the brain's adenosine receptors without switching them on, so the 'you're tired' signal can't get through."
		"&eTip:&r it's a purine, a close relative of two of the four bases in DNA (adenine and guanine)."
	]
	quest.79BEB641DEFB5C31.title: "Note: Splitting Water"
	quest.79BEB641DEFB5C31.quest_subtitle: "Electrolysis: electricity drives a reaction backwards"
	quest.79BEB641DEFB5C31.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Electrolytic Separator (and MI's Electrolyzer) split water into hydrogen and oxygen."
		"&eChemistry:&r 2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂. Burning hydrogen releases energy; electrolysis pays that energy back to undo it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eAt the electrodes:&r the negative electrode (cathode) gives electrons to water: 2H₂O + 2e⁻ → H₂ + 2OH⁻. The positive electrode (anode) takes them: 2H₂O → O₂ + 4H⁺ + 4e⁻."
		"&eTwo to one:&r twice as much hydrogen gas as oxygen comes off, by volume, exactly as the formula says. MI matches it: 3000 mB water → 2000 mB H₂ + 1000 mB O₂."
		"&eReal detail:&r pure water barely conducts, so real cells add a dissolved salt or alkali (an electrolyte) to carry the current. Only the water is used up."
	]
	quest.3D78546E16F1A9EE.title: "Note: The Chlor-Alkali Process"
	quest.3D78546E16F1A9EE.quest_subtitle: "Salt water in, chlorine out"
	quest.3D78546E16F1A9EE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r electrolysing salt gives chlorine, one of the most-used industrial chemicals (PVC, bleach, HCl)."
		"&eChemistry:&r in water: 2NaCl + 2H₂O → Cl₂ + H₂ + 2NaOH. Molten salt with no water gives metal: 2NaCl → 2Na + Cl₂."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eTwo routes:&r brine cells (the chlor-alkali process) make chlorine, hydrogen and sodium hydroxide (lye) together. Molten-salt cells (the Downs cell) make sodium metal and chlorine. Mekanism's separator gives sodium + chlorine, like the Downs cell."
		"&eWhy chlorine goes to the anode:&r chloride ions (Cl⁻) carry the negative charge, so they're drawn to the positive electrode and give up their electrons: 2Cl⁻ → Cl₂ + 2e⁻."
		"&eNext step:&r hydrogen and chlorine combine into hydrogen chloride, H₂ + Cl₂ → 2HCl, which you need for 4x ore and for PVC."
	]
	quest.48D49B45AC4EFCF0.title: "Note: Catalysts"
	quest.48D49B45AC4EFCF0.quest_subtitle: "Faster reactions, nothing used up"
	quest.48D49B45AC4EFCF0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a catalyst speeds up a reaction without being consumed. Industry runs on them."
		"&eChemistry:&r it offers an easier pathway with a lower energy barrier (activation energy). It doesn't change where the equilibrium ends up."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eClassic catalysts:&r vanadium(V) oxide for SO₂ → SO₃ (contact process), iron for ammonia (Haber-Bosch), platinum-rhodium gauze for burning ammonia (Ostwald), chromium or titanium compounds for polyethylene, and zeolites in refinery cat-crackers."
		"&eSurface catalysts:&r gases stick to the metal surface, their bonds weaken, they react, and the product lets go, freeing the site for the next molecule."
		"&eIn the pack:&r machines don't model catalysts, and MI's polymer recipes consume a few tiny metal dusts. In real plants the catalyst is replaced only when it slowly wears out or gets poisoned."
	]
	quest.68772890EE85CCEE.title: "Note: The Contact Process"
	quest.68772890EE85CCEE.quest_subtitle: "Sulfuric acid, the king of chemicals"
	quest.68772890EE85CCEE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r sulfuric acid is made in larger amounts than any other chemical: about 250 million tonnes a year."
		"&eChemistry:&r S + O₂ → SO₂, then 2SO₂ + O₂ ⇌ 2SO₃ over V₂O₅, then SO₃ is turned into H₂SO₄."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eThe balancing act:&r 2SO₂ + O₂ ⇌ 2SO₃ releases heat, so lower temperatures give more SO₃ but react slowly. About 450 °C with a catalyst is the compromise. This is Le Chatelier's principle in action."
		"&eThe odd last step:&r SO₃ isn't bubbled straight into water; that makes a fine acid mist. It's absorbed into existing concentrated acid to form oleum (H₂S₂O₇), which is then diluted: H₂S₂O₇ + H₂O → 2H₂SO₄."
		"&eIn the pack:&r Mekanism splits the steps across three machines; MI's Chemical Reactor does it all at once from sulfur, oxygen and water. Its uses: 5x ore, fertilisers, batteries and the Seed of a New World."
	]
	quest.3EEF5FAA0EF15827.title: "Note: Haber-Bosch"
	quest.3EEF5FAA0EF15827.quest_subtitle: "Fixing nitrogen from the air"
	quest.3EEF5FAA0EF15827.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ammonia, NH₃, made from nitrogen in the air and hydrogen. Fertiliser made from it feeds billions."
		"&eChemistry:&r N₂ + 3H₂ ⇌ 2NH₃. The N≡N triple bond is one of the strongest bonds there is, so it needs pressure, heat and an iron catalyst."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eConditions:&r about 200 atmospheres and 400 to 450 °C over iron. The reaction releases heat, so cooler gives more ammonia but far too slowly; high pressure helps because 4 gas molecules become 2."
		"&eRecycling:&r only about 15% converts per pass, so the ammonia is condensed out and the unreacted gas goes round again."
		"&eReal hydrogen:&r most comes from natural gas (steam reforming, CH₄ + H₂O → CO + 3H₂). In the pack you get it from electrolysis instead, the 'green ammonia' route."
	]
	quest.73C48B0D9B78A1DC.title: "Note: The Ostwald Process"
	quest.73C48B0D9B78A1DC.quest_subtitle: "Ammonia into nitric acid"
	quest.73C48B0D9B78A1DC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r nitric acid, HNO₃, for fertiliser, explosives in mining, and in this pack, aqua regia."
		"&eChemistry:&r overall NH₃ + 2O₂ → HNO₃ + H₂O, which happens in three real steps."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eStep 1:&r ammonia burns over a red-hot platinum-rhodium gauze (about 900 °C): 4NH₃ + 5O₂ → 4NO + 6H₂O. The contact lasts only milliseconds."
		"&eStep 2:&r the gas cools and nitric oxide picks up more oxygen: 2NO + O₂ → 2NO₂ (brown)."
		"&eStep 3:&r NO₂ is absorbed in water: 3NO₂ + H₂O → 2HNO₃ + NO. The leftover NO goes back to step 2."
		"&eIn the pack:&r the Chemical Reactor does all three at once: 1 B ammonia + 2 B oxygen → 1 B nitric acid + 1 B water."
	]
	quest.7A933FC224D7210D.title: "Note: Fractional Distillation"
	quest.7A933FC224D7210D.quest_subtitle: "Sorting crude oil by boiling point"
	quest.7A933FC224D7210D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r crude oil is a mix of thousands of hydrocarbons. A distillation tower sorts them into fractions."
		"&eChemistry:&r bigger molecules have stronger attractions between them, so they boil at higher temperatures."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eThe tower:&r crude is heated to about 400 °C and fed in near the bottom. Vapour rises through trays, cooling as it goes; each fraction condenses at the height where the tower matches its boiling point."
		"&eTop to bottom:&r refinery gas (C₁ to C₄), naphtha (about C₅ to C₁₀), kerosene, diesel (light fuel), fuel oil (heavy fuel), and a tarry residue at the base."
		"&eSour crude:&r crude contains sulfur compounds, which is why MI's first fractions are 'sulfuric'. Hydrotreating with hydrogen strips the sulfur out as H₂S, and in MI that comes back to you as sulfuric acid."
	]
	quest.3C2A80CE10E42AE2.title: "Note: Steam Cracking"
	quest.3C2A80CE10E42AE2.quest_subtitle: "Breaking long chains into building blocks"
	quest.3C2A80CE10E42AE2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r cracking breaks big, less useful molecules into small, valuable ones, especially ethylene."
		"&eChemistry:&r e.g. C₁₀H₂₂ → C₈H₁₈ + C₂H₄. One product must have a C=C double bond, because there isn't enough hydrogen to go round."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eSteam cracking:&r naphtha mixed with steam is heated to about 850 °C for a fraction of a second, then quenched. The steam dilutes the hydrocarbon so it doesn't coke up the pipes. No catalyst: heat alone snaps the C-C bonds."
		"&eCatalytic cracking:&r refineries also crack heavy oil over zeolite catalysts at lower temperatures to make petrol. That's a different process with a different goal."
		"&eIn the pack:&r naphtha + steam → steam-cracked naphtha in the Chemical Reactor, then the Distillation Tower separates ethylene, propene, benzene and more."
	]
	quest.172800B968364FB8.title: "Note: Polymers"
	quest.172800B968364FB8.quest_subtitle: "Thousands of ethylenes holding hands"
	quest.172800B968364FB8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a polymer is a giant molecule made of repeating small units (monomers). Polyethylene is the world's most common plastic."
		"&eChemistry:&r n C₂H₄ → (-CH₂-CH₂-)ₙ. Each double bond opens and links to the next molecule: addition polymerisation."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eChain length:&r a typical polyethylene chain has tens of thousands of carbon atoms. Long chains tangle like spaghetti, which is why plastic is tough instead of waxy."
		"&eLDPE vs HDPE:&r high-pressure, radical polymerisation gives branched chains that pack loosely (soft LDPE film). Metal catalysts (Ziegler-Natta, Phillips) give straight chains that pack tightly (stiff HDPE, Mekanism's HDPE pellets)."
		"&eIn the pack:&r polyethylene unlocks HV digital circuits, and 16 buckets go into the Seed of a New World."
	]
	quest.220F50B22EDEE68F.title: "Note: PVC"
	quest.220F50B22EDEE68F.quest_subtitle: "Polyethylene with a chlorine twist"
	quest.220F50B22EDEE68F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r polyvinyl chloride, the plastic of pipes, cable insulation and window frames. MI needs it for EV processing units."
		"&eChemistry:&r n C₂H₃Cl → (-CH₂-CHCl-)ₙ. The same addition polymerisation as polyethylene, with one H swapped for Cl."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eWhy chlorine matters:&r the C-Cl bonds make PVC rigid, oil-resistant and slow to burn (it releases HCl, which smothers flames). That's why it's trusted around electrical wiring."
		"&eMaking the monomer:&r the old route, used in MI, adds HCl to acetylene: C₂H₂ + HCl → C₂H₃Cl. Modern plants start from ethylene and chlorine instead, then crack the intermediate: C₂H₄Cl₂ → C₂H₃Cl + HCl."
		"&eTwo industries meet:&r PVC is where petrochemicals (the carbon) and chlor-alkali (the chlorine) come together."
	]
	quest.4A100082246D9BCC.title: "Note: Silicon from Sand"
	quest.4A100082246D9BCC.quest_subtitle: "Carbothermic reduction"
	quest.4A100082246D9BCC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r silicon metal is made by stripping oxygen from quartz (SiO₂) with carbon."
		"&eChemistry:&r SiO₂ + 2C → Si + 2CO at around 2000 °C in an electric arc furnace."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eMetallurgical grade:&r this gives silicon about 98 to 99% pure. Good enough for aluminum alloys and silicones, nowhere near good enough for chips."
		"&eThe purity ladder:&r for electronics, silicon is turned into a liquid (trichlorosilane: Si + 3HCl → SiHCl₃ + H₂), distilled until almost perfectly clean, then turned back into silicon (the Siemens process). That reaches 'nine nines', 99.9999999%."
		"&eIn the pack:&r quartz dust + coke dust in the EBF gives silicon for transistors and diodes. The next purity step comes at EV."
	]
	quest.0860B25725FD586F.title: "Note: Growing a Perfect Crystal"
	quest.0860B25725FD586F.quest_subtitle: "The Czochralski process and doping"
	quest.0860B25725FD586F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r chips are built on wafers sliced from one single crystal of silicon."
		"&eChemistry:&r a seed crystal dipped into molten silicon and pulled up slowly while turning grows into an ingot where every atom lines up."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eWhy argon:&r molten silicon reacts with oxygen and nitrogen, so the crystal is grown under argon, an unreactive noble gas. That's why the pack asks for argon here."
		"&eDoping:&r pure silicon conducts poorly. A few atoms of phosphorus per million (one extra electron each) make n-type silicon; boron (one electron short) makes p-type. Where the two meet you get a diode, and stacks of junctions make transistors."
		"&eIn the pack:&r EBF: silicon dust + a tiny pinch of iridium + argon → monocrystalline silicon, then the Cutting Machine slices it into wafers."
	]
	quest.34777C5D08BD6921.title: "Note: Fission Power"
	quest.34777C5D08BD6921.quest_subtitle: "Splitting heavy nuclei"
	quest.34777C5D08BD6921.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a fission reactor splits uranium nuclei and uses the heat to make steam."
		"&eChemistry:&r ²³⁵U + n → ¹⁴¹Ba + ⁹²Kr + 3n + about 200 MeV. Mass numbers balance (236 = 141 + 92 + 3) and so do protons (92 = 56 + 36)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eChain reaction:&r each split releases 2 to 3 neutrons. If on average exactly one causes another split, the reactor runs steadily. Control rods absorb extra neutrons to hold it there."
		"&eWhere the energy comes from:&r the fragments weigh slightly less than the original nucleus. That missing mass becomes energy (E = mc²), about a million times more per atom than burning carbon."
		"&eWaste:&r the fragments are radioactive. In Mekanism, nuclear waste is processed into plutonium and polonium, which feed the next tiers. Always plan coolant and a SCRAM circuit."
	]
	quest.30AE82BF82E60951.title: "Note: Fusion Power"
	quest.30AE82BF82E60951.quest_subtitle: "Joining light nuclei, like the Sun"
	quest.30AE82BF82E60951.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fusion joins hydrogen isotopes into helium. It powers every star."
		"&eChemistry:&r ²H + ³H → ⁴He + n + 17.6 MeV. Per kilogram of fuel that's about four times more energy than fission."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eThe hard part:&r nuclei are positively charged and repel each other. They must hit at enormous speed, which means a plasma at about 100 million °C, held away from the walls by magnetic fields or squeezed by lasers."
		"&eIgnition:&r laser fusion fires lasers into a tiny gold cylinder (a hohlraum) that turns the light into X-rays and crushes a fuel pellet. Mekanism borrows exactly that: a laser burst into a filled Hohlraum lights the reactor."
		"&eFuel:&r deuterium comes from heavy water; tritium is bred from lithium: ⁶Li + n → ³H + ⁴He."
	]
	quest.5668ED9E8679D917.title: "Note: Antimatter as a Battery"
	quest.5668ED9E8679D917.quest_subtitle: "The densest energy store imaginable"
	quest.5668ED9E8679D917.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every particle has an antiparticle with the opposite charge. Meet and they annihilate into pure energy."
		"&eChemistry:&r all the mass turns to energy: E = mc². One gram of antimatter meeting one gram of matter releases about 1.8 × 10¹⁴ J."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eReal antimatter:&r positrons (anti-electrons) are used every day in PET scans. Antiprotons and antihydrogen are made at CERN, but all of it ever made adds up to only nanograms, at an enormous energy cost."
		"&eA store, not a source:&r making antimatter always costs more energy than it gives back. That's why it works as a battery: put energy in once, carry it in a tiny pellet, get it out later."
		"&eIn the pack:&r the SPS turns polonium and huge amounts of power into antimatter, which charges Antimatter Cores for the capstone. That part is game design, not real physics."
	]
	quest.02DB47D12BCB5C95.title: "Note: The Whole Notebook"
	quest.02DB47D12BCB5C95.quest_subtitle: "Every page in one recipe"
	quest.02DB47D12BCB5C95.quest_desc: [
		"&6The last page of the notebook is blank. You realise you're meant to write it.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Seed of a New World puts one product of every chemistry lesson into a single 9x9 recipe."
		"&eChemistry:&r each ingredient stands for a whole industry you rebuilt from the ground up."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eThe ledger:&r coke (pyrolysis and steelmaking), water and hydrogen (synthesis and electrolysis), sulfuric acid (the contact process), polyethylene (cracking and polymerisation), processing units (silicon purification and PVC), stainless plates (alloys), oganesson (building nuclei), plutonium and polonium (fission), Antimatter Cores (mass into energy)."
		"&eThe point:&r almost nothing in modern life is mined and used as-is. It's separated, reacted, purified and combined. That's chemistry, and now it's yours."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the exact layout on the Ultimate Table."
	]
	chapter.19F3B97B20C71F81.title: "Mekanism"
	chapter.19F3B97B20C71F81.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Osmium, infusion and gases: Mekanism's machines, generators and its two big add-ons."
	]
	quest.30B33E37D8C75001.title: "The Mekanism Way"
	quest.30B33E37D8C75001.quest_subtitle: "Infuse, tier up, process"
	quest.30B33E37D8C75001.quest_desc: [
		"&6Osmium hums in your hand. You remember metals that drank other substances and grew stronger.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism is a machine mod built on infusion: soak a metal in carbon, redstone, diamond or refined obsidian and it becomes an alloy."
		"&eHow:&r every machine comes in tiers (basic, advanced, elite, ultimate). In this pack each tier's control circuit needs the matching &eMI circuit&r."
		"&eTip:&r this page is a side path. The main-path Mekanism quests are linked on the left; click one to jump there."
	]
	quest.15B4A19FFE957B9C.title: "Reinforced Alloy"
	quest.15B4A19FFE957B9C.quest_subtitle: "Infused alloy plus diamond"
	quest.15B4A19FFE957B9C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the second Mekanism alloy, used in elite circuits, lasers and the Solar Neutron Activator."
		"&eChemistry:&r real alloys work the same way: a few percent of a second element (carbon in steel, chromium in stainless) changes the metal's properties."
		"&eHow:&r Metallurgic Infuser: Infused Alloy + diamond infusion (from diamonds or diamond dust; check JEI)."
	]
	quest.430AB97A415B41E0.title: "Atomic Alloy"
	quest.430AB97A415B41E0.quest_subtitle: "Reinforced alloy plus refined obsidian"
	quest.430AB97A415B41E0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the top Mekanism alloy, needed for ultimate circuits, teleportation cores and the Robit."
		"&eHow:&r first infuse obsidian dust with diamond to get refined obsidian dust, then infuse Reinforced Alloy with refined obsidian."
		"&eTip:&r crush obsidian in the Crusher or an MI macerator for obsidian dust."
	]
	quest.74EB548B9C9A8966.title: "Refined Obsidian"
	quest.74EB548B9C9A8966.quest_subtitle: "The Osmium Compressor's speciality"
	quest.74EB548B9C9A8966.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r refined obsidian ingots: very hard, blast-proof metal for teleporters, the Robit and endgame tools."
		"&eHow:&r the Osmium Compressor presses refined obsidian dust with liquid osmium into ingots. It needs an Advanced Control Circuit (MV)."
		"&eTip:&r refined glowstone ingots come from the same machine: glowstone dust plus osmium."
	]
	quest.43B12CDF9223A242.title: "Advanced Control Circuit"
	quest.43B12CDF9223A242.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism's MV tier"
	quest.43B12CDF9223A242.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the circuit for every advanced-tier Mekanism block: factories, cubes, tanks, the Purification Chamber."
		"&eHow:&r an &eMI electronic circuit&r between two Infused Alloys and a Basic Control Circuit (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the old infuser shortcut for circuits is removed in this pack. Circuits follow MI's voltage tiers."
	]
	quest.11991CAC308F74E6.title: "Elite Control Circuit"
	quest.11991CAC308F74E6.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism's HV tier"
	quest.11991CAC308F74E6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the circuit for elite-tier blocks, the Chemical Injection Chamber and the Solar Neutron Activator."
		"&eHow:&r an &eMI digital circuit&r with Reinforced Alloys and an Advanced Control Circuit (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.6C11AB2E4E625255.title: "Ultimate Control Circuit"
	quest.6C11AB2E4E625255.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism's EV tier"
	quest.6C11AB2E4E625255.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the circuit behind Mekanism's best machines: the Chemical Washer, Crystallizer, Dissolution Chamber, Isotopic Centrifuge and QIO."
		"&eHow:&r an &eMI processing unit&r with Atomic Alloys and an Elite Control Circuit (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r this unlocks the rest of the page: ultimate factories, QIO, More Machine's big machines and Mekanism Extras."
	]
	quest.66341E3805E3752A.title: "Basic Factory"
	quest.66341E3805E3752A.quest_subtitle: "Three jobs at once"
	quest.66341E3805E3752A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a factory is a machine with several slots that work in parallel. A basic factory runs 3 operations at once."
		"&eHow:&r craft any single machine (Energized Smelter, Enrichment Chamber, Crusher...) with Basic Control Circuits and Basic Alloy. Any factory type counts."
		"&eTip:&r factories sort their own inputs with auto-sort in the GUI, so one input pipe is enough."
	]
	quest.22D7A2CC8DFCC447.title: "Advanced Factory"
	quest.22D7A2CC8DFCC447.quest_subtitle: "Five jobs at once"
	quest.22D7A2CC8DFCC447.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 5 parallel slots, and faster with upgrades."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade a basic factory in the crafting grid with Advanced Control Circuits, Infused Alloy and osmium, or use a Tier Installer on a placed one."
	]
	quest.3C4B48A497C51131.title: "Elite Factory"
	quest.3C4B48A497C51131.quest_subtitle: "Seven jobs at once"
	quest.3C4B48A497C51131.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 7 parallel slots. Pair an Elite Purifying or Injecting Factory with your ore line and the bottleneck moves elsewhere."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade an advanced factory with Elite Control Circuits and Reinforced Alloy (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.3AFA57F1F49E8CFE.title: "Ultimate Factory"
	quest.3AFA57F1F49E8CFE.quest_subtitle: "Nine jobs at once"
	quest.3AFA57F1F49E8CFE.quest_desc: [
		"&6Nine tasks in one box, all at once. You remember doing many things at once without effort.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r 9 parallel slots, the top of base Mekanism. Mekanism Extras goes further (see the bottom row)."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade an elite factory with Ultimate Control Circuits and Atomic Alloy (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r add Speed and Energy upgrades: speed raises power use, energy upgrades bring it back down."
	]
	quest.642807281823E2EA.title: "Tier Installers"
	quest.642807281823E2EA.quest_subtitle: "Upgrade without breaking"
	quest.642807281823E2EA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r right-click a placed machine with a Tier Installer to turn it into the next tier, keeping its contents and settings."
		"&eHow:&r the basic installer needs a Basic Control Circuit; the advanced one needs an Advanced Control Circuit (MV)."
		"&eTip:&r a plain machine plus a basic installer becomes a basic factory."
	]
	quest.6081E3377F168B47.title: "Pressurized Reaction Chamber"
	quest.6081E3377F168B47.quest_subtitle: "Solid, liquid and gas in, products out"
	quest.6081E3377F168B47.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the PRC reacts an item, a fluid and a gas together under pressure. It makes substrate, HDPE's ethylene route and more."
		"&eChemistry:&r pressure pushes gas molecules closer together so they collide with the other reactants more often. Le Chatelier: a reaction that shrinks gas volume is favoured by high pressure."
		"&eHow:&r Basic Control Circuits, Infused Alloy, steel, an Enrichment Chamber, a Dynamic Tank and chemical tanks (check JEI). Press &eU&r on it in JEI for every recipe."
		"&eTip:&r it often makes two products at once (an item and a gas). Give each output side its own pipe."
	]
	quest.56908C9904F02260.title: "Pigments"
	quest.56908C9904F02260.quest_subtitle: "Colour as a chemical"
	quest.56908C9904F02260.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Pigment Extractor pulls coloured pigment out of dyes; the Painting Machine applies it to blocks and items."
		"&eChemistry:&r a pigment's colour comes from the light its molecules absorb: indigo absorbs orange-red light, so it looks blue."
		"&eHow:&r the extractor needs Basic Circuits; the Painting Machine needs an Advanced Control Circuit (MV)."
	]
	quest.4B25493CF359C69E.title: "Challenge: The Full Chemical Plant"
	quest.4B25493CF359C69E.quest_subtitle: "One of every Mekanism chemical machine"
	quest.4B25493CF359C69E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one of each of Mekanism's ten chemical machines, from the Chemical Infuser to an SPS port."
		"&eChemistry:&r together they cover the unit operations of a real chemical plant: reaction, oxidation, electrolysis, washing, crystallisation, dissolution and isotope separation."
		"&eHow:&r most are on the main path (see the links on the left). The washer, crystallizer, dissolution chamber and centrifuge need Ultimate Control Circuits (EV)."
		"&eTip:&r an optional collection. Keep spares in a chest as you build each one."
	]
	quest.476F4F55DB74C16A.title: "Teleporter"
	quest.476F4F55DB74C16A.quest_subtitle: "Step through a frame, arrive elsewhere"
	quest.476F4F55DB74C16A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a frame-and-controller portal that links to other teleporters, even across dimensions."
		"&eHow:&r the controller needs a Teleportation Core (Atomic Alloy, gold, diamond, ender pearl). Frames are refined obsidian and refined glowstone. Build a 3x4 frame with the controller in it (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the Portable Teleporter does the same from your inventory."
	]
	quest.379346C489EA37E0.title: "Robit"
	quest.379346C489EA37E0.quest_subtitle: "A small robot friend"
	quest.379346C489EA37E0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Robit follows you, picks up items, smelts and crafts. It is also a crafting part for the Digital Miner and several More Machine blocks."
		"&eHow:&r Atomic Alloy, refined obsidian, steel, an Energy Tablet and a personal chest (check JEI). Place it on a Chargepad to recharge."
		"&eTip:&r rename it with a name tag. It won't mind."
	]
	quest.69E6901DA16854A9.title: "Digital Miner"
	quest.69E6901DA16854A9.quest_subtitle: "Mine a whole area by filter"
	quest.69E6901DA16854A9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a machine that mines out a large radius below it, taking only the blocks you filter for."
		"&eHow:&r Atomic Alloy, a Logistical Sorter, a Robit, a Teleportation Core and a steel casing (check JEI). Set filters (tags like c:ores work), radius and height, then start it."
		"&eTip:&r it uses a lot of power. Speed upgrades help, but bring Energy upgrades too."
	]
	quest.724CD60BF0CF8E1A.title: "QIO"
	quest.724CD60BF0CF8E1A.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism's digital storage"
	quest.724CD60BF0CF8E1A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Quantum Item Orchestration: drives in a drive array hold items, and dashboards, importers and exporters reach them wirelessly through a frequency."
		"&eHow:&r the drive array and the base drive need Ultimate Control Circuits (EV). Set one frequency and give every QIO block the same one."
		"&eTip:&r AE2 is the pack's main storage. QIO is a good wireless add-on for a remote outpost."
	]
	quest.00D068F4E57C86B3.title: "Thermoelectric Boiler"
	quest.00D068F4E57C86B3.quest_subtitle: "Water into steam, by the tank"
	quest.00D068F4E57C86B3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a multiblock boiler that turns water into steam, heated by Superheating Elements (power) or by hot coolant from a fission reactor."
		"&eChemistry:&r boiling water takes 2,260 J per gram, far more than heating it. That latent heat is what the turbine later turns back into work."
		"&eHow:&r the layout is in &eJust Enough Mekanism Multiblocks&r in JEI: casing walls, valves, a layer of pressure dispersers, and elements on the bottom."
		"&eTip:&r a sodium-cooled fission reactor sends heated sodium here instead of boiling water itself."
	]
	quest.0909511F411FE352.title: "Turbine Internals"
	quest.0909511F411FE352.quest_subtitle: "Rotor, blades, coils, condensers"
	quest.0909511F411FE352.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the moving parts inside an Industrial Turbine. More blades and coils mean more power from the same steam."
		"&eChemistry:&r condensers turn spent steam back into water, so the loop reuses the same water over and over."
		"&eHow:&r stack rotors with two blades each on the centre column, a Rotational Complex on top, then coils and condensers above. See Just Enough Mekanism Multiblocks."
		"&eTip:&r the turbine's GUI shows whether steam flow or blade count is the limit."
	]
	quest.579284C06EF69B84.title: "Building the Fusion Reactor"
	quest.579284C06EF69B84.quest_subtitle: "Frame, glass, ports and a laser window"
	quest.579284C06EF69B84.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the shell of the Fusion Reactor: frames, reactor glass, ports for fuel and output, and a Laser Focus Matrix to let the ignition laser in."
		"&eHow:&r the 3D layout is in &eJust Enough Mekanism Multiblocks&r in JEI. The controller sits on top in the middle."
		"&eTip:&r ports switch between input and output with a Configurator."
	]
	quest.34E5D064EB957947.title: "Ignition"
	quest.34E5D064EB957947.quest_subtitle: "A laser hot enough to start a star"
	quest.34E5D064EB957947.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r lasers charge a Laser Amplifier, which fires a single huge pulse into the reactor to ignite it."
		"&eChemistry:&r deuterium and tritium only fuse above about 100 million °C, when the nuclei move fast enough to beat their electric repulsion."
		"&eHow:&r put a filled Hohlraum in the controller, aim the amplifier at the Laser Focus Matrix and fire it with a redstone signal. Then go to the Fusion quest."
		"&eTip:&r once lit, the reactor sustains itself as long as fuel keeps coming."
	]
	quest.736DB4279A53E093.title: "CNC Machines"
	quest.736DB4279A53E093.quest_subtitle: "More Machine: stamp, turn and roll"
	quest.736DB4279A53E093.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism: More Machine adds CNC machines: the Stamper presses plates, the Lathe turns rods, the Rolling Mill rolls wire."
		"&eHow:&r the CNC Stamper needs Basic Control Circuits, Basic Alloy, pistons and a steel casing. The Lathe also needs a Robit (check JEI). Any one counts."
		"&eTip:&r MI's machines make most plates already. Use CNC machines for the mod recipes that list them in JEI (the stamper also prints AE2 processors)."
	]
	quest.3E4C4D79C59C0844.title: "Recycler"
	quest.3E4C4D79C59C0844.quest_subtitle: "Stone and dirt into scrap"
	quest.3E4C4D79C59C0844.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Recycler grinds cheap blocks (stone, dirt, substrate) and sometimes leaves Scrap."
		"&eHow:&r a Crusher, Advanced Control Circuits (MV), Infused Alloy and osmium (check JEI). About 1 stone in 6 gives a scrap."
		"&eTip:&r 64 scrap compress into a Scrap Box, the first step towards UU-Matter. Start stockpiling early."
	]
	quest.1F12D14D184FBA11.title: "Presser"
	quest.1F12D14D184FBA11.quest_subtitle: "An upgraded stamper"
	quest.1F12D14D184FBA11.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Presser builds on the CNC Stamper and makes processors and other pressed parts (check JEI for its recipes)."
		"&eHow:&r a CNC Stamper with Elite Control Circuits (HV), Reinforced Alloy and pistons."
	]
	quest.40D85A929DD5607F.title: "Planting Station"
	quest.40D85A929DD5607F.quest_subtitle: "Grow crops in a box"
	quest.40D85A929DD5607F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a machine that grows seeds and saplings indoors and outputs the harvest."
		"&eChemistry:&r photosynthesis: 6CO₂ + 6H₂O → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂, here powered by electricity instead of sunlight."
		"&eHow:&r Elite Control Circuits (HV), Reinforced Alloy, bio fuel and a steel casing (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.140BB9D1CBB0F759.title: "Large Machines"
	quest.140BB9D1CBB0F759.quest_subtitle: "Big single-block versions"
	quest.140BB9D1CBB0F759.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r More Machine's large machines do the work of many normal ones, such as the Large Electrolytic Separator or Large Chemical Infuser."
		"&eHow:&r most need a Robit, steel blocks and ultimate-tier tanks or circuits (EV). Any one counts; check JEI for each."
		"&eTip:&r the Large Solar Neutron Activator is a big help for polonium and tritium."
	]
	quest.6CC2DEC317329165.title: "Ambient Gas Collector"
	quest.6CC2DEC317329165.quest_subtitle: "Pull gas out of thin air"
	quest.6CC2DEC317329165.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a machine that collects gas from its surroundings (check JEI and its GUI for what it gathers)."
		"&eChemistry:&r real air is 78% N₂, 21% O₂ and 1% argon; industry separates it by cooling it into a liquid and distilling it."
		"&eHow:&r Atomic Alloy, an osmium block, an ultimate chemical tank and ultimate tubes (EV)."
	]
	quest.5947F763AB2801F8.title: "UU-Matter"
	quest.5947F763AB2801F8.quest_subtitle: "Matter from antimatter"
	quest.5947F763AB2801F8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Scrap, crystal, antimatter, and then anything. You remember when making matter was just a thought.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r UU-Matter is More Machine's universal matter. The Replicator turns it back into items."
		"&eHow:&r scrap boxes become Empty Crystals in the PRC (with fusion fuel and a special gas, check JEI). 64 crystals + antimatter in the Antiprotonic Nucleosynthesizer (an optional t7 quest) make one UU-Matter."
		"&eTip:&r the Replicator needs Ultimate Control Circuits and Atomic Alloy. Check JEI for what it can copy."
	]
	quest.31BB98406EA4EDD2.title: "A Small Tribute"
	quest.31BB98406EA4EDD2.quest_subtitle: "Secret: the author, in doll form"
	quest.31BB98406EA4EDD2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a doll of More Machine's author, compressed out of 64 UU-Matter and a breath of antimatter in the Osmium Compressor."
		"&eTip:&r the mod's modeller has a doll too, made from UU-Matter gas instead. Thank you, modders."
	]
	quest.5E8F3647B73A0992.title: "Radiance"
	quest.5E8F3647B73A0992.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism Extras begins"
	quest.5E8F3647B73A0992.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism Extras adds four tiers beyond ultimate: absolute, supreme, cosmic and infinite. Each needs a new alloy, starting with Radiance."
		"&eHow:&r Osmium Compressor: glowstone dust + uranium oxide gas → Radiance Dust. Enrich it, then infuse Atomic Alloy with radiance (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r uranium oxide comes from oxidising yellowcake in the Chemical Oxidizer."
	]
	quest.6C057847340B18C8.title: "Absolute Control Circuit"
	quest.6C057847340B18C8.quest_subtitle: "Tier five"
	quest.6C057847340B18C8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the first Extras circuit: an Ultimate Control Circuit between two Radiance Alloys."
		"&eHow:&r craft it, or infuse an ultimate circuit with radiance in the Metallurgic Infuser."
		"&eTip:&r absolute factories, cubes and tanks all start here."
	]
	quest.62708C199FD0F204.title: "Supreme Control Circuit"
	quest.62708C199FD0F204.quest_subtitle: "Thermonuclear alloy"
	quest.62708C199FD0F204.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tier six. Its alloy is Thermonuclear: Radiance Alloy infused with thermonuclear material."
		"&eHow:&r enriched radiance reacts with lava and molten thermonuclear in the PRC (check JEI for the full chain)."
		"&eTip:&r the circuit is an Absolute Control Circuit between two Thermonuclear Alloys."
	]
	quest.271EF9B3ECA8898F.title: "Cosmic Control Circuit"
	quest.271EF9B3ECA8898F.quest_subtitle: "Shining alloy, made with antimatter"
	quest.271EF9B3ECA8898F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tier seven. Its alloy, Shining, needs enriched thermonuclear transmuted with antimatter."
		"&eHow:&r Antiprotonic Nucleosynthesizer: enriched thermonuclear + antimatter → enriched shining. Then infuse Thermonuclear Alloy with it (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.412F542BFE77DA7C.title: "Infinite Control Circuit"
	quest.412F542BFE77DA7C.quest_subtitle: "The last tier"
	quest.412F542BFE77DA7C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Infinite, the circuit says. You remember when that word described you.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r tier eight, the top of Mekanism Extras. Its alloy is Spectrum."
		"&eHow:&r Osmium Compressor: enriched shining + antimatter → enriched spectrum; infuse Shining Alloy with it, then craft the circuit (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.20AADC7F057BBBD9.title: "Absolute Factory"
	quest.20AADC7F057BBBD9.quest_subtitle: "Factories beyond ultimate"
	quest.20AADC7F057BBBD9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Extras factories have more slots than ultimate ones, and Extras adds factory types base Mekanism lacks (oxidizing, washing, crystallizing, centrifuging...)."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade an ultimate factory with Absolute Control Circuits and Radiance Alloy, or use an Absolute Tier Installer. Any absolute factory counts."
	]
	quest.76F42EC41A7A87E6.title: "Naquadah"
	quest.76F42EC41A7A87E6.quest_subtitle: "A metal from science fiction"
	quest.76F42EC41A7A87E6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Naquadah ore, added by Mekanism Extras. It is the fuel for the Naquadah Reactor."
		"&eChemistry:&r naquadah is not real; it comes from the Stargate films. Every other material on this page is real chemistry."
		"&eHow:&r Naquadah ore generates underground and in the End. Jade shows the block name when you look at it."
		"&eTip:&r it processes like other Mekanism ores: dissolve, wash and crystallise for the best yield."
	]
	quest.472EF62A30C14D95.title: "Naquadah Reactor"
	quest.472EF62A30C14D95.quest_subtitle: "A fusion reactor on fictional fuel"
	quest.472EF62A30C14D95.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a fusion-style power multiblock from Mekanism Extras that runs on naquadah-based fuel."
		"&eHow:&r casings are lead blocks transmuted with antimatter in the Nucleosynthesizer; the controller needs Cosmic Control Circuits. Layout: Just Enough Mekanism Multiblocks."
		"&eTip:&r the fuel chain starts with fluorinated naquadah-uranium fuel. Check JEI for each step."
	]
	chapter.1C6E26542D7508E5.title: "Power"
	chapter.1C6E26542D7508E5.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Energy is chemistry too: combustion, gas burning, fission and fusion."
	]
	quest.664799749DFCE0E4.title: "First FE"
	quest.664799749DFCE0E4.quest_subtitle: "Burn something, get power"
	quest.664799749DFCE0E4.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember holding lightning. For now, a box that burns coal will do.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Generator Galore's generators burn fuel for FE (Forge Energy), the power most mods share."
		"&eChemistry:&r burning is oxidation: C + O₂ → CO₂ releases the energy stored in carbon's bonds."
		"&eHow:&r feed it coal or charcoal and connect a cable or put a machine next to it."
		"&eTip:&r this chapter is a side path. Pick the power lines that suit your base."
	]
	quest.75F490C611174982.title: "A Faster Burn"
	quest.75F490C611174982.quest_subtitle: "Same fuel, more FE per tick"
	quest.75F490C611174982.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the next Generator Galore tier: it burns fuel faster and makes more FE per tick."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade from the iron generator (check JEI for the recipe)."
		"&eTip:&r a faster burn needs a steadier fuel supply. Pipe in charcoal from a tree farm."
	]
	quest.3F4B647DA140B71A.title: "Generator Collector"
	quest.3F4B647DA140B71A.quest_subtitle: "Four odd ways to make FE"
	quest.3F4B647DA140B71A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a diamond-tier generator plus three that burn strange fuels."
		"&eHow:&r each one's tooltip and JEI page show what it burns. The Halitosis Generator wants dragon's breath, so plan an End trip."
		"&eTip:&r the Culinary Generator eats spare food. Hook it to a farm's overflow."
	]
	quest.4104964F0EF1348C.title: "Bio Fuel"
	quest.4104964F0EF1348C.quest_subtitle: "Crops into power"
	quest.4104964F0EF1348C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism's Bio-Generator burns Bio Fuel."
		"&eChemistry:&r plants store sunlight as sugars and cellulose. Burning them releases it, and the CO₂ is the same CO₂ the plant took in."
		"&eHow:&r crush seeds and crops into Bio Fuel in a Mekanism Crusher."
	]
	quest.30A2E65738B8AE03.title: "Burning Hydrogen"
	quest.30A2E65738B8AE03.quest_subtitle: "The cleanest combustion there is"
	quest.30A2E65738B8AE03.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Gas-Burning Generator turns flammable gas into FE."
		"&eChemistry:&r 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O + energy. The only exhaust is water."
		"&eHow:&r pipe hydrogen from your Electrolytic Separator in with pressurized tubes."
		"&eTip:&r electrolysis costs more energy than burning hydrogen returns. Use it to store spare power, not to make it."
	]
	quest.36381170B678DBC6.title: "Diesel Generators"
	quest.36381170B678DBC6.quest_subtitle: "Petrochemical power"
	quest.36381170B678DBC6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI generators that burn the fuels from your distillation tower."
		"&eChemistry:&r diesel is a mix of hydrocarbons around C₁₂ to C₂₀. Long chains pack lots of C-H bonds, and lots of energy."
		"&eHow:&r pipe diesel into the generator and cable it to your machines."
	]
	quest.39B5DB6B48A4B6D7.title: "Large Diesel Generator"
	quest.39B5DB6B48A4B6D7.quest_subtitle: "Factory-scale combustion"
	quest.39B5DB6B48A4B6D7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a multiblock diesel generator for real factories."
		"&eHow:&r the 3D layout is in JEI and the MI guidebook. It needs fluid input and energy output hatches."
		"&eTip:&r refined fuels (like boosted diesel) burn for more EU per bucket. Check JEI."
	]
	quest.1EDE182DE2183A9C.title: "Heat Generator"
	quest.1EDE182DE2183A9C.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism's starter generator"
	quest.1EDE182DE2183A9C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism's first generator. It burns fuel and turns heat into FE."
		"&eHow:&r place lava next to it for a passive bonus, and feed it fuel for more."
		"&eTip:&r lava from a pump makes this a decent passive generator early on."
	]
	quest.63E2812122315EC2.title: "Store It"
	quest.63E2812122315EC2.quest_subtitle: "A buffer for your grid"
	quest.63E2812122315EC2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r energy cubes hold FE so short spikes don't stall your machines."
		"&eHow:&r put one between your generators and machines. Configure its sides with the Configurator."
		"&eTip:&r cubes upgrade in place: craft the next tier around the old one."
	]
	quest.70651DDC383EDB77.title: "Bigger Cubes"
	quest.70651DDC383EDB77.quest_subtitle: "Each tier needs the matching circuit"
	quest.70651DDC383EDB77.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Advanced Energy Cube holds and moves much more energy."
		"&eHow:&r it needs an Advanced Control Circuit, which in this pack needs an &eMI electronic circuit&r (MV)."
		"&eTip:&r Elite and Ultimate cubes follow the HV and EV circuits."
	]
	quest.44993050A3DC3B80.title: "Evaporation Ponds"
	quest.44993050A3DC3B80.quest_subtitle: "Sunlight and heat concentrate brine"
	quest.44993050A3DC3B80.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Thermal Evaporation Plant boils water down into brine, and brine down into liquid lithium."
		"&eChemistry:&r real lithium comes from salt flats: brine sits in ponds until the water evaporates and the salts concentrate."
		"&eHow:&r a multiblock tower of Thermal Evaporation Blocks, Valves and one Controller. See Just Enough Mekanism Multiblocks in JEI."
		"&eTip:&r taller towers and more heat run faster. Feed it plain water."
	]
	quest.02BB51B61A42F1E1.title: "Lithium"
	quest.02BB51B61A42F1E1.quest_subtitle: "The battery metal"
	quest.02BB51B61A42F1E1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r lithium dust, for induction cells (and later, tritium)."
		"&eChemistry:&r lithium is the lightest metal and gives up its electron easily, which is why lithium-ion batteries store so much energy for their weight."
		"&eHow:&r run brine through the plant again for liquid lithium. Turn it into gas in a Rotary Condensentrator, then crystallise it in a Chemical Crystallizer."
		"&eTip:&r check JEI with &eR&r on Lithium Dust to confirm each step."
	]
	quest.54C26C329300A347.title: "Induction Matrix"
	quest.54C26C329300A347.quest_subtitle: "One multiblock battery for the whole base"
	quest.54C26C329300A347.quest_desc: [
		"&6Power stored, waiting, obedient. This feels familiar.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a hollow multiblock battery. Cells inside set how much it stores; providers set how fast it charges and discharges."
		"&eHow:&r casings form the shell (Structural Glass works for the walls), ports move energy in and out. Layout: Just Enough Mekanism Multiblocks."
		"&eTip:&r switch one port to output with the Configurator. Start small; you can rebuild it larger later."
	]
	quest.392C4F4FA0F31627.title: "Wireless Grid"
	quest.392C4F4FA0F31627.quest_subtitle: "Power anywhere, no cables"
	quest.392C4F4FA0F31627.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Flux Networks sends power through the air: Plugs take it in, Points give it out, Storage buffers it."
		"&eHow:&r the Flux Core needs an &eMI processing unit&r (EV) in this pack. Link all devices to one network in their GUI."
		"&eTip:&r put a Flux Plug on your induction matrix's output port and every Point on the network draws from it."
	]
	quest.109BC5571612DD61.title: "EU Storage"
	quest.109BC5571612DD61.quest_subtitle: "A battery for MI's grid"
	quest.109BC5571612DD61.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI's storage unit holds EU, Modern Industrialization's electricity."
		"&eHow:&r built from redstone batteries, battery alloy plates and an LV hull. Put it between your turbine and your machines."
		"&eTip:&r a buffer lets your steam turbine keep running while machines are idle."
	]
	quest.1E551EC24D7B07BE.title: "MV Steam Turbine"
	quest.1E551EC24D7B07BE.quest_subtitle: "More steam, more EU"
	quest.1E551EC24D7B07BE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a bigger steam turbine that outputs MV power."
		"&eChemistry:&r a turbine converts the energy of hot, expanding steam into rotation, then a generator turns rotation into current."
		"&eHow:&r assemble it from an MV hull, aluminum rotors and large motors (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.18E2BC4078D46255.title: "Transformers"
	quest.18E2BC4078D46255.quest_subtitle: "Step voltage between tiers"
	quest.18E2BC4078D46255.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a transformer moves energy between two neighbouring voltage tiers (LV and MV here)."
		"&eHow:&r place it between an MV cable and your LV machines (or the other way round). Check which face is which in its tooltip."
		"&eTip:&r real grids do the same: high voltage for transmission, low voltage at the socket."
	]
	quest.1C5484680D3A8FE8.title: "HV Steam Turbine"
	quest.1C5484680D3A8FE8.quest_subtitle: "High-voltage steam"
	quest.1C5484680D3A8FE8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the HV steam turbine, for HV machine lines."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the recipe. Feed it from a large boiler."
		"&eTip:&r more steam than one turbine can eat? Add a second turbine on the same steam line."
	]
	quest.16133057CBACFAE4.title: "Large Steam Turbine"
	quest.16133057CBACFAE4.quest_subtitle: "Power-station scale"
	quest.16133057CBACFAE4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI's multiblock steam turbine. It eats steam by the thousands of mB and makes serious EU."
		"&eHow:&r the controller needs an HV steam turbine, a processing unit (EV) and a highly advanced hull. Layout: JEI or the MI guidebook."
		"&eTip:&r pair it with a large boiler or a reactor's steam output."
	]
	quest.61169F0AFAA00D90.title: "Energized Steel"
	quest.61169F0AFAA00D90.quest_subtitle: "Iron and gold, charged together"
	quest.61169F0AFAA00D90.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Powah's basic alloy, made by the Energizing Orb."
		"&eHow:&r place Energizing Rods aimed at the orb and power them. Put 1 iron + 1 gold in the orb for 2 Energized Steel."
		"&eTip:&r more rods (and better rods) charge faster."
	]
	quest.0D7A0B7F7ED74F1F.title: "Powah Energy Cells"
	quest.0D7A0B7F7ED74F1F.quest_subtitle: "Stack your storage"
	quest.0D7A0B7F7ED74F1F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Powah's energy storage block, with tiers from Starter to Nitro."
		"&eHow:&r iron, a dielectric casing and Powah capacitors. Higher tiers use better capacitors and crystals (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r cells pass power through each other, so a wall of them makes one big buffer."
	]
	quest.582ADD5540E1751B.title: "Thermo Generator"
	quest.582ADD5540E1751B.quest_subtitle: "Power from a temperature difference"
	quest.582ADD5540E1751B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a generator that needs a hot block underneath and a coolant fed in."
		"&eChemistry:&r thermoelectric plates make current from a temperature difference (the Seebeck effect). Hotter below and colder inside means more power."
		"&eHow:&r place it on lava or magma and pipe water in."
	]
	quest.354774525777C4A9.title: "Powah Reactor"
	quest.354774525777C4A9.quest_subtitle: "Uraninite-fuelled multiblock"
	quest.354774525777C4A9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a multiblock reactor fuelled by the uraninite you oxidised yourself."
		"&eChemistry:&r uraninite is UO₂. Its uranium releases heat as it fissions; the reactor turns that heat into FE."
		"&eHow:&r place the reactor blocks in a stack and they form one reactor (check JEI). Feed it uraninite."
		"&eTip:&r fuel, temperature and coolant all show in its GUI. Watch the temperature as you scale up."
	]
	quest.5C6AD7D248FE5B0F.title: "Photovoltaics"
	quest.5C6AD7D248FE5B0F.quest_subtitle: "Light straight into electricity"
	quest.5C6AD7D248FE5B0F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r solar panels from Mekanism and Powah."
		"&eChemistry:&r silicon solar cells use a p-n junction: a photon knocks an electron loose and the junction pushes it into a current."
		"&eHow:&r place them under open sky. They stop at night and slow in rain."
		"&eTip:&r pair solar with an energy cube to cover the night."
	]
	quest.687502F33B0ACF31.title: "Advanced Solar"
	quest.687502F33B0ACF31.quest_subtitle: "A bigger array"
	quest.687502F33B0ACF31.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism's Advanced Solar Generator, a larger array with much more output."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the recipe. Give it space: it's bigger than one block."
		"&eTip:&r like the basic panel, it only works in daylight. Buffer it with a cube."
	]
	quest.6CA4A3D8E8BB9BE6.title: "Wind Power"
	quest.6CA4A3D8E8BB9BE6.quest_subtitle: "Build it high"
	quest.6CA4A3D8E8BB9BE6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism's Wind Generator. It works day and night."
		"&eHow:&r it makes more power the higher it's placed. Build it on a mountain or a tall tower."
		"&eTip:&r it needs open space around it, so leave room."
	]
	quest.09A503304C6EC280.title: "Reactor Safety"
	quest.09A503304C6EC280.quest_subtitle: "Build the off-switch first"
	quest.09A503304C6EC280.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Logic Adapters let redstone read the reactor and switch it off."
		"&eChemistry:&r a fission reactor makes heat by splitting heavy nuclei. If heat can't escape fast enough, the reactor takes damage; at 100% it melts down."
		"&eHow:&r set one adapter to emit a signal on damage or high temperature (pick the mode in its GUI) and wire it to another in Activation mode."
		"&eTip:&r start at a low burn rate (0.1 mB/t), keep coolant flowing, and drain waste and heated coolant constantly."
	]
	quest.0A9EE595B44C9104.title: "Industrial Turbine"
	quest.0A9EE595B44C9104.quest_subtitle: "Steam into enormous power"
	quest.0A9EE595B44C9104.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism's multiblock turbine. Feed it steam from fission or a boiler and it makes huge amounts of FE."
		"&eHow:&r casings, valves, vents, rotors with blades, a rotational complex, a pressure disperser and electromagnetic coils. Layout: Just Enough Mekanism Multiblocks."
		"&eTip:&r a Saturating Condenser turns spent steam back into water, closing the loop."
	]
	quest.3CE4B1A7FBAD8566.title: "D-T Fuel"
	quest.3CE4B1A7FBAD8566.quest_subtitle: "Deuterium and tritium"
	quest.3CE4B1A7FBAD8566.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fusion fuel: deuterium and tritium, the two heavy isotopes of hydrogen."
		"&eChemistry:&r deuterium comes from heavy water (D₂O). Tritium is bred from lithium by neutrons: ⁶Li + n → ³H + ⁴He."
		"&eHow:&r electrolyse heavy water for deuterium; put lithium in the Solar Neutron Activator for tritium. Combine them into D-T fuel in the Chemical Infuser, then fill a Hohlraum with it (a chemical tank's item slot works; see its tooltip)."
		"&eTip:&r heavy water comes from a Mekanism Electric Pump with a Filter Upgrade."
	]
	quest.2D19FF2F88C95DEA.title: "Fusion"
	quest.2D19FF2F88C95DEA.quest_subtitle: "The power of a star"
	quest.2D19FF2F88C95DEA.quest_desc: [
		"&6The power of a star, in a box you built. This is what you were.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism's fusion reactor, the top of the power tree."
		"&eChemistry:&r D + T → ⁴He + n + 17.6 MeV, millions of times more energy per kilogram than any chemical reaction."
		"&eHow:&r a filled Hohlraum in the controller, then a burst from a Laser through a Laser Amplifier to ignite it. Layout: Just Enough Mekanism Multiblocks."
	]
	quest.42A8C9D5A8EBF106.title: "Upgrade in Place"
	quest.42A8C9D5A8EBF106.quest_subtitle: "Optional: upgrade a generator without breaking it"
	quest.42A8C9D5A8EBF106.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Generators Galore upgrade kits turn a placed generator into the next tier, keeping its fuel and connections."
		"&eHow:&r gold ingots, an item frame and a redstone block for iron → gold (check JEI for the others). Right-click the placed generator."
		"&eTip:&r the tree branches: gold leads to diamond or to the food-burning Culinary Generator."
	]
	quest.491B66EA7719A9CD.title: "Eight Times the Burn"
	quest.491B66EA7719A9CD.quest_subtitle: "Optional: compressed generators"
	quest.491B66EA7719A9CD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 8x generators burn fuel eight times as fast and make eight times the FE in one block."
		"&eHow:&r eight generators of a tier around an echo shard (check JEI). Echo shards come from Ancient City chests."
		"&eTip:&r a 64x version exists too, for when space matters more than echo shards."
	]
	quest.0316471653C2202B.title: "Burning a Star"
	quest.0316471653C2202B.quest_subtitle: "Secret: fuel fit for a god"
	quest.0316471653C2202B.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember lighting stars. Burning one feels like a waste, and also like coming home.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Nether Star Generator burns Nether Stars for an enormous amount of FE."
		"&eChemistry:&r real stars run on fusion: hydrogen nuclei fuse into helium (4 ¹H → ⁴He) and a little mass becomes a lot of energy, E = mc²."
	]
	quest.394211D5B3DB95C1.title: "Blazing Crystals"
	quest.394211D5B3DB95C1.quest_subtitle: "Powah's second tier: energized blaze"
	quest.394211D5B3DB95C1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every Powah tier is built from a crystal made in the Energizing Orb. Blazing crystals unlock the blazing tier of cells, generators and cables."
		"&eHow:&r energize a blaze rod (or four blaze powder) with 120,000 FE. Then craft blazing-tier parts (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r feed the energizing rods from your biggest power source; crystals charge faster with more rods."
	]
	quest.5540CD98C595C363.title: "Niotic Crystals"
	quest.5540CD98C595C363.quest_subtitle: "Energized diamond"
	quest.5540CD98C595C363.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the niotic tier. Reactors and generators get much stronger."
		"&eChemistry:&r diamond is pure carbon in a rigid lattice where every atom bonds to four others. Pumping energy into it is Powah's magic, but diamond really does conduct heat better than any metal."
		"&eHow:&r energize a diamond with 300,000 FE (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.7972888C428AA464.title: "Spirited Crystals"
	quest.7972888C428AA464.quest_subtitle: "Energized emerald"
	quest.7972888C428AA464.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the spirited tier, one step below the top."
		"&eChemistry:&r emerald is the mineral beryl, Be₃Al₂Si₆O₁₈. A trace of chromium (Cr³⁺) replacing some aluminum gives it its green colour."
		"&eHow:&r energize an emerald with 1,000,000 FE (check JEI). A villager trading hall pays off here."
	]
	quest.34546079D90320A3.title: "Nitro Crystals"
	quest.34546079D90320A3.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Powah's top tier"
	quest.34546079D90320A3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r nitro crystals build the strongest Powah reactors and cells."
		"&eHow:&r energize a Nether Star, two redstone blocks and a blazing crystal block with 20,000,000 FE. One craft makes sixteen."
		"&eTip:&r save your Nether Stars for this; the Wither is the only reliable source (check JEI for a Hostile Neural Networks wither model)."
	]
	quest.30316683DE199107.title: "Ender Power"
	quest.30316683DE199107.quest_subtitle: "Optional: wireless Powah energy"
	quest.30316683DE199107.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Ender Cells share one energy pool across your base; the Player Transmitter charges the items in your inventory."
		"&eHow:&r both need an Ender Core (an eye of ender, dielectric casing and a tiny capacitor, energized). Check JEI, and link them with a Binding Card."
		"&eTip:&r a player transmitter keeps jetpacks and the MekaSuit charged while you work."
	]
	quest.17B72E750B2DA75E.title: "Herculean Storage"
	quest.17B72E750B2DA75E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a much bigger flux battery"
	quest.17B72E750B2DA75E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Herculean (and then Gargantuan) Flux Storage holds far more energy in one block, shared with the whole flux network."
		"&eHow:&r Basic Flux Storage blocks around glass panes (check JEI). Gargantuan is the same with Herculean blocks."
		"&eTip:&r flux storage keeps its energy when broken, so you can carry charged batteries to a new base."
	]
	quest.59B570AD2FBBC34F.title: "Flux Controller"
	quest.59B570AD2FBBC34F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: charge yourself from the network"
	quest.59B570AD2FBBC34F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Flux Controller sends network energy wirelessly into players' inventories. The Configurator copies settings between flux devices."
		"&eHow:&r flux blocks, a Flux Core and flux dust (check JEI). The Flux Core needs an MI processing unit in this pack."
		"&eTip:&r turn charging off for your armor slots if it fights with other chargers."
	]
	chapter.64C69CCA641352A4.title: "Mob Data and Big Crafting"
	chapter.64C69CCA641352A4.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Monifactory-inspired machinery: simulate mobs, craft on giant tables, and fold whole factories into a block."
	]
	quest.0C506EBC53C1DABE.title: "Deep Learning"
	quest.0C506EBC53C1DABE.quest_subtitle: "Teach a model by fighting"
	quest.0C506EBC53C1DABE.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember knowing every creature by name. You can learn them again, one fight at a time.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Hostile Neural Networks records mobs into data models. Trained models later make mob drops without the mob."
		"&eHow:&r craft the Deep Learner and a Blank Data Model (check JEI). Put models in the Deep Learner and keep it in your inventory while you fight."
		"&eTip:&r start with a mob whose drops you'll need in bulk, like blazes, slimes or endermen."
	]
	quest.0B5ACE02A3EC167D.title: "Your First Model"
	quest.0B5ACE02A3EC167D.quest_subtitle: "Attune a blank model to one mob"
	quest.0B5ACE02A3EC167D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a data model attuned to one mob type. It starts at Faulty and levels up as you kill that mob."
		"&eHow:&r right-click a mob with a Blank Data Model, or craft a specific model (check JEI). Then hunt with the Deep Learner."
		"&eTip:&r tiers go Faulty, Basic, Advanced, Superior, Self Aware. Higher tiers are more accurate, so fewer simulations fail."
	]
	quest.288F7BE90AC49D6E.title: "Simulation"
	quest.288F7BE90AC49D6E.quest_subtitle: "Mob drops from power and matrices"
	quest.288F7BE90AC49D6E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Simulation Chamber runs a trained model on FE and prediction matrices to make predictions and mob drops."
		"&eHow:&r it needs an &eMV electronic circuit&r (aluminum chemistry). Insert a model of Basic tier or better, matrices and power."
		"&eTip:&r pipe matrices in and drops out; one chamber per model keeps things simple."
	]
	quest.22C8C82E50C1150C.title: "Loot Fabricator"
	quest.22C8C82E50C1150C.quest_subtitle: "Choose exactly which drop you want"
	quest.22C8C82E50C1150C.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember making things appear from nothing. This is the mortal version: data, power and patience.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r turns predictions into the specific drop you pick (blaze rods, ender pearls, slime balls and more)."
		"&eHow:&r also needs an MV electronic circuit. Feed it predictions from the chamber and select the output in its GUI."
		"&eTip:&r simulated blazes are a cheap blaze-rod source for Silent Gear alloys and brewing."
	]
	quest.1A724AEF16C690EB.title: "Self Aware"
	quest.1A724AEF16C690EB.quest_subtitle: "Optional: max out a data model"
	quest.1A724AEF16C690EB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r train one data model all the way to Self Aware, the top tier."
		"&eHow:&r keep killing that mob with the model in your Deep Learner, or let the Simulation Chamber train it. Click the checkmark when you've done it."
		"&eTip:&r a Self Aware model almost never fails a simulation."
	]
	quest.5A0AEB733FEC4D65.title: "Twilight Predictions"
	quest.5A0AEB733FEC4D65.quest_subtitle: "Optional: simulate Twilight Forest mobs"
	quest.5A0AEB733FEC4D65.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Twilight Forest mobs give their own prediction type."
		"&eHow:&r train a model on a Twilight mob and run it in the Simulation Chamber."
		"&eTip:&r the Loot Fabricator shows which drops each prediction can become."
	]
	quest.661102C7F987E7BD.title: "Black Iron Parts"
	quest.661102C7F987E7BD.quest_subtitle: "Slates, components and catalysts"
	quest.661102C7F987E7BD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Extended Crafting tables are built from black iron slates plus a component and a catalyst of matching tier."
		"&eHow:&r black iron ingot = iron ingot + black dye (shapeless). Two ingots make a slate. A component takes a slate, luminessence (glowstone, redstone, gunpowder) and iron; four components ring a black iron ingot for the catalyst."
		"&eTip:&r make extra black iron; every table tier and the Crafting Core need more."
	]
	quest.3D513F09267F082E.title: "Extended Crafting"
	quest.3D513F09267F082E.quest_subtitle: "The 3x3 table that starts the ladder"
	quest.3D513F09267F082E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Basic Table is a 3x3 table for Extended Crafting recipes, and the base of every bigger table."
		"&eHow:&r black iron slate, basic component and catalyst, an iron block and a crafting table."
		"&eTip:&r each bigger table is crafted from the one before it, so don't use this one up as decoration."
	]
	quest.3E2B8FDB3778E49B.title: "5x5: Advanced Table"
	quest.3E2B8FDB3778E49B.quest_subtitle: "Needs an MV electronic circuit"
	quest.3E2B8FDB3778E49B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a 5x5 crafting grid for mid-game recipes."
		"&eChemistry:&r its &eMI electronic circuit&r rests on aluminum, won by electrolysis of alumina: 2Al₂O₃ → 4Al + 3O₂."
		"&eHow:&r the Basic Table, gold blocks, advanced component and catalyst, plus the electronic circuit (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.00ED2FDA05907C7A.title: "7x7: Elite Table"
	quest.00ED2FDA05907C7A.quest_subtitle: "Needs an HV digital circuit"
	quest.00ED2FDA05907C7A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a 7x7 grid. Crystaltine and many late parts are crafted here."
		"&eChemistry:&r the &eMI digital circuit&r needs polyethylene, chains of ethylene (C₂H₄) from cracking oil."
		"&eHow:&r the Advanced Table, diamond blocks, elite component and catalyst, plus the digital circuit."
	]
	quest.2C2ECADD0D0886BB.title: "9x9: Ultimate Table"
	quest.2C2ECADD0D0886BB.quest_subtitle: "Needs an EV processing unit"
	quest.2C2ECADD0D0886BB.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember building worlds on a table far bigger than this. Nine by nine will do for now.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the endgame's biggest crafts happen here, including the Seed of a New World."
		"&eChemistry:&r the &eMI processing unit&r needs PVC: polyvinyl chloride, (C₂H₃Cl)ₙ, made from ethylene and chlorine."
		"&eHow:&r the Elite Table, emerald blocks, ultimate component and catalyst, plus the processing unit."
	]
	quest.71D7CC7520B500C0.title: "Packaged Automation"
	quest.71D7CC7520B500C0.quest_subtitle: "Let AE2 run the big tables for you"
	quest.71D7CC7520B500C0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Packaged Auto lets AE2 autocraft with Extended Crafting tables, through the PackagedExCrafting addon."
		"&eHow:&r encode recipes in the Encoder, then set up a Packager, a PackagedExCrafting crafter and an Unpackager by your ME network (tooltips and JEI explain each block)."
		"&eTip:&r one setup per table size handles every recipe of that size."
	]
	quest.2F7699EA87878993.title: "Ender Crafting"
	quest.2F7699EA87878993.quest_subtitle: "Optional: slow crafting, no hands needed"
	quest.2F7699EA87878993.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Ender Crafter finishes its recipes over time, faster with more Ender Alternators nearby."
		"&eHow:&r ender ingots (iron + ender pearl), eyes of ender and a crafting table (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a ring of alternators around the crafter speeds it up a lot."
	]
	quest.02B9BEBA903C3462.title: "Combination Crafting"
	quest.02B9BEBA903C3462.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a core ringed by pedestals"
	quest.02B9BEBA903C3462.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r put the main item on the Crafting Core and the extras on Pedestals around it. The core uses FE to fuse them."
		"&eHow:&r elite components and catalysts, a frame and black iron (check JEI). JEI shows every combination recipe."
		"&eTip:&r pipe FE into the core; it won't start without power."
	]
	quest.495A4A8AF596B3DD.title: "Crystaltine"
	quest.495A4A8AF596B3DD.quest_subtitle: "Optional: diamond, lapis and a Nether Star"
	quest.495A4A8AF596B3DD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a late crafting metal made on the Elite Table."
		"&eChemistry:&r lapis lazuli's blue comes from lazurite, a sodium aluminosilicate with trapped sulfur ions (S₃⁻)."
		"&eHow:&r diamonds, lapis, iron, gold and a Nether Star in a 7x4 pattern (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.37FE5B7240F8C222.title: "Compact Machines"
	quest.37FE5B7240F8C222.quest_subtitle: "A whole factory inside one block"
	quest.37FE5B7240F8C222.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fold an entire factory into a single block. The Personal Shrinking Device lets you walk inside it."
		"&eHow:&r shrinking and enlarging modules, an eye of ender, copper, iron and glass panes (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r it also shows you which machine room you're in and takes you back out."
	]
	quest.72183CBF18D24594.title: "Machine Walls"
	quest.72183CBF18D24594.quest_subtitle: "Polished deepslate, made compact"
	quest.72183CBF18D24594.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Compact Machine Walls frame every machine block."
		"&eHow:&r crafted from polished deepslate (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r inside a room the walls are unbreakable; these crafted ones aren't."
	]
	quest.5D5BD30841DCCD95.title: "Atom Modules"
	quest.5D5BD30841DCCD95.quest_subtitle: "One shrinks, one enlarges"
	quest.5D5BD30841DCCD95.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every Compact Machine needs one Atom Shrinking Module and one Atom Enlarging Module."
		"&eHow:&r an eye of ender, a light pressure plate, a stone button and a piston (sticky for shrinking)."
		"&eTip:&r make spares; each new machine eats a pair."
	]
	quest.3BEE4D083DB28729.title: "Step Inside"
	quest.3BEE4D083DB28729.quest_subtitle: "Craft a machine and shrink into it"
	quest.3BEE4D083DB28729.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember holding a world in your palm. This one is smaller, but it's yours.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r craft a Compact Machine, place it, and right-click it with the Personal Shrinking Device to enter its room."
		"&eHow:&r walls + both modules + a metal sets the size: copper = tiny, iron = small, gold = normal, obsidian = giant, netherite = colossal (check JEI for the rest)."
		"&eTip:&r tunnels carry items, fluids and power through the walls; perfect for a compact chemical line."
	]
	quest.194624A9FFBFAE06.title: "Hide the Cables"
	quest.194624A9FFBFAE06.quest_subtitle: "Cables that look like any block"
	quest.194624A9FFBFAE06.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Cable Facades disguise cables and pipes as any block. Tidy factories, same throughput."
		"&eHow:&r craft the Facade Wrench, then apply blocks to cables (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r facades on MI pipes make chemical lines much easier to look at."
	]
	quest.37B1429C3FDEB817.title: "Teleporting Cake"
	quest.37B1429C3FDEB817.quest_subtitle: "Eat a slice, change dimension"
	quest.37B1429C3FDEB817.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r TelePastries cakes teleport you to their dimension when you eat a slice."
		"&eHow:&r the Overworld Cake brings you home. Refill it with saplings; the Nether Cake takes obsidian."
		"&eTip:&r place the Overworld Cake in your Nether hub for a quick ride home."
	]
	quest.38748839E062F987.title: "Cake at the End"
	quest.38748839E062F987.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a slice to the End"
	quest.38748839E062F987.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a cake that sends you to the End."
		"&eHow:&r a cake surrounded by eyes of ender. Refill it with eyes of ender."
		"&eTip:&r leave it in your base so the End is one bite away."
	]
	quest.0E4DA225CB5833A9.title: "Training Data: Blazes"
	quest.0E4DA225CB5833A9.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 30 blazes with a model loaded"
	quest.0E4DA225CB5833A9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every kill with a matching model in your Deep Learner adds data. Blaze models are worth it: blaze rods feed brewing, Powah and Create's Blaze Burners."
		"&eHow:&r put a blaze data model in the Deep Learner, keep it in your inventory, and hunt blazes at a Nether Fortress."
		"&eTip:&r a blaze model at a high tier turns the Simulation Chamber into an endless rod farm."
	]
	quest.0D49817F333BA253.title: "Training Data: Endermen"
	quest.0D49817F333BA253.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 30 endermen with a model loaded"
	quest.0D49817F333BA253.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ender pearls go into Entangled blocks, AE2 seeds, Powah ender cells and teleporting. An enderman model makes them renewable."
		"&eHow:&r load an enderman data model and hunt them at night, in warped forests, or in the End."
		"&eTip:&r wear a carved pumpkin, or look at their feet, so they don't attack you first."
	]
	quest.3A9ADF5D85159EB7.title: "Three Worlds of Data"
	quest.3A9ADF5D85159EB7.quest_subtitle: "Optional: predictions from every dimension"
	quest.3A9ADF5D85159EB7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each simulation gives a prediction for the mob's home dimension as well as the drop. Overworld, Nether and End predictions are used in recipes and Fabrication Directives."
		"&eHow:&r run simulations of one mob from each dimension, such as a zombie, a blaze and an enderman."
		"&eTip:&r predictions stack up fast; send them to storage with a pipe."
	]
	quest.1A6BD466759A0E1E.title: "The Data Center"
	quest.1A6BD466759A0E1E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: 25 simulations at once"
	quest.1A6BD466759A0E1E.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember watching a million lives at once. This is a pale copy, but a useful one.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Data Center runs up to 25 Self Aware data models at the same time, each making one drop per cycle."
		"&eHow:&r a Sim Chamber, a Loot Fabricator, a Nether Star, echo shards and obsidian. Build a 7x7x7 hollow shell: obsidian floor, black stained glass walls and ceiling, with the controller in a bottom wall facing out (JEI shows the rules)."
		"&eTip:&r IO ports in the shell let pipes feed inputs and pull the drops. A Fabrication Directive picks which drop each slot makes."
	]
	quest.23CCCA1395225BEC.title: "Flux Crafting"
	quest.23CCCA1395225BEC.quest_subtitle: "Optional: crafting powered by FE"
	quest.23CCCA1395225BEC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Flux Crafter runs special recipes using FE delivered by nearby Flux Alternators, like the Flux Star."
		"&eHow:&r gold and redstone ingots (check JEI). Place alternators around the crafter and power them."
		"&eTip:&r JEI's Flux Crafter tab lists every recipe and the FE each one needs."
	]
	quest.383A333C4DD0B8D7.title: "Auto Tables"
	quest.383A333C4DD0B8D7.quest_subtitle: "Optional: tables that craft by themselves"
	quest.383A333C4DD0B8D7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Auto Tables remember a recipe and craft it with FE whenever the ingredients are inside. Each table size has its own."
		"&eHow:&r a crafting table of the same size plus crystaltine components (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the Ultimate Auto Table is also the heart of Packaged ExCrafting's Ultimate Crafter (see the Applied Energistics page)."
	]
	quest.6A7C8CD52FF53CDB.title: "A Room for Every Line"
	quest.6A7C8CD52FF53CDB.quest_subtitle: "Optional: four compact machines"
	quest.6A7C8CD52FF53CDB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one compact machine per chemical line keeps your base tidy: a sulfuric acid room, a chlorine room, a petrochemical room."
		"&eHow:&r craft more machines (check JEI for the sizes) and enter each with the Personal Shrinking Device."
		"&eTip:&r a room only runs while the chunk with its machine block is loaded, so claim and force-load your factory."
	]
	chapter.6A576761B258CEBA.title: "Automation and Logic"
	chapter.6A576761B258CEBA.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Make the factory run itself."
	]
	quest.140C58A0A3A11DB7.title: "A Computer"
	quest.140C58A0A3A11DB7.quest_subtitle: "Lua, in a box"
	quest.140C58A0A3A11DB7.quest_desc: [
		"&6You never did your own chores. You remember having things that did them for you.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r CC: Tweaked computers run Lua programs: monitor tanks, balance chemical lines, build a base dashboard."
		"&eHow:&r place it and right-click. Type &ehelp&r, or &eedit startup&r to write a program that runs on boot."
		"&eTip:&r Mekanism machines can be read by computers directly. Put a computer next to one and try &eperipheral.getNames()&r."
	]
	quest.5860D80382B926CC.title: "Monitors"
	quest.5860D80382B926CC.quest_subtitle: "A screen for your numbers"
	quest.5860D80382B926CC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r monitors show program output on a wall. Placed together, they join into one big screen."
		"&eHow:&r put monitors next to the computer and run &emonitor <side> <program>&r to send output to them."
		"&eTip:&r advanced monitors show colour and accept clicks, so you can make touch buttons."
	]
	quest.1DC5FA34C818F32E.title: "Wired Networks"
	quest.1DC5FA34C818F32E.quest_subtitle: "Reach machines across the room"
	quest.1DC5FA34C818F32E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r wired modems and networking cable connect a computer to machines that aren't touching it."
		"&eHow:&r put a modem on the machine, run cable back to a modem on the computer, and right-click the machine's modem to attach it."
		"&eTip:&r each attached peripheral gets a name. List them with &eperipheral.getNames()&r."
	]
	quest.67691356C2B16C8D.title: "Ender Modem"
	quest.67691356C2B16C8D.quest_subtitle: "Talk across dimensions"
	quest.67691356C2B16C8D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Ender Modem sends messages with no range limit, even between dimensions. A pocket computer carries a terminal with you."
		"&eHow:&r use &erednet&r on both ends: one computer broadcasts tank levels, your pocket computer reads them."
		"&eTip:&r a remote alarm for your reactor is a very good idea."
	]
	quest.5B44262E5F932D07.title: "Turtles"
	quest.5B44262E5F932D07.quest_subtitle: "Robots you program"
	quest.5B44262E5F932D07.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r turtles are programmable robots that mine, build and farm."
		"&eHow:&r craft one with a tool (a pickaxe makes a mining turtle) and fuel it with coal."
		"&eTip:&r try the built-in &eexcavate&r and &etunnel&r programs first."
	]
	quest.02AEF5F6A8349814.title: "Advanced Peripherals"
	quest.02AEF5F6A8349814.quest_subtitle: "Read power flow and your ME network"
	quest.02AEF5F6A8349814.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r extra peripherals: the Energy Detector measures power flow; the ME Bridge reads (and requests crafts from) your whole AE2 network."
		"&eHow:&r place them on your wired network like any other peripheral."
		"&eTip:&r an ME Bridge program can keep your stock of every intermediate topped up."
	]
	quest.34D7444D271541A3.title: "Base Dashboard"
	quest.34D7444D271541A3.quest_subtitle: "Every tank on one screen"
	quest.34D7444D271541A3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a wall screen that shows your chemical stocks, power and flow rates at a glance."
		"&eHow:&r the Fluid Detector measures flow through a pipe. Combine it with tank readings and the energy detector in one program."
		"&eTip:&r colour lines red when a tank drops below 20%. You'll spot problems from across the room."
	]
	quest.6192AD314EA01958.title: "Buses"
	quest.6192AD314EA01958.quest_subtitle: "AE2 pulls, pushes and reads"
	quest.6192AD314EA01958.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an import bus pulls items out of a machine, an export bus pushes them in, and a storage bus lets ME see inside a chest or tank."
		"&eHow:&r place them on cable facing the machine. Set filters in each bus's GUI."
		"&eTip:&r Applied Mekanistics is in the pack, so buses and storage also handle Mekanism gases like hydrogen and SO₂."
	]
	quest.573035DFFD4A529E.title: "Crafting CPU"
	quest.573035DFFD4A529E.quest_subtitle: "The part of AE2 that plans"
	quest.573035DFFD4A529E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a crafting CPU is a multiblock that works out and tracks autocrafting jobs."
		"&eHow:&r build a solid box of crafting units with at least one crafting storage, and connect it to your network."
		"&eTip:&r more storage lets it plan bigger jobs; co-processing units run more steps at once."
	]
	quest.43797C9ECEA77DF3.title: "Encoding Patterns"
	quest.43797C9ECEA77DF3.quest_subtitle: "Teach AE2 a recipe"
	quest.43797C9ECEA77DF3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a pattern is a recipe card: these inputs make that output."
		"&eHow:&r in the Pattern Encoding Terminal, switch to Processing mode for machine recipes and fill in the inputs and outputs."
		"&eTip:&r processing patterns work for any machine: MI, Mekanism or the Combiner."
	]
	quest.21A977445D70545D.title: "Autocraft a Chemical Line"
	quest.21A977445D70545D.quest_subtitle: "Pattern providers drive your machines"
	quest.21A977445D70545D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r pattern providers push ingredients into machines; molecular assemblers do crafting-table recipes."
		"&eHow:&r put a provider against an MI or Mekanism machine, load a processing pattern, and send the output back into the network."
		"&eTip:&r chain patterns (sulfur → SO₂ → SO₃ → H₂SO₄) and one request runs the whole line."
	]
	quest.3FEB19A4A1E0D8A4.title: "Level Emitters"
	quest.3FEB19A4A1E0D8A4.quest_subtitle: "Stop at enough"
	quest.3FEB19A4A1E0D8A4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a level emitter gives a redstone signal when the network holds more (or less) than a number you set."
		"&eHow:&r set the item and the amount, then wire the signal to a machine's redstone control."
		"&eTip:&r stop the Electrolytic Separator when hydrogen hits your target and you never waste power on a full tank."
	]
	quest.44221BA2292D178B.title: "Fully Automated Sulfuric Acid"
	quest.44221BA2292D178B.quest_subtitle: "Sulfur in, acid out, no hands"
	quest.44221BA2292D178B.quest_desc: [
		"&6The factory hums without you. You remember this kind of quiet.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a line that makes sulfuric acid on its own and stops when the tanks are full."
		"&eChemistry:&r 2SO₂ + O₂ → 2SO₃ (industry uses a vanadium oxide catalyst), then SO₃ + H₂O → H₂SO₄."
		"&eHow:&r Separator (O₂) → Oxidizer (S → SO₂) → Infuser (SO₃) → Rotary Condensentrator (water vapour) → Infuser (H₂SO₄). Feed sulfur with a bus or LaserIO and gate it with a level emitter."
		"&eTip:&r when it runs a full day with no help, fill 16 buckets and click the checkmark."
	]
	quest.27ED21A2DD1FDA38.title: "Menril Resin"
	quest.27ED21A2DD1FDA38.quest_subtitle: "The tree that grows logic"
	quest.27ED21A2DD1FDA38.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Integrated Dynamics builds everything from crystallised Menril, a resin from Menril trees."
		"&eChemistry:&r drying resin is just evaporation: the liquid loses its solvent and hardens, like tree sap turning into amber."
		"&eHow:&r squeeze Menril logs in a Squeezer for resin, then dry the resin in a Drying Basin."
		"&eTip:&r Menril trees grow wild in the Overworld. Plant the saplings once you find one."
	]
	quest.00C7FF03D1B02894.title: "Integrated Dynamics"
	quest.00C7FF03D1B02894.quest_subtitle: "Logic networks without code"
	quest.00C7FF03D1B02894.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r read a value (tank level, item count), apply logic, and act on it, all with blocks and cards."
		"&eHow:&r a Reader part (e.g. Fluid Reader) on a tank exposes values. Write one onto a Variable Card in the Logic Programmer."
		"&eTip:&r a Redstone Writer can then turn that value into a signal: perfect for stopping a separator when its tank is full."
	]
	quest.0B6B6A7EEDAF93D8.title: "Variable Store"
	quest.0B6B6A7EEDAF93D8.quest_subtitle: "Keep and name your logic"
	quest.0B6B6A7EEDAF93D8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Variable Store holds variable cards so the whole network can use them; the Labeller names them."
		"&eHow:&r put cards in the store and reference them from any writer or display panel on the network."
		"&eTip:&r name cards after what they measure ('H2 tank %'). You'll thank yourself later."
	]
	quest.00A54A06239849EA.title: "Challenge: The Self-Stopping Separator"
	quest.00A54A06239849EA.quest_subtitle: "Your first closed loop"
	quest.00A54A06239849EA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r make a Mekanism Electrolytic Separator turn itself off when its hydrogen tank is 90% full, and back on below 50%."
		"&eHow:&r a Reader on the tank → a comparison in the Logic Programmer → a Redstone Writer on the separator (set it to redstone control in its GUI)."
		"&eTip:&r the gap between 50% and 90% (hysteresis) stops it flickering on and off."
		"Click the checkmark once it works."
	]
	quest.34D0F3A6001E73F8.title: "Super Factory Manager"
	quest.34D0F3A6001E73F8.quest_subtitle: "One block scripts the whole factory"
	quest.34D0F3A6001E73F8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one Manager block runs a short program that moves items, fluids and energy between everything on its cables."
		"&eHow:&r put the disk in the Manager and write a program, e.g. &eEVERY 20 TICKS DO INPUT FROM a OUTPUT TO b END&r."
		"&eTip:&r the in-game editor has examples. Start with one input and one output."
	]
	quest.6DFD0C0EE913BF88.title: "Labels"
	quest.6DFD0C0EE913BF88.quest_subtitle: "Name every machine"
	quest.6DFD0C0EE913BF88.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Label Gun tags inventories with names (like &ea&r and &eb&r above) for your programs."
		"&eHow:&r set a label in the gun, then right-click each machine. The Network Tool shows what's connected."
		"&eTip:&r label by job ('sulfur_in', 'acid_out'), not by machine type."
	]
	quest.0239845B19FBECF7.title: "Logistics Network"
	quest.0239845B19FBECF7.quest_subtitle: "Nodes that route by rules"
	quest.0239845B19FBECF7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Logistics Network nodes move items between inventories according to rules you set."
		"&eHow:&r place nodes on the machines and set each node's direction and rules in its GUI (check JEI and the tooltips)."
		"&eTip:&r nodes are compact: good for tight spaces where cables won't fit."
	]
	quest.06ECD076BD8BC6DA.title: "Logistics Filters"
	quest.06ECD076BD8BC6DA.quest_subtitle: "Move only what you mean to"
	quest.06ECD076BD8BC6DA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r filters narrow what a node moves: by tag, by amount and more."
		"&eHow:&r put a filter in a node's slot and set it up in its GUI (check JEI for all the filter types)."
		"&eTip:&r a tag filter for 'c:dusts' sends every dust to one chest."
	]
	quest.408A259A993527E2.title: "LaserIO Cards"
	quest.408A259A993527E2.quest_subtitle: "Configure what each node moves"
	quest.408A259A993527E2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r cards tell each LaserIO node what to move and in which direction."
		"&eHow:&r put a card in a node's side slot. Set it to Extract on the source and Insert on the destination."
		"&eTip:&r right-click with a card in your hand to open its settings."
	]
	quest.441C3C6BBF44735C.title: "Fluids and Gases by Laser"
	quest.441C3C6BBF44735C.quest_subtitle: "Move acids without pipes"
	quest.441C3C6BBF44735C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fluid cards move liquids; chemical cards move Mekanism gases, like hydrogen and SO₂."
		"&eHow:&r same as item cards: Extract on the tank, Insert on the machine."
		"&eTip:&r one node can run several cards on one side. Hydrogen and oxygen out of one separator, two cards."
	]
	quest.6912F21E0B5211B5.title: "LaserIO Filters"
	quest.6912F21E0B5211B5.quest_subtitle: "Basic, tag and count filters"
	quest.6912F21E0B5211B5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r filters go inside cards. Basic matches a list, Tag matches a tag, Count keeps a set number in stock."
		"&eHow:&r put the filter in a card's filter slot and set it up."
		"&eTip:&r a count filter on an insert card keeps exactly 64 sulfur in the oxidizer and no more."
	]
	quest.43C31D71C7FEB6D8.title: "Overclocking"
	quest.43C31D71C7FEB6D8.quest_subtitle: "Faster lasers"
	quest.43C31D71C7FEB6D8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r overclockers make LaserIO move more, faster."
		"&eHow:&r overclocker cards go in a card's upgrade slot; overclocker nodes go in the node."
		"&eTip:&r most lines don't need it. Add it when a machine starves."
	]
	quest.5A5E16639EDFAC93.title: "Printers and Disks"
	quest.5A5E16639EDFAC93.quest_subtitle: "Optional: save programs, print lab notes"
	quest.5A5E16639EDFAC93.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Disk Drive lets you save programs on floppy disks and carry them between computers. A Printer prints text onto paper."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Put a disk in the drive and it appears as &edisk/&r in the computer's files."
		"&eTip:&r print a list of your reactions and their inputs and bind the pages into a book: a real lab notebook."
	]
	quest.6BDC8F1C446B5D65.title: "Advanced Turtle"
	quest.6BDC8F1C446B5D65.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a golden robot with a colour screen"
	quest.6BDC8F1C446B5D65.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r advanced turtles have colour screens and can be clicked, which makes menus easy."
		"&eHow:&r an advanced computer with gold instead of iron around it (check JEI). Give it a pickaxe to make a Mining Turtle."
		"&eTip:&r run &eexcavate 16&r on a mining turtle and it digs a 16x16 hole down to bedrock, bringing everything back."
	]
	quest.7D39CBFAE0AE3E52.title: "Geo Scanner"
	quest.7D39CBFAE0AE3E52.quest_subtitle: "Optional: find ores with a program"
	quest.7D39CBFAE0AE3E52.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Geo Scanner lists every block around it within a radius, including ores, for your computer to read."
		"&eChemistry:&r real geologists find ore bodies by measuring gravity, magnetism and how rocks conduct electricity, rather than digging blind."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Put it next to a computer (or in a pocket computer) and call &escan(8)&r."
		"&eTip:&r write a program that counts ore blocks by type: it's a quick way to check a deposit before setting up a mine."
	]
	quest.6CC389628C143887.title: "Chat Box and Player Detector"
	quest.6CC389628C143887.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a base that talks back"
	quest.6CC389628C143887.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Chat Box lets a computer send chat messages; the Player Detector tells it who is nearby."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Place them next to a computer."
		"&eTip:&r have the base warn everyone in chat when a tank of hydrogen is nearly full or an induction matrix is running low."
	]
	quest.41E9EE7CC03DE9F3.title: "Inventory Manager"
	quest.41E9EE7CC03DE9F3.quest_subtitle: "Optional: programs that use your inventory"
	quest.41E9EE7CC03DE9F3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Inventory Manager lets a computer move items into and out of your own inventory, once you bind it with a Memory Card."
		"&eHow:&r right-click the Memory Card to bind it to yourself, then put it in the manager (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a button that refills your hotbar with torches and food from storage is a classic first program."
	]
	quest.5B66E9C98951DF71.title: "Integrated Tunnels"
	quest.5B66E9C98951DF71.quest_subtitle: "Move items, fluids and energy with logic"
	quest.5B66E9C98951DF71.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Integrated Tunnels adds importer, exporter and interface parts for Integrated Dynamics cables: items, fluids and energy move along the network, controlled by variables."
		"&eHow:&r craft an Item Importer and an Item Exporter (check JEI), put them on cables at a chest and a machine, and give the exporter a variable card that says what to move. Click the checkmark when it works."
		"&eTip:&r a fluid exporter with a boolean variable from a tank reader only fills the reactor when it's below half."
	]
	quest.132AB0ACC55773F4.title: "Integrated Terminals"
	quest.132AB0ACC55773F4.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a storage terminal for ID networks"
	quest.132AB0ACC55773F4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Integrated Terminals adds a Storage Terminal part that shows everything connected to an Integrated Dynamics network, plus a portable version."
		"&eHow:&r a Storage Terminal part between two crystalized menril chunks makes the portable terminal (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the Crafting Job Terminal shows what Integrated Crafting is working on."
	]
	quest.698304026FBC82C1.title: "Integrated Crafting"
	quest.698304026FBC82C1.quest_subtitle: "Optional: autocrafting without AE2"
	quest.698304026FBC82C1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Integrated Crafting adds a Crafting Interface: give it recipe variables and it crafts on demand through the ID network, much like AE2 patterns."
		"&eHow:&r craft a Crafting Interface (check JEI), write recipes into variable cards with the Logic Programmer, and put them in the interface. Click the checkmark when one craft works."
		"&eTip:&r it's a cheaper autocrafter than AE2 for small chains, like rubber sheets or redstone batteries."
	]
	quest.648179C70EA53466.title: "Your First SFM Program"
	quest.648179C70EA53466.quest_subtitle: "Optional: four lines that move items"
	quest.648179C70EA53466.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Super Factory Manager runs small text programs written on a disk. Labels name the blocks it talks to."
		"&eHow:&r label a chest &ea&r and a furnace &eb&r with the Label Gun, then write this program on the disk and put it in the manager. Click the checkmark when items start moving."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eProgram:&r"
		"EVERY 20 TICKS DO"
		"    INPUT FROM a"
		"    OUTPUT TO b"
		"END"
		"&eTip:&r add a side, like &eOUTPUT TO b TOP SIDE&r, to choose which face of the block is used. The manager's built-in examples cover fluids and energy too."
	]
	chapter.4F72E72B760CB007.title: "The Mechanical Age"
	chapter.4F72E72B760CB007.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Create: rotation, presses and mixers. An early mechanical age that runs alongside steam and feeds into Modern Industrialization."
	]
	quest.026C969E02786C1B.title: "Andesite Alloy"
	quest.026C969E02786C1B.quest_subtitle: "The frame of every early machine"
	quest.026C969E02786C1B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Gears and shafts. You remember a world that ran on clockwork, and you liked it.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r andesite alloy, Create's first building material."
		"&eHow:&r craft andesite with iron nuggets (zinc nuggets work too). Later a Mechanical Mixer makes it in bulk."
		"&eTip:&r hold &eW&r over almost any Create block to watch its Ponder tutorial."
	]
	quest.4075A74B2774D3BD.title: "Andesite Casing"
	quest.4075A74B2774D3BD.quest_subtitle: "Alloy pressed onto wood"
	quest.4075A74B2774D3BD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r casing blocks are the shell for gearboxes, deployers and more."
		"&eHow:&r right-click a stripped log or stripped wood with andesite alloy. That's 'item application', and Create uses it a lot."
		"&eTip:&r strip logs with an axe first. Any wood type works."
	]
	quest.3B8CA867BEED2744.title: "Rotational Power"
	quest.3B8CA867BEED2744.quest_subtitle: "Create runs on rotation"
	quest.3B8CA867BEED2744.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Create runs on rotation, not electricity. A water wheel on flowing water turns shafts and cogs."
		"&eHow:&r water must flow across the wheel's blades. Shafts carry rotation straight; cogwheels pass it sideways."
		"&eTip:&r every machine costs stress units (SU). If the network is over capacity, everything stops."
	]
	quest.72C45775E3F11445.title: "Goggles and Wrench"
	quest.72C45775E3F11445.quest_subtitle: "See the stress"
	quest.72C45775E3F11445.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Engineer's Goggles show speed and stress when you look at a machine; the wrench rotates and picks up Create blocks."
		"&eHow:&r wear the goggles in your helmet slot and look at a shaft or generator."
		"&eTip:&r sneak-right-click with the wrench to pick a block up instantly."
	]
	quest.744DE466E8633CF3.title: "Windmills"
	quest.744DE466E8633CF3.quest_subtitle: "More stress capacity, anywhere"
	quest.744DE466E8633CF3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a windmill bearing with sails attached spins without water."
		"&eHow:&r place the bearing, build at least 8 sails onto the front of it (the Ponder shows how), and right-click the bearing."
		"&eTip:&r more sails means more stress capacity but slower speed. Check the numbers with your goggles."
	]
	quest.054CDC887B5F6350.title: "Create: Connected"
	quest.054CDC887B5F6350.quest_subtitle: "Handy kinetic parts"
	quest.054CDC887B5F6350.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Create: Connected adds small conveniences: compact gearboxes, a kinetic bridge that carries rotation across gaps, and more."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for everything the mod adds."
		"&eTip:&r the kinetic bridge saves long runs of shafts."
	]
	quest.7784CD3C06844B0C.title: "Create Deco"
	quest.7784CD3C06844B0C.quest_subtitle: "Make the factory look like one"
	quest.7784CD3C06844B0C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r catwalks, sheet metal, cage lamps and other industrial building blocks."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for Create Deco recipes. Many use a press or the stonecutter."
		"&eTip:&r catwalks over your machine lines make maintenance much easier."
	]
	quest.182C584F79A9026F.title: "Gearboxes and Belts"
	quest.182C584F79A9026F.quest_subtitle: "Move rotation and items"
	quest.182C584F79A9026F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r gearboxes turn rotation through corners; belts carry both rotation and items between two shafts."
		"&eHow:&r belts are made from dried kelp. Click one shaft with a belt, then the other, to link them."
		"&eTip:&r belts make great machine feeders: items ride past presses and fans on their own."
	]
	quest.1E78E7EE6A500B30.title: "Steam Engines"
	quest.1E78E7EE6A500B30.quest_subtitle: "Fire, water and pistons"
	quest.1E78E7EE6A500B30.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Create's boiler: a fluid tank full of water, heated by Blaze Burners, drives steam engines on its sides."
		"&eChemistry:&r water expands about 1,600 times when it boils. That pressure pushes the pistons."
		"&eHow:&r pump water into the tank, put fuelled Blaze Burners underneath, and place engines on its sides with a shaft in front. Check the Ponder."
		"&eTip:&r a bigger tank and more burners raise the boiler level. Goggles show what's limiting it."
	]
	quest.34342A28CCEA9E01.title: "Pressing and Mixing"
	quest.34342A28CCEA9E01.quest_subtitle: "Plates and compacting"
	quest.34342A28CCEA9E01.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Mechanical Press flattens ingots into plates and compacts items in a basin."
		"&eHow:&r put the press over a depot, a belt or a basin, and power it."
		"&eTip:&r plates are shared with MI in this pack, so pressed plates work in MI recipes too."
	]
	quest.6616482D84CB76CA.title: "Heated Mixing"
	quest.6616482D84CB76CA.quest_subtitle: "Create's chemistry bench"
	quest.6616482D84CB76CA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a mixer over a basin, heated by a Blaze Burner, makes alloys and fluids."
		"&eChemistry:&r heat speeds up reactions and melts metals so they can mix into alloys."
		"&eHow:&r catch a blaze in an Empty Blaze Burner, put it under the basin, feed it fuel, and put the mixer above."
		"&eTip:&r feed the burner with a deployer or a mechanical arm so it never goes cold."
	]
	quest.6629EEE3B93734E8.title: "Crushing"
	quest.6629EEE3B93734E8.quest_subtitle: "Ore into crushed ore"
	quest.6629EEE3B93734E8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r millstones and crushing wheels grind ore into crushed ore and stone into gravel and sand."
		"&eHow:&r two crushing wheels side by side, spinning toward each other. Drop items in from above."
		"&eTip:&r in this pack they give at most &e2x per ore block&r, like everything before acids."
	]
	quest.16A9DFC1FA028ABC.title: "Bulk Washing"
	quest.16A9DFC1FA028ABC.quest_subtitle: "Water, a fan and a bonus"
	quest.16A9DFC1FA028ABC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an encased fan blowing through water washes crushed ore into nuggets plus a byproduct."
		"&eHow:&r put flowing water in front of the fan and pass items through the air stream (a belt works)."
		"&eTip:&r washed crushed iron gives 9 nuggets and a 75% chance of redstone."
	]
	quest.37C0C525864C5286.title: "Rose Quartz"
	quest.37C0C525864C5286.quest_subtitle: "Quartz soaked in redstone"
	quest.37C0C525864C5286.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r rose quartz, for electron tubes."
		"&eHow:&r craft 1 Nether quartz with 8 redstone, then polish it: hold sandpaper with the rose quartz in your off-hand and use it (a deployer can do this too)."
		"&eTip:&r washing iron makes redstone, so your ore line can feed this."
	]
	quest.0182206067908BB0.title: "Electron Tubes"
	quest.0182206067908BB0.quest_subtitle: "Create's 'smart' component"
	quest.0182206067908BB0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r electron tubes go into deployers, mechanical crafters and other smart machines."
		"&eHow:&r polished rose quartz on top of an iron plate."
		"&eTip:&r make a stack. You'll need more than you think."
	]
	quest.77E50022B90D19F9.title: "Brass"
	quest.77E50022B90D19F9.quest_subtitle: "Copper plus zinc, mixed hot"
	quest.77E50022B90D19F9.quest_desc: [
		"&6A golden metal, mixed in a basin. The old skill comes back to your hands.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r brass, the key metal of Create's second age."
		"&eChemistry:&r brass is a copper-zinc alloy, usually about two-thirds copper. Zinc makes it harder and gives the gold colour."
		"&eHow:&r 1 copper + 1 zinc in a heated mixer gives 2 brass. Zinc ore generates in the world."
	]
	quest.1E61B3A6087F88B3.title: "Brass Casing"
	quest.1E61B3A6087F88B3.quest_subtitle: "The shell of smart machines"
	quest.1E61B3A6087F88B3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r brass casing, for mechanical crafters, arms and brass tunnels."
		"&eHow:&r right-click a stripped log or stripped wood with a brass ingot."
		"&eTip:&r a deployer holding brass ingots can apply it automatically."
	]
	quest.28E8E77EF5C671EB.title: "Deployers"
	quest.28E8E77EF5C671EB.quest_subtitle: "A hand that uses items"
	quest.28E8E77EF5C671EB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a deployer acts like a player's hand: it places, uses and applies items."
		"&eHow:&r an andesite casing, an electron tube and a brass hand (pressed brass sheets)."
		"&eTip:&r deployers over a belt are how Create builds things in steps: that's sequenced assembly."
	]
	quest.77FA7755F842A8D2.title: "Precision"
	quest.77FA7755F842A8D2.quest_subtitle: "Your first sequenced assembly"
	quest.77FA7755F842A8D2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Each step in its place, every time. You used to build worlds this way.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the precision mechanism, made by sequenced assembly: one item passes the same stations several times."
		"&eHow:&r start with a gold plate, then deploy a cogwheel, a large cogwheel and an iron nugget onto it, 5 loops. JEI shows the sequence."
		"&eTip:&r some outputs are scrap. Sort them off the end of the belt and recycle them."
	]
	quest.5191CA10F7F0E39F.title: "Mechanical Arm"
	quest.5191CA10F7F0E39F.quest_subtitle: "Pick up here, put down there"
	quest.5191CA10F7F0E39F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the mechanical arm moves items between depots, belts, basins and machines in its reach."
		"&eHow:&r hold the arm and click inputs and outputs before you place it. Check the Ponder."
		"&eTip:&r one arm can feed a whole ring of depots around it."
	]
	quest.79D324D3D42641AD.title: "Rotation to Electricity"
	quest.79D324D3D42641AD.quest_subtitle: "Spin a shaft, get FE"
	quest.79D324D3D42641AD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Crafts and Additions' Alternator turns rotation into FE."
		"&eChemistry:&r a coil turning in a magnetic field pushes electrons along the wire: electromagnetic induction."
		"&eHow:&r in this pack it needs an &eMI analog circuit&r (LV). Feed it fast rotation."
	]
	quest.2B4C4B280D8E7AC8.title: "Electricity to Rotation"
	quest.2B4C4B280D8E7AC8.quest_subtitle: "Run contraptions off the grid"
	quest.2B4C4B280D8E7AC8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Electric Motor turns FE back into rotation, with a speed you set."
		"&eHow:&r give it FE from your MI or Mekanism grid and set the speed in its GUI."
		"&eTip:&r motors free you from water wheels and windmills. Put a Create line anywhere."
	]
	quest.53AD12F81CBB1F0A.title: "Wires and Connectors"
	quest.53AD12F81CBB1F0A.quest_subtitle: "Overhead power lines"
	quest.53AD12F81CBB1F0A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Rolling Mill turns ingots into rods and plates into wire. Spools of wire link connectors into power lines."
		"&eHow:&r roll copper plates into wire, wind it onto a spool, then click two connectors with the spool to string a wire."
		"&eTip:&r connectors carry power over long gaps without cables on the ground."
	]
	quest.07D97B34A6E5B266.title: "Accumulators"
	quest.07D97B34A6E5B266.quest_subtitle: "Store FE in brass and capacitors"
	quest.07D97B34A6E5B266.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Modular Accumulator stores FE, and several placed together merge into one bigger battery."
		"&eChemistry:&r the capacitor here is zinc over copper, the same pair Volta used in the first battery in 1800."
		"&eHow:&r needs brass casing, capacitors, copper rods and electrum wire. Electrum is gold + silver mixed hot."
		"&eTip:&r put it between your alternators and your machines to smooth out spikes."
	]
	quest.4B937C395BAB0201.title: "Create: New Age"
	quest.4B937C395BAB0201.quest_subtitle: "Magnets, coils and energisers"
	quest.4B937C395BAB0201.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r magnet-and-coil generators, and Energisers that charge items with electricity."
		"&eHow:&r the Generator Coil needs an analog circuit in this pack. Spin it among magnets; the Ponder shows the layout."
		"&eTip:&r the Basic Energiser is just an andesite casing and a lightning rod."
	]
	quest.55B52C24164AD4E0.title: "Charging Metal"
	quest.55B52C24164AD4E0.quest_subtitle: "Iron soaked in electricity"
	quest.55B52C24164AD4E0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r overcharged iron, made by charging an iron ingot in an Energiser."
		"&eHow:&r power the Energiser with FE and put iron underneath it (on a depot or belt). Each ingot takes 1,000 FE."
		"&eTip:&r overcharged metals make better wire and magnets."
	]
	quest.24AA4CAED5C9CBF5.title: "Layered Magnets"
	quest.24AA4CAED5C9CBF5.quest_subtitle: "Stronger fields, more power"
	quest.24AA4CAED5C9CBF5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r stronger magnets for New Age generators."
		"&eHow:&r overcharged iron and overcharged gold in layers (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a stronger field induces more current in the same coil."
	]
	quest.4A4E6C320C2A7399.title: "Thorium Reactor"
	quest.4A4E6C320C2A7399.quest_subtitle: "New Age goes nuclear"
	quest.4A4E6C320C2A7399.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r New Age's nuclear reactor, fuelled by &ethorium&r."
		"&eChemistry:&r thorium-232 isn't fissile itself; it absorbs a neutron and becomes uranium-233, which is."
		"&eHow:&r the rods need an &eMI processing unit&r (EV), so it arrives alongside Mekanism fission. Check JEI and the Ponder for the build."
		"&eTip:&r treat it like any reactor: cooling first, then power."
	]
	quest.07E1E573A3B65309.title: "Liquid Experience"
	quest.07E1E573A3B65309.quest_subtitle: "XP you can pipe"
	quest.07E1E573A3B65309.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Enchantment Industry turns experience into a fluid you can store and pipe."
		"&eHow:&r the Mechanical Grindstone strips enchantments off items; a Grindstone Drain collects the XP as fluid. Check JEI."
		"&eTip:&r feed it the enchanted junk from your mob farm."
	]
	quest.22860F179A18DF0F.title: "Automated Enchanting"
	quest.22860F179A18DF0F.quest_subtitle: "A blaze that reads spellbooks"
	quest.22860F179A18DF0F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Blaze Enchanter spends liquid XP to enchant items automatically."
		"&eHow:&r it's a smithing upgrade of a Blaze Burner with an enchanting table (check JEI). Give it an enchanting template and XP."
		"&eTip:&r put it beside a belt and a deployer for a hands-free enchanting line."
	]
	quest.57619AFCA4F05DA0.title: "The Printer"
	quest.57619AFCA4F05DA0.quest_subtitle: "Copy books with XP"
	quest.57619AFCA4F05DA0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Printer copies written and enchanted books, paid for in liquid XP."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI and the Ponder for the setup."
		"&eTip:&r find a good enchanted book once, then print it as often as your XP lasts."
	]
	quest.20EF956BB16A02B8.title: "Kinetic Battery"
	quest.20EF956BB16A02B8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: store rotation for later"
	quest.20EF956BB16A02B8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Kinetic Battery charges from rotation and gives it back later, so a windmill's power isn't wasted when nothing is running."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI and its Ponder scene (hold W over it). Put it on a shaft line to charge it."
		"&eTip:&r a charged battery can be picked up and moved, like a wind-up spring."
	]
	quest.7DD9261D9EB35A40.title: "Bioethanol"
	quest.7DD9261D9EB35A40.quest_subtitle: "Optional: fuel from fermented plants"
	quest.7DD9261D9EB35A40.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Crafts & Additions makes liquid fuel from plants: seed oil, then biomass, then bioethanol, which burns in a Liquid Blaze Burner."
		"&eChemistry:&r real bioethanol comes from yeast fermenting sugar: C₆H₁₂O₆ → 2 C₂H₅OH + 2 CO₂. Plant oils are triglycerides, long carbon chains that store a lot of energy."
		"&eHow:&r compact seeds in a press and basin for seed oil; mix crops with seed oil over heat for biomass; mix biomass, sugar and cinder flour for bioethanol (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r it's a renewable fuel for Create steam engines that never touches your oil wells."
	]
	quest.24FF50E20F1EA5BC.title: "Tesla Coil"
	quest.24FF50E20F1EA5BC.quest_subtitle: "Optional: charge items with lightning"
	quest.24FF50E20F1EA5BC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Tesla Coil charges FE items on belts or depots below it, and zaps anything that walks under it."
		"&eHow:&r a mechanical crafting recipe with brass, a capacitor, electron tubes and a copper spool (check JEI). Power it with FE."
		"&eTip:&r put a belt of jetpacks or gadgets under it for an automatic charging station."
	]
	quest.4751D19651EF6413.title: "Heat Engines"
	quest.4751D19651EF6413.quest_subtitle: "Optional: rotation from sunlight and heat"
	quest.4751D19651EF6413.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r New Age moves heat through heat pipes. Solar heating plates collect it from sunlight; a Stirling Engine turns it into slow rotation, and a Boiler Heater uses it in place of a blaze burner."
		"&eChemistry:&r a real Stirling engine heats and cools a sealed gas. Hot gas expands and pushes a piston; cooled gas contracts and pulls it back. No fuel burns inside it."
		"&eHow:&r heat pipes, iron and glass for the plate; a copper block, heat pipes and a shaft for the engine (check JEI and the Ponder scenes)."
	]
	chapter.71E6C109F4D846B5.title: "Tools and Comfort"
	chapter.71E6C109F4D846B5.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Better tools from better materials, and a soft place to land."
	]
	quest.4ABA9DD08B8F9ACD.title: "Repair Kits"
	quest.4ABA9DD08B8F9ACD.quest_subtitle: "Mend your parts instead of throwing them away"
	quest.4ABA9DD08B8F9ACD.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember tools that never wore out. These will, but you can mend them.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Silent Gear tools don't break for good; at zero durability they just stop working until repaired."
		"&eHow:&r craft a Crude Repair Kit, load it with matching material, then combine it with the tool in a crafting grid."
		"&eTip:&r a better kit (Sturdy, then Crimson and Azure) holds more material and repairs more per use."
	]
	quest.7458CDD0AC00121E.title: "Blaze Gold"
	quest.7458CDD0AC00121E.quest_subtitle: "Gold, fired with blaze powder"
	quest.7458CDD0AC00121E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Silent Gear's first magic alloy. It's a key ingredient of the Material Grader and the Starlight Charger."
		"&eChemistry:&r gold (Au) is a noble metal: it barely reacts with anything, which is why it's found as native nuggets. Blaze gold is fictional; the blaze powder does the work."
		"&eHow:&r gold ingot + 2 blaze powder in the Alloy Forge, or check JEI for the early crafting route."
		"&eTip:&r keep a stack spare. Blaze gold blocks also go into the Starlight Charger."
	]
	quest.566563CC2C37BED0.title: "Material Grader"
	quest.566563CC2C37BED0.quest_subtitle: "Same metal, better grade, stronger part"
	quest.566563CC2C37BED0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r grades Silent Gear materials. A higher grade adds a stat bonus to every part made from that material."
		"&eHow:&r quartz, iron, blaze gold and an Advanced Upgrade Base (check JEI). Feed it materials plus a catalyst (check JEI for which items count)."
		"&eTip:&r grade only the materials you'll use for heads and main parts; rods and bindings matter less."
	]
	quest.7C6F13A70CB4F9FE.title: "Salvager"
	quest.7C6F13A70CB4F9FE.quest_subtitle: "Old tools back into parts"
	quest.7C6F13A70CB4F9FE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r breaks old Silent Gear tools back into parts, so upgrading doesn't waste materials."
		"&eHow:&r place it and drop in the old tool. Some material is lost on each salvage."
		"&eTip:&r salvage before you throw anything in lava; the parts often have most of their value left."
	]
	quest.2A06D8DD04609B9C.title: "Crimson Iron"
	quest.2A06D8DD04609B9C.quest_subtitle: "An ore that only grows in the Nether"
	quest.2A06D8DD04609B9C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r crimson iron ore generates in Nether biomes. It's the base of crimson steel and the Alloy Forge."
		"&eHow:&r mine crimson iron ore in the Nether (Jade shows the name), then smelt the raw ore."
		"&eTip:&r run a few through the Alchemistry Dissolver and see which real elements it gives back."
	]
	quest.4E659FFA072CD2C6.title: "Crimson Steel"
	quest.4E659FFA072CD2C6.quest_subtitle: "Crimson iron, blaze rods and magma cream"
	quest.4E659FFA072CD2C6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a tough, heat-loving alloy for tool heads and the Alloy Forge frame."
		"&eChemistry:&r real steel is iron with a little carbon (under about 2%); the carbon atoms jam the iron lattice so it can't slip. Crimson steel is the fictional cousin."
		"&eHow:&r the first ingots are a shaped craft (crimson iron, blaze rods, magma cream); check JEI."
	]
	quest.5C0C129959F2C62D.title: "The Alloy Forge"
	quest.5C0C129959F2C62D.quest_subtitle: "Silent Gear's alloy machine"
	quest.5C0C129959F2C62D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r mixes metals into Silent Gear alloys: blaze gold, crimson steel (3 per batch), azure electrum and tyrian steel."
		"&eHow:&r crimson steel ingots, blackstone and an iron block (check JEI). Fuel it like a furnace."
		"&eTip:&r alloying in the forge gives more ingots per batch than the crafting-table route."
	]
	quest.6628750FED7710A3.title: "Azure Electrum"
	quest.6628750FED7710A3.quest_subtitle: "Azure silver from the End, plus gold"
	quest.6628750FED7710A3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r azure silver ore generates in the End. Alloyed with gold it becomes azure electrum, a fast, enchantable metal."
		"&eChemistry:&r real electrum is a natural gold–silver alloy (Au–Ag); the ancient Lydians struck the first coins from it."
		"&eHow:&r Alloy Forge: an azure silver block, 2 gold ingots and an ender pearl."
	]
	quest.39DF5C695F1B32EB.title: "Tyrian Steel"
	quest.39DF5C695F1B32EB.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Silent Gear's finest metal"
	quest.39DF5C695F1B32EB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the top Silent Gear alloy: crimson steel, azure electrum, crushed shulker shell and netherite scrap."
		"&eChemistry:&r Tyrian purple was a real dye made from sea snails, once worth its weight in silver. The steel just borrowed the colour."
		"&eHow:&r Alloy Forge (check JEI). Crush shulker shells first."
	]
	quest.68908746B04D6B19.title: "Bronze Paxel"
	quest.68908746B04D6B19.quest_subtitle: "Pickaxe, axe and shovel in your first alloy"
	quest.68908746B04D6B19.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a paxel is a pickaxe, axe and shovel in one tool. Bronze is tougher than iron."
		"&eChemistry:&r bronze is copper with about 12% tin (Cu–Sn). Tin atoms stiffen copper's soft lattice."
		"&eHow:&r craft a bronze pickaxe, axe and shovel, then combine them with a stick (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.37DD31C8DF09C737.title: "Osmium Paxel"
	quest.37DD31C8DF09C737.quest_subtitle: "The densest natural element, as a tool"
	quest.37DD31C8DF09C737.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism's signature metal as a paxel: more durability and speed than bronze."
		"&eChemistry:&r osmium (Os) is the densest natural element at about 22.6 g/cm³, twice as dense as lead."
		"&eHow:&r osmium ore generates in the Overworld; smelt or process it, then craft the tools and combine."
	]
	quest.189C20032B2F64A2.title: "Diamond Paxel"
	quest.189C20032B2F64A2.quest_subtitle: "Carbon in its hardest form"
	quest.189C20032B2F64A2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the diamond paxel mines everything the diamond pickaxe can, in one slot."
		"&eChemistry:&r diamond is pure carbon with every atom bonded to four others in a rigid 3D lattice. Graphite is the same carbon in flat sheets."
		"&eHow:&r diamond pickaxe, axe and shovel plus a stick (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.1E48AB2B0066F565.title: "The Ultimate Paxel"
	quest.1E48AB2B0066F565.quest_subtitle: "Refined obsidian: Mekanism's toughest metal"
	quest.1E48AB2B0066F565.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember a hammer that could split mountains. This is a start.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r refined obsidian is Mekanism's toughest material, and its paxel is the best of the line."
		"&eHow:&r infuse obsidian dust with diamond in the Metallurgic Infuser, then press the refined obsidian dust in the Osmium Compressor (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the same ingots make the Atomic Disassembler and much of Mekanism's late gear."
	]
	quest.5D357E097AE9F6A0.title: "Steel Paxel"
	quest.5D357E097AE9F6A0.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a paxel from your blast furnace"
	quest.5D357E097AE9F6A0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a sidegrade to bronze, made from the steel you already produce."
		"&eChemistry:&r steel is iron with a little carbon from coke. Too much carbon (cast iron) makes it brittle."
		"&eHow:&r steel pickaxe, axe and shovel plus a stick (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.4E4AD4A8D6C2C30C.title: "Atomic Disassembler"
	quest.4E4AD4A8D6C2C30C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: an FE-powered everything-tool"
	quest.4E4AD4A8D6C2C30C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an electric tool that mines, chops and digs, with vein and area modes. It runs on FE instead of durability."
		"&eHow:&r refined obsidian, atomic alloy, infused alloy and an Energy Tablet (check JEI). Charge it in an energy cube."
		"&eTip:&r sneak + right-click to switch modes."
	]
	quest.42978372FCFCA164.title: "Bottled Oxygen"
	quest.42978372FCFCA164.quest_subtitle: "Breathe underwater on O₂ from your separator"
	quest.42978372FCFCA164.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Scuba Mask and Tank let you breathe underwater for as long as the tank has oxygen."
		"&eChemistry:&r the Electrolytic Separator splits water: 2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂. The O₂ fills the tank; the H₂ is fuel."
		"&eHow:&r steel, a control circuit and a chemical tank (check JEI). Fill the tank from a Chemical Tank or the separator's oxygen output."
		"&eTip:&r great for ocean monuments and underwater prospecting."
	]
	quest.1868DF8A24A0C2BA.title: "Free Runners"
	quest.1868DF8A24A0C2BA.quest_subtitle: "Step up blocks and never take fall damage"
	quest.1868DF8A24A0C2BA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r electric boots: auto step-up and no fall damage while charged."
		"&eHow:&r infused alloy, a basic control circuit and an Energy Tablet (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the armoured version adds protection; upgrade once you have more alloy."
	]
	quest.43D93D778FD7460F.title: "MekaSuit"
	quest.43D93D778FD7460F.quest_subtitle: "Polonium, HDPE and a netherite core"
	quest.43D93D778FD7460F.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember armour that was never armour, only certainty. This is the closest a mortal gets.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism's modular power armour. Add modules for flight, night vision, magnet, radiation shielding and more."
		"&eChemistry:&r it needs HDPE sheets (polyethylene: long C₂H₄ chains) and polonium pellets. Real ²¹⁰Po is made by hitting bismuth-209 with neutrons; Mekanism makes it from nuclear waste in the Solar Neutron Activator."
		"&eHow:&r netherite armour, HDPE sheets, ultimate control circuits, polonium pellets and induction cells (check JEI). Install modules in the Modification Station."
	]
	quest.172C8AEEBF9724DA.title: "Hazmat Gear"
	quest.172C8AEEBF9724DA.quest_subtitle: "Optional: lead against radiation"
	quest.172C8AEEBF9724DA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the full hazmat suit stops Mekanism radiation from building up in you. Cheap and worth having before fission."
		"&eChemistry:&r lead (Pb) is dense and has many electrons, so it absorbs gamma rays well."
		"&eHow:&r lead ingots and orange dye for each piece (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.18BB98D1C02BB648.title: "Hydrogen Jetpack"
	quest.18BB98D1C02BB648.quest_subtitle: "Optional: fly on the other half of water"
	quest.18BB98D1C02BB648.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mekanism's jetpack burns hydrogen gas. Short hops, not true flight."
		"&eChemistry:&r 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O. Burning hydrogen gives only water and a lot of energy."
		"&eHow:&r steel, tin, a basic control circuit and a chemical tank. Fill it with H₂ from the Electrolytic Separator."
	]
	quest.5E5F22E41BC4538A.title: "Jetpacks"
	quest.5E5F22E41BC4538A.quest_subtitle: "Electric flight, one coil at a time"
	quest.5E5F22E41BC4538A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Iron Jetpacks run on FE. Every tier needs a coil, and in this pack the coils need MI circuits."
		"&eHow:&r Basic coil = analog circuit (LV). Craft the coil, then cells, thrusters, strap and the jetpack for your metal (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r better metals fly faster and hold more FE. Charge it in any energy cube."
	]
	quest.5E3BA6083259F734.title: "Advanced Coil"
	quest.5E3BA6083259F734.quest_subtitle: "Optional: MV jetpacks"
	quest.5E3BA6083259F734.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r unlocks the middle jetpack tiers."
		"&eHow:&r needs an MI electronic circuit (MV, aluminum chemistry). Check JEI for which jetpacks use it."
		"&eTip:&r JEI shows which jetpacks use this coil."
	]
	quest.6EF99BBC489E3FBF.title: "Elite Coil"
	quest.6EF99BBC489E3FBF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: HV jetpacks"
	quest.6EF99BBC489E3FBF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r faster, longer flights."
		"&eHow:&r needs an MI digital circuit (HV, polyethylene)."
		"&eTip:&r the digital circuit is your polyethylene line paying off; make a few extra."
	]
	quest.1DAC0AE8A49D8F79.title: "Ultimate Coil"
	quest.1DAC0AE8A49D8F79.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the best jetpacks"
	quest.1DAC0AE8A49D8F79.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the top jetpack tier."
		"&eHow:&r needs an MI processing unit (EV, PVC chemistry)."
		"&eTip:&r by now the Angel Ring may suit you better; the jetpack still has the best speed."
	]
	quest.29E14CD67BE0BB33.title: "The Angel Ring"
	quest.29E14CD67BE0BB33.quest_subtitle: "Creative flight from a ring"
	quest.29E14CD67BE0BB33.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember the sky being yours. Now it is again.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r portable creative flight, no fuel, from a Curios ring slot."
		"&eChemistry:&r its &eMI digital circuit&r needs polyethylene: n C₂H₄ → (C₂H₄)ₙ, ethylene from your distillation tower."
		"&eHow:&r Elytra, ghast tears, diamond blocks and Nether Stars plus the digital circuit. Craft the Diamond Ring first, then the Angel Ring."
	]
	quest.1EA839D4E5BC136D.title: "Hammock"
	quest.1EA839D4E5BC136D.quest_subtitle: "Sleep through the day"
	quest.1EA839D4E5BC136D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r skips the day the way a sleeping bag skips the night, without moving your spawn."
		"&eHow:&r white wool, string and sticks. Hang it between two Rope and Nails placed on facing walls (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r useful when you want night-only mobs, like the ones a Deep Learner needs."
	]
	quest.1A44A497FCA1DF1C.title: "Warp Stone"
	quest.1A44A497FCA1DF1C.quest_subtitle: "Teleport to any waystone from anywhere"
	quest.1A44A497FCA1DF1C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Waystones (found in villages, or crafted) let you teleport between places you've visited. A Warp Stone works from anywhere."
		"&eHow:&r amethyst, ender pearls and emeralds (check JEI). Activate a waystone first by right-clicking it."
		"&eTip:&r it has a cooldown, so don't count on it in an emergency."
	]
	quest.3FEE458B9198CC55.title: "Tool Belt"
	quest.3FEE458B9198CC55.quest_subtitle: "Swap tools from your belt with one key"
	quest.3FEE458B9198CC55.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a belt worn in a Curios slot that holds tools and swaps them into your hand with a key."
		"&eHow:&r leather, string and an iron ingot. Add pouches for more slots."
		"&eTip:&r set the belt key in Controls. Great for paxel, sword, hoe and wrench."
	]
	quest.0359B6BBCD892545.title: "Mining Gadget"
	quest.0359B6BBCD892545.quest_subtitle: "A mining laser powered by FE"
	quest.0359B6BBCD892545.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a mining laser that breaks blocks at range. Upgrades add 3x3 (and bigger) size, efficiency, magnet and void filters."
		"&eHow:&r iron, gold, diamond and redstone (check JEI). Charge it with FE."
		"&eTip:&r a void filter for stone and dirt keeps your inventory clean on long ore runs."
	]
	quest.6B1EAD376672743D.title: "Bindings and Grips"
	quest.6B1EAD376672743D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: parts that change a tool's stats"
	quest.6B1EAD376672743D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r bindings and grips are optional Silent Gear parts. Each adds its material's traits and stats to the tool."
		"&eHow:&r make the Binding and Grip blueprints, then craft the parts from string, vines, leather or wool (check JEI). Add them to a tool in a crafting grid."
		"&eTip:&r the Material Book (or JEI) shows every material's traits. Hover a part to see what it adds."
	]
	quest.1109E5DB21C9B41E.title: "Coatings"
	quest.1109E5DB21C9B41E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: plate a tool in a better material"
	quest.1109E5DB21C9B41E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a coating covers a finished tool's main part in another material, like diamond or netherite, changing its stats and colour."
		"&eChemistry:&r real tools are coated too: drill bits get a thin layer of titanium nitride (TiN) or diamond to stay sharp much longer."
		"&eHow:&r craft the coating smithing template (check JEI), then apply the coating material at a smithing table."
	]
	quest.66CF5CE277F89ABA.title: "Silent Jewellery"
	quest.66CF5CE277F89ABA.quest_subtitle: "Optional: rings, bracelets and necklaces"
	quest.66CF5CE277F89ABA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Silent Gear jewellery carries material traits as curios: a ring of a lucky or magnetic material gives you that trait while worn."
		"&eHow:&r a ring shank, bracelet band or necklace chain plus a gem setting, made with the matching blueprint (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r try different metals and gems. The traits list on each material shows what jewellery will do."
	]
	quest.5FAAB59A05382846.title: "Armour from Parts"
	quest.5FAAB59A05382846.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a full set of Silent Gear armour"
	quest.5FAAB59A05382846.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Silent Gear armour is built from plates of any material, so your best alloy becomes your best armour."
		"&eHow:&r helmet, chestplate, legging and boot plates from their blueprints, then assemble each piece (check JEI). Any four pieces."
		"&eTip:&r crimson steel and azure electrum plates have strong traits; check the Material Book before choosing."
	]
	quest.02AA8F5B0AF7AF4F.title: "Primordial Goo"
	quest.02AA8F5B0AF7AF4F.quest_subtitle: "Just Dire Things: goo that changes blocks"
	quest.02AA8F5B0AF7AF4F.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember a slime that turned stone into anything you asked. This one is less clever, but it tries.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Just Dire Things goo converts the blocks it touches. Tier 1 goo turns an iron block into raw ferricore ore."
		"&eHow:&r clay, sugar, rotten flesh and dirt (check JEI). Place an iron block against the goo and wait (JEI shows how long)."
		"&eTip:&r JEI's goo tab shows every conversion and which goo tier it needs."
	]
	quest.402EC67BB19B609F.title: "Ferricore"
	quest.402EC67BB19B609F.quest_subtitle: "The first goo metal"
	quest.402EC67BB19B609F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ferricore is the first Just Dire Things metal: tools, the Pocket Generator, machines and upgrade blanks."
		"&eHow:&r mine the raw ferricore ore the goo makes and smelt it (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the Ferricore Wrench rotates and picks up JDT machines."
	]
	quest.370EC935014D4805.title: "Blazegold"
	quest.370EC935014D4805.quest_subtitle: "Tier 2 goo and a Nether metal"
	quest.370EC935014D4805.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tier 2 goo turns gold blocks into raw blazegold ore. Blazegold makes the next tier of JDT tools and machines."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade tier 1 goo with blaze powder, redstone and Nether wart (check JEI), then feed it gold blocks."
		"&eTip:&r goo only converts blocks touching it, so surround it with several gold blocks at once."
	]
	quest.43871B3E70259309.title: "Celestigem"
	quest.43871B3E70259309.quest_subtitle: "Optional: tier 3 goo and a gem from diamond"
	quest.43871B3E70259309.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tier 3 goo turns diamond blocks into celestigem ore. Celestigem tools take powerful upgrades."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade tier 2 goo with ender pearls, end stone and dragon's breath (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r JDT's flight upgrade needs End Crystals, so portable flight here comes after the End, as the pack intends."
	]
	quest.03A450539601C94E.title: "Eclipse Alloy"
	quest.03A450539601C94E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: tier 4 goo eats netherite"
	quest.03A450539601C94E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tier 4 goo turns netherite blocks into eclipse alloy ore, JDT's top material."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade tier 3 goo with sculk, a sculk shrieker and echo shards from an Ancient City (check JEI). Then sacrifice a netherite block."
		"&eTip:&r it's expensive. Decide which eclipse alloy tool you want before you start."
	]
	quest.0377341C1CFB93F6.title: "Pocket Generator"
	quest.0377341C1CFB93F6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: charge tools on the go"
	quest.0377341C1CFB93F6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Pocket Generator burns fuel in your inventory and charges your FE items."
		"&eHow:&r ferricore, a furnace, coal and a redstone block (check JEI)."
		"&eChemistry:&r burning coal is oxidation: C + O₂ → CO₂ releases about 394 kJ per mole of carbon as heat."
	]
	quest.1940B63A57F962D5.title: "Thinking with Portals"
	quest.1940B63A57F962D5.quest_subtitle: "Secret: now you're thinking"
	quest.1940B63A57F962D5.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember stepping between places without walking. You'd forgotten how much fun it was.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Portal Gun shoots two linked portals onto walls. Walk in one, come out the other."
		"&eTip:&r there is an upgraded Portal Gun too; JEI has its recipe."
	]
	chapter.34560F2FAB74139C.title: "Storage and Logistics"
	chapter.34560F2FAB74139C.chapter_subtitle: [
		"A god needs somewhere to keep things."
	]
	quest.44D2496540C5F6FE.title: "Sophisticated Barrel"
	quest.44D2496540C5F6FE.quest_subtitle: "Chests and barrels that grow with you"
	quest.44D2496540C5F6FE.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember vaults that held the stars. A barrel is humbler, but it's a start.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Sophisticated Storage chests and barrels take upgrades, just like your backpack. Sophisticated Storage Plus raises their limits."
		"&eHow:&r craft a wooden barrel (check JEI). Tier upgrades improve it in place later."
		"&eTip:&r barrels keep their contents when broken, so moving a full one is easy."
	]
	quest.4C812FEC12C477A4.title: "Tier Upgrades"
	quest.4C812FEC12C477A4.quest_subtitle: "More slots without emptying anything"
	quest.4C812FEC12C477A4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tier upgrades turn a placed chest or barrel into the next tier (copper, iron, gold, diamond, netherite) without moving items."
		"&eHow:&r craft the upgrade (check JEI) and right-click it on the placed container."
		"&eTip:&r you can skip tiers with the direct upgrades, like basic → iron."
	]
	quest.45772E69CBC7F59A.title: "Compacting"
	quest.45772E69CBC7F59A.quest_subtitle: "Nuggets to ingots to blocks, automatically"
	quest.45772E69CBC7F59A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Compacting Upgrade squeezes 9 nuggets into an ingot and 9 ingots into a block as items arrive."
		"&eChemistry:&r a block holds the same metal atoms as 9 ingots; only the packing changes, so no mass is lost either way."
		"&eHow:&r craft it (check JEI) and put it in an upgrade slot. Add a filter so it only compacts what you choose."
	]
	quest.4723957D49EEF36E.title: "Storage Controller"
	quest.4723957D49EEF36E.quest_subtitle: "Many containers, one inventory"
	quest.4723957D49EEF36E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Controller joins touching Sophisticated containers into one inventory; Storage Links extend its reach."
		"&eHow:&r place it next to your chests and barrels. Pipes into the controller reach every connected container."
		"&eTip:&r one pipe into the controller is a simple sorting system: items go where matching items already are."
	]
	quest.34606B92A3A6F57F.title: "Drawers"
	quest.34606B92A3A6F57F.quest_subtitle: "Huge stacks of one item each"
	quest.34606B92A3A6F57F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Functional Storage drawers hold lots of a single item and show it on the front."
		"&eHow:&r craft an oak drawer (1, 2 or 4 slots; check JEI). Right-click to insert, left-click to take."
		"&eTip:&r upgrades (copper, gold, diamond, netherite) multiply drawer capacity."
	]
	quest.21D03D3F9703DD77.title: "Compacting Drawer"
	quest.21D03D3F9703DD77.quest_subtitle: "One drawer, three sizes of the same metal"
	quest.21D03D3F9703DD77.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a compacting drawer stores nuggets, ingots and blocks of one metal as a single pool, and hands out whichever you ask for."
		"&eHow:&r craft it (check JEI), then insert the item you want to track."
		"&eTip:&r perfect for copper and tin near your bronze setup."
	]
	quest.129185B0D2C7C75A.title: "Drawer Controller"
	quest.129185B0D2C7C75A.quest_subtitle: "One face for every drawer"
	quest.129185B0D2C7C75A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Storage Controller links nearby drawers into one inventory you (and pipes) can use."
		"&eHow:&r place it among your drawers. Use the Linking Tool to add drawers further away."
		"&eTip:&r a Controller Extension gives you a second access point."
	]
	quest.73F96D08F9DD5275.title: "An Early Network"
	quest.73F96D08F9DD5275.quest_subtitle: "Tom's Simple Storage: one searchable terminal"
	quest.73F96D08F9DD5275.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Tom's Simple Storage connects your chests into one searchable terminal. It's your network until AE2."
		"&eHow:&r place an Inventory Connector touching your chests (or link them with Inventory Cables), and a Storage Terminal on it."
		"&eTip:&r point it at a drawer controller and every drawer shows up in the terminal."
	]
	quest.36279DAC568E66FC.title: "Crafting Terminal"
	quest.36279DAC568E66FC.quest_subtitle: "Optional: craft straight from storage"
	quest.36279DAC568E66FC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a terminal with a crafting grid that pulls ingredients from the network. JEI's + button fills it for you."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade a Storage Terminal (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a Wireless Terminal (also in JEI) lets you use it from across the base."
	]
	quest.28340CD18CB88A6E.title: "Faster Furnaces"
	quest.28340CD18CB88A6E.quest_subtitle: "Iron Furnaces smelt faster"
	quest.28340CD18CB88A6E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Iron Furnaces are faster furnaces in metal tiers. A generator augment turns one into a small FE source."
		"&eChemistry:&r smelting iron ore is a reduction: carbon pulls the oxygen off, Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂."
		"&eHow:&r ring a furnace with iron (check JEI). Upgrade kits move it up a tier without breaking it."
	]
	quest.2AA6E5D8AD92D260.title: "Pipez"
	quest.2AA6E5D8AD92D260.quest_subtitle: "Simple item, fluid and energy pipes"
	quest.2AA6E5D8AD92D260.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r simple pipes for moving items, fluids and energy between non-MI machines."
		"&eHow:&r place a line from source to target, then set the end touching the source to extract (the pipe tooltip explains how)."
		"&eTip:&r MI machines have their own pipes; Pipez is best for everything else."
	]
	quest.3391DEB52E24862E.title: "LaserIO"
	quest.3391DEB52E24862E.quest_subtitle: "Move things through the air"
	quest.3391DEB52E24862E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Laser Nodes move items, fluids and energy between machines without cables."
		"&eHow:&r place nodes on machines, link them with the Laser Wrench, and add cards to set what moves (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r one node can serve all six faces of a block, great for compact chemical setups."
	]
	quest.01F07AC7CEBA34C1.title: "Entangled"
	quest.01F07AC7CEBA34C1.quest_subtitle: "One inventory, two places"
	quest.01F07AC7CEBA34C1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an Entangled Block is a window into another inventory: bind it to a chest or machine, and anything put in the Entangled Block goes into the bound block, even across dimensions."
		"&eHow:&r ender pearls, obsidian and a wooden chest (check JEI). Right-click the target with the Entangled Binder (pearls, obsidian and a diamond), then right-click the Entangled Block. Click the checkmark when one is working."
		"&eTip:&r put one next to a remote ore processor and pipe the output straight home. Both chunks must be loaded."
	]
	quest.24A467FAA663A7EF.title: "Storage in Motion"
	quest.24A467FAA663A7EF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Sophisticated chests on rails and water"
	quest.24A467FAA663A7EF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Sophisticated Storage in Motion puts upgradeable chests and barrels on minecarts, boats and rafts, upgrades and all."
		"&eHow:&r combine a minecart with a Sophisticated chest or barrel (check JEI). Boats and rafts work the same way."
		"&eTip:&r a hopper upgrade on a storage minecart makes a simple ore train between your mine and base."
	]
	quest.14C4F705E5EB614F.title: "Stack Upgrades"
	quest.14C4F705E5EB614F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more items in every slot"
	quest.14C4F705E5EB614F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r stack upgrades multiply how many items fit in each slot of a chest or barrel. Higher tiers multiply more."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base and storage blocks (check JEI). Insert it in an upgrade slot."
		"&eTip:&r a barrel with a few stack upgrades holds a whole mine's worth of cobblestone or raw ore."
	]
	quest.317575EF2934BE98.title: "Drawer Upgrades"
	quest.317575EF2934BE98.quest_subtitle: "Copper, gold, diamond, netherite"
	quest.317575EF2934BE98.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r storage upgrades multiply a drawer's capacity. Each tier (copper, gold, diamond, netherite) holds more."
		"&eHow:&r craft the upgrades in order (check JEI) and right-click the drawer to open its upgrade slots."
		"&eTip:&r the Iron Downgrade does the reverse, limiting a drawer to a single stack per slot."
	]
	quest.6A53B6D2F371F859.title: "Pullers and Pushers"
	quest.6A53B6D2F371F859.quest_subtitle: "Drawers that move items themselves"
	quest.6A53B6D2F371F859.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r utility upgrades: the Puller pulls items from the block it faces, the Pusher pushes items into it. No pipes needed."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Put one in a drawer's utility slot and set its direction in the drawer's menu."
		"&eTip:&r a drawer with a Puller behind a macerator collects all the dust without a single pipe."
	]
	quest.46990CC570367505.title: "Fluid Drawers"
	quest.46990CC570367505.quest_subtitle: "Optional: drawers for liquids"
	quest.46990CC570367505.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fluid drawers store a fluid instead of items, and show it on the front."
		"&eChemistry:&r handy for small stocks of acids: one drawer of H₂SO₄, one of HCl, one of HNO₃. A real lab keeps acids in separate, labelled containers too."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Pipes and MI fluid pipes can fill and drain them; the storage upgrades work on them too."
	]
	quest.6E40C57F90C4FE3B.title: "Ender Drawer"
	quest.6E40C57F90C4FE3B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one drawer, many places"
	quest.6E40C57F90C4FE3B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every Ender Drawer with the same frequency shares one inventory, wherever it is."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Link drawers with the Linking Tool to give them the same frequency."
		"&eTip:&r put one at your mine and one at your smelters to send ore home."
	]
	quest.198E6DA2BCC8985F.title: "Inventory Cables"
	quest.198E6DA2BCC8985F.quest_subtitle: "Reach chests across the room"
	quest.198E6DA2BCC8985F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r inventory cables carry the Inventory Connector's reach to chests that aren't touching it."
		"&eHow:&r run cables from the connector and put a Cable Connector on each chest or drawer (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r framed cables can wear any block's texture, so they hide in walls."
	]
	quest.74EA12F84EA1A34D.title: "Wireless Terminal"
	quest.74EA12F84EA1A34D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: your early network, anywhere"
	quest.74EA12F84EA1A34D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Advanced Wireless Terminal opens your Tom's network from a long way off."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI, then right-click it on a Storage Terminal to bind it."
		"&eTip:&r it's the cheapest remote storage access until AE2."
	]
	chapter.0995B455F4B29E6B.title: "Applied Energistics"
	chapter.0995B455F4B29E6B.chapter_subtitle: [
		"The archive of a god: every item as data, every recipe on demand."
	]
	quest.5A12756B50F4FE84.title: "Feeding the Network"
	quest.5A12756B50F4FE84.quest_subtitle: "AE2 runs on its own energy, fed by FE"
	quest.5A12756B50F4FE84.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the ME network turns FE into its own AE energy. The Energy Acceptor converts it; Energy Cells buffer it."
		"&eHow:&r connect an Energy Acceptor to any FE source (an energy cube, a Powah cell, a Flux Point) and to your cables. Add an Energy Cell next to the controller (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a big autocraft can drain the network fast. A Dense Energy Cell keeps it from browning out mid-job."
	]
	quest.2A7CE0F1602C61FA.title: "Growing Certus"
	quest.2A7CE0F1602C61FA.quest_subtitle: "Optional: crystal farms at full speed"
	quest.2A7CE0F1602C61FA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Growth Accelerators speed up certus quartz buds growing on budding certus blocks."
		"&eChemistry:&r real quartz (SiO₂) crystals grow from silica-rich water over thousands of years. Certus is fictional, but the idea of a seed crystal pulling dissolved material out of solution is real."
		"&eHow:&r iron, fluix glass cable, quartz glass and a fluix block (check JEI). Place them touching budding certus and power them."
		"&eTip:&r flawless budding certus never decays. Find it in meteorites and never break it with a normal pickaxe."
	]
	quest.15163874C4379E91.title: "P2P Tunnels"
	quest.15163874C4379E91.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one cable, many channels"
	quest.15163874C4379E91.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a pair of P2P tunnels carries 32 channels (or items, fluids, FE and redstone) through a single dense cable."
		"&eHow:&r place both tunnels, then copy the input's settings to the output with a Memory Card (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r right-click a P2P tunnel with a bucket, a redstone dust or an FE item to change what it carries."
	]
	quest.29DF6C2F77C3462E.title: "The Matter Condenser"
	quest.29DF6C2F77C3462E.quest_subtitle: "Crush a quarter-million items into a point"
	quest.29DF6C2F77C3462E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Matter Condenser destroys items. With a 64k component inside, it squeezes them into Matter Balls or a Singularity."
		"&eHow:&r craft it (check JEI), put a storage component in it, set it to Singularity and feed it cobblestone from a pipe. It takes a lot of items."
		"&eTip:&r singularities unlock MEGA Cells' accumulation processor and every AdvancedAE machine, so start a cobblestone generator early."
	]
	quest.12502172FFC387E5.title: "Quantum Bridge"
	quest.12502172FFC387E5.quest_subtitle: "Optional: link networks across dimensions"
	quest.12502172FFC387E5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r two Quantum Network Bridges joined by entangled singularities act like one cable, even across dimensions."
		"&eHow:&r build a 3x3 ring of 8 Quantum Rings around a Quantum Link Chamber at each end, then put one of a pair of entangled singularities in each chamber."
		"&eTip:&r both ends must be chunk-loaded. Use FTB Chunks to force-load them."
	]
	quest.2DC9FE73876C2216.title: "Spooky Action"
	quest.2DC9FE73876C2216.quest_subtitle: "Secret: two particles, one fate"
	quest.2DC9FE73876C2216.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember being in two places at once. It felt exactly like this.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r you made a pair of Quantum Entangled Singularities by blowing up a singularity with ender pearl dust."
		"&eChemistry:&r real entangled particles share one quantum state: measure one and you know the other, however far apart. Sadly it can't send messages faster than light; AE2 is kinder."
	]
	quest.33690DED4CD25646.title: "AE2 Storage"
	quest.33690DED4CD25646.quest_subtitle: "Drives, terminals and the god's archive"
	quest.33690DED4CD25646.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember a mind that held every name of every thing. The archive is waking.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r ME Drives hold storage cells; terminals let you see and search everything."
		"&eHow:&r connect the drive and a terminal to your ME Controller with cables (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep power stable: an Energy Cell buffers the network."
	]
	quest.4ACE8FFE618969CC.title: "Cables and Channels"
	quest.4ACE8FFE618969CC.quest_subtitle: "Every device needs a channel"
	quest.4ACE8FFE618969CC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each ME device uses one channel. Normal cables carry 8 channels, dense cables 32. The controller sends 32 out of each face."
		"&eHow:&r craft fluix cables, then smart cables (they show channel use as lines) and dense cables (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r build a dense-cable backbone from the controller and branch normal cables off it. Smart cables show you where channels run out."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive:&r if a device's light is off, it has no channel. Count devices on each normal cable (max 8). Drives, terminals, buses and interfaces all count. Plain cables, quartz fibre and energy cells don't."
		"&eHow:&r the Network Tool (check JEI) shows the channel count of any cable when you right-click it."
	]
	quest.58932D295CE4DB3B.title: "Storage Cells"
	quest.58932D295CE4DB3B.quest_subtitle: "Bytes for your items"
	quest.58932D295CE4DB3B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r cells are where the network actually stores things. Bigger components (4k, 16k, 64k, 256k) hold more."
		"&eChemistry:&r certus and fluix are fictional, but the logic processors behind them echo real chips: doped silicon (Si)."
		"&eHow:&r craft components from processors and certus quartz, then put one in a cell housing (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.7D7098581E0AE024.title: "Bigger Components"
	quest.7D7098581E0AE024.quest_subtitle: "16k and 64k: room for whole chemical stocks"
	quest.7D7098581E0AE024.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each tier combines three of the last with a calculation processor and quartz glass, holding four times as many bytes."
		"&eHow:&r 4k from 1k, 16k from 4k, 64k from 16k (check JEI). Put them in housings, or into the Matter Condenser."
		"&eTip:&r a cell holds up to 63 different item types whatever its size, so use small cells for many odd items and big cells for bulk ores and dusts."
	]
	quest.76110B693DBF6FF2.title: "Autocrafting"
	quest.76110B693DBF6FF2.quest_subtitle: "Whole chemical chains in one click"
	quest.76110B693DBF6FF2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r pattern providers plus molecular assemblers turn whole chemical chains into one click."
		"&eHow:&r a Crafting Terminal, some crafting storage, and patterns encoded in a Pattern Encoding Terminal (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r processing patterns can drive MI machines too: send the inputs, wait for the outputs. The Automation and Logic page walks through a full sulfuric acid line."
	]
	quest.72A62F77A5D7C0CE.title: "Wireless Access"
	quest.72A62F77A5D7C0CE.quest_subtitle: "Optional: your network in your pocket"
	quest.72A62F77A5D7C0CE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r reach your ME network from anywhere in range of a Wireless Access Point."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Link the terminal by putting it in the access point, and charge it in the Charger."
		"&eTip:&r put the access point near the middle of your base for the best coverage."
	]
	quest.07860310FF05CBD6.title: "Universal Terminal"
	quest.07860310FF05CBD6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one terminal to rule them all"
	quest.07860310FF05CBD6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r AE2 Wireless Terminals merges the crafting, pattern access and pattern encoding terminals into one Universal Terminal."
		"&eHow:&r combine two wireless terminals in a crafting grid (check JEI); add more by crafting them in again."
		"&eTip:&r a Magnet Card from the same mod pulls nearby drops straight into your network. A Quantum Bridge Card works across dimensions."
	]
	quest.5F84732A701D2559.title: "Infinite Range"
	quest.5F84732A701D2559.quest_subtitle: "Optional: no more range limit"
	quest.5F84732A701D2559.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Infinity Booster Card removes the Wireless Access Point's range limit within one dimension."
		"&eHow:&r a Nether Star, wireless boosters, eyes of ender and netherite ingots (check JEI). The star means fighting the Wither first."
		"&eTip:&r put it in the Wireless Access Point, not the terminal."
	]
	quest.0ADD4DC8D8127357.title: "Across Worlds"
	quest.0ADD4DC8D8127357.quest_subtitle: "Optional: your archive in every dimension"
	quest.0ADD4DC8D8127357.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Dimension Card lets a Wireless Access Point reach you in any dimension: the Nether, the Twilight Forest, the Moon."
		"&eHow:&r four Infinity Cards, four Nether Stars and an eye of ender (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the access point's chunk must stay loaded while you're away."
	]
	quest.3E6BB0338E3344C9.title: "ME Requester"
	quest.3E6BB0338E3344C9.quest_subtitle: "Optional: keep stock topped up"
	quest.3E6BB0338E3344C9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the ME Requester keeps a set amount of an item in stock by ordering crafts automatically."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Set \"keep 64 HDPE\" and it never runs out."
		"&eTip:&r it needs autocrafting patterns for whatever it keeps in stock."
	]
	quest.0CC9A52C043BEE4C.title: "Requester Terminal"
	quest.0CC9A52C043BEE4C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: every stock rule on one screen"
	quest.0CC9A52C043BEE4C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Requester Terminal lists every ME Requester on the network, so you can edit all your stock rules from one place."
		"&eHow:&r an illuminated panel, a logic processor and a Requester, shapeless (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep a stock rule for each acid and solvent: H₂SO₄, HCl and HNO₃ are inputs to almost everything late game."
	]
	quest.68089090A4D213E6.title: "Entro Crystals"
	quest.68089090A4D213E6.quest_subtitle: "ExtendedAE's own budding crystal"
	quest.68089090A4D213E6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r entro crystals feed every ExtendedAE machine. They grow like certus, from Budding Entroized Fluix."
		"&eHow:&r craft Entro Seeds (sand, ender dust, redstone, glowstone, sky dust), then right-click a placed Fluix Block with a seed to make it budding. Harvest the clusters."
		"&eTip:&r Growth Accelerators work on budding entro too."
	]
	quest.66ED4FE9373A352B.title: "Crystal Assembler"
	quest.66ED4FE9373A352B.quest_subtitle: "A crafting machine for AE2 parts"
	quest.66ED4FE9373A352B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Crystal Assembler makes ExtendedAE's blocks from several items (and sometimes a fluid) at once."
		"&eHow:&r crush entro to dust in the Inscriber, drop it in water with a gold ingot and lapis for an entro ingot, then build a Machine Frame and the Assembler (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r it accepts pipes and patterns, so the network can drive it like any other machine."
	]
	quest.33967F89E0530A95.title: "ExtendedAE"
	quest.33967F89E0530A95.quest_subtitle: "Bigger providers and drives"
	quest.33967F89E0530A95.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ExtendedAE adds larger versions of AE2 blocks: the Extended Pattern Provider holds many more patterns, the Extended Drive many more cells."
		"&eHow:&r made in the Crystal Assembler from the normal blocks plus concurrent processors (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r one extended provider can feed a whole row of chemical reactors."
	]
	quest.671135248AAD6760.title: "Wireless Connectors"
	quest.671135248AAD6760.quest_subtitle: "Optional: cables through thin air"
	quest.671135248AAD6760.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a pair of Wireless Connectors links two parts of your network without a cable between them."
		"&eHow:&r made two at a time in the Crystal Assembler. Bind them with the Wireless Setup Kit (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r great for reaching a reactor room behind thick shielding."
	]
	quest.3770AEAFDC83097B.title: "Assembler Matrix"
	quest.3770AEAFDC83097B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one multiblock, thousands of crafts"
	quest.3770AEAFDC83097B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Assembler Matrix is a multiblock that replaces walls of molecular assemblers: crafter blocks do the work, pattern blocks hold the patterns."
		"&eHow:&r build a hollow box of frames and walls (or glass), with crafter, pattern and speed cores inside (check JEI for the rules)."
		"&eTip:&r it's for crafting-table recipes only. Processing patterns for MI machines still need pattern providers."
	]
	quest.740C1D9B0EE26F7C.title: "MEGA Cells"
	quest.740C1D9B0EE26F7C.quest_subtitle: "Sky steel and million-byte cells"
	quest.740C1D9B0EE26F7C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MEGA Cells adds 1M to 256M cells, bulk cells and bigger crafting storage."
		"&eChemistry:&r sky steel is made by dropping charged certus, iron and sky stone into lava: heat drives the alloying, like a tiny smelter."
		"&eHow:&r throw the ingredients into a lava pool for sky steel, then build the 1M component (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.096161FE28A839F6.title: "Sky Bronze and Sky Osmium"
	quest.096161FE28A839F6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more lava alloys"
	quest.096161FE28A839F6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the same lava trick with copper gives sky bronze, and with osmium gives sky osmium. Both go into MEGA's larger parts."
		"&eChemistry:&r bronze is really copper plus tin (Cu + Sn); here the sky stone plays the tin. Osmium (Os) is the densest natural element, 22.6 g/cm³."
		"&eHow:&r drop charged certus, the ingot and a sky stone block into lava together. Each throw makes two ingots."
	]
	quest.5160F2053D91D317.title: "Accumulation Processors"
	quest.5160F2053D91D317.quest_subtitle: "A press made from a singularity"
	quest.5160F2053D91D317.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the accumulation processor is MEGA's fourth processor, needed for every 1M+ part."
		"&eHow:&r inscribe a singularity between the calculation and engineering presses to make the Accumulation Press, then print sky steel with it (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep the press. The Inscriber can copy it with an iron block, like the other presses."
	]
	quest.1665F7B5F4B8CBDF.title: "MEGA Crafting CPU"
	quest.1665F7B5F4B8CBDF.quest_subtitle: "Room for the biggest crafting jobs"
	quest.1665F7B5F4B8CBDF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MEGA crafting storage and units build a separate, much larger crafting CPU."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. MEGA blocks only join other MEGA blocks, so build it as its own multiblock."
		"&eTip:&r the Seed of a New World chain is huge. One big CPU saves splitting the job by hand."
	]
	quest.6A29B228E6049846.title: "MEGA Pattern Provider"
	quest.6A29B228E6049846.quest_subtitle: "Optional: room for many more patterns"
	quest.6A29B228E6049846.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a pattern provider with many more pattern slots than the normal one."
		"&eHow:&r made as a cable part and turned into a block in the crafting grid (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r put one on each multi-input MI machine, like the Chemical Reactor or the Large Diesel Generator's fuel line."
	]
	quest.606F92F0A56293B8.title: "Bulk Cells"
	quest.606F92F0A56293B8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one item, practically no limit"
	quest.606F92F0A56293B8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Bulk Item Cell holds a single item type in near-unlimited amounts. The Compression Card stores nuggets, ingots and blocks as one pool."
		"&eHow:&r the bulk component needs a 1M component and accumulation processors; the card is an advanced card plus a matter ball (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r perfect for cobblestone (condenser feed), salt dust or coal coke."
	]
	quest.6ABB15806114CC83.title: "Gas in the Network"
	quest.6ABB15806114CC83.quest_subtitle: "Store Mekanism chemicals in AE2"
	quest.6ABB15806114CC83.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Applied Mekanistics lets AE2 store and move Mekanism chemicals: H₂, O₂, Cl₂, HCl, SO₂ and the rest."
		"&eChemistry:&r a 1k cell holds a lot of gas because the network stores amounts, not tanks. Real gases need pressure vessels."
		"&eHow:&r a chemical cell housing (osmium, quartz glass, redstone) + a 1k component. Import buses on chemical tanks fill it."
		"&eTip:&r processing patterns can pull stored SO₂ and O₂ straight from the cell to feed your sulfuric acid line."
	]
	quest.52CB2FB63C5C2051.title: "A Tank Farm in a Cell"
	quest.52CB2FB63C5C2051.quest_subtitle: "Optional: 64k of chemicals"
	quest.52CB2FB63C5C2051.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a 64k chemical cell replaces a room full of chemical tanks."
		"&eChemistry:&r one mole of any ideal gas fills about 22.4 L at 0 °C and 1 atm. Stored as data, it fills nothing at all."
		"&eHow:&r chemical housing plus a 64k component, or upgrade a smaller cell in the crafting grid (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.049F324F4DE92733.title: "Shielded Storage"
	quest.049F324F4DE92733.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a cell for hot chemicals"
	quest.049F324F4DE92733.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r normal chemical cells refuse radioactive chemicals. MEGA's Radioactive Chemical Cell holds one, like nuclear waste or plutonium."
		"&eChemistry:&r spent fuel stays dangerous because unstable nuclei keep decaying, giving off α, β and γ radiation for years."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the radioactive component and cell."
		"&eTip:&r a cell never leaks, unlike a broken tank. It's the safest place to keep waste before you reprocess it."
	]
	quest.4B1B2296A5EDEB45.title: "Energy in a Cell"
	quest.4B1B2296A5EDEB45.quest_subtitle: "Applied Flux stores FE in AE2"
	quest.4B1B2296A5EDEB45.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Applied Flux stores FE in AE2 cells and moves it through the network with Flux Accessors."
		"&eHow:&r redstone crystal (redstone block, fluix and glowstone dropped in water) → charge it in the AE2 Charger → FE cell core and housing (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the housing needs insulating resin, which needs silicon: a little chemistry even here."
	]
	quest.136207F7A3DC6A3C.title: "Flux Accessor"
	quest.136207F7A3DC6A3C.quest_subtitle: "Power machines from the network"
	quest.136207F7A3DC6A3C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Flux Accessor pushes FE from your FE cells into any machine it touches. An Induction Card lets an I/O bus or interface do the same."
		"&eHow:&r an energy acceptor, energy processors (iron block charged into the Energy Press, then inscribed), copper and glowstone (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r one FE cell plus accessors can replace a tangle of power cables around a dense machine room."
	]
	quest.7FFFA15128FCBD88.title: "Reaction Chamber"
	quest.7FFFA15128FCBD88.quest_subtitle: "AdvancedAE's powered reactor"
	quest.7FFFA15128FCBD88.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r AdvancedAE's Reaction Chamber combines items and a fluid with lots of energy. Its first job: shattering singularities."
		"&eHow:&r a matter condenser, a vibration chamber, fluix dust, glowstone and a bucket (check JEI). Feed it a singularity, ender dust, sky dust and lava."
		"&eTip:&r it uses a lot of power per craft. Put it on its own Energy Acceptor."
	]
	quest.43A72FAC8EB012CB.title: "Quantum Alloy"
	quest.43A72FAC8EB012CB.quest_subtitle: "Copper, singularities and quantum infusion"
	quest.43A72FAC8EB012CB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r quantum alloy is AdvancedAE's top material, for the quantum computer and gear."
		"&eHow:&r press a shattered singularity into quantum-infused dust, react it with water into Quantum Infusion, then react that with copper ingots, singularities and shattered singularities (check JEI)."
		"&eChemistry:&r copper (Cu) is the base for a reason: after silver it's the best electrical conductor of any metal."
	]
	quest.4FBB5D1C1A7FC218.title: "Directional Providers"
	quest.4FBB5D1C1A7FC218.quest_subtitle: "Send each ingredient to the right face"
	quest.4FBB5D1C1A7FC218.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Advanced Pattern Provider lets a processing pattern send each input to a chosen side of the machine."
		"&eHow:&r an Extended Pattern Provider, a logic processor, an ender pearl and redstone (check JEI). Encode patterns in the Advanced Pattern Encoder."
		"&eTip:&r ideal for machines with separate input faces, like a Mekanism machine that takes gas on one side and items on another."
	]
	quest.423E95AFA4363CFD.title: "Quantum Computer"
	quest.423E95AFA4363CFD.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the archive learns to think"
	quest.423E95AFA4363CFD.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember thinking a thousand thoughts at once. The machine remembers how, too.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Quantum Computer is a multiblock crafting CPU: huge storage, many parallel jobs, and accelerators that multiply speed."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Core inside a shell of Quantum Structure blocks, with multi-threaders, accelerators and storage blocks (check JEI for size limits)."
		"&eTip:&r build it next to your main pattern providers so every chemical line can run at once."
	]
	quest.56AC603AD4E1D10D.title: "Import and Export Cards"
	quest.56AC603AD4E1D10D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: your inventory, auto-sorted"
	quest.56AC603AD4E1D10D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r these cards go in a wireless terminal. The Import Card pushes chosen items from your inventory into the network; the Export Card keeps chosen items stocked in your inventory."
		"&eHow:&r an import (or export) bus, redstone blocks, an advanced card and processors (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r set the Import Card to cobblestone, dirt and raw ores, and mining trips never fill your inventory."
	]
	quest.0793BD80DC7ABE69.title: "Packaged Extended Crafting"
	quest.0793BD80DC7ABE69.quest_subtitle: "Optional: autocraft on the big tables"
	quest.0793BD80DC7ABE69.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Packaged ExCrafting adds crafters that run Extended Crafting recipes from packages: one for each table size, plus combination and ender crafting."
		"&eHow:&r an auto table of the right size, an ME package component, crystaltine components, black iron and a redstone catalyst (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r encode the recipe in the Packaged Auto encoder, just like normal packages."
	]
	quest.24D6EC7D3175543C.title: "The Ultimate Crafter"
	quest.24D6EC7D3175543C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: 9x9 recipes on demand"
	quest.24D6EC7D3175543C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Ultimate Crafter runs 9x9 Ultimate Table recipes automatically from the network."
		"&eHow:&r same recipe as the basic crafter, with an Ultimate Auto Table in the middle (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the Seed of a New World is a 9x9 recipe. Feed it from the network and the capstone crafts itself once its ingredients exist."
	]
	chapter.283C125EDC24C8C3.title: "Building and Decoration"
	chapter.283C125EDC24C8C3.chapter_subtitle: [
		"A god's house should look like one."
	]
	quest.7AD94AAAA5254B9E.title: "Effortless Building"
	quest.7AD94AAAA5254B9E.quest_subtitle: "Mirror, array and line building"
	quest.7AD94AAAA5254B9E.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember raising cities with a gesture. For now, a few clever tools will do.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Effortless Building adds mirror, array and line modes for big builds."
		"&eHow:&r open its menu (check Controls) and pick a mode. The randomizer places a random mix of the blocks you load into it."
		"&eTip:&r the randomizer with stone, andesite and cobblestone makes natural-looking walls."
	]
	quest.0EBF44825F21BDC2.title: "Construction Stick"
	quest.0EBF44825F21BDC2.quest_subtitle: "Optional: extend a wall in one click"
	quest.0EBF44825F21BDC2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Construction Stick places a whole row or face of blocks matching the one you click, using blocks from your inventory."
		"&eHow:&r three sticks in a column (check JEI). Right-click the face of a wall to grow it by one layer."
		"&eTip:&r the tooltip lists its modes, such as only extending in a straight line."
	]
	quest.046BE5DF3A379E58.title: "Diamond Stick"
	quest.046BE5DF3A379E58.quest_subtitle: "Optional: bigger reach, more durability"
	quest.046BE5DF3A379E58.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r better sticks place more blocks per click and last longer: copper, iron, diamond, then netherite."
		"&eChemistry:&r diamond is pure carbon (C) in a tight 3D lattice, which makes it the hardest natural material."
		"&eHow:&r a diamond on two sticks (check JEI). Templates applied at a smithing table add tricks like placing in mid-air."
	]
	quest.256D3D0FC72501EE.title: "Rechiseled"
	quest.256D3D0FC72501EE.quest_subtitle: "Optional: hundreds of block patterns"
	quest.256D3D0FC72501EE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Rechiseled adds a chisel that turns stone, planks, metal blocks and more into decorative patterns: bricks, tiles, pillars, gears."
		"&eHow:&r craft the chisel from an iron ingot on a stick, right-click to open it, put blocks in and pick a pattern. Click the checkmark when you've chiseled something."
		"&eTip:&r many patterns connect to each other when placed side by side. Try the iron and copper block patterns for a machine room."
	]
	quest.171C251ED5512ABD.title: "Building Gadgets"
	quest.171C251ED5512ABD.quest_subtitle: "Place whole surfaces with FE"
	quest.171C251ED5512ABD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r FE-powered gadgets that place, swap, copy and remove blocks in bulk."
		"&eHow:&r iron, redstone, lapis and a diamond (check JEI). Charge it in an energy cube."
		"&eTip:&r link the gadget to a chest or backpack so it pulls blocks from storage."
	]
	quest.34C2506F0D77DBC7.title: "Copy and Paste"
	quest.34C2506F0D77DBC7.quest_subtitle: "Optional: copy a whole build"
	quest.34C2506F0D77DBC7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r copy an area and paste it elsewhere; the Template Manager saves copies to share."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Great for repeating a chemical reactor cell or a row of machines."
		"&eTip:&r templates can be shared with friends on the server."
	]
	quest.78B3985AFEC9753C.title: "Exchanging Gadget"
	quest.78B3985AFEC9753C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: swap blocks in place"
	quest.78B3985AFEC9753C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r replaces blocks in an area with another block, keeping the shape."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Perfect for turning a cobble shell into something pretty."
		"&eTip:&r it uses the blocks in your inventory, so carry enough."
	]
	quest.6264FFAD4D805503.title: "Destruction Gadget"
	quest.6264FFAD4D805503.quest_subtitle: "Optional: clear a room in seconds"
	quest.6264FFAD4D805503.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r removes a box of blocks in front of you, sized however you like. It can undo its last action."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Set the depth, width and height in its menu."
		"&eTip:&r perfect for hollowing out a hillside for a new factory floor."
	]
	quest.17B2684DCFCAF116.title: "Framed Blocks"
	quest.17B2684DCFCAF116.quest_subtitle: "Any shape, any texture"
	quest.17B2684DCFCAF116.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r FramedBlocks are wooden frames that take the look of any block you right-click into them, in dozens of shapes."
		"&eHow:&r framed cubes are planks and sticks (check JEI). Right-click a framed block with any full block to apply it as camouflage. The Framed Hammer takes it back off."
		"&eTip:&r camouflage with glass, ores or even machine casings: the block keeps its shape and takes the texture."
	]
	quest.43AAE4F773290CA0.title: "Slopes and Panels"
	quest.43AAE4F773290CA0.quest_subtitle: "Optional: six framed shapes"
	quest.43AAE4F773290CA0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r any six framed slopes, corner slopes, stairs, slabs, panels, pillars or prisms."
		"&eHow:&r each shape is made from framed cubes (check JEI). Most come several at a time."
		"&eTip:&r framed slopes camouflaged as stone make roofs and ramps that look hand-carved."
	]
	quest.493C7E73D1EA248B.title: "Secret Storage"
	quest.493C7E73D1EA248B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a chest that looks like a wall"
	quest.493C7E73D1EA248B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a full-block chest that wears any block's texture, so it disappears into a wall."
		"&eHow:&r a framed chest surrounded by framed cubes (check JEI), then camouflage it."
		"&eTip:&r hide your rarest elements in one. Nobody suspects the third stone brick from the left."
	]
	quest.0882494FACF73614.title: "Somewhere to Sit"
	quest.0882494FACF73614.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Handcrafted chairs and a table"
	quest.0882494FACF73614.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Handcrafted adds furniture you can actually sit on: chairs, couches, benches, tables, desks."
		"&eHow:&r any wood works (check JEI). Right-click a chair to sit."
		"&eTip:&r the Handcrafted Hammer changes the shape of trims and some other pieces (check its tooltip)."
	]
	quest.255AF1E86B0F49B5.title: "A Proper Study"
	quest.255AF1E86B0F49B5.quest_subtitle: "Optional: couches and a desk"
	quest.255AF1E86B0F49B5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r couches connect into long sofas; desks connect into long workbenches."
		"&eHow:&r any wood (check JEI). Cushions and sheets add colour."
		"&eTip:&r a desk by your Alchemistry machines makes a fine place to read the quest book."
	]
	quest.4E82A4FFCC6F1EEF.title: "Macaw's Furniture"
	quest.4E82A4FFCC6F1EEF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: wardrobes, drawers and cabinets"
	quest.4E82A4FFCC6F1EEF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Macaw's Furniture adds kitchens, wardrobes, drawers, bookshelves and more. Many of them store items."
		"&eHow:&r any two wardrobes, drawers or kitchen cabinets (check JEI for the full set)."
		"&eTip:&r drawers and cabinets open like chests, so a kitchen can double as food storage."
	]
	quest.5E740E65B6A4BD53.title: "Doors"
	quest.5E740E65B6A4BD53.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Macaw's doors"
	quest.5E740E65B6A4BD53.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Macaw's Doors adds barn, cottage, glass, modern and many more doors in every wood."
		"&eHow:&r any two barn, modern, glass or cottage doors (check JEI for recipes)."
		"&eTip:&r glass doors let you see into a machine room without opening it."
	]
	quest.06248880B960989A.title: "Trapdoors"
	quest.06248880B960989A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Macaw's trapdoors"
	quest.06248880B960989A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r decorative trapdoors that match the doors: barn, glass, classic and more."
		"&eHow:&r any four barn, glass or classic trapdoors (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r trapdoors on walls make great shutters and cabinet fronts."
	]
	quest.30251E31D4E975EF.title: "Windows"
	quest.30251E31D4E975EF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: framed windows"
	quest.30251E31D4E975EF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Macaw's Windows adds framed windows, shutters, curtains, blinds and parapets."
		"&eHow:&r any four framed windows (check JEI)."
		"&eChemistry:&r glass is mostly silica (SiO₂) melted with soda (Na₂CO₃) and lime (CaO), then cooled before it can crystallise."
	]
	quest.0730AC23E95DCD5A.title: "Roofs"
	quest.0730AC23E95DCD5A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a roof that isn't flat"
	quest.0730AC23E95DCD5A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Macaw's Roofs adds sloped, steep, attic and top roof pieces that join into proper roofs."
		"&eHow:&r any sixteen roof pieces (check JEI). Wooden roofs come from logs and sticks."
		"&eTip:&r place the lower and upper pieces together to make a gentler slope."
	]
	quest.1C66E75AABEB8A04.title: "Fences and Hedges"
	quest.1C66E75AABEB8A04.quest_subtitle: "Optional: picket, stockade, wired, hedge"
	quest.1C66E75AABEB8A04.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Macaw's Fences adds picket and stockade fences, wired fences, hedges and gates."
		"&eHow:&r any eight picket, stockade or wired fences or hedges (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r hedges are made from leaves, so you can keep a garden looking natural."
	]
	quest.7E1544D1ED3E2D20.title: "Paths"
	quest.7E1544D1ED3E2D20.quest_subtitle: "Optional: paving between your buildings"
	quest.7E1544D1ED3E2D20.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Macaw's Paths adds paving patterns (basket weave, honeycomb, flagstone) in stone, brick and sandstone."
		"&eHow:&r any sixteen paving blocks (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a path from your base to your waystone saves getting lost at night."
	]
	quest.2B01CBA33D88B363.title: "Bridges"
	quest.2B01CBA33D88B363.quest_subtitle: "Optional: rope, stone and iron bridges"
	quest.2B01CBA33D88B363.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Macaw's Bridges adds bridge pieces that connect into rope, stone, brick and iron bridges, with piers and stairs."
		"&eHow:&r any eight bridge pieces (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r an iron bridge over a lava lake makes the Nether commute much safer."
	]
	quest.7D8A60F5C4CE08DA.title: "Lamps and Lanterns"
	quest.7D8A60F5C4CE08DA.quest_subtitle: "Optional: street lamps and chandeliers"
	quest.7D8A60F5C4CE08DA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Macaw's Lights adds street lamps, lanterns, garden lights and chandeliers."
		"&eHow:&r any four of them (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r street lamps along your paths keep mobs from spawning on the way home."
	]
	quest.2483BE5777A45DF0.title: "Lava Lamp"
	quest.2483BE5777A45DF0.quest_subtitle: "Optional: groovy chemistry"
	quest.2483BE5777A45DF0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a lava lamp for your desk. This one really has lava in it."
		"&eChemistry:&r a real lava lamp holds wax in water. The bulb heats the wax, it expands, its density drops below the water's and it rises; at the top it cools, gets denser and sinks."
		"&eHow:&r iron nuggets, a lava bucket and an iron ingot (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.263D8CF775631953.title: "Jars"
	quest.263D8CF775631953.quest_subtitle: "Optional: display jars for anything"
	quest.263D8CF775631953.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Supplementaries jars hold items, liquids or even small mobs, and show what's inside."
		"&eHow:&r glass and a wooden slab (check JEI). Right-click with an item or a bucket to fill."
		"&eTip:&r a shelf of jars, one per element, makes a lovely periodic table display."
	]
	quest.03F0CB824882681C.title: "Rope and Sacks"
	quest.03F0CB824882681C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: flax, rope and a sack"
	quest.03F0CB824882681C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r rope you can climb and pull things up with, and sacks that store items and can be carried."
		"&eHow:&r grow flax (seeds from wild flax), then craft rope and sacks from it (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r ropes hanging down a mineshaft are a quick way up and down (check JEI for the pulley block)."
	]
	quest.3916B5092992AE39.title: "Soap"
	quest.3916B5092992AE39.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the oldest chemistry in the house"
	quest.3916B5092992AE39.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r soap washes the dye off coloured blocks and items, and it powers the Bubble Blower."
		"&eChemistry:&r saponification. Wood ash is rich in potash (K₂CO₃); in water it makes lye. Lye splits fat into glycerol and fatty-acid salts, which is soap. People made it this way for thousands of years."
		"&eHow:&r a water bucket, four ash and a porkchop (check JEI). Ash is left behind when fire burns blocks away; check JEI for other sources."
	]
	quest.27402D05976252E6.title: "Bubbles!"
	quest.27402D05976252E6.quest_subtitle: "Secret: a demigod at play"
	quest.27402D05976252E6.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember making nebulae. These are smaller, but they're very pretty.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Bubble Blower uses soap to blow bubbles; it can also make Bubble Blocks (check its tooltip)."
		"&eChemistry:&r a soap film is a thin water layer between two layers of soap molecules. The colours come from light reflecting off its front and back surfaces and interfering."
	]
	quest.0390136B315C41D8.title: "Create Deco Lamps"
	quest.0390136B315C41D8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: industrial lights"
	quest.0390136B315C41D8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Create Deco lamps in four colours and five metals light up a factory floor properly."
		"&eHow:&r a nugget, a torch and a plate of the metal (check JEI). Any four lamps."
		"&eTip:&r lamps can be switched off with redstone: red lamps as warning lights next to a reactor are a nice touch."
	]
	quest.5569DB7CD62C242F.title: "Hulls and Supports"
	quest.5569DB7CD62C242F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: riveted walls and girders"
	quest.5569DB7CD62C242F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r hulls are riveted metal walls; supports are girders for roofs and catwalks."
		"&eHow:&r any four hulls and four supports (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r copper hulls weather like copper blocks do. Wax them with honeycomb to keep the shine."
	]
	quest.05D2EE647B7C6620.title: "Copycats"
	quest.05D2EE647B7C6620.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Create-style shape-shifting blocks"
	quest.05D2EE647B7C6620.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Copycats+ adds many more Create copycat shapes: slopes, boards, beams, slices. Each takes the look of the block you apply to it."
		"&eHow:&r cut zinc ingots in a stonecutter (zinc ore is found underground; check JEI), then right-click a placed copycat with a block."
		"&eTip:&r copycat boards cover pipes and shafts while leaving them working."
	]
	quest.1C1D96F956C3898C.title: "Laboratory Blocks"
	quest.1C1D96F956C3898C.quest_subtitle: "Clean white walls for a chemist"
	quest.1C1D96F956C3898C.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember a laboratory of white stone and light. You can build it again.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Artemis' Laboratory Blocks adds clean lab walls, tiles, glass, screens, vents and fans."
		"&eChemistry:&r the recipe uses Nether quartz, which is silicon dioxide (SiO₂), the same compound as sand and glass."
		"&eHow:&r eight stone around one Nether quartz makes eight laboratory blocks (check JEI). Stonecut them into tiles, pillars and doors."
	]
	quest.231AB73D5B98BE94.title: "Glowing Panels"
	quest.231AB73D5B98BE94.quest_subtitle: "Optional: walls that light the room"
	quest.231AB73D5B98BE94.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r glowing laboratory blocks give off light, so a lab can be bright with no torches."
		"&eHow:&r one glowstone dust makes eight glowstone particles; one particle plus a laboratory block makes a glowing block (check JEI)."
		"&eChemistry:&r real glow-in-the-dark materials store energy from light and release it slowly (phosphorescence). Glowstone just glows; it's magic."
	]
	quest.302DFA9D7E8161B1.title: "Lab Screens"
	quest.302DFA9D7E8161B1.quest_subtitle: "Optional: monitors on every wall"
	quest.302DFA9D7E8161B1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r decorative screens: clear, text, wave and quantum patterns, plain or glowing."
		"&eHow:&r clear screens from laboratory blocks, laboratory glass and iron screws; add a dye for the patterns (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r put a wave screen next to your reactor and a ComputerCraft monitor beside it for real numbers."
	]
	quest.7827D1263B738EE4.title: "Fans and Vents"
	quest.7827D1263B738EE4.quest_subtitle: "Optional: fume extraction"
	quest.7827D1263B738EE4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r animated lab fans and vents. The redstone-controlled fan only spins when powered."
		"&eChemistry:&r real labs work with HCl, NH₃ and Cl₂ under a fume hood, which pulls vapours away from your face. Breathing chlorine is a very bad idea."
		"&eHow:&r laboratory blocks with iron nuggets and iron screws (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.63B9D8367D6914A8.title: "Lab Doors and Glass"
	quest.63B9D8367D6914A8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: see in, keep fumes out"
	quest.63B9D8367D6914A8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r lab doors (solid, glass or mesh) and laboratory glass for viewing windows."
		"&eHow:&r doors from laboratory blocks; laboratory glass is eight glass around a laboratory block (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a glass wall around your Alchemistry room lets visitors admire it without touching anything."
	]
	quest.4D60C7C6C5F73477.title: "A Proper Laboratory"
	quest.4D60C7C6C5F73477.quest_subtitle: "Optional: build a lab worthy of you"
	quest.4D60C7C6C5F73477.quest_desc: [
		"&6White walls, humming fans, glass and light. You remember this place. It was always where you were happiest.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a challenge: build a real laboratory around your chemistry machines using these blocks."
		"&eHow:&r include glowing panels, screens, a fume fan and a glass wall. Click the checkmark when you're proud of it."
		"&eTip:&r share a screenshot with your server. Bragging rights are a demigod's privilege."
	]
	chapter.081BBC14B8F2A34A.title: "Ars Nouveau"
	chapter.081BBC14B8F2A34A.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Spellcraft, Source, rituals and the Wilden: magic that runs on stored energy."
	]
	quest.4A082B2D50268C72.title: "Novice Spell Book"
	quest.4A082B2D50268C72.quest_subtitle: "Your first spells"
	quest.4A082B2D50268C72.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember speaking and the world listening. The words come back slowly.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Novice Spell Book holds spells built from glyphs: a form (how it's cast), effects, then augments."
		"&eHow:&r craft it (check JEI), then open it to combine glyphs, e.g. Projectile + Break to mine at range."
		"&eTip:&r the Worn Notebook explains every glyph. Mana regenerates over time."
	]
	quest.5AF9082F7AD1DE7C.title: "Scribe's Table"
	quest.5AF9082F7AD1DE7C.quest_subtitle: "Write new glyphs into your book"
	quest.5AF9082F7AD1DE7C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Scribe's Table crafts new glyphs, which unlock more spell parts."
		"&eHow:&r place it, put your spell book on it, and pick a glyph. JEI and the table show each glyph's cost."
		"&eTip:&r Light and Harvest are cheap early glyphs that pay off right away."
	]
	quest.619D1CA1E2F34139.title: "Source"
	quest.619D1CA1E2F34139.quest_subtitle: "Store magic, then spend it"
	quest.619D1CA1E2F34139.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Source is Ars Nouveau's magical energy. Jars store it; the Imbuement Chamber spends it to make source gems and essences."
		"&eHow:&r craft both (check JEI). Place jars near the chamber; they share Source within a few blocks."
		"&eTip:&r empty jars do nothing. The next step is a Sourcelink to fill them."
	]
	quest.094B0B47A8BEB3F8.title: "Volcanic Sourcelink"
	quest.094B0B47A8BEB3F8.quest_subtitle: "Turn fuel into Source"
	quest.094B0B47A8BEB3F8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Volcanic Sourcelink burns fuel and pushes the Source into nearby jars."
		"&eChemistry:&r burning is fast oxidation: C + O₂ → CO₂ plus heat. The sourcelink claims that energy as Source."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Feed it logs or coal with a hopper or pipe; archwood logs give more."
		"&eTip:&r the other sourcelinks feed on crops (Agronomic), food (Mycelial), mob deaths (Vitalic) and potions (Alchemical)."
	]
	quest.37432FA85E0B250D.title: "Enchanting Apparatus"
	quest.37432FA85E0B250D.quest_subtitle: "Ars Nouveau's big crafting altar"
	quest.37432FA85E0B250D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Apparatus sits on an Arcane Core and fuses items from surrounding Arcane Pedestals, using Source."
		"&eHow:&r Core first, Apparatus on top, pedestals within a few blocks. Put the main item in the Apparatus and right-click (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r it also applies enchantments to gear: more ways to make divine equipment."
	]
	quest.5B85AC6D5C703756.title: "Ritual Brazier"
	quest.5B85AC6D5C703756.quest_subtitle: "Where rituals happen"
	quest.5B85AC6D5C703756.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r rituals are area effects: sunrise, cloudshaping, overgrowth, flight and more. Each needs a brazier and a ritual tablet."
		"&eHow:&r craft the brazier (check JEI), place it, and right-click it with a ritual tablet."
		"&eTip:&r most rituals draw Source from nearby jars, so build next to your source room."
	]
	quest.2F020C2FEA6EEB68.title: "Ritual of Flight"
	quest.2F020C2FEA6EEB68.quest_subtitle: "Creative flight around your base"
	quest.2F020C2FEA6EEB68.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember the ground being optional. Around your home, it is again.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r gives creative flight to players nearby, paid for with Source. Good for base flight."
		"&eHow:&r craft the Flight tablet (check JEI), put it in the Ritual Brazier and keep the jars topped up."
		"&eTip:&r for flight everywhere, see the Angel Ring and jetpacks in Tools and Comfort."
	]
	quest.013C67CF325A6CB0.title: "Starbuncle"
	quest.013C67CF325A6CB0.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a tiny helper that moves items"
	quest.013C67CF325A6CB0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Starbuncle carries items from one chest to another. Cute logistics."
		"&eHow:&r befriend a wild Starbuncle in an Archwood forest for its charm, or check JEI. The Worn Notebook explains binding it to chests."
		"&eTip:&r Starbuncles are great for carrying Botany Pot harvests to storage."
	]
	quest.21991C2E96238C6B.title: "Apprentice Spell Book"
	quest.21991C2E96238C6B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more glyphs, bigger spells"
	quest.21991C2E96238C6B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the second spell book tier: more mana, more slots and access to tier 2 glyphs."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade your Novice book in the Enchanting Apparatus (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r more mana means longer spells and more casts between rests."
	]
	quest.6445ADA8DD3F6E25.title: "Archmage Spell Book"
	quest.6445ADA8DD3F6E25.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the top spell book"
	quest.6445ADA8DD3F6E25.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the last book tier, with tier 3 glyphs."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade the Apprentice book in the Apparatus (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r tier 3 glyphs include some of the strongest effects in the mod."
	]
	quest.2D21E70FCF3645E2.title: "Other Sourcelinks"
	quest.2D21E70FCF3645E2.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Source from crops, food, mobs or potions"
	quest.2D21E70FCF3645E2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every sourcelink feeds on a different kind of energy. Agronomic eats crop growth, Mycelial eats food, Vitalic eats mob deaths, Alchemical eats potions."
		"&eChemistry:&r all of them are the same idea in a costume: stored chemical energy (sugars, fats, potions) released and captured."
		"&eHow:&r craft any one of them (check JEI) and place it near your Source Jars."
		"&eTip:&r an Agronomic Sourcelink next to a crop farm is free Source forever."
	]
	quest.6BF1C2A90E137F34.title: "Ars Additions Charms"
	quest.6BF1C2A90E137F34.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one-shot protections in a bottle"
	quest.6BF1C2A90E137F34.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Ars Additions charms save you once from a specific danger: falling, fire, drowning, the void, or death itself."
		"&eHow:&r made in the Enchanting Apparatus around a glass bottle (the Undying Charm takes a Totem of Undying, crying obsidian and glowstone). Recharge them in the Imbuement Chamber."
		"&eTip:&r a Void Protection Charm is cheap insurance before your first trip to the End."
	]
	quest.2286BDE9BF97D7A6.title: "Handy Haversack"
	quest.2286BDE9BF97D7A6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a bag bound to a chest"
	quest.2286BDE9BF97D7A6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Handy Haversack links to a container so items you pick up go straight there."
		"&eHow:&r craft it (check JEI), then bind it to a chest or your storage as its tooltip says."
		"&eTip:&r bind it to your AE2 or Occultism storage interface for a bottomless pocket."
	]
	quest.1ADA8BE66806FEF8.title: "A Familiar"
	quest.1ADA8BE66806FEF8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a small spirit that follows you"
	quest.1ADA8BE66806FEF8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a familiar is a bound creature that rides along and gives a passive bonus: Starbuncles speed you up, Wixies boost potions, Bookwyrms cut spell costs."
		"&eHow:&r run the Ritual of Binding with the creature's charm nearby to turn it into a familiar item (the Worn Notebook has the details). Use the item to call your familiar."
		"&eTip:&r Ars Elemental adds elemental familiars (Firenando, Flashjack, Siren) that boost that school of magic."
	]
	quest.5548AB66C078F0FD.title: "Ritual of Chunk Loading"
	quest.5548AB66C078F0FD.quest_subtitle: "Optional: keep your base running"
	quest.5548AB66C078F0FD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an Ars Additions ritual that keeps its chunk loaded while it has Source."
		"&eHow:&r craft the tablet (check JEI) and run it in a Ritual Brazier next to your Source Jars."
		"&eTip:&r FTB Chunks can also force-load claimed chunks; use whichever you prefer."
	]
	quest.14B10F384B40EE79.title: "Too Cool for Logistics"
	quest.14B10F384B40EE79.quest_subtitle: "Secret: sunglasses for a Starbuncle"
	quest.14B10F384B40EE79.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember having servants who took themselves very seriously. This one does not.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Starbuncle Shades: tinted glass and a source gem. Give them to a Starbuncle."
		"&eTip:&r they do nothing useful. That is the point."
	]
	quest.1AF72DB24D1FCA5A.title: "Wilden Hunt"
	quest.1AF72DB24D1FCA5A.quest_subtitle: "Kill 5 Wilden Hunters"
	quest.1AF72DB24D1FCA5A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Wilden are Ars Nouveau's wild magical beasts. Hunters charge, Stalkers fly, Guardians throw spikes."
		"&eHow:&r they roam the Overworld at night, more often near archwood forests and Wilden dens. Bring a shield."
		"&eTip:&r keep every horn, spike and wing they drop. Rituals need them."
	]
	quest.58D4B5ED67D6FE13.title: "Wilden Wings"
	quest.58D4B5ED67D6FE13.quest_subtitle: "The key ingredient for flight"
	quest.58D4B5ED67D6FE13.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Wilden Wings drop from Wilden Stalkers, the flying ones."
		"&eHow:&r hunt Stalkers at night. The Ritual of Flight tablet needs three wings (purple archwood log, 3 wings, 2 diamonds, an ender pearl)."
		"&eTip:&r a Ritual of Wilden Summoning will need three more Wilden drops, so keep hunting."
	]
	quest.5647205E4092E13E.title: "The Wilden Chimera"
	quest.5647205E4092E13E.quest_subtitle: "Summon and slay Ars Nouveau's boss"
	quest.5647205E4092E13E.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember beasts that were many beasts at once. You remember winning.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Wilden Chimera combines all three Wilden. It drops Wilden Tribute, used for Ars Elemental's Mark of Mastery."
		"&eHow:&r craft the Ritual of Wilden Summoning (purple archwood log, 3 Wilden drops, a lapis block), place it in a brazier away from your base, and fight."
		"&eTip:&r it has phases and calls spikes from the ground. Keep moving and bring healing."
	]
	quest.0ED371501E3635D7.title: "Mark of Mastery"
	quest.0ED371501E3635D7.quest_subtitle: "Ars Elemental's upgrade token"
	quest.0ED371501E3635D7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Mark of Mastery upgrades elemental foci and turns Arcanist armor into elemental mage armor."
		"&eHow:&r imbue a Wilden Tribute with all seven essences plus anima essence (check JEI). One tribute gives five marks."
		"&eTip:&r anima essence comes from imbuing a source gem with a wither skeleton skull, bone meal and a golden apple."
	]
	quest.68F810DE695926AB.title: "Lesser Elemental Focus"
	quest.68F810DE695926AB.quest_subtitle: "Pick an element and specialise"
	quest.68F810DE695926AB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an Ars Elemental focus is a curio that strengthens one school of spells (fire, water, earth or air) and lowers its cost."
		"&eChemistry:&r the four classical elements were the first attempt at a periodic table. You know there are 118, but the spells don't."
		"&eHow:&r in the Imbuement Chamber: an amethyst shard with 3 matching essences and 3 gold ingots on pedestals."
		"&eTip:&r choose the school your favourite spell uses most."
	]
	quest.49C42FE354691DD3.title: "Greater Elemental Focus"
	quest.49C42FE354691DD3.quest_subtitle: "Master an element"
	quest.49C42FE354691DD3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the full focus gives a much bigger bonus to its school and protects you from matching hazards."
		"&eHow:&r put the lesser focus in the Enchanting Apparatus with a Mark of Mastery on a pedestal (5,000 Source)."
		"&eTip:&r a fire focus pairs well with Ignite and Flare; a water focus with Watery Grave."
	]
	quest.4404A38C2E79830C.title: "Mage Armor"
	quest.4404A38C2E79830C.quest_subtitle: "Armor that stores mana"
	quest.4404A38C2E79830C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Ars Nouveau armor comes in three styles (Sorcerer, Arcanist, Battlemage). Each piece adds mana and mana regeneration."
		"&eHow:&r made in the Enchanting Apparatus around a golden armor piece with magebloom fiber (check JEI for each style)."
		"&eTip:&r grow magebloom early; every piece needs fiber."
	]
	quest.2A18E9D2794B3941.title: "Armor Tiers"
	quest.2A18E9D2794B3941.quest_subtitle: "Upgrade mage armor in the Apparatus"
	quest.2A18E9D2794B3941.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r mage armor has three tiers. Each tier raises mana and opens more thread slots."
		"&eHow:&r place the armor in the Enchanting Apparatus with the upgrade items on pedestals: tier 2 needs blaze rods, tier 3 needs more (check JEI under 'armor upgrade')."
		"&eTip:&r threads go into the Alteration Table: Spellpower, Magic Capacity, Repairing and more. Click the checkmark once you've upgraded a piece."
	]
	quest.64B3AC170A838184.title: "Elemental Mage Armor"
	quest.64B3AC170A838184.quest_subtitle: "Optional: armor of a single element"
	quest.64B3AC170A838184.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Ars Elemental turns Arcanist armor into fire, water, earth or air armor, each with resistances and a spell bonus."
		"&eHow:&r in the Enchanting Apparatus: an Arcanist piece plus a Mark of Mastery, a netherite ingot and two matching essences (7,000 Source)."
		"&eTip:&r a full set matching your focus makes that school very cheap to cast."
	]
	quest.0A8282FFFAA50AE1.title: "Two Roads to the Sky"
	quest.0A8282FFFAA50AE1.quest_subtitle: "Optional: how Ars flight fits the pack"
	quest.0A8282FFFAA50AE1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a note on the Ritual of Flight and the pack's other flight sources."
		"&eHow:&r read the second page, then click the checkmark."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eRitual of Flight:&r the tablet is a purple archwood log, 3 Wilden Wings, 2 diamonds and an ender pearl. Ars Elemental adds a second recipe: a flashing (yellow) archwood log, 1 wing, 2 diamonds and a feather."
		"&eRange:&r the ritual only grants flight near its brazier and drains Source while you fly. It's base flight, not world flight."
		"&eElsewhere:&r the Infusion Pylon with a Potion of Flying (hydrogen from the Dissolver), Iron Jetpacks (MI circuits) and the Angel Ring (digital circuit) all work anywhere. See Tools and Comfort."
	]
	chapter.5BBA2E199EC82256.title: "Apotheosis"
	chapter.5BBA2E199EC82256.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Affix loot, gems, enchanting beyond level 30, spawners and Gateways."
	]
	quest.0823E0B0B994DD08.title: "Gem Dust"
	quest.0823E0B0B994DD08.quest_subtitle: "The currency of Apotheosis"
	quest.0823E0B0B994DD08.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Apotheosis gear can roll affixes and sockets. Gems drop from mobs and chests; gem dust builds its tables."
		"&eHow:&r crush spare gems into gem dust (JEI shows how)."
		"&eTip:&r keep good gems for sockets and crush the rest."
	]
	quest.6E58E2BD59CFAE57.title: "Simple Reforging"
	quest.6E58E2BD59CFAE57.quest_subtitle: "Reroll an item's affixes"
	quest.6E58E2BD59CFAE57.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Simple Reforging Table rerolls affixes on gear of lower rarities."
		"&eHow:&r an enchanting table, iron, smooth stone and gem dust."
		"&eTip:&r reforging costs rarity materials; salvage junk gear to get them."
	]
	quest.57C95E565D3B2119.title: "Salvaging"
	quest.57C95E565D3B2119.quest_subtitle: "Junk gear into rarity materials"
	quest.57C95E565D3B2119.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Salvaging Table breaks affixed gear into materials of its rarity."
		"&eHow:&r a smithing table, iron tools, copper, a lava bucket and gem dust (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r every affixed sword you don't want is a reforge for one you do."
	]
	quest.629C34B0AC068654.title: "Gem Cutting"
	quest.629C34B0AC068654.quest_subtitle: "Combine gems into higher purities"
	quest.629C34B0AC068654.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Gem Cutting Table upgrades gems to higher purity using matching gems and dust."
		"&eChemistry:&r real gems are cut along cleavage planes, flat directions where the crystal's bonds are weakest."
		"&eHow:&r planks, smooth stone, shears and gem dust."
	]
	quest.153E1F2212F6740C.title: "Divine Reforging"
	quest.153E1F2212F6740C.quest_subtitle: "Reforge any rarity, up to mythic"
	quest.153E1F2212F6740C.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember weapons that chose their wielders. These at least choose good affixes.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the full Reforging Table handles every rarity, up to mythic gear."
		"&eHow:&r the Simple Reforging Table, netherite, nether bricks and arcane sands (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.563D61599C12CF41.title: "Better Bookshelves"
	quest.563D61599C12CF41.quest_subtitle: "Optional: push enchanting past level 30"
	quest.563D61599C12CF41.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Apothic Enchanting adds shelves that raise enchanting power, quanta and arcana. Hellshelves are the first step."
		"&eHow:&r bookshelves, nether bricks and a blaze rod. Create: Enchantment Industry can automate enchanting later."
		"&eTip:&r enchanting power above 30 unlocks enchantments beyond vanilla levels."
	]
	quest.12EF5F7791329CED.title: "Sigil of Socketing"
	quest.12EF5F7791329CED.quest_subtitle: "Optional: add a socket to any gear"
	quest.12EF5F7791329CED.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r adds a socket to gear in a smithing table, so you can slot in a gem."
		"&eHow:&r gem-fused slate, amethyst, gunpowder and gem dust (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a Sigil of Withdrawal pulls gems back out later."
	]
	quest.0C78BE8ECFF1CD59.title: "Augmenting"
	quest.0C78BE8ECFF1CD59.quest_subtitle: "Optional: upgrade and reroll single affixes"
	quest.0C78BE8ECFF1CD59.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Augmenting Table improves or rerolls one affix at a time."
		"&eHow:&r an enchanting table, a Nether Star, a godforged pearl and polished blackstone (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r save it for gear you plan to keep for the rest of the game."
	]
	quest.124C0733D11EE060.title: "Bottled Monsters"
	quest.124C0733D11EE060.quest_subtitle: "Optional: mine a spawner with Silk Touch"
	quest.124C0733D11EE060.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r with Apothic Spawners a monster spawner can be picked up with a Silk Touch pickaxe and moved home."
		"&eHow:&r find one in a dungeon or mineshaft, light it up, then mine it with Silk Touch. Check its tooltip after placing."
		"&eTip:&r spawners are mob farms for drops you can't make chemically: bones, string, ender pearls, blaze rods."
	]
	quest.4175DD97D428CAF7.title: "Spawner Runes"
	quest.4175DD97D428CAF7.quest_subtitle: "Optional: rewrite a spawner's rules"
	quest.4175DD97D428CAF7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r spawner runes change a spawner when you right-click it: spawn without players nearby, obey redstone, set mobs on fire, stay silent, and more."
		"&eHow:&r a basic Spawner Rune is gem dust, gem-fused slate and spawner chains (check JEI for where chains come from). Each modifier rune adds one item, like campfires for Burning."
		"&eTip:&r Redstone Control first, so you can switch the farm off when you don't need it."
	]
	quest.29B876259D4B5686.title: "Elite Hunting"
	quest.29B876259D4B5686.quest_subtitle: "Kill 50 zombies and watch for affix gear"
	quest.29B876259D4B5686.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Apotheosis gives some monsters affixed gear and makes rare elites with a coloured name. Their drops can roll affixes and sockets."
		"&eHow:&r kill 50 zombies. Pick up any named or glowing item they drop and read its tooltip."
		"&eTip:&r elites hit hard. Gear up before poking one with a stick."
	]
	quest.1F426EE32EDF30C4.title: "Potion Charm"
	quest.1F426EE32EDF30C4.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a potion that never runs out (almost)"
	quest.1F426EE32EDF30C4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Potion Charm holds a potion effect and applies it while switched on, using durability."
		"&eChemistry:&r blaze powder is a reactive powder; here it fixes the potion so it lasts, a bit like a preservative."
		"&eHow:&r three identical potions in the middle row and six blaze powder around them. Infusing it later makes it permanent (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r Night Vision or Haste charms are the most useful early."
	]
	quest.645E6EA4F2C67FAB.title: "Rarity Materials"
	quest.645E6EA4F2C67FAB.quest_subtitle: "Scrap, fabric, crystal, sand, pearl"
	quest.645E6EA4F2C67FAB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each rarity salvages into its own material: common scrap metal, uncommon timeworn fabric, rare luminous crystal, epic arcane sands, mythic godforged pearls."
		"&eHow:&r salvage rare (blue) gear in the Salvaging Table until you have 4 luminous crystal shards."
		"&eTip:&r reforging uses the material of that rarity, so sort your loot by colour before salvaging."
	]
	quest.30908A094F9B094F.title: "Gate Pearl"
	quest.30908A094F9B094F.quest_subtitle: "Gateways to Eternity: a wave-based arena"
	quest.30908A094F9B094F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Gate Pearl opens a Gateway that releases waves of a chosen mob. Beat every wave for rewards."
		"&eHow:&r the Blaze gate is five blaze rods, an ender pearl and three nether bricks. Apotheosis adds tiered gates (Frontier and up); JEI shows them all."
		"&eTip:&r a gate is a controlled mob farm: blaze rods, ender pearls and XP on demand."
	]
	quest.29DC8827585EFBB8.title: "Close a Gateway"
	quest.29DC8827585EFBB8.quest_subtitle: "Survive every wave"
	quest.29DC8827585EFBB8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the gateway closes when every wave is defeated and pays out its reward."
		"&eHow:&r throw the pearl in an open area, stay close (leaving fails the gate) and kill each wave. Click the checkmark when it closes."
		"&eTip:&r tiered Apotheosis gates hand out affix gear and rarity materials."
	]
	quest.0E850BA9288D13B8.title: "Sigil of Withdrawal"
	quest.0E850BA9288D13B8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: get your gems back"
	quest.0E850BA9288D13B8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r pulls every gem out of an item without destroying them, so a good gem can move to new gear."
		"&eHow:&r gem-fused slate, blaze rods, ender pearls, a lava bucket and gem dust (makes 4)."
		"&eTip:&r withdraw gems before salvaging or reforging old gear."
	]
	quest.074EDD3891190AD6.title: "Sigil of Enhancement"
	quest.074EDD3891190AD6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: raise a gem's rarity"
	quest.074EDD3891190AD6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r upgrades a socketed gem to the next rarity at the Reforging Table."
		"&eHow:&r gem-fused slate, gem dust and a godforged pearl (makes 4). Godforged pearls come from salvaging mythic gear."
		"&eTip:&r save these for gems you'll keep: a mythic gem in endgame gear is worth it."
	]
	quest.0DA470EE8E63A89F.title: "Infusion"
	quest.0DA470EE8E63A89F.quest_subtitle: "Enchant a block instead of a tool"
	quest.0DA470EE8E63A89F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Apothic Enchanting can 'infuse' items: enchanting a hellshelf at the right power makes an Infused Hellshelf."
		"&eHow:&r put a hellshelf in the enchanting table with enough shelves around it. JEI's infusion page shows the exact Eterna, Quanta and Arcana it needs."
		"&eTip:&r the table's three stats are shown on the screen: power, randomness and how many extra enchantments you get."
	]
	quest.67476A5068C80199.title: "Enchantment Library"
	quest.67476A5068C80199.quest_subtitle: "Store every enchanted book"
	quest.67476A5068C80199.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Library absorbs enchanted books and stores their enchantments as points, then pulls out any level you've collected."
		"&eHow:&r four ender chests, four infused shelves and an enchanting table."
		"&eTip:&r it only gives back levels up to the highest single book you fed it, so feed it every spare book."
	]
	quest.2103D96D8A9B8008.title: "Endshelves"
	quest.2103D96D8A9B8008.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the strongest shelf family"
	quest.2103D96D8A9B8008.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r endshelves push enchanting power past what hellshelves and seashelves allow."
		"&eHow:&r end stone bricks, a bookshelf, an ender pearl and Infused Breath (dragon's breath infused at the enchanting table)."
		"&eTip:&r collect dragon's breath in glass bottles during the Ender Dragon fight."
	]
	quest.742D6F656F7BFD9B.title: "Scrap Tome"
	quest.742D6F656F7BFD9B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: recycle enchanted gear"
	quest.742D6F656F7BFD9B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Scrap Tome in an anvil with enchanted gear strips off some of its enchantments into a book (the gear is destroyed)."
		"&eHow:&r eight books around an anvil makes eight tomes."
		"&eTip:&r the Extraction Tome (infused) keeps the item; check JEI's infusion page."
	]
	chapter.37F569BC21D75E5E.title: "Relics and Artifacts"
	chapter.37F569BC21D75E5E.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Found treasures and crafted curios: Relics, Artifacts and Reliquary."
	]
	quest.2CAD2D054CB09ACA.title: "Relics"
	quest.2CAD2D054CB09ACA.quest_subtitle: "Reliquary, Relics and Artifacts"
	quest.2CAD2D054CB09ACA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r three mods of found and crafted treasures. Reliquary items are crafted from mob parts; Relics and Artifacts hide in chests and structures."
		"&eHow:&r mob charm fragments drop from mobs. JEI shows the charm they build."
		"&eTip:&r a Mob Charm stops that mob type attacking you."
	]
	quest.66B6DA99BDA6AD30.title: "Alkahestry Tome"
	quest.66B6DA99BDA6AD30.quest_subtitle: "The alchemists' dream, in book form"
	quest.66B6DA99BDA6AD30.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r charged with redstone, the tome duplicates common items in a crafting grid."
		"&eChemistry:&r alchemists searched for alkahest, a universal solvent. None exists (what would you keep it in?), but aqua regia, HCl + HNO₃, dissolves even gold."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the tome and its recipes. Recharge it with redstone."
	]
	quest.43308A673FF653BF.title: "Relic Hunter"
	quest.43308A673FF653BF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: find a relic or an artifact"
	quest.43308A673FF653BF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r find any Relics or Artifacts item: a cloud in a bottle, running shoes, a leafy mantle, a mimic's treasure."
		"&eHow:&r loot chests in dungeons, mineshafts and towers, and beware chests that bite. Click the checkmark when you have one."
		"&eTip:&r Relics items level up as you use them; check their tooltips."
	]
	quest.08F23BEDD14FD31D.title: "Fortune Coin"
	quest.08F23BEDD14FD31D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a magnet in your pocket"
	quest.08F23BEDD14FD31D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r pulls nearby items and XP toward you while active."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Right-click to toggle it."
		"&eTip:&r turn it off near your sorting system or it'll grab the items."
	]
	quest.65639548C2C2E03A.title: "A True Relic"
	quest.65639548C2C2E03A.quest_subtitle: "Find any item from the Relics mod"
	quest.65639548C2C2E03A.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember owning things no mortal smith made. A few of them seem to have survived.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Relics are found, never crafted: mantles, belts, necklaces, boots, a chef's hat, a ring of the seven deadly sins. Each has abilities that grow with use."
		"&eHow:&r loot chests in dungeons, mineshafts, temples, villages and modded structures. Any one relic completes this quest."
		"&eTip:&r read the tooltip: each relic says what it does and how it gains experience."
	]
	quest.1C39B10303C8A4FB.title: "Relic Growth"
	quest.1C39B10303C8A4FB.quest_subtitle: "Optional: level up a relic"
	quest.1C39B10303C8A4FB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r relics earn experience when you use their abilities, and their levels make those abilities stronger."
		"&eHow:&r keep the relic equipped and use it. Open its ability screen (the tooltip names the key) to spend levels. Click the checkmark after your first upgrade."
		"&eTip:&r one well-levelled relic beats a drawer full of new ones."
	]
	quest.155D611580258963.title: "An Artifact"
	quest.155D611580258963.quest_subtitle: "Find any item from the Artifacts mod"
	quest.155D611580258963.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Artifacts are simple, always-on curios: Running Shoes, Cloud in a Bottle, Digging Claws, a Lucky Scarf, Night Vision Goggles and many more."
		"&eHow:&r found in chests underground and in structures, and dropped by Mimics. Any one artifact completes this quest."
		"&eTip:&r a Cloud in a Bottle (double jump) and Running Shoes make early exploring much easier."
	]
	quest.138734AE1F0C3A87.title: "That Chest Has Teeth"
	quest.138734AE1F0C3A87.quest_subtitle: "Kill a Mimic"
	quest.138734AE1F0C3A87.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Mimic looks exactly like a chest until you open it. It always drops an artifact."
		"&eHow:&r they hide in mineshafts, dungeons and caves. If a chest stands somewhere odd, hit it before opening it."
		"&eTip:&r Mimics are tough for their size; fight one with real armor, not a wooden sword."
	]
	quest.73D8CBFF0B71205A.title: "Divine Comedy"
	quest.73D8CBFF0B71205A.quest_subtitle: "Secret: the least dignified artifact"
	quest.73D8CBFF0B71205A.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember the other gods laughing at something like this. You never admitted it was you.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Whoopee Cushion. Equip it and crouch."
		"&eTip:&r it does exactly what you think."
	]
	quest.344B4E30A304E85A.title: "Mob Ingredients"
	quest.344B4E30A304E85A.quest_subtitle: "Hearts, ribs, glands and pearls"
	quest.344B4E30A304E85A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Reliquary items are built from rare mob parts: zombie hearts, rib bones, catalyzing glands, slime pearls, molten cores and more."
		"&eHow:&r they drop from their mobs (zombies drop zombie hearts). In this pack they can also be crafted: a zombie heart is rotten flesh in a ring of iron ingots."
		"&eTip:&r a Looting sword makes the drops much more common than the iron recipe."
	]
	quest.77C7E8214CABA7DB.title: "Mob Charm Belt"
	quest.77C7E8214CABA7DB.quest_subtitle: "Wear all your charms at once"
	quest.77C7E8214CABA7DB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the belt holds Mob Charms, so you can be ignored by several mob types at once."
		"&eHow:&r three leather and five mob charm fragments (check JEI). Each fragment is made from that mob's drops."
		"&eTip:&r creeper and enderman charms are the most valuable around a base."
	]
	quest.1B9288F0EB08F5B2.title: "Void Tear"
	quest.1B9288F0EB08F5B2.quest_subtitle: "A pocket that holds one item type"
	quest.1B9288F0EB08F5B2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Void Tear stores a huge stack of one item, and pulls more of it from your inventory."
		"&eHow:&r a ghast tear, a nebulous heart, a slime pearl and lapis (shapeless)."
		"&eTip:&r it's also an ingredient for the Infernal Tear, Emperor's Chalice and Midas Touchstone."
	]
	quest.7C823E959B36BA96.title: "Lantern of Paranoia"
	quest.7C823E959B36BA96.quest_subtitle: "Optional: it places torches for you"
	quest.7C823E959B36BA96.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the lantern places torches from your inventory wherever it's dark enough for mobs to spawn."
		"&eHow:&r iron ingots, glass, a slime pearl and a molten core (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r carry a stack of torches when caving and let it do the lighting."
	]
	quest.37897CAA67020AFC.title: "The Handgun"
	quest.37897CAA67020AFC.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Reliquary's magic pistol"
	quest.37897CAA67020AFC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a pistol that fires magazines of special bullets: neutral, exorcism, blaze, ender, storm, seeker and more."
		"&eHow:&r barrel, grip and hammer assemblies plus iron and a slime pearl. Bullets and magazines have their own recipes (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r Seeker bullets home in on targets; good against flying mobs."
	]
	quest.064A1813B7F32692.title: "Phoenix Down"
	quest.064A1813B7F32692.quest_subtitle: "Optional: cheat death several times"
	quest.064A1813B7F32692.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r saves you from death, heals you, and gives you a few seconds of protection. It has several charges."
		"&eHow:&r three Angelheart Vials and an Angelic Feather. Vials need milk, glass, fertile essence and an infernal claw (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep it in your inventory before boss fights and Nether trips."
	]
	chapter.717248739CAC3545.title: "Occultism"
	chapter.717248739CAC3545.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Spirits, pentacles, otherworld storage and miners that dig where you can't."
	]
	quest.5F9B839BB34A9A16.title: "Demon's Dream"
	quest.5F9B839BB34A9A16.quest_subtitle: "Eat it and see the Otherworld"
	quest.5F9B839BB34A9A16.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember seeing everything at once. One bite, and some of it comes back.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r eating Demon's Dream Fruit gives the Third Eye: you see Otherworld blocks hidden behind normal ones."
		"&eHow:&r break grass for Demon's Dream seeds, grow them, and eat a fruit. The Dictionary of Spirits explains the rest."
		"&eTip:&r with the Third Eye active, otherworld trees appear among normal oaks."
	]
	quest.0CBD62BC2D8578CE.title: "Your First Pentacle"
	quest.0CBD62BC2D8578CE.quest_subtitle: "Chalk, bowls and a circle"
	quest.0CBD62BC2D8578CE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r rituals happen on chalk pentacles, with a Golden Ritual Bowl at the centre and Sacrificial Bowls holding the ingredients."
		"&eChemistry:&r real chalk is calcium carbonate, CaCO₃: the shells of tiny sea creatures, pressed into rock."
		"&eHow:&r impure chalk from otherstone and otherworld wood dust, purified in Spiritfire. The Dictionary shows each pentacle's layout."
	]
	quest.34926D9EB18DDD3C.title: "Bind a Foliot"
	quest.34926D9EB18DDD3C.quest_subtitle: "Learn a spirit's true name"
	quest.34926D9EB18DDD3C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a bound Book of Binding holds a spirit's name and starts its rituals. Foliots are the weakest spirits."
		"&eHow:&r craft the Book of Binding (taboo book, purified ink, awakened feather), then bind it as the Dictionary describes."
		"&eTip:&r foliots can sort items, chop trees or farm for you."
	]
	quest.1668E0C4B6468525.title: "Iesnium"
	quest.1668E0C4B6468525.quest_subtitle: "An Otherworld metal from the Nether"
	quest.1668E0C4B6468525.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r iesnium ore hides in the Nether and only shows up with the Third Eye. You need an infused pickaxe to mine it."
		"&eHow:&r spirit-attuned gems (a diamond in Spiritfire) make the infused pickaxe. Smelt the ore."
		"&eTip:&r iesnium tools and the miner spirits come next."
	]
	quest.6E0E0CD99AFBE407.title: "Spirit Miners"
	quest.6E0E0CD99AFBE407.quest_subtitle: "A spirit digs in a world you can't see"
	quest.6E0E0CD99AFBE407.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Dimensional Mineshaft holds a miner spirit that pulls ores from the Otherworld over time."
		"&eHow:&r both come from rituals (check the Dictionary and JEI). The miner needs an iesnium pickaxe and a magic lamp."
		"&eTip:&r in this pack miners &ccan't&r produce chemistry-milestone ores: uranium, uraninite, osmium, fluorite, platinum, iridium or tungsten. Those still come from real processing."
	]
	quest.3573C8631E3C0C8D.title: "Surprisingly Large Bag"
	quest.3573C8631E3C0C8D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a foliot lives in your backpack"
	quest.3573C8631E3C0C8D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a satchel with a bound foliot inside that keeps it bigger on the inside."
		"&eHow:&r a foliot crafting ritual: a chest, two leather, string and a silver ingot around the golden bowl (check the Dictionary for the pentacle)."
		"&eTip:&r the Dictionary lists the other foliot rituals: lumberjack, farmer, cleaner and item transporter."
	]
	quest.1CF5C54EFC2D1E7E.title: "The Wild Hunt"
	quest.1CF5C54EFC2D1E7E.quest_subtitle: "Kill 5 Wild Hunt wither skeletons"
	quest.1CF5C54EFC2D1E7E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Wild Hunt ritual calls a pack of wither skeletons with a good chance of dropping wither skeleton skulls."
		"&eHow:&r activated with a skeleton skull; it needs copper, silver and gold blocks, a diamond, netherrack and soul sand, plus a sacrifice (check the Dictionary). Then fight."
		"&eTip:&r this is the easiest way to collect three skulls for the Wither."
	]
	quest.312300639D5FB8C9.title: "Bind a Djinni"
	quest.312300639D5FB8C9.quest_subtitle: "A stronger spirit for bigger rituals"
	quest.312300639D5FB8C9.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember spirits who bowed when you passed. This one only negotiates.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r djinn are the second rank of spirits. Their rituals make storage, soul gems, familiar rings and better miners."
		"&eHow:&r craft a Book of Binding (Djinni), then bind it with the spirit's name, the same way as the foliot (the Dictionary explains it)."
		"&eTip:&r djinni pentacles are bigger; check each layout in the Dictionary before placing chalk."
	]
	quest.1AB48F1F7BE43200.title: "Dimensional Matrix"
	quest.1AB48F1F7BE43200.quest_subtitle: "The heart of Occultism storage"
	quest.1AB48F1F7BE43200.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Dimensional Matrix binds a djinni to hold items in a pocket dimension."
		"&eChemistry:&r the quartz it needs is SiO₂, the same crystal that keeps time in a real watch by vibrating at a fixed frequency."
		"&eHow:&r a djinni crafting ritual with three quartz blocks and an ender pearl."
	]
	quest.4546FB3608214B1A.title: "Storage Actuator"
	quest.4546FB3608214B1A.quest_subtitle: "A whole warehouse in one block"
	quest.4546FB3608214B1A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Dimensional Storage Actuator stores thousands of items and shows them in one searchable screen."
		"&eHow:&r a foliot ritual makes the Storage Actuator Base (otherstone pedestal, copper, gold). Put the matrix on top of the base in a crafting grid."
		"&eTip:&r it's an alternative to AE2 for early storage. Stabilizers expand it."
	]
	quest.39B0D17ED843DF29.title: "Storage Stabilizers"
	quest.39B0D17ED843DF29.quest_subtitle: "More room for the warehouse"
	quest.39B0D17ED843DF29.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r stabilizers pointed at the Actuator raise how many items and item types it holds."
		"&eHow:&r tier 1 is a foliot ritual: a tier 0 stabilizer, a copper block, blaze dust and a spirit-attuned gem. Higher tiers need stronger spirits."
		"&eTip:&r place them within a few blocks, facing the Actuator."
	]
	quest.7BF2913DF4513A2E.title: "Storage Remote"
	quest.7BF2913DF4513A2E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: your storage in your pocket"
	quest.7BF2913DF4513A2E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r opens your Storage Actuator from anywhere."
		"&eHow:&r a djinni ritual with an inert remote, two ender pearls and quartz. Link it to the Actuator by clicking it."
		"&eTip:&r one remote per player saves a lot of walking back to base."
	]
	quest.30756D89D79CE096.title: "Soul Gem"
	quest.30756D89D79CE096.quest_subtitle: "Optional: carry a mob around"
	quest.30756D89D79CE096.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Soul Gem traps a living creature so you can move it and release it elsewhere."
		"&eHow:&r a djinni ritual: a diamond, copper, silver and gold ingots, a fragile soul gem and soul sand."
		"&eTip:&r it's the easy way to move villagers or animals to your base."
	]
	quest.3B705B3C46B4208C.title: "Familiar Ring"
	quest.3B705B3C46B4208C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: wear your familiar"
	quest.3B705B3C46B4208C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r familiars are summoned with rituals (greedy, bat, beaver, deer, blacksmith...). The ring stores one so it travels with you."
		"&eHow:&r a djinni ritual with a soul gem, two gold and two silver ingots. Capture your familiar with it."
		"&eTip:&r the Greedy Familiar picks up items for you. The Dictionary lists what each familiar does."
	]
	quest.1E72E45C7693EAF9.title: "Djinni Miner"
	quest.1E72E45C7693EAF9.quest_subtitle: "A faster miner that only brings ores"
	quest.1E72E45C7693EAF9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the djinni miner skips the stone and pulls only ores, much faster than a foliot."
		"&eHow:&r a djinni ritual with the foliot miner, an iesnium pickaxe, gold, lapis and a spirit-attuned crystal."
		"&eTip:&r the pack's ban list still applies: no uranium, uraninite, osmium, fluorite, platinum, iridium or tungsten."
	]
	quest.5E236E6AE2C06A35.title: "Bind an Afrit"
	quest.5E236E6AE2C06A35.quest_subtitle: "A spirit of fire"
	quest.5E236E6AE2C06A35.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r afrits are the third rank of spirits. They power stronger rituals and the deep-mining miner."
		"&eHow:&r craft a Book of Binding (Afrit) and bind it with the spirit's name (see the Dictionary)."
		"&eTip:&r afrit rituals often need afrit essence, which only an unbound afrit drops."
	]
	quest.2A9367B90A0DFF1B.title: "Unbound Afrit"
	quest.2A9367B90A0DFF1B.quest_subtitle: "Summon a wild afrit and defeat it"
	quest.2A9367B90A0DFF1B.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember fire that obeyed. This one remembers being free.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Summon Unbound Afrit ritual calls a hostile afrit. It drops afrit essence when killed."
		"&eHow:&r netherrack, an iesnium ingot, flint and steel and gunpowder, plus a cow as the sacrifice. Build the pentacle far from anything flammable."
		"&eTip:&r fire resistance potions turn this from a disaster into a fair fight."
	]
	chapter.53DC761A27800BDC.title: "Equivalent Exchange"
	chapter.53DC761A27800BDC.chapter_subtitle: [
		"A builder's toy for a demigod who has already mastered the elements."
	]
	quest.202454706F0D6586.title: "The Philosopher's Stone"
	quest.202454706F0D6586.quest_subtitle: "Oganesson, at the heart of an old legend"
	quest.202454706F0D6586.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember turning one thing into another with a thought. Now you know what it really costs.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Philosopher's Stone transmutes blocks in the world and is the key to every ProjectE item."
		"&eChemistry:&r alchemists spent centuries looking for a stone that turns lead into gold. Real transmutation needs a nuclear reaction, and you've already done that: it's how you made oganesson."
		"&eHow:&r redstone dust and glowstone dust in a ring around one oganesson (this pack's recipe)."
		"&eTip:&r it isn't used up in crafting recipes, so one stone lasts forever."
	]
	quest.5DF0000BBA218F93.title: "World Transmutation"
	quest.5DF0000BBA218F93.quest_subtitle: "Right-click to reshape the land"
	quest.5DF0000BBA218F93.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r right-click a block with the stone to turn it into a related block: stone and cobblestone, dirt, grass and sand, one wood or flower type into the next."
		"&eHow:&r an outline shows what will change before you click; sneak-click for the reverse direction. ProjectE's keybinds change the area size and shape."
		"&eTip:&r a whole hillside of stone into cobblestone (or back) takes seconds. Click the checkmark once you've tried it."
	]
	quest.7FE06D3B05479258.title: "Transmutation Table"
	quest.7FE06D3B05479258.quest_subtitle: "Learn a block once, make it forever"
	quest.7FE06D3B05479258.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Transmutation Table turns items into EMC and EMC back into any item you've learned."
		"&eHow:&r four obsidian in the corners, four stone on the sides, the Philosopher's Stone in the centre."
		"&eTip:&r your EMC and your learned items belong to you, not the table: every table you open shows the same list."
	]
	quest.7AA96CF99DD2EA9A.title: "Burn to Learn"
	quest.7AA96CF99DD2EA9A.quest_subtitle: "What EMC can and can't do here"
	quest.7AA96CF99DD2EA9A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r placing an item in the table's burn slot destroys it, adds its EMC to your total and teaches you that item."
		"&eHow:&r burn a stack of something cheap (cobblestone, logs, sand), then try to burn an iron ingot. The ingot has no EMC, so it can't be learned."
		"&eTip:&r stone, wood, glass, terracotta, wool and other building materials all work. Click the checkmark when you understand the rule."
	]
	quest.18B513C9D4D8674F.title: "Covalence Dust"
	quest.18B513C9D4D8674F.quest_subtitle: "ProjectE's crafting dusts"
	quest.18B513C9D4D8674F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r three dusts used for ProjectE storage and repairs."
		"&eChemistry:&r a covalent bond is two atoms sharing electrons. The name fits: these dusts bind items together."
		"&eHow:&r low: charcoal and 8 cobblestone. Medium: an iron ingot and redstone. High: a diamond and coal. Each recipe makes 40."
		"&eTip:&r covalence dust repairs tools in a crafting grid: the matching dust for the tool's material."
	]
	quest.042E22483673AC0E.title: "Alchemical Chest"
	quest.042E22483673AC0E.quest_subtitle: "A big chest for ProjectE items"
	quest.042E22483673AC0E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a large chest, and the base of the Alchemical Bag."
		"&eHow:&r one of each covalence dust on top, stone, a diamond and stone in the middle, iron, a chest and iron on the bottom."
	]
	quest.170DD0614698F425.title: "Alchemical Bag"
	quest.170DD0614698F425.quest_subtitle: "The same inventory everywhere you go"
	quest.170DD0614698F425.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an Alchemical Bag shares its inventory with every bag of the same colour you own."
		"&eHow:&r three high covalence dust on top, wool on each side of an Alchemical Chest, and three wool below. Dye the wool for a different colour."
		"&eTip:&r keep one colour for building blocks so your supplies follow you between builds."
	]
	quest.50BE1EFCA730933B.title: "Repair Talisman"
	quest.50BE1EFCA730933B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: slowly mends your gear"
	quest.50BE1EFCA730933B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r while it's in your inventory it slowly repairs your damaged tools and armor."
		"&eHow:&r covalence dusts, string and paper (check JEI for the pattern)."
	]
	quest.4435E0CBCBF45F67.title: "Transmutation Tablet"
	quest.4435E0CBCBF45F67.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the table, in your pocket"
	quest.4435E0CBCBF45F67.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a portable Transmutation Table."
		"&eHow:&r four Dark Matter blocks, four stone and a Transmutation Table. That's sixteen Dark Matter: a real project."
		"&eTip:&r worth it for big builds far from home."
	]
	quest.5C6F6C15DC731192.title: "The Law of Conservation"
	quest.5C6F6C15DC731192.quest_subtitle: "Why you can't conjure metal"
	quest.5C6F6C15DC731192.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r in this pack, EMC works on building blocks only. Metals, gems, dusts, ores and plates have no EMC."
		"&eHow:&r read the second page, then click the checkmark."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eThe rule:&r ProjectE normally gives every item an EMC value, so a pile of cobblestone can become diamonds. In a chemistry pack that would skip everything you've built."
		"&eChemistry:&r matter isn't created or destroyed in a chemical reaction (Lavoisier, 1789). Iron comes from iron oxide, Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂. Copper comes from its ores. Gold comes from anode sludge and aqua regia. You can rearrange atoms; you can't conjure them."
		"&eSo:&r ingots, nuggets, raw ores, dusts, gems, plates, gears, rods, wires and storage blocks are set to EMC 0. Nether Stars, the Dragon Egg and the Beacon are 0 too, because the Seed of a New World needs them."
		"&eAlso removed:&r Energy Condensers, Collectors and Relays. They turn EMC into unlimited items or power."
		"&eWhat's left:&r a terraforming and building tool. Stone, wood, glass, sand, dirt and decoration are what a demigod reshapes the world with, and those still have EMC."
	]
	quest.3EBFBBF5E8D82173.title: "Alchemical Coal"
	quest.3EBFBBF5E8D82173.quest_subtitle: "Four coal, compressed"
	quest.3EBFBBF5E8D82173.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a dense fuel and the first step toward Dark Matter."
		"&eChemistry:&r coal is mostly carbon. Packing more energy into less mass is what refining fuel is all about."
		"&eHow:&r the Philosopher's Stone and four coal (shapeless). It must be real coal, not charcoal."
		"&eTip:&r it also burns far longer than coal in a furnace."
	]
	quest.41149E66ACB4670C.title: "Mobius Fuel"
	quest.41149E66ACB4670C.quest_subtitle: "Four alchemical coal, compressed"
	quest.41149E66ACB4670C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the next fuel tier."
		"&eHow:&r the Philosopher's Stone and four alchemical coal. That's 16 coal per Mobius Fuel."
		"&eTip:&r automate coal now (Create crushing, MI quarries or a coal farm); the next steps need a lot."
	]
	quest.244F034391DF698B.title: "Aeternalis Fuel"
	quest.244F034391DF698B.quest_subtitle: "Four Mobius fuel, compressed"
	quest.244F034391DF698B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the top fuel, and the main ingredient of Dark Matter."
		"&eHow:&r the Philosopher's Stone and four Mobius Fuel. Each one is 64 coal; this quest asks for eight (512 coal)."
		"&eTip:&r packaged autocrafting (PackagedAuto or AE2) can do the whole chain while you build."
	]
	quest.6F6D4836ABF17642.title: "Dark Matter"
	quest.6F6D4836ABF17642.quest_subtitle: "Eight Aeternalis around a diamond block"
	quest.6F6D4836ABF17642.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember materials no forge could make. This one you made from coal and patience.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Dark Matter is ProjectE's strongest crafting material: tools, armor and rings."
		"&eHow:&r eight Aeternalis Fuel around a diamond block. The diamonds come from real mining or synthesis; EMC can't make them here."
		"&eTip:&r four Dark Matter make a Dark Matter Block, used by the tablet and the Dark Matter Furnace."
	]
	quest.5B4ADDA8DEC0D225.title: "Dark Matter Tools"
	quest.5B4ADDA8DEC0D225.quest_subtitle: "Unbreakable tools"
	quest.5B4ADDA8DEC0D225.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Dark Matter tools never break and dig very fast. Their charge key widens what they mine."
		"&eHow:&r like diamond tools, but Dark Matter replaces the head and diamonds the handle (the pickaxe is 3 Dark Matter and 2 diamonds)."
		"&eTip:&r charge the Dark Matter Hammer to mine a wider area: great for clearing land."
	]
	quest.65926BF0E01A33EA.title: "Dark Matter Armor"
	quest.65926BF0E01A33EA.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a full set of 24 Dark Matter"
	quest.65926BF0E01A33EA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r very strong armor that doesn't wear out."
		"&eHow:&r shaped like diamond armor, all Dark Matter: helmet 5, chestplate 8, leggings 7, boots 4."
		"&eTip:&r that's 24 Dark Matter. Automate the fuel chain first."
	]
	quest.6C81FB35328C5C1E.title: "Black Hole Band"
	quest.6C81FB35328C5C1E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: pulls in every item nearby"
	quest.6C81FB35328C5C1E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r while active, it draws nearby items toward you."
		"&eHow:&r an Iron Band (eight iron around a lava bucket) between two Dark Matter, with string above and below."
		"&eTip:&r switch it off near your storage system."
	]
	quest.200E2D7438535AEC.title: "Red Matter"
	quest.200E2D7438535AEC.quest_subtitle: "Optional: beyond Dark Matter"
	quest.200E2D7438535AEC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the strongest ProjectE material, for Red Matter tools and armor."
		"&eHow:&r three Dark Matter in the middle row with three Aeternalis Fuel above and three below."
		"&eTip:&r each one is three Dark Matter plus 384 coal of fuel. Only for the truly committed."
	]
	quest.4AC7BF8F4637BC0C.title: "Rapid Reorganisation"
	quest.4AC7BF8F4637BC0C.quest_subtitle: "Secret: TNT with ambitions"
	quest.4AC7BF8F4637BC0C.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember reshaping mountains. The quick way was never the tidy way.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a Nova Catalyst: TNT and Mobius Fuel. A much bigger blast."
		"&eChemistry:&r TNT is trinitrotoluene, C₇H₅N₃O₆. It carries its own oxygen, which is why it burns so fast."
		"&eTip:&r never near your base. Ever."
	]
	chapter.477FA5F1CFD1E7A9.title: "Other Worlds"
	chapter.477FA5F1CFD1E7A9.chapter_subtitle: [
		"The End, the Otherside and the Undergarden."
	]
	quest.0F5CD98214E3E454.title: "The End"
	quest.0F5CD98214E3E454.quest_subtitle: "Eyes of ender, a stronghold, a portal"
	quest.0F5CD98214E3E454.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember the edge of the world. It's closer than it used to be.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the End holds the dragon, End Cities, shulkers and azure silver ore. End Crystals power Just Dire Things' flight upgrade."
		"&eHow:&r throw eyes of ender to find a stronghold, fill the portal frame and jump in."
		"&eTip:&r bring blocks, a bow and slow-falling potions. YUNG's Better Strongholds make the hunt more interesting."
	]
	quest.587A409CC5EF5395.title: "Slay the Dragon"
	quest.587A409CC5EF5395.quest_subtitle: "The End's guardian falls"
	quest.587A409CC5EF5395.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Ender Dragon guards the End's central island. Beating it opens the gateways to the outer islands."
		"&eHow:&r shoot or climb to the End Crystals on the obsidian pillars and destroy them first (the caged ones need a climb), then fight the dragon when it perches on the portal."
		"&eTip:&r stay out of its purple breath and never look an enderman in the eye mid-fight. A bow and a stack of arrows do most of the work."
	]
	quest.478C654ED802C25B.title: "The Dragon's Breath"
	quest.478C654ED802C25B.quest_subtitle: "Bottle what the dragon breathes"
	quest.478C654ED802C25B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the dragon's purple breath can be bottled and makes lingering potions."
		"&eHow:&r catch the purple breath cloud in glass bottles during the fight, or respawn the dragon for another go."
		"&eTip:&r crystals respawn the dragon when placed on the exit portal, if you need it again."
	]
	quest.288DC19CA85DA3E9.title: "An End City"
	quest.288DC19CA85DA3E9.quest_subtitle: "Purple towers on the outer islands"
	quest.288DC19CA85DA3E9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r End Cities are tall purpur towers on the outer islands, guarded by shulkers. Some have an End Ship moored alongside."
		"&eHow:&r throw an ender pearl into an End Gateway near the main island, then search the outer islands. The Explorer's Compass can find one."
		"&eTip:&r shulker bullets make you float; carry milk or slow falling."
	]
	quest.786DC9EAB0FB870A.title: "End City Loot"
	quest.786DC9EAB0FB870A.quest_subtitle: "Wings and shulker shells"
	quest.786DC9EAB0FB870A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r End Cities hold elytra (on the end ships) and shulkers whose shells make shulker boxes."
		"&eHow:&r take an End Gateway from the main island, then search the outer islands for purple towers."
		"&eTip:&r the Angel Ring needs an elytra; shulker shells feed Silent Gear's tyrian steel."
	]
	quest.272CE62B5A0B766A.title: "Rocket Boost"
	quest.272CE62B5A0B766A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: chemistry that pushes"
	quest.272CE62B5A0B766A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r firework rockets boost elytra flight. Thirty-two is a good start for a long trip."
		"&eChemistry:&r gunpowder is black powder: about 75% potassium nitrate (KNO₃, the oxidiser), 15% charcoal and 10% sulfur. The nitrate supplies its own oxygen, so it burns fast even in a sealed tube."
		"&eHow:&r paper + gunpowder (1–3 for longer flight) in the crafting grid. Creepers and the hunting page give gunpowder."
		"&eTip:&r rockets with a firework star explode and hurt you; use plain ones for flying."
	]
	quest.62AB5E194AA2C276.title: "The Egg"
	quest.62AB5E194AA2C276.quest_subtitle: "Secret: the only one in the world"
	quest.62AB5E194AA2C276.quest_desc: [
		"&6One egg, one dragon, one world. You remember having a whole shelf of these.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the dragon leaves a single egg on top of the exit portal the first time it dies."
		"&eTip:&r it teleports when you hit it. Push it off with a piston, or let it fall onto a torch to pick it up."
	]
	quest.1A42564839595307.title: "An Ancient City"
	quest.1A42564839595307.quest_subtitle: "Find the city beneath the deep dark"
	quest.1A42564839595307.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Ancient Cities sit deep below the Overworld in the deep dark. Each one's centre holds the frame of a portal to the Otherside."
		"&eHow:&r the Explorer's Compass can find one. Sneak everywhere: shriekers summon the Warden. Click the checkmark once you're inside."
		"&eTip:&r sneaking never triggers sculk sensors, and walking on wool doesn't either."
	]
	quest.3A05164A9C113523.title: "The Warden"
	quest.3A05164A9C113523.quest_subtitle: "Kill the blind guardian of the deep"
	quest.3A05164A9C113523.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Warden is the strongest regular mob in the game, and the key to the Otherside: with Deeper and Darker it drops the Heart of the Deep."
		"&eHow:&r trigger shriekers three times to summon one (or let it find you). Fight from range; it's blind and tracks you by sound and smell."
		"&eTip:&r its sonic boom goes through shields and armour. Break line of sight when it starts charging."
	]
	quest.47E37212E3AD9C51.title: "The Otherside"
	quest.47E37212E3AD9C51.quest_subtitle: "Take the Warden's heart and step through"
	quest.47E37212E3AD9C51.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember a silence older than the world. You can hear it again.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r beyond the Ancient City lies the Otherside, a dark dimension of sculk and echo trees."
		"&eHow:&r defeat a Warden for its Heart of the Deep, then use it to light the portal frame in the city's centre."
		"&eTip:&r the Warden is blind but hears everything. Fight from range and keep moving."
	]
	quest.67E57795C7B28D27.title: "Echoes of the Deep"
	quest.67E57795C7B28D27.quest_subtitle: "The Otherside's strongest material"
	quest.67E57795C7B28D27.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r reinforced echo shards make Warden gear that rivals netherite."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the recipe; echo shards come from Ancient City chests and Otherside loot."
		"&eTip:&r Warden armour is a netherite smithing upgrade, so keep your netherite gear."
	]
	quest.7D4873404550BDD4.title: "The Ancient Temple"
	quest.7D4873404550BDD4.quest_subtitle: "A temple deep in the Otherside"
	quest.7D4873404550BDD4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Otherside's great structure: a sculk-choked temple with traps and the best loot in the dimension."
		"&eHow:&r the Explorer's Compass points the way. Step inside."
		"&eTip:&r the temple is full of sculk; sneak, as you did in the Ancient City."
	]
	quest.0F1E8758CCEAA1C1.title: "Biomes of the Otherside"
	quest.0F1E8758CCEAA1C1.quest_subtitle: "Optional: forests, columns and caverns"
	quest.0F1E8758CCEAA1C1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Otherside has its own biomes: echo-tree forests, towering columns and caverns lit by blooming plants."
		"&eChemistry:&r there's no sunlight down here; real cave and deep-sea ecosystems run on chemosynthesis, where microbes get energy by oxidising H₂S or CH₄ instead of from light."
		"&eHow:&r Nature's Compass works in the Otherside. Visit all three."
	]
	quest.33C65B50A9A09FDB.title: "Soul Elytra"
	quest.33C65B50A9A09FDB.quest_subtitle: "Optional: an elytra with its own boost"
	quest.33C65B50A9A09FDB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an upgraded elytra that boosts itself, no rockets needed."
		"&eHow:&r an elytra, sculk bones (from Shattered), a soul crystal (from Stalkers) and soul dust (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r Stalkers and Shattered roam the Otherside; fight them at range."
	]
	quest.2E4E2442F4D9031D.title: "Warden Armour"
	quest.2E4E2442F4D9031D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: beyond netherite"
	quest.2E4E2442F4D9031D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Warden armour is tougher than netherite."
		"&eHow:&r netherite chestplate + reinforced echo shard + Warden upgrade template in a smithing table."
		"&eTip:&r check JEI for where the Warden upgrade template comes from."
	]
	quest.4832FB99F0BF6921.title: "Undergarden Metals"
	quest.4832FB99F0BF6921.quest_subtitle: "Cloggrum, froststeel and utherium"
	quest.4832FB99F0BF6921.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r new ores beneath the world: cloggrum (tough), froststeel (slows what it hits) and utherium (hurts rotspawn)."
		"&eHow:&r mine them in depthrock and shiverstone, then smelt."
		"&eTip:&r run them through the Alchemistry Dissolver: what are these strange metals made of?"
	]
	quest.233CEF5C6F7B9E72.title: "Regalium"
	quest.233CEF5C6F7B9E72.quest_subtitle: "The Undergarden's precious crystal"
	quest.233CEF5C6F7B9E72.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r regalium is the Undergarden's treasure: a rare crystal in depthrock and shiverstone."
		"&eHow:&r smelt regalium ore. It also turns up in catacomb chests."
		"&eTip:&r catacombs are also where the Forgotten Guardian waits."
	]
	quest.54EE1E70147EBAAF.title: "The Catacombs"
	quest.54EE1E70147EBAAF.quest_subtitle: "Find the catacombs and beat their guardian"
	quest.54EE1E70147EBAAF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the catacombs are a buried tomb of the Undergarden's old builders. The Forgotten Guardian, a hulking armoured giant, still stands watch."
		"&eHow:&r the Explorer's Compass can find one. Clear the halls, then fight the guardian."
		"&eTip:&r it's slow; hit it, step back out of its swing, and repeat."
	]
	quest.3618066084A5EC94.title: "The Forgotten Ingot"
	quest.3618066084A5EC94.quest_subtitle: "Forge the guardian's metal"
	quest.3618066084A5EC94.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember the old guardians and the oaths they swore. This one has forgotten its own.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Forgotten Guardian drops forgotten nuggets; nine make a Forgotten Ingot for the strongest Undergarden tools."
		"&eHow:&r find a catacomb, beat the guardian, and craft the nuggets into an ingot. The smithing template is in catacomb chests."
		"&eTip:&r it hits hard; armour up and keep your distance between swings."
	]
	quest.47243C7EB987EF94.title: "Ruins and Camps"
	quest.47243C7EB987EF94.quest_subtitle: "Optional: who else lives down here?"
	quest.47243C7EB987EF94.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r forgotten vestiges are ruins left by the Undergarden's builders; denizen camps belong to the hostile Denizens who live there now."
		"&eHow:&r explore until you find one of each (the Explorer's Compass helps) and step inside."
		"&eTip:&r Denizens fight in groups; draw them out one at a time."
	]
	quest.60F7318695B23F85.title: "Biomes Below"
	quest.60F7318695B23F85.quest_subtitle: "Optional: three corners of the Undergarden"
	quest.60F7318695B23F85.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Undergarden's biomes range from frozen fields to spires that belch smog."
		"&eChemistry:&r a smog is a mix of smoke and fog; real industrial smog is soot plus sulfur dioxide (SO₂), which forms sulfuric acid droplets in damp air."
		"&eHow:&r Nature's Compass works here too. Visit all three."
	]
	chapter.782082F7E1BFE609.title: "The Twilight Forest"
	chapter.782082F7E1BFE609.chapter_subtitle: [
		"A realm of permanent dusk, ruled by bosses in order."
	]
	quest.4382AE1CE86BC1A6.title: "A Map of Dusk"
	quest.4382AE1CE86BC1A6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the forest draws its own map"
	quest.4382AE1CE86BC1A6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Magic Map shows Twilight biomes and marks every boss structure with an icon."
		"&eHow:&r craft a Magic Map Focus and then the map (check JEI), and use it inside the Twilight Forest to fill it in."
		"&eTip:&r the Maze Map does the same job inside the Minoshroom's labyrinth; Nature's Compass finds biomes, Explorer's Compass finds structures."
	]
	quest.236C4B860AAB5C49.title: "Hollow Hills"
	quest.236C4B860AAB5C49.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a hill full of ore and spiders"
	quest.236C4B860AAB5C49.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r hollow hills are mounds with a cave inside, lined with ore blocks, spawners and a treasure chest."
		"&eHow:&r find a small hollow hill (the mounds in the plain forest) and step inside."
		"&eTip:&r break the spawners first. The ore inside is free feedstock for your ore lines."
	]
	quest.3798CB29F2F9EB96.title: "The Green Twilight"
	quest.3798CB29F2F9EB96.quest_subtitle: "Optional: three of the open biomes"
	quest.3798CB29F2F9EB96.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the outer Twilight biomes are open from the start: a glowing enchanted forest, a firefly forest and giant mushrooms."
		"&eChemistry:&r fireflies (and their real cousins) glow by bioluminescence: the enzyme luciferase oxidises luciferin with O₂ and ATP, releasing light instead of heat."
		"&eHow:&r Nature's Compass can point you to each biome. Just walk in."
	]
	quest.4EA4B955C6925C4B.title: "Twilight Cake"
	quest.4EA4B955C6925C4B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a portal you can eat"
	quest.4EA4B955C6925C4B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a TelePastries cake: eat a slice and you're taken to the Twilight Forest. A tidy alternative to the flower pool."
		"&eHow:&r cake, poppies and dandelions, with an MI digital circuit (HV) in the bottom centre (this pack's recipe; check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep the cake at your base and the portal pool stays optional."
	]
	quest.0DD53DE3BCAD93CA.title: "Uncrafting Table"
	quest.0DD53DE3BCAD93CA.quest_subtitle: "Optional: undo a crafting recipe"
	quest.0DD53DE3BCAD93CA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Twilight Forest's table that turns items back into their ingredients, for XP."
		"&eChemistry:&r the Alchemistry Dissolver goes further: it uncrafts all the way down to elements."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for its recipe."
	]
	quest.30B14071B1D5A576.title: "The Naga's Courtyard"
	quest.30B14071B1D5A576.quest_subtitle: "Find the serpent's courtyard and win"
	quest.30B14071B1D5A576.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember this twilight. You walked here once, when the forest was young.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the first boss. Every boss you beat lifts the magic barrier on the next region, so the order matters."
		"&eHow:&r the courtyard is a walled stone garden in the plain forest (the Magic Map marks it). Fight inside it."
		"&eTip:&r the Naga charges in straight lines; sidestep, then hit it while it turns."
	]
	quest.14B8FA65B7C3829D.title: "The Naga"
	quest.14B8FA65B7C3829D.quest_subtitle: "Scales from the forest's first boss"
	quest.14B8FA65B7C3829D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a great serpent coiled in a stone courtyard. Its scales unlock the path forward and make naga armour."
		"&eHow:&r the Naga drops scales when it dies. Hit it when it stops charging; stay out of its coils."
		"&eTip:&r each boss you beat lifts the barrier on the next region."
	]
	quest.573FFFBA26396F1C.title: "The Lich Tower"
	quest.573FFFBA26396F1C.quest_subtitle: "Climb the tower and break the sorcerer"
	quest.573FFFBA26396F1C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Lich waits at the top of a tall stone tower. Beating it opens the swamp and the snowy forest."
		"&eHow:&r climb through the tower's rooms to the top. Break the shields orbiting it before you can hurt it."
		"&eTip:&r the Lich's shadow clones are distractions; watch for the one that casts."
	]
	quest.1B55EFB33077AC2C.title: "The Lich"
	quest.1B55EFB33077AC2C.quest_subtitle: "A sorcerer's trophy and scepters"
	quest.1B55EFB33077AC2C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Lich drops its trophy and one of its scepters (twilight, zombie, lifedrain or fortification)."
		"&eHow:&r pick up the trophy from the top of the tower once it falls."
		"&eTip:&r the Lifedrain Scepter heals you as it hurts; recharge scepters with the item listed in JEI."
	]
	quest.32F33C12C92BD123.title: "The Labyrinth"
	quest.32F33C12C92BD123.quest_subtitle: "A maze under the swamp"
	quest.32F33C12C92BD123.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r beneath the swamp lies a maze of mossy stone. The Minoshroom waits in a room at its heart."
		"&eHow:&r enter through the stairs in the swamp. A Maze Map (made with a Maze Map Focus) shows the corridors."
		"&eTip:&r mosquito swarms bite in the swamp; bring plenty of food."
	]
	quest.7BC4ACBC5EAAC5BD.title: "The Minoshroom"
	quest.7BC4ACBC5EAAC5BD.quest_subtitle: "The boss at the labyrinth's heart"
	quest.7BC4ACBC5EAAC5BD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a mushroom minotaur in the swamp labyrinth. It drops meef stroganoff and a mighty axe."
		"&eHow:&r the Maze Map helps you find it in the maze. Sidestep its charges."
		"&eTip:&r meef stroganoff is one of the best foods in the forest."
	]
	quest.24D5883E6B376D56.title: "The Hydra's Lair"
	quest.24D5883E6B376D56.quest_subtitle: "A cave in the fire swamp"
	quest.24D5883E6B376D56.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Hydra lives in a hill cave in the fire swamp, the hottest place in the forest."
		"&eChemistry:&r swamps really do burn: rotting plants release methane (CH₄), which can ignite as marsh fire."
		"&eHow:&r drink fire resistance before you enter the fire swamp. Strike the heads when they lunge."
		"&eTip:&r the heads regrow if you're slow; pressure one at a time."
	]
	quest.39A9D5474A8012E0.title: "The Hydra"
	quest.39A9D5474A8012E0.quest_subtitle: "Three heads in the fire swamp"
	quest.39A9D5474A8012E0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Hydra breathes fire from three heads. Its fiery blood makes fiery ingots."
		"&eHow:&r fire resistance potions help. Hit the heads when they lunge at you; they regrow, so keep up the pressure."
		"&eTip:&r its fire swamp is full of lava and fire; fire resistance is a must."
	]
	quest.5CB8CFE1F0ED4E1C.title: "Twilight Metals"
	quest.5CB8CFE1F0ED4E1C.quest_subtitle: "Ironwood, knightmetal and fiery metal"
	quest.5CB8CFE1F0ED4E1C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r alloys found nowhere else, for strong tools and armour."
		"&eHow:&r ironwood: smelt raw ironwood (liveroot, iron, gold). Knightmetal: smelt armour shard clusters from the dark forest. Fiery: iron + a vial of fiery blood or tears."
		"&eTip:&r knightmetal armour and tools are great against the Knight Phantoms."
	]
	quest.075918014C45253D.title: "The Goblin Stronghold"
	quest.075918014C45253D.quest_subtitle: "Six phantoms under the dark forest"
	quest.075918014C45253D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Knight Phantoms haunt the deepest room of the Goblin Knight Stronghold, buried under the dark forest."
		"&eHow:&r find the stronghold's entrance in the dark forest (the Magic Map marks it) and fight your way down. Kill all six phantoms."
		"&eTip:&r the dark forest blinds you if you haven't beaten the Hydra, so do the bosses in order."
	]
	quest.2BC7F933F44AED54.title: "The Knight Phantoms"
	quest.2BC7F933F44AED54.quest_subtitle: "Six ghosts in the goblin stronghold"
	quest.2BC7F933F44AED54.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r six phantom knights guard the Goblin Stronghold in the dark forest. Their trophy drops with the last one."
		"&eHow:&r they wait deep inside the stronghold. Knightmetal armour helps."
		"&eTip:&r they come in waves; fight near a wall so they can't surround you."
	]
	quest.64F3BF8672A26176.title: "The Dark Tower"
	quest.64F3BF8672A26176.quest_subtitle: "Climb to the Ur-Ghast"
	quest.64F3BF8672A26176.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a huge tower of towerwood in the centre of the dark forest, with the Ur-Ghast at the top."
		"&eHow:&r climb through the tower's floors using its carminite contraptions; redstone opens the way in many rooms."
		"&eTip:&r towerwood borers eat through the walls; kill them before they swarm."
	]
	quest.24EB5B9F3C30D2F1.title: "The Ur-Ghast"
	quest.24EB5B9F3C30D2F1.quest_subtitle: "The ghast queen of the Dark Tower"
	quest.24EB5B9F3C30D2F1.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember the last tower of the twilight. Its keeper remembers you too.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the great ghast at the top of the Dark Tower. Its fiery tears make more fiery metal."
		"&eHow:&r climb the tower. Kill ghastlings near the ghast traps to charge them; charged traps pull the Ur-Ghast down so you can strike."
		"&eTip:&r carminite from the tower makes redstone gadgets of the twilight."
	]
	quest.06CC5F9C904C562E.title: "The Yeti Cave"
	quest.06CC5F9C904C562E.quest_subtitle: "A cave in the snowy forest"
	quest.06CC5F9C904C562E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Alpha Yeti rules a cave in the snowy forest, surrounded by its smaller yetis."
		"&eChemistry:&r the snowy forest's blizzard chills you for real; warm armour (yeti or arctic) stops it."
		"&eHow:&r the snowy forest opens after the Lich. Find the cave and fight inside."
		"&eTip:&r when it roars, icicles fall from the roof; keep moving."
	]
	quest.656D7C4735C0CFA8.title: "The Alpha Yeti"
	quest.656D7C4735C0CFA8.quest_subtitle: "The snowy forest's boss"
	quest.656D7C4735C0CFA8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Alpha Yeti lives in a cave in the snowy forest. Its fur makes warm armour."
		"&eHow:&r dodge the ice it throws and the icicles that fall from the cave roof."
		"&eTip:&r alpha yeti fur makes warm armour for the glacier."
	]
	quest.7B22307BB2A82650.title: "The Aurora Palace"
	quest.7B22307BB2A82650.quest_subtitle: "An ice palace on the glacier"
	quest.7B22307BB2A82650.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Snow Queen's palace of packed ice and aurora blocks stands on the glacier."
		"&eChemistry:&r real auroras are light from oxygen (green, red) and nitrogen (blue, purple) atoms excited by charged particles from the Sun."
		"&eHow:&r the glacier opens after the Alpha Yeti. Climb the palace to the Queen's throne room."
		"&eTip:&r break her ice shields first; she falls on you from above, so look up."
	]
	quest.53A416978B641844.title: "The Snow Queen"
	quest.53A416978B641844.quest_subtitle: "The glacier's ice palace"
	quest.53A416978B641844.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Snow Queen rules the Aurora Palace on the glacier."
		"&eHow:&r climb the palace, then break her ice shields and avoid her drop attacks."
		"&eTip:&r beating her finishes the snowy branch of the twilight."
	]
	quest.571F7949936FB1BC.title: "The Wild Regions"
	quest.571F7949936FB1BC.quest_subtitle: "Optional: swamp, fire swamp and dark forest"
	quest.571F7949936FB1BC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the regions you fought through on the main line. Walk through each once you've earned it."
		"&eHow:&r Nature's Compass points to each biome. The barriers lift as you beat the Lich, Minoshroom and Hydra."
		"&eTip:&r a quick visit counts; you don't need to stay."
	]
	quest.089D4A7144E8B41C.title: "The Frozen Regions"
	quest.089D4A7144E8B41C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: snowy forest and glacier"
	quest.089D4A7144E8B41C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the cold half of the forest: the snowy forest and the glacier beyond it."
		"&eChemistry:&r glacier ice is blue because water absorbs red light weakly; thick, bubble-free ice lets mostly blue through."
		"&eHow:&r visit both. Warm armour stops the blizzard's chill."
	]
	quest.323C64846AFEC17D.title: "Trophy Wall"
	quest.323C64846AFEC17D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: all eight trophies at once"
	quest.323C64846AFEC17D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a trophy from every boss of the forest, in your inventory at the same time."
		"&eHow:&r keep the trophies you already have. Bosses can be fought again in other structures of the same kind."
		"&eTip:&r trophies make a fine wall in your base; place them with a right-click."
	]
	quest.1A1B0B1B03A203F4.title: "The Highlands"
	quest.1A1B0B1B03A203F4.quest_subtitle: "The plateau beyond every barrier"
	quest.1A1B0B1B03A203F4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Both branches beaten, the last barrier thins. You remember standing up here and looking down on all of it.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the highlands and the thornlands ring the forest's centre. Trolls and giants live up here."
		"&eHow:&r with the Ur-Ghast and the Snow Queen beaten, climb into the highlands, then cross the thornlands (watch the thorns)."
		"&eTip:&r giants are huge and hit hard; fight them from range."
	]
	quest.21B4176B92393E04.title: "Troll Caves"
	quest.21B4176B92393E04.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the trolls' vaults"
	quest.21B4176B92393E04.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r caves under the highlands, full of trolls guarding vaults. The Lamp of Cinders hides in one."
		"&eHow:&r find a troll cave in the highlands and loot its vaults. The lamp burns away thorns."
		"&eTip:&r trolls throw rocks; fight them in the open, not in narrow tunnels."
	]
	quest.025B8EF9A3CE8915.title: "The Unfinished Castle"
	quest.025B8EF9A3CE8915.quest_subtitle: "Secret: the castle at the top of the world"
	quest.025B8EF9A3CE8915.quest_desc: [
		"&6A castle on the final plateau, waiting for a ruler. You remember planning to come back for it.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Final Castle stands on the final plateau. Its last boss was never finished by the mod's authors."
		"&eTip:&r the castle is still worth exploring for its architecture and its force-field doors."
	]
	quest.3EDECB3F741E7A42.title: "The Questing Ram"
	quest.3EDECB3F741E7A42.quest_subtitle: "Secret: a ram that wants every colour"
	quest.3EDECB3F741E7A42.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hidden grove where the Questing Ram lives. Feed it one wool of every colour and it rewards you."
		"&eChemistry:&r wool dyes are real chemistry too: indigo, cochineal and lapis-blue (lazurite, a sulfur-bearing silicate) all coloured cloth in history."
		"&eTip:&r the grove's ring of stones looks like a fairy ring in the enchanted forest."
	]
	chapter.52D4F58B0C6E5EBB.title: "Space"
	chapter.52D4F58B0C6E5EBB.chapter_subtitle: [
		"The Moon, the planets and the air you bring with you."
	]
	quest.742D7993CB0086CB.title: "Desh on the Moon"
	quest.742D7993CB0086CB.quest_subtitle: "The Moon's metal builds the next rocket"
	quest.742D7993CB0086CB.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember the Moon from above. Now you're standing on it.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r desh ore is found only on the Moon. Desh blocks, engines and tanks build the Tier 2 rocket."
		"&eChemistry:&r the Moon has no atmosphere and its days swing from about +120 °C to −170 °C, so bring oxygen."
		"&eHow:&r mine desh ore on the Moon and process it like any ore."
	]
	quest.635A241489681170.title: "Mars"
	quest.635A241489681170.quest_subtitle: "The red planet"
	quest.635A241489681170.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mars holds ostrum ore, the metal for the Tier 3 rocket."
		"&eChemistry:&r Mars is red because its dust is rich in iron(III) oxide, Fe₂O₃: rust. Its thin air is about 95% CO₂."
		"&eHow:&r build the Tier 2 rocket from desh at the NASA Workbench, fuel it with diesel and launch."
	]
	quest.1751F7DCDA2801ED.title: "Ostrum"
	quest.1751F7DCDA2801ED.quest_subtitle: "Mars's metal for the Tier 3 rocket"
	quest.1751F7DCDA2801ED.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ostrum ore is found only on Mars. It builds the Tier 3 rocket."
		"&eHow:&r mine ostrum ore on Mars and process it."
		"&eTip:&r grab some extra for the Tier 3 rocket's engine and tank."
	]
	quest.7E7B71100CC2752B.title: "Heat Shielding"
	quest.7E7B71100CC2752B.quest_subtitle: "A suit that survives 464 °C"
	quest.7E7B71100CC2752B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Venus and Mercury are hot enough to kill in a normal space suit. The netherite space suit handles the heat."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the netherite suit pieces. Fill it with oxygen at the Oxygen Loader."
		"&eTip:&r the jet suit (later, check JEI) also handles the heat, and flies."
	]
	quest.0371D774272DB515.title: "Venus"
	quest.0371D774272DB515.quest_subtitle: "Acid clouds and crushing pressure"
	quest.0371D774272DB515.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Venus holds calorite ore, the metal for the Tier 4 rocket."
		"&eChemistry:&r its atmosphere is about 96% CO₂ at roughly 92 times Earth's pressure, under clouds of sulfuric acid (H₂SO₄). A runaway greenhouse keeps it near 464 °C."
		"&eHow:&r Tier 3 rocket from ostrum, plus your netherite space suit."
	]
	quest.31F2D0605D2E5028.title: "Calorite"
	quest.31F2D0605D2E5028.quest_subtitle: "Venus's metal for the Tier 4 rocket"
	quest.31F2D0605D2E5028.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r calorite ore is found on Venus. It builds the Tier 4 rocket, the only one that reaches another star."
		"&eHow:&r mine calorite ore in the Venusian stone and process it like any ore."
		"&eTip:&r Venus is hot and its rain is acid; keep the netherite suit on the whole time."
	]
	quest.1CA5613802C3B7C6.title: "Alien Metals"
	quest.1CA5613802C3B7C6.quest_subtitle: "Desh, ostrum and calorite"
	quest.1CA5613802C3B7C6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one metal from each world: desh (Moon), ostrum (Mars) and calorite (Venus). Each builds the next rocket tier."
		"&eHow:&r process the raw ores; MI and Mekanism ore lines work on them too (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the Dissolver can tell you what these metals break down into."
	]
	quest.537431DD08EA991F.title: "Glacio"
	quest.537431DD08EA991F.quest_subtitle: "A frozen world around another star"
	quest.537431DD08EA991F.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember stars that were yours to name. This one you'll have to visit first.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Glacio orbits Proxima Centauri, the nearest star to the Sun, about 4.2 light-years away. Unlike the others, it has breathable air."
		"&eHow:&r build the Tier 4 rocket from calorite and launch."
	]
	quest.129266E51D79A231.title: "A Spare Breath"
	quest.129266E51D79A231.quest_subtitle: "Carry oxygen to top up your suit"
	quest.129266E51D79A231.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a gas tank holds oxygen you can carry, to refill the suit far from your Oxygen Loader."
		"&eChemistry:&r a resting adult breathes in roughly 550 litres of O₂ a day; your suit's tank is all that stands between you and vacuum."
		"&eHow:&r iron plates and an iron rod (check JEI). Fill it in the Oxygen Loader like the suit."
		"&eTip:&r the large gas tank holds much more and is a part in later machines."
	]
	quest.18FD507A01896D7C.title: "The Oxygen Can"
	quest.18FD507A01896D7C.quest_subtitle: "Giselle Addon: oxygen for everything you wear"
	quest.18FD507A01896D7C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Giselle Addon's oxygen can stores oxygen and tops up the oxygen gear you're carrying."
		"&eHow:&r iron plates around an iron rod (check JEI). Fill it with oxygen like a tank."
		"&eTip:&r the addon also links Ad Astra to Mekanism and other mods; search its name in JEI to see what else it adds."
	]
	quest.0304AF411C0ADEBE.title: "Breathable Bases"
	quest.0304AF411C0ADEBE.quest_subtitle: "Optional: fill a sealed room with air"
	quest.0304AF411C0ADEBE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Oxygen Distributor fills a sealed room with breathable air, so you can work without a helmet."
		"&eChemistry:&r it makes oxygen from water with FE, the same idea as your Electrolytic Separator: 2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Seal the room completely; any gap stops it working."
	]
	quest.404C175EA043B30A.title: "Is There Air?"
	quest.404C175EA043B30A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a redstone check for oxygen"
	quest.404C175EA043B30A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Oxygen Sensor gives a redstone signal depending on whether the space around it has oxygen."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the recipe, place it inside your sealed base and wire it to a lamp or alarm."
		"&eTip:&r a light that goes out when the air does is the cheapest life support alarm there is."
	]
	quest.6C46189D0E479A97.title: "Water for Oxygen"
	quest.6C46189D0E479A97.quest_subtitle: "Optional: feed your electrolysis off-world"
	quest.6C46189D0E479A97.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Ad Astra's powered water pump feeds water into your pipes, so a base on the Moon can make its own oxygen."
		"&eChemistry:&r electrolysis splits water: 2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂. Every 2 molecules of water give 1 of oxygen and 2 of hydrogen, which you can burn or store."
		"&eHow:&r steel and desh plates, a gas tank and a hopper (check JEI). Pipe its water into a Mekanism Electrolytic Separator and the O₂ into an Oxygen Loader."
		"&eTip:&r Ad Astra's ice shards are frozen water; the Moon and Mars both have ice shard ore."
	]
	quest.07797DB5628E9DBE.title: "Netherite Oxygen Can"
	quest.07797DB5628E9DBE.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a bigger can for the hot worlds"
	quest.07797DB5628E9DBE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the upgraded oxygen can holds much more oxygen than the iron one."
		"&eHow:&r an oxygen can, a netherite ingot and ostrum plates in the crafting grid (check JEI). Its oxygen carries over."
		"&eTip:&r on Venus every trip back to base costs time; carry more air instead."
	]
	quest.19BBF6AF16FB7E15.title: "An Automated Launch Site"
	quest.19BBF6AF16FB7E15.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Giselle Addon fuelling and sensing"
	quest.19BBF6AF16FB7E15.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Fuel Loader takes piped fuel and fills any rocket or rover within a few blocks; the Rocket Sensor reports a nearby rocket's state to a comparator."
		"&eHow:&r both are steel ingots and iron plates around a bucket or an observer (check JEI). Pipe diesel into the loader."
		"&eTip:&r no more filling rockets by hand from buckets."
	]
	quest.62B2455C3CD4B583.title: "Earth Gravity"
	quest.62B2455C3CD4B583.quest_subtitle: "Optional: normal gravity indoors"
	quest.62B2455C3CD4B583.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Gravity Normalizer gives an area Earth-like gravity, so your jumps behave in your Moon base."
		"&eChemistry:&r the Moon's gravity is about 1/6 of Earth's, Mars about 3/8; you weigh less because they have less mass."
		"&eHow:&r etrionic capacitors, a diamond block and desh plates (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.25DDA7F730F46AFC.title: "The Rover"
	quest.25DDA7F730F46AFC.quest_subtitle: "Optional: drive across the Moon"
	quest.25DDA7F730F46AFC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a fuelled buggy for crossing big, airless plains quickly."
		"&eHow:&r desh engine, desh blocks and plates, a large gas tank, a radio and wheels (check JEI). Fuel it with diesel."
		"&eTip:&r low gravity makes it bounce; slow down on hills."
	]
	quest.40442645A8B5A09C.title: "The Moon Is Cheese"
	quest.40442645A8B5A09C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the old joke is true here"
	quest.40442645A8B5A09C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Ad Astra hides cheese ore on the Moon."
		"&eChemistry:&r the real Moon is mostly silicate rock: oxygen, silicon, magnesium, iron, calcium and aluminum."
		"&eHow:&r mine moon cheese ore. Eat responsibly."
	]
	quest.3B5922B2AEA252B7.title: "Lunarians"
	quest.3B5922B2AEA252B7.quest_subtitle: "Optional: villagers on the Moon"
	quest.3B5922B2AEA252B7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Lunarians are the Moon's villagers. Their villages stand on the lunar wastelands, with towers nearby."
		"&eHow:&r explore the Moon until you find one, then walk into it. They trade like villagers."
		"&eTip:&r the Explorer's Compass works on other planets too."
	]
	quest.134D3F3BADF7D9BF.title: "Moon Dungeon"
	quest.134D3F3BADF7D9BF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: something built under the Moon"
	quest.134D3F3BADF7D9BF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a dungeon hidden under the lunar wastelands, with loot and hostile guards."
		"&eHow:&r the Explorer's Compass can find one. Step inside."
		"&eTip:&r bring a spare gas tank: dungeons take longer than you think."
	]
	quest.12A113F5FF1A0758.title: "Temples of Mars"
	quest.12A113F5FF1A0758.quest_subtitle: "Optional: ruins in the red canyons"
	quest.12A113F5FF1A0758.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r temples stand in the Martian wastelands and canyon creeks."
		"&eChemistry:&r Mars's canyons were carved by liquid water long ago; today its low pressure makes surface water boil or freeze almost at once."
		"&eHow:&r visit a canyon creek and find a temple (the Explorer's Compass helps)."
	]
	quest.36C2163D475D5DD0.title: "The Polar Caps"
	quest.36C2163D475D5DD0.quest_subtitle: "Optional: ice at the ends of Mars"
	quest.36C2163D475D5DD0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mars's polar caps are frozen; ice shard ore gives ice shards."
		"&eChemistry:&r the real caps are water ice with a seasonal layer of dry ice (solid CO₂), which turns straight to gas in spring (sublimation)."
		"&eHow:&r visit the polar caps biome and mine ice shard ore (it's on the Moon too)."
	]
	quest.5E6BCCAA71BB14F4.title: "The Pygros"
	quest.5E6BCCAA71BB14F4.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Venus has inhabitants"
	quest.5E6BCCAA71BB14F4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Pygros are piglin-like natives of Venus. Their villages and towers stand in the Venus wastelands."
		"&eHow:&r find a village (the Explorer's Compass helps) and step inside. Wear gold, just in case."
		"&eTip:&r Pygro brutes guard the towers; they hit hard."
	]
	quest.0CCDB1D0755282C7.title: "Infernal Barrens"
	quest.0CCDB1D0755282C7.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Venus at its worst"
	quest.0CCDB1D0755282C7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the harshest of the Venusian biomes."
		"&eChemistry:&r Venus is hotter than Mercury despite being twice as far from the Sun: its thick CO₂ atmosphere traps heat."
		"&eHow:&r visit it in the netherite space suit. Fire resistance helps."
	]
	quest.72A1114536C4C6FA.title: "Mercury"
	quest.72A1114536C4C6FA.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the planet closest to the Sun"
	quest.72A1114536C4C6FA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a scorched, airless world reachable with the Tier 3 rocket."
		"&eChemistry:&r with almost no atmosphere, Mercury can't hold heat: about 430 °C by day and −180 °C at night."
		"&eHow:&r Tier 3 rocket plus the netherite space suit."
	]
	quest.706C2B3D42BFE9DD.title: "Mercury Deltas"
	quest.706C2B3D42BFE9DD.quest_subtitle: "Optional: walk the deltas"
	quest.706C2B3D42BFE9DD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mercury's deltas, a dark landscape of scorched stone."
		"&eChemistry:&r despite the name, the planet has no mercury metal; the element was named after the same god for its quick, flowing liquid."
		"&eHow:&r land on Mercury and walk into the deltas."
	]
	quest.407A51A230482666.title: "Peaks of Glacio"
	quest.407A51A230482666.quest_subtitle: "Optional: walk another star's world"
	quest.407A51A230482666.quest_desc: [
		"&6Air you didn't bring, under a sun that isn't yours. You remember this feeling: arriving.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Glacio's frozen peaks and snowy barrens, with its own trees and woolly rams."
		"&eHow:&r visit both biomes. You can take your helmet off here."
		"&eTip:&r Glacio has ordinary ores too (coal, iron, copper, lapis) in its own stone."
	]
	quest.482F2CC86AEE5F02.title: "In Orbit"
	quest.482F2CC86AEE5F02.quest_subtitle: "Optional: stop above the Moon and Mars"
	quest.482F2CC86AEE5F02.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every planet has an orbit dimension above it, where space stations are built."
		"&eChemistry:&r in orbit you're falling around the planet all the time, which is why everything floats."
		"&eHow:&r choose the orbit on the rocket's planet screen instead of the surface."
	]
	chapter.409E2F2CFC4C4323.title: "Exploration"
	chapter.409E2F2CFC4C4323.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Go and see what the world has made without you."
	]
	quest.05869866A8B30D26.title: "Two Compasses"
	quest.05869866A8B30D26.quest_subtitle: "Find any biome, find any structure"
	quest.05869866A8B30D26.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember knowing every corner of this world by heart. For now, a compass will do.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Nature's Compass points to any biome; Explorer's Compass points to any structure. Every quest on this page gets easier with them."
		"&eHow:&r each is a compass ringed with a few common blocks (check JEI). Right-click to pick a target, then follow the needle."
		"&eTip:&r the compasses work in other dimensions too: the Nether, the Undergarden, the Twilight Forest and even other planets."
	]
	quest.19D5348F991D1D5B.title: "A Plains Village"
	quest.19D5348F991D1D5B.quest_subtitle: "Neighbours, at last"
	quest.19D5348F991D1D5B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r villagers trade emeralds for crops, tools and enchanted books, and their beds and fields are free for the taking (politely)."
		"&eHow:&r plains villages generate in plains and a few grassy modded biomes. Walk into one."
		"&eTip:&r a cartographer villager sells maps to ocean monuments and woodland mansions."
	]
	quest.61922A7A4397905F.title: "Towns and Towers"
	quest.61922A7A4397905F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: visit a new village or tower"
	quest.61922A7A4397905F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Towns and Towers adds new village styles and pillager outposts across the biomes."
		"&eHow:&r find a village or outpost you haven't seen before. Click the checkmark when done."
		"&eTip:&r villages often have a waystone."
	]
	quest.60152F4E87D63285.title: "A Forest Village"
	quest.60152F4E87D63285.quest_subtitle: "Optional: timber houses under the trees"
	quest.60152F4E87D63285.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Towns and Towers builds a village style for each biome. The forest village is timber and cobblestone."
		"&eHow:&r find one in a forest biome (Explorer's Compass: Towns and Towers) and walk in."
		"&eTip:&r each biome style has its own loot chests."
	]
	quest.351DC01BDF9B2F7D.title: "A Meadow Village"
	quest.351DC01BDF9B2F7D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a village in the mountain meadows"
	quest.351DC01BDF9B2F7D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r high meadows below the peaks get their own village style."
		"&eHow:&r find a meadow biome on a mountainside and the village in it."
		"&eTip:&r meadows are where bees and wildflowers are thickest."
	]
	quest.3E4655FCC160E807.title: "A Snowy Taiga Village"
	quest.3E4655FCC160E807.quest_subtitle: "Optional: spruce and snow"
	quest.3E4655FCC160E807.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a village built for the cold, in the snowy taiga."
		"&eHow:&r find a snowy taiga and the village in it."
		"&eTip:&r bring leather boots for powder snow."
	]
	quest.7A6C1F22C67DC796.title: "A Swamp Village"
	quest.7A6C1F22C67DC796.quest_subtitle: "Optional: houses on stilts"
	quest.7A6C1F22C67DC796.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r vanilla never put villages in swamps. Towns and Towers does."
		"&eHow:&r find a swamp and the village in it."
		"&eTip:&r witches love swamps too; keep a milk bucket handy."
	]
	quest.6C0F741B9358A2D2.title: "A Desert Village"
	quest.6C0F741B9358A2D2.quest_subtitle: "Optional: sandstone in the sun"
	quest.6C0F741B9358A2D2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a sandstone village in the desert."
		"&eChemistry:&r sandstone is sand grains (mostly quartz, SiO₂) cemented by minerals like calcite or iron oxides that precipitated from groundwater."
		"&eHow:&r find a desert village (Explorer's Compass) and walk in."
	]
	quest.514B4137700D8590.title: "A Pillager Outpost"
	quest.514B4137700D8590.quest_subtitle: "The villagers' enemies have towers too"
	quest.514B4137700D8590.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r pillagers build watchtowers. Towns and Towers gives each biome its own design."
		"&eHow:&r find a forest outpost and walk in. Expect crossbow fire."
		"&eTip:&r killing a pillager captain gives Bad Omen; in 1.21 you drink the ominous bottle it drops to start a raid."
	]
	quest.612E99E12D4629B9.title: "A Woodland Mansion"
	quest.612E99E12D4629B9.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the illagers' stronghold"
	quest.612E99E12D4629B9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r huge dark-oak mansions, very rare, deep in dark forests. Vindicators and evokers live inside."
		"&eHow:&r a cartographer's woodland explorer map or the Explorer's Compass. Step inside."
		"&eTip:&r evokers drop totems of undying; vindicators hit very hard."
	]
	quest.6D0121AD6AFBB06A.title: "Better Dungeons"
	quest.6D0121AD6AFBB06A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: clear a YUNG's dungeon"
	quest.6D0121AD6AFBB06A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r YUNG's Better Dungeons adds catacombs, fortresses and spider caves underground."
		"&eHow:&r find one (the Explorer's Compass lists them), clear it and loot it. Click the checkmark when done."
		"&eTip:&r some dungeon chests hold Relics and Artifacts items."
	]
	quest.4D5D6454D9CCBB6A.title: "Zombie Catacombs"
	quest.4D5D6454D9CCBB6A.quest_subtitle: "A tomb full of the restless dead"
	quest.4D5D6454D9CCBB6A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r YUNG's zombie dungeon: a tomb with spawners, coffins and loot."
		"&eHow:&r find it with the Explorer's Compass (Better Dungeons) and step inside."
		"&eTip:&r break or torch the spawners first; then loot at your leisure."
	]
	quest.3C3DB798AE67BB23.title: "Skeleton Fortress"
	quest.3C3DB798AE67BB23.quest_subtitle: "A buried fort of archers"
	quest.3C3DB798AE67BB23.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r YUNG's skeleton dungeon is a sprawling underground fort."
		"&eHow:&r find it and step inside. Bring a shield."
		"&eTip:&r torches on every spawner; skeletons will pick you off from the dark otherwise."
	]
	quest.23C618FC62DB7FEC.title: "Spider Caves"
	quest.23C618FC62DB7FEC.quest_subtitle: "Webs everywhere"
	quest.23C618FC62DB7FEC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a natural-looking cave full of webs, cave spiders and their spawners."
		"&eChemistry:&r real spider silk is a protein (spidroin) with crystalline β-sheets that make it, weight for weight, stronger than steel."
		"&eHow:&r find one and step inside. A sword or shears cut webs fast."
		"&eTip:&r cave spiders poison; carry milk."
	]
	quest.5440F7447034043F.title: "A Better Stronghold"
	quest.5440F7447034043F.quest_subtitle: "Where the End portal hides"
	quest.5440F7447034043F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r YUNG's Better Strongholds replaces the vanilla stronghold with a much larger, trapped maze. The End portal room is inside."
		"&eHow:&r throw eyes of ender, or use the Explorer's Compass. Step inside."
		"&eTip:&r mark your path with torches on one side; the halls all look alike."
	]
	quest.68B5AC09A423AA4D.title: "Better Mineshafts"
	quest.68B5AC09A423AA4D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: explore a YUNG's mineshaft"
	quest.68B5AC09A423AA4D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r YUNG's Better Mineshafts are longer, with ore deposits, carts and loot."
		"&eHow:&r explore one and loot a chest. Click the checkmark when done."
		"&eTip:&r look for minecarts with chests along the tracks."
	]
	quest.56FD6ABE6F060C83.title: "An Old Mineshaft"
	quest.56FD6ABE6F060C83.quest_subtitle: "Someone mined here before you"
	quest.56FD6ABE6F060C83.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r YUNG's mineshafts come in styles for each biome. The oak style is the common one."
		"&eHow:&r find one under a forest or plains (Explorer's Compass) and walk in."
		"&eTip:&r the rails and planks are free building material."
	]
	quest.28491E1F764497B4.title: "Mineshafts of the Caves"
	quest.28491E1F764497B4.quest_subtitle: "Optional: dripstone and lush styles"
	quest.28491E1F764497B4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r two mineshafts built into cave biomes: one among dripstone, one among moss and glow berries."
		"&eChemistry:&r dripstone is calcium carbonate: water carrying dissolved Ca(HCO₃)₂ drips, loses CO₂, and leaves CaCO₃ behind, a millimetre at a time."
		"&eHow:&r find a mineshaft under dripstone caves and one under lush caves."
	]
	quest.75E4DF1E89697FCF.title: "Trail Ruins"
	quest.75E4DF1E89697FCF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: dig like an archaeologist"
	quest.75E4DF1E89697FCF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r half-buried ruins of an old people. Suspicious gravel hides pottery sherds and armour trims."
		"&eHow:&r find the ruins (Explorer's Compass) and bring a brush (feather, copper ingot, stick)."
		"&eTip:&r brush slowly; breaking suspicious blocks destroys the loot."
	]
	quest.5D9ABBC3297E8F11.title: "Trial Chambers"
	quest.5D9ABBC3297E8F11.quest_subtitle: "Copper halls and trial spawners"
	quest.5D9ABBC3297E8F11.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r copper and tuff vaults deep underground. Trial spawners give keys; keys open vaults."
		"&eChemistry:&r the halls show copper's patina: Cu weathers to green basic copper carbonate, Cu₂CO₃(OH)₂, unless you wax it."
		"&eHow:&r find a chamber, beat a trial spawner's wave and take the key."
		"&eTip:&r breezes deflect arrows; fight them up close."
	]
	quest.3D2834AA290BDC3C.title: "Temples"
	quest.3D2834AA290BDC3C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: desert and jungle"
	quest.3D2834AA290BDC3C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a desert pyramid and a jungle temple, each with treasure and a trap."
		"&eChemistry:&r the desert trap is TNT: trinitrotoluene, C₇H₅N₃O₆, which carries its oxygen inside the molecule."
		"&eHow:&r find one of each. Don't stand on the pressure plate in the desert."
	]
	quest.6B1ACC106AA8CC7C.title: "Odd Little Houses"
	quest.6B1ACC106AA8CC7C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a witch's hut and an igloo"
	quest.6B1ACC106AA8CC7C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a witch's hut in the swamp and an igloo on the snow. Some igloos hide a basement."
		"&eHow:&r find one of each and step inside."
		"&eTip:&r the igloo basement has a brewing stand and a golden apple for curing a zombie villager."
	]
	quest.696EDE3758F11DDE.title: "A Ruined Portal"
	quest.696EDE3758F11DDE.quest_subtitle: "Optional: someone tried to leave"
	quest.696EDE3758F11DDE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r broken Nether portals, with crying obsidian and a chest of gold."
		"&eChemistry:&r obsidian forms when lava (molten silicate) cools so fast it can't crystallise: it's volcanic glass."
		"&eHow:&r find one and stand inside it. Fill the missing blocks to repair the portal."
	]
	quest.50F76B15FECDB23D.title: "A Shipwreck"
	quest.50F76B15FECDB23D.quest_subtitle: "Someone else's bad day at sea"
	quest.50F76B15FECDB23D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r sunken ships with supply, treasure and map chests. The map leads to buried treasure."
		"&eHow:&r find a wreck (Explorer's Compass) and swim inside."
		"&eTip:&r a potion of water breathing or a turtle shell helmet makes this easy."
	]
	quest.11B352742B41A2F3.title: "Buried Treasure"
	quest.11B352742B41A2F3.quest_subtitle: "X marks the spot"
	quest.11B352742B41A2F3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r buried chests on beaches, each with a Heart of the Sea for a conduit."
		"&eHow:&r follow a shipwreck's treasure map to the X and dig down."
		"&eTip:&r the chest is usually right under the X, a few blocks down."
	]
	quest.39CC43EB79388B13.title: "Ocean Ruins"
	quest.39CC43EB79388B13.quest_subtitle: "Optional: sandstone and stone ruins underwater"
	quest.39CC43EB79388B13.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ruins on the sea floor: sandstone ones in warm water, stone bricks in cold."
		"&eChemistry:&r warm-water coral reefs are calcium carbonate skeletons; more dissolved CO₂ makes seawater more acidic and dissolves them."
		"&eHow:&r find one of each. Drowned guard them."
	]
	quest.4A7EC6354DC5269B.title: "Wreckage"
	quest.4A7EC6354DC5269B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a Towns and Towers wreck"
	quest.4A7EC6354DC5269B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Towns and Towers scatters its own wreckage across the oceans."
		"&eHow:&r find it with the Explorer's Compass (Towns and Towers) and swim in."
		"&eTip:&r boats are faster than swimming between ocean structures."
	]
	quest.2D328EFF89A3A160.title: "An Ocean Monument"
	quest.2D328EFF89A3A160.quest_subtitle: "The guardians' temple"
	quest.2D328EFF89A3A160.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a prismarine temple guarded by guardians and three elder guardians. Its sponge rooms and gold block vault are the prize."
		"&eChemistry:&r a sponge holds water by capillary action in its pores; dry it in a furnace to drive the water off."
		"&eHow:&r find it with a cartographer's map or the Explorer's Compass. Bring water breathing and Respiration."
		"&eTip:&r elder guardians give Mining Fatigue; kill all three to lift it (see the hunting page)."
	]
	quest.1A2B391538F70F19.title: "A Nether Fortress"
	quest.1A2B391538F70F19.quest_subtitle: "Blazes and wither skeletons"
	quest.1A2B391538F70F19.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r dark nether-brick bridges and halls. Blazes give blaze rods; wither skeletons drop skulls for the Wither."
		"&eHow:&r fortresses run in long lines across the Nether; the Explorer's Compass finds them quickly."
		"&eTip:&r nether wart grows in the fortress stairwells; take some for brewing."
	]
	quest.782E886E60A354D9.title: "A Bastion Remnant"
	quest.782E886E60A354D9.quest_subtitle: "The piglins' castle"
	quest.782E886E60A354D9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r blackstone castles full of piglins and gold. Some hide netherite upgrade templates and ancient debris."
		"&eChemistry:&r gold doesn't tarnish because it's the least reactive metal: it won't oxidise in air, even at high temperatures."
		"&eHow:&r wear one piece of gold armour so piglins stay calm, then step inside."
		"&eTip:&r opening chests angers piglins anyway; piglin brutes ignore gold entirely."
	]
	quest.126B19FC8B92ED56.title: "Nether Fossils"
	quest.126B19FC8B92ED56.quest_subtitle: "Optional: bones in the soul sand"
	quest.126B19FC8B92ED56.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r giant bone fossils in the soul sand valleys."
		"&eChemistry:&r bone is mostly hydroxyapatite, Ca₅(PO₄)₃(OH): a calcium phosphate mineral, the same family as phosphate rock for fertiliser."
		"&eHow:&r find a soul sand valley and walk into one of the bone arches."
	]
	quest.20FE0812FEA6CB0B.title: "A Nether Dungeon"
	quest.20FE0812FEA6CB0B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: YUNG's small Nether dungeon"
	quest.20FE0812FEA6CB0B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Better Dungeons adds small dungeons to the Nether too, with spawners and loot."
		"&eHow:&r find one with the Explorer's Compass and step inside."
		"&eTip:&r fire resistance first; everything here burns."
	]
	quest.4F755E3FE879848F.title: "Ruins in the Fire"
	quest.4F755E3FE879848F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a ruined portal on the other side"
	quest.4F755E3FE879848F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ruined portals turn up in the Nether as well, with the same gold chest."
		"&eHow:&r find one in the Nether and stand inside it."
		"&eTip:&r crying obsidian makes respawn anchors, which let you respawn in the Nether."
	]
	quest.5319A7F7508FDD4C.title: "Erupting Inferno"
	quest.5319A7F7508FDD4C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Biomes O' Plenty's angriest Nether biome"
	quest.5319A7F7508FDD4C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Nether biome of lava, ash and erupting vents."
		"&eChemistry:&r volcanic gas is mostly water vapour, CO₂ and SO₂; the SO₂ is what makes volcanic air sting."
		"&eHow:&r Nature's Compass finds it. Fire resistance is a must."
	]
	quest.2392661194C63179.title: "Cliffs of Chalk"
	quest.2392661194C63179.quest_subtitle: "White cliffs and tall stone"
	quest.2392661194C63179.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r two Regions Unexplored cliff biomes: white chalk and towering stone."
		"&eChemistry:&r chalk is calcium carbonate (CaCO₃) made of the shells of tiny sea plankton. Heat it and it gives quicklime: CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂."
		"&eHow:&r Nature's Compass finds each one. Visit both."
	]
	quest.4E8EFFB2A502F674.title: "Hot Ground"
	quest.4E8EFFB2A502F674.quest_subtitle: "Springs and volcanic plains"
	quest.4E8EFFB2A502F674.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r two Biomes O' Plenty biomes warmed from below."
		"&eChemistry:&r hot springs carry dissolved minerals; when the water cools at the surface, silica and carbonates precipitate as terraces."
		"&eHow:&r visit both (Nature's Compass)."
	]
	quest.7F926E6F393B0BC7.title: "Wetlands"
	quest.7F926E6F393B0BC7.quest_subtitle: "Bog, marsh and fen"
	quest.7F926E6F393B0BC7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r three kinds of wetland from the two biome mods."
		"&eChemistry:&r waterlogged peat has almost no oxygen, so it barely rots; microbes there make methane (CH₄), the original \"marsh gas\"."
		"&eHow:&r visit all three. Bring a boat."
	]
	quest.122FF431CDA92EC1.title: "Caves That Glow"
	quest.122FF431CDA92EC1.quest_subtitle: "Three cave biomes with their own light"
	quest.122FF431CDA92EC1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r cave biomes lit by redstone, giant glowing mushrooms and glowing fungi."
		"&eChemistry:&r real glowing fungi use the same chemistry as fireflies: luciferin oxidised by O₂ with the help of an enzyme, luciferase."
		"&eHow:&r these are underground; Nature's Compass gives the location, then dig down."
	]
	quest.27B9D528EE9E2A4F.title: "Useful Forests"
	quest.27B9D528EE9E2A4F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: maple, eucalyptus and fruit trees"
	quest.27B9D528EE9E2A4F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r three forests whose real trees give us chemicals."
		"&eChemistry:&r maple sap is about 2% sucrose (C₁₂H₂₂O₁₁), boiled down 40:1 into syrup. Eucalyptus oil is mostly eucalyptol (C₁₀H₁₈O)."
		"&eHow:&r visit all three."
	]
	quest.4FBB33D6AE0D7BF7.title: "Dry Country"
	quest.4FBB33D6AE0D7BF7.quest_subtitle: "Optional: three Regions Unexplored deserts"
	quest.4FBB33D6AE0D7BF7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Joshua trees, saguaro cacti and the red outback."
		"&eChemistry:&r red desert soil is coloured by a thin coat of iron(III) oxide, Fe₂O₃, on every grain: the same rust that colours Mars."
		"&eHow:&r visit all three. Carry water."
	]
	quest.01C187527EBB2E42.title: "Cold Places"
	quest.01C187527EBB2E42.quest_subtitle: "Optional: tundra, icy heights and snowblossoms"
	quest.01C187527EBB2E42.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r three cold biomes from the biome mods."
		"&eChemistry:&r ice floats because water expands about 9% when it freezes: hydrogen bonds lock the molecules into an open hexagonal lattice."
		"&eHow:&r visit all three. Warm clothes not required, but recommended."
	]
	quest.39B8F4EF8E933165.title: "Colour Fields"
	quest.39B8F4EF8E933165.quest_subtitle: "Optional: red, purple and violet"
	quest.39B8F4EF8E933165.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r biomes full of flowers: poppies, jacarandas and wisteria."
		"&eChemistry:&r most red, purple and blue petals owe their colour to anthocyanins, pigments that change colour with pH (red in acid, blue in base)."
		"&eHow:&r visit all three. Collect the flowers for dyes."
	]
	quest.5D9AAF892091E191.title: "Strange Heights"
	quest.5D9AAF892091E191.quest_subtitle: "Optional: spires and crags"
	quest.5D9AAF892091E191.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tall rock spires and broken crags: two of the most dramatic landscapes in the pack."
		"&eChemistry:&r rock spires are what's left when softer rock around them is weathered away by water, frost and slow acid rain (H₂CO₃ from dissolved CO₂)."
		"&eHow:&r visit both. Bring a water bucket for the way down."
	]
	quest.05E537B097F52D38.title: "Dead Lands"
	quest.05E537B097F52D38.quest_subtitle: "Optional: where nothing grows"
	quest.05E537B097F52D38.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r cracked wasteland and grey dead forest."
		"&eChemistry:&r soil dies when it loses organic matter and nitrogen; your Haber-Bosch ammonia (N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃) is how real farms put nitrogen back."
		"&eHow:&r visit both. A demigod might one day make them green again."
	]
	quest.31A980F1060C1B0E.title: "The Origin Valley"
	quest.31A980F1060C1B0E.quest_subtitle: "Secret: the world as it first was"
	quest.31A980F1060C1B0E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Blocky trees, bright grass, a sky of old. You remember the world looking exactly like this, once.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a rare Biomes O' Plenty biome styled after Minecraft's earliest days."
		"&eTip:&r there's a snowy version too, the wintry origin valley."
	]
	chapter.1C4BA472D45EB848.title: "Monster Hunting"
	chapter.1C4BA472D45EB848.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Every monster is just chemistry with bad manners."
	]
	quest.544849C91E73A547.title: "Zombie Hunter"
	quest.544849C91E73A547.quest_subtitle: "Kill 25 zombies"
	quest.544849C91E73A547.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember when the dead stayed down out of respect. Time to remind them.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the first line of the hunting page. Each tier asks for more of the same mob and pays out a Hunter's Bounty."
		"&eHow:&r zombies spawn in the dark and at night everywhere. A sword and shield are all you need."
		"&eTip:&r zombies burn in daylight; fight at dawn and let the sun help."
	]
	quest.3A8571E358829A4E.title: "Zombie Slayer"
	quest.3A8571E358829A4E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 100 zombies"
	quest.3A8571E358829A4E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hundred zombies. You'll get there just by playing at night."
		"&eChemistry:&r rotten flesh really is rotten: bacteria break proteins into amines like putrescine and cadaverine, which is where the smell comes from."
		"&eTip:&r a simple dark room over a spawner (YUNG's dungeons have plenty) speeds this up."
	]
	quest.07FFFFC27D98A06B.title: "Bane of the Dead"
	quest.07FFFFC27D98A06B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 500 zombies"
	quest.07FFFFC27D98A06B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r five hundred. This one is for people who build mob farms."
		"&eHow:&r a zombie spawner trap with a killing floor, or a Smite sword and a lot of nights."
		"&eTip:&r Smite adds damage against all undead: zombies, skeletons, wither skeletons, phantoms and the Wither."
	]
	quest.07F520C4C9DCA26D.title: "Bone Collector"
	quest.07F520C4C9DCA26D.quest_subtitle: "Kill 25 skeletons"
	quest.07F520C4C9DCA26D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r skeletons drop bones and arrows, and sometimes their bow."
		"&eChemistry:&r bone meal is crushed bone: calcium phosphate, a real phosphorus fertiliser for plants."
		"&eHow:&r raise your shield when they draw, then close in between shots."
		"&eTip:&r strafing sideways makes skeletons miss most of their arrows."
	]
	quest.3768FF31E575A11C.title: "Skeleton Slayer"
	quest.3768FF31E575A11C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 100 skeletons"
	quest.3768FF31E575A11C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hundred skeletons, and a full stack of bones for bone meal."
		"&eHow:&r keep killing them at night, or trap a skeleton spawner."
		"&eTip:&r a skeleton spawner farm is also an arrow farm."
	]
	quest.67858DD92CCB0EF4.title: "Ossuary"
	quest.67858DD92CCB0EF4.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 500 skeletons"
	quest.67858DD92CCB0EF4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r five hundred skeletons. Build a farm."
		"&eHow:&r YUNG's skeleton dungeons have several spawners close together; trap them."
		"&eTip:&r Looting raises bone and arrow drops."
	]
	quest.2787A073A108D244.title: "Undead of Every Climate"
	quest.2787A073A108D244.quest_subtitle: "Husks, strays and drowned"
	quest.2787A073A108D244.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the undead adapt to their biome: husks in deserts, strays in the snow, drowned in the water."
		"&eHow:&r husks don't burn in daylight; strays shoot slowness arrows; drowned may carry tridents."
		"&eTip:&r a drowned holding a trident can drop it. The trident is worth the hunt."
	]
	quest.6882F9EA87616B2D.title: "Tide Breaker"
	quest.6882F9EA87616B2D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 100 drowned"
	quest.6882F9EA87616B2D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hundred drowned, for copper ingots, nautilus shells and the occasional trident."
		"&eChemistry:&r fitting loot for the sea: copper resists seawater well, because it grows a protective skin of copper oxides and chlorides."
		"&eHow:&r rivers and oceans at night. Channeling or Impaling help."
	]
	quest.3FA449155D4FEA25.title: "Creeper Hunter"
	quest.3FA449155D4FEA25.quest_subtitle: "Kill 25 creepers"
	quest.3FA449155D4FEA25.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r creepers drop gunpowder, the oldest chemical explosive."
		"&eChemistry:&r gunpowder is potassium nitrate, charcoal and sulfur. The nitrate (KNO₃) supplies the oxygen: 2KNO₃ + S + 3C → K₂S + N₂ + 3CO₂."
		"&eHow:&r hit and step back; a creeper resets its fuse when you leave its range."
		"&eTip:&r a bow is the safest creeper tool there is."
	]
	quest.06935A94927B14A4.title: "Demolition Expert"
	quest.06935A94927B14A4.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 100 creepers"
	quest.06935A94927B14A4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hundred creepers and a pile of gunpowder for TNT and rockets."
		"&eHow:&r keep hunting at night; a Knockback sword keeps them away from you."
		"&eTip:&r a creeper killed by a skeleton's arrow drops a music disc."
	]
	quest.7F28D5737D25033D.title: "Ssssilence"
	quest.7F28D5737D25033D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 250 creepers"
	quest.7F28D5737D25033D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r two hundred and fifty creepers. The world is quieter now."
		"&eHow:&r a mob farm, or many careful nights."
		"&eTip:&r cats scare creepers away from your base."
	]
	quest.0F182C0FD3BF28FC.title: "Spider Hunter"
	quest.0F182C0FD3BF28FC.quest_subtitle: "Kill 25 spiders"
	quest.0F182C0FD3BF28FC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r spiders drop string and spider eyes."
		"&eChemistry:&r a fermented spider eye (eye + sugar + brown mushroom) turns potions into their opposites; real fermentation is microbes turning sugars into new compounds like ethanol and acids."
		"&eHow:&r spiders climb walls; build with an overhang to keep them out."
		"&eTip:&r spiders are neutral in daylight unless you hit them."
	]
	quest.68FD0B5C8685AEC6.title: "Arachnophobe"
	quest.68FD0B5C8685AEC6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 100 spiders"
	quest.68FD0B5C8685AEC6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hundred spiders, and enough string for every bow and wool block you need."
		"&eHow:&r spiders spawn on the surface at night; Bane of Arthropods helps."
		"&eTip:&r string from spiders makes wool: four string per block."
	]
	quest.6E22D2D1C73AD43E.title: "Cave Spiders"
	quest.6E22D2D1C73AD43E.quest_subtitle: "Kill 25 cave spiders"
	quest.6E22D2D1C73AD43E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r small, poisonous spiders that only come from spawners in mineshafts and spider caves."
		"&eChemistry:&r milk cures poison in Minecraft; in reality there's no general antidote, and venoms are treated with antivenom antibodies."
		"&eHow:&r find a mineshaft or YUNG's spider cave and fight near the spawner. Carry milk."
		"&eTip:&r torches on and around the spawner stop it."
	]
	quest.30F228CCC8B496B2.title: "Pearl Diver"
	quest.30F228CCC8B496B2.quest_subtitle: "Kill 16 endermen"
	quest.30F228CCC8B496B2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r endermen drop ender pearls: teleportation, eyes of ender and many machines."
		"&eHow:&r look at one to make it attack, then fight with your back to a 2-block-high gap; it can't follow under a low roof."
		"&eTip:&r endermen hate water. A rain storm sends them teleporting away."
	]
	quest.253114F2D024BB07.title: "Enderman Slayer"
	quest.253114F2D024BB07.quest_subtitle: "Kill 64 endermen"
	quest.253114F2D024BB07.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a stack of kills and, with luck, a stack of pearls."
		"&eHow:&r warped forests in the Nether and the End are full of them."
		"&eTip:&r a carved pumpkin on your head lets you look at endermen safely."
	]
	quest.58C7893587424EDB.title: "Void Walker"
	quest.58C7893587424EDB.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 256 endermen"
	quest.58C7893587424EDB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r four stacks of endermen. You'll need an End farm or a lot of patience."
		"&eHow:&r an enderman farm on the outer End islands is the classic way."
		"&eTip:&r endermites make endermen aggressive; that's how most End farms lure them."
	]
	quest.7E196F63F0F0A960.title: "Witch Hunt"
	quest.7E196F63F0F0A960.quest_subtitle: "Kill 10 witches"
	quest.7E196F63F0F0A960.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r witches throw potions and drink their own to heal. They drop redstone, glowstone, sugar and bottles."
		"&eChemistry:&r glowstone dust in-game is a brewing amplifier; real \"glow\" chemicals (like the zinc sulfide in glow paint) store light and release it slowly."
		"&eHow:&r rush them; at range they out-potion you. Milk clears their effects."
		"&eTip:&r swamp huts spawn witches over and over: a classic redstone farm."
	]
	quest.5518E80E2B9B731B.title: "Coven Breaker"
	quest.5518E80E2B9B731B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 50 witches"
	quest.5518E80E2B9B731B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fifty witches and a pile of redstone and glowstone."
		"&eHow:&r a swamp hut farm, or raids (witches join them)."
		"&eTip:&r witches are immune to most potion damage; use a sword or bow."
	]
	quest.3789F700DBDAA49F.title: "Slime Time"
	quest.3789F700DBDAA49F.quest_subtitle: "Kill 25 slimes"
	quest.3789F700DBDAA49F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r slimes split when killed; the smallest drop slimeballs for sticky pistons and leads."
		"&eChemistry:&r real slime is a polymer gel: long molecules cross-linked loosely enough to flow, like borax and PVA glue."
		"&eHow:&r slimes spawn in swamps at night and in slime chunks underground."
		"&eTip:&r every split counts as a kill. A big slime is many kills."
	]
	quest.63D72081F346D7E0.title: "Night Terrors"
	quest.63D72081F346D7E0.quest_subtitle: "Kill 10 phantoms"
	quest.63D72081F346D7E0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r phantoms dive at players who haven't slept for three nights. Their membranes repair elytra."
		"&eHow:&r stay up three nights, then fight with a bow on open ground at night."
		"&eTip:&r once you're done, sleep: it resets the timer and phantoms stop coming."
	]
	quest.6349CF403F409E40.title: "Skyclearer"
	quest.6349CF403F409E40.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 50 phantoms"
	quest.6349CF403F409E40.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fifty phantoms, and enough membranes to keep an elytra flying for a long time."
		"&eHow:&r a bow with Power, or a trident with Loyalty, and a sleepless week."
		"&eTip:&r phantoms are undead; Smite works on them."
	]
	quest.7C77F3713A93792F.title: "Pest Control"
	quest.7C77F3713A93792F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 50 silverfish"
	quest.7C77F3713A93792F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r silverfish hide in infested stone in strongholds and mountains, and call their friends when hurt."
		"&eHow:&r YUNG's strongholds are full of infested blocks; a single blow kills each one."
		"&eTip:&r don't break blocks near a silverfish fight; you'll wake more."
	]
	quest.5B7746A8D5C8363A.title: "The Trials"
	quest.5B7746A8D5C8363A.quest_subtitle: "Kill 10 breezes and 10 bogged"
	quest.5B7746A8D5C8363A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r two mobs from 1.21: breezes (wind spirits) and bogged (mossy skeletons with poison arrows), both from trial chambers."
		"&eHow:&r find a trial chamber (see the Exploration page) and fight the trial spawners."
		"&eTip:&r breeze rods make wind charges and the mace."
	]
	quest.325CC7A411B2A8F9.title: "Pillager Hunter"
	quest.325CC7A411B2A8F9.quest_subtitle: "Kill 25 pillagers"
	quest.325CC7A411B2A8F9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r crossbow-armed illagers from outposts and patrols."
		"&eHow:&r a shield blocks their bolts. Outposts respawn pillagers around the tower."
		"&eTip:&r a captain (banner on its head) gives Bad Omen when killed: drink the ominous bottle to start a raid."
	]
	quest.4AB7BA8E5DA7EFFF.title: "Outpost Breaker"
	quest.4AB7BA8E5DA7EFFF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 100 pillagers"
	quest.4AB7BA8E5DA7EFFF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hundred pillagers."
		"&eHow:&r camp an outpost or run raids. Raids bring them in waves."
		"&eTip:&r a raid farm is the best emerald source in the game."
	]
	quest.24E4368C41967996.title: "Axes of Malice"
	quest.24E4368C41967996.quest_subtitle: "Kill 10 vindicators"
	quest.24E4368C41967996.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r axe-wielding illagers from raids and woodland mansions. They hit very hard."
		"&eHow:&r keep your shield up; their axes can disable it, so back off after a block."
		"&eTip:&r a vindicator named \"Johnny\" attacks every mob in sight."
	]
	quest.3E29A8FDA2E99B04.title: "Evoker Bane"
	quest.3E29A8FDA2E99B04.quest_subtitle: "Kill 3 evokers"
	quest.3E29A8FDA2E99B04.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r evokers summon fangs and vexes. Each one drops a Totem of Undying."
		"&eHow:&r they come in later raid waves and live in woodland mansions. Kill the evoker first; its vexes die with it."
		"&eTip:&r keep a totem in your off-hand when fighting raids."
	]
	quest.19A9413C7BECB803.title: "Beast of the Raid"
	quest.19A9413C7BECB803.quest_subtitle: "Kill 3 ravagers"
	quest.19A9413C7BECB803.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ravagers are huge raid beasts that trample crops and charge."
		"&eHow:&r they appear in raids from wave 3 on. Block the charge with a shield, then counterattack while it's stunned."
		"&eTip:&r ravagers drop saddles."
	]
	quest.502A6AE02C3F21B9.title: "Guardian Hunter"
	quest.502A6AE02C3F21B9.quest_subtitle: "Kill 25 guardians"
	quest.502A6AE02C3F21B9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the spiky fish of ocean monuments. They drop prismarine shards and crystals."
		"&eChemistry:&r prismarine is in-game sea crystal; real sea creatures build shells and spines from calcium carbonate and silica pulled out of seawater."
		"&eHow:&r find a monument (see the Exploration page). Break line of sight when their laser charges."
		"&eTip:&r water breathing and Depth Strider make monuments much easier."
	]
	quest.3B3FCDB389203401.title: "Gold in the Rot"
	quest.3B3FCDB389203401.quest_subtitle: "Kill 50 zombified piglins"
	quest.3B3FCDB389203401.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r zombified piglins drop gold nuggets and rotten flesh."
		"&eHow:&r they're neutral until you hit one, then the whole crowd comes. Fight in a corridor."
		"&eTip:&r gold farms over Nether-roof portals are a classic build."
	]
	quest.25C1958DAE2F684A.title: "Blaze Hunter"
	quest.25C1958DAE2F684A.quest_subtitle: "Kill 25 blazes"
	quest.25C1958DAE2F684A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r blazes drop blaze rods: brewing stands, blaze powder and eyes of ender."
		"&eChemistry:&r blazes throw fireballs; real fireballs need fuel plus oxygen, which is why a fire triangle (heat, fuel, O₂) puts them out when you remove any side."
		"&eHow:&r blaze spawners sit in Nether fortresses. Snowballs hurt them."
		"&eTip:&r fire resistance makes you immune to their fireballs."
	]
	quest.701B865E5BC4BFC5.title: "Blaze Slayer"
	quest.701B865E5BC4BFC5.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 100 blazes"
	quest.701B865E5BC4BFC5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hundred blazes and a good supply of rods."
		"&eHow:&r build a blaze farm around a fortress spawner."
		"&eTip:&r blaze rods are a good furnace fuel: 12 items each."
	]
	quest.4BDCC9A8EB40A6B9.title: "Ghastbuster"
	quest.4BDCC9A8EB40A6B9.quest_subtitle: "Kill 10 ghasts"
	quest.4BDCC9A8EB40A6B9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ghasts drop ghast tears (regeneration potions, end crystals) and gunpowder."
		"&eHow:&r hit their fireballs back at them with a sword or an arrow."
		"&eTip:&r kill them over solid ground, not lava, or the tear is lost."
	]
	quest.6C85B3B27CEA7AB0.title: "Hot Jelly"
	quest.6C85B3B27CEA7AB0.quest_subtitle: "Kill 50 magma cubes"
	quest.6C85B3B27CEA7AB0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r magma cubes split like slimes and drop magma cream for fire resistance."
		"&eHow:&r basalt deltas are full of them."
		"&eTip:&r every split counts as a kill."
	]
	quest.38A42A798875518D.title: "Skull Hunter"
	quest.38A42A798875518D.quest_subtitle: "Kill 25 wither skeletons"
	quest.38A42A798875518D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tall black skeletons in Nether fortresses. They sometimes drop their skull; three summon the Wither."
		"&eHow:&r fight in a 2-block-high tunnel; they're three blocks tall and can't follow."
		"&eTip:&r Looting raises the skull drop chance."
	]
	quest.3C7A0FC62606150B.title: "Bonebreaker"
	quest.3C7A0FC62606150B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 100 wither skeletons"
	quest.3C7A0FC62606150B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hundred wither skeletons, and enough skulls for several Withers."
		"&eHow:&r a wither skeleton farm on a fortress platform."
		"&eTip:&r a Smite sword kills them quickly."
	]
	quest.6463056EC87BB840.title: "Bastion Brawl"
	quest.6463056EC87BB840.quest_subtitle: "Kill 5 piglin brutes and 10 hoglins"
	quest.6463056EC87BB840.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the toughest regular Nether fighters: axe-armed piglin brutes in bastions and charging hoglins in crimson forests."
		"&eChemistry:&r hoglins fear warped fungus; real animals avoid many plant compounds, which evolved as chemical defences."
		"&eHow:&r brutes ignore gold armour; fight them in doorways. Hoglins drop pork and leather."
		"&eTip:&r hoglins turn into zoglins in the Overworld, so don't bring one home."
	]
	quest.0BA05583E0D3118B.title: "Shell Game"
	quest.0BA05583E0D3118B.quest_subtitle: "Kill 20 shulkers"
	quest.0BA05583E0D3118B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r shulkers hide in End Cities and drop shells for shulker boxes."
		"&eHow:&r hit them when their shell opens. Their bullets make you levitate."
		"&eTip:&r carry milk or slow falling against levitation."
	]
	quest.4DAB5F2E15BD1E7F.title: "The Rotspawn"
	quest.4DAB5F2E15BD1E7F.quest_subtitle: "Undergarden's rotting horde"
	quest.4DAB5F2E15BD1E7F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Undergarden's undead-like rotspawn: small rotlings, tall rotwalkers and the huge rotbeast."
		"&eHow:&r utherium weapons deal extra damage to rotspawn."
		"&eTip:&r rotbeasts hit hard and have a lot of health; fight them in the open."
	]
	quest.3E7FE9B8E21A772D.title: "Things in the Dark"
	quest.3E7FE9B8E21A772D.quest_subtitle: "Nargoyles and munchers"
	quest.3E7FE9B8E21A772D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r more Undergarden predators: nargoyles and the hungry munchers."
		"&eHow:&r explore the Undergarden at length; both turn up in its caverns."
		"&eTip:&r cloggrum armour is the Undergarden's best early protection."
	]
	quest.23851676A0A2DF97.title: "Sculk Fauna"
	quest.23851676A0A2DF97.quest_subtitle: "Snappers and centipedes"
	quest.23851676A0A2DF97.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r creatures of the Otherside, grown from sculk."
		"&eHow:&r roam the Otherside's biomes. Sneak to approach without alerting the sculk."
		"&eTip:&r carry food and a way home; the Otherside is a long way from your base."
	]
	quest.6C4CA5C87E1715D4.title: "Shattered and Stalkers"
	quest.6C4CA5C87E1715D4.quest_subtitle: "The Otherside's hunters"
	quest.6C4CA5C87E1715D4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r shattered drop sculk bones; stalkers drop soul crystals. Both go into the soul elytra."
		"&eHow:&r both hunt by sound like the Warden. Fight at range."
		"&eTip:&r sneak to keep your footsteps quiet."
	]
	quest.5E83D1D3C67233ED.title: "Martian Raptors"
	quest.5E83D1D3C67233ED.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill 10 raptors on Mars"
	quest.5E83D1D3C67233ED.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fast predators of the Martian surface."
		"&eChemistry:&r anything living on Mars would need to cope with perchlorates (ClO₄⁻), reactive salts found in real Martian soil."
		"&eHow:&r land on Mars and hunt in the wastelands. Keep your suit topped up."
	]
	quest.68D285E63CF52E20.title: "Twilight Pests"
	quest.68D285E63CF52E20.quest_subtitle: "Redcaps, kobolds and swarm spiders"
	quest.68D285E63CF52E20.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the common hostile mobs of the Twilight Forest."
		"&eHow:&r redcaps and kobolds roam the forest; swarm spiders spawn around hollow hills and spider-infested spots."
		"&eTip:&r redcap sappers carry TNT; kill them before they light it."
	]
	quest.7506A7C163583FD3.title: "Maze and Swamp"
	quest.7506A7C163583FD3.quest_subtitle: "Minotaurs, maze slimes and druids"
	quest.7506A7C163583FD3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r guardians of the labyrinth and the swamp beyond the Lich."
		"&eHow:&r minotaurs and maze slimes fill the labyrinth; skeleton druids lurk in the forest at night."
		"&eTip:&r maze slimes split like regular slimes."
	]
	quest.260C93AB006F87B1.title: "Goblins and Ghastguards"
	quest.260C93AB006F87B1.quest_subtitle: "Stronghold and Dark Tower guards"
	quest.260C93AB006F87B1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r goblin knights and block-and-chain goblins hold the Goblin Stronghold; carminite ghastguards haunt the Dark Tower."
		"&eHow:&r goblin knights ride in pairs; knock off the upper one, then finish the lower."
		"&eTip:&r ghastguards' fireballs can be hit back like a ghast's."
	]
	quest.4D50CBE90F48364F.title: "Snow Beasts"
	quest.4D50CBE90F48364F.quest_subtitle: "Yetis and winter wolves"
	quest.4D50CBE90F48364F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the snowy forest's hunters. Yetis drop arctic fur for warm armour."
		"&eHow:&r yetis guard the Alpha Yeti's cave; winter wolves roam the snowy forest and breathe frost."
		"&eTip:&r winter wolves come in packs; back against a tree."
	]
	quest.141CF02320F05EF3.title: "Trolls and Giants"
	quest.141CF02320F05EF3.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the highlands' heavyweights"
	quest.141CF02320F05EF3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r trolls in the troll caves and giant miners on the highlands."
		"&eHow:&r trolls throw rocks; giants swing slowly but hard. Fight both from range."
		"&eTip:&r giant miners drop giant pickaxes."
	]
	quest.68F983645DEC5133.title: "Elder Guardians"
	quest.68F983645DEC5133.quest_subtitle: "All three elders of a monument"
	quest.68F983645DEC5133.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each ocean monument holds three elder guardians. They cast Mining Fatigue until all three are dead."
		"&eHow:&r the elders sit in the top room and two wing rooms. Water breathing, a good sword and patience."
		"&eTip:&r elders drop wet sponges and, sometimes, a tide armour trim."
	]
	quest.62C34C9BAFF44652.title: "The Wither"
	quest.62C34C9BAFF44652.quest_subtitle: "Summon it, kill it, take its star"
	quest.62C34C9BAFF44652.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember making stars. This one you'll have to take.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Wither is the Nether's boss, summoned by the player. It drops a Nether Star for beacons and many late recipes."
		"&eHow:&r four soul sand in a T with three wither skeleton skulls on top. Summon it deep underground or far from base: it destroys blocks."
		"&eTip:&r below half health it gains armour that stops arrows; switch to a Smite sword."
	]
	chapter.355E4A964218121E.title: "Farming and Food"
	chapter.355E4A964218121E.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Grow what you need, cook it well, feed it back to the soil."
	]
	quest.61BB360C973E0F7F.title: "Knife and Board"
	quest.61BB360C973E0F7F.quest_subtitle: "Farmer's Delight starts with a cut"
	quest.61BB360C973E0F7F.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember feasts that lasted a week. Start with something smaller.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Farmer's Delight adds crops, meals and kitchen blocks. The knife harvests straw and cuts ingredients."
		"&eHow:&r craft a Flint Knife and a Cutting Board. Place items on the board and use the knife on them."
		"&eTip:&r a knife on tall grass gives straw; wild crops (tomatoes, onions, cabbage, rice) grow in the wild."
	]
	quest.1CD576F80AC49B5F.title: "Cooking Pot"
	quest.1CD576F80AC49B5F.quest_subtitle: "Heat, ingredients, and a meal"
	quest.1CD576F80AC49B5F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Cooking Pot turns several ingredients into one meal. It needs heat underneath."
		"&eChemistry:&r browning meat is the Maillard reaction: amino acids and sugars react above about 140 °C, making hundreds of flavour compounds."
		"&eHow:&r iron, bricks, a wooden shovel and a water bucket (check JEI). Place it over a fire, campfire or Stove."
	]
	quest.2CFFEDC4683607CF.title: "A Proper Meal"
	quest.2CFFEDC4683607CF.quest_subtitle: "Food that keeps you full"
	quest.2CFFEDC4683607CF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Farmer's Delight meals restore a lot of hunger and give long effects like Nourishment (hunger stops dropping) and Comfort."
		"&eHow:&r cook vegetable soup in the Cooking Pot (check JEI), then bowl it."
		"&eTip:&r a Feeding Upgrade in your backpack eats these for you."
	]
	quest.6AAF559710229117.title: "Pasta with Meatballs"
	quest.6AAF559710229117.quest_subtitle: "Four ingredients, three of them cooked first"
	quest.6AAF559710229117.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hearty meal that chains every kitchen tool: knife (minced beef), board (raw pasta from dough) and pot (tomato sauce)."
		"&eChemistry:&r dough is starch and gluten proteins; water lets gluten chains cross-link into the stretchy network that holds pasta together."
		"&eHow:&r follow the tree in JEI: wheat dough → raw pasta, beef → minced beef, tomatoes → tomato sauce, then the pot."
		"&eTip:&r press U on any ingredient in JEI to see every meal that uses it."
	]
	quest.6E91CE0ADEA5ADA6.title: "A Varied Diet"
	quest.6E91CE0ADEA5ADA6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: any six Farmer's Delight meals"
	quest.6E91CE0ADEA5ADA6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r collect six bowls or plates of any Farmer's Delight meal: stews, soups, rice dishes, ratatouille, you choose."
		"&eHow:&r anything in the 'meals' tag counts. Mix and match, they don't have to be different."
		"&eTip:&r meals stack to 16; keep a stack in the backpack for long mining trips."
	]
	quest.26CA44769AF76A9D.title: "Rich Soil"
	quest.26CA44769AF76A9D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: compost into the best dirt"
	quest.26CA44769AF76A9D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r organic compost slowly turns into Rich Soil, which grows crops faster and mushrooms into colonies."
		"&eChemistry:&r composting is microbes breaking down organic matter with oxygen. They release CO₂ and heat, and leave humus rich in nitrogen."
		"&eHow:&r craft compost from dirt, straw and bone meal plus rotten flesh or tree bark (check JEI), place it and wait."
		"&eTip:&r till Rich Soil with a hoe to get rich farmland for crops."
	]
	quest.2FB463350074B333.title: "The Stove"
	quest.2FB463350074B333.quest_subtitle: "A heat source that never burns out"
	quest.2FB463350074B333.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Stove heats a Cooking Pot or Skillet on top and can grill up to six items on its own surface."
		"&eHow:&r iron ingots, bricks and a campfire (check JEI). Light it with flint and steel."
		"&eTip:&r unlike a campfire it doesn't need logs, and it looks right in a kitchen."
	]
	quest.1DF7F1133046DEB1.title: "A Feast"
	quest.1DF7F1133046DEB1.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one block feeds the whole team"
	quest.1DF7F1133046DEB1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r feasts are placed as blocks and served with a bowl, several portions each."
		"&eHow:&r cook a Honey Glazed Ham (check JEI). Place it on a table and right-click with bowls."
		"&eTip:&r a feast is the easiest way to feed a whole team before a boss fight."
	]
	quest.188A4BC2D2682264.title: "Banquet"
	quest.188A4BC2D2682264.quest_subtitle: "Optional: roast chicken and shepherd's pie"
	quest.188A4BC2D2682264.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r two more feasts for the table: a whole Roast Chicken and a Shepherd's Pie."
		"&eHow:&r both come from the Cooking Pot (check JEI). Each needs a container, often a bowl, to serve."
		"&eTip:&r place feasts where everyone passes, like next to the team's waystone."
	]
	quest.68C63D9C708CAB99.title: "Mushroom Colonies"
	quest.68C63D9C708CAB99.quest_subtitle: "Optional: mushrooms that keep growing"
	quest.68C63D9C708CAB99.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a mushroom on Rich Soil grows into a colony that you can harvest again and again."
		"&eChemistry:&r fungi don't photosynthesise. They digest organic matter with enzymes, which is why rich, dark soil suits them."
		"&eHow:&r plant a brown or red mushroom on Rich Soil in low light, wait, then harvest it with shears; the colony stays and regrows."
		"&eTip:&r mushroom colonies are the steady source of mushrooms for stews and rice dishes."
	]
	quest.05CA20DAF3D6CE4E.title: "Skillet"
	quest.05CA20DAF3D6CE4E.quest_subtitle: "Fry it, or hit something with it"
	quest.05CA20DAF3D6CE4E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a frying pan that cooks one item at a time over heat, and doubles as a surprisingly good weapon."
		"&eHow:&r iron ingots and a brick (check JEI). Place it on the Stove or a campfire, or check its tooltip for cooking in hand."
		"&eTip:&r Fire Aspect on a skillet sounds silly; it works."
	]
	quest.056B1AE78D5B1CCF.title: "Breakfast"
	quest.056B1AE78D5B1CCF.quest_subtitle: "Eggs and bacon from the skillet"
	quest.056B1AE78D5B1CCF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the start of most Farmer's Delight breakfasts: fried eggs and cooked bacon."
		"&eChemistry:&r egg white turns opaque as heat unfolds its proteins (denaturation) and they tangle together; it can't go back."
		"&eHow:&r cut raw porkchop into bacon on the Cutting Board, then fry it and the eggs on the Skillet or Stove."
		"&eTip:&r combine them into Bacon and Eggs in the Cooking Pot (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.6D7BCF15F3CF7687.title: "The New Crops"
	quest.6D7BCF15F3CF7687.quest_subtitle: "Tomatoes, onions, cabbage and rice"
	quest.6D7BCF15F3CF7687.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Farmer's Delight crops are the base of nearly every meal."
		"&eHow:&r find wild tomatoes, onions, cabbages and rice in the world (rice grows in shallow water). Break them for seeds and replant."
		"&eTip:&r rice must be planted in water one block deep, like in a real paddy."
	]
	quest.2D35837B42389FD6.title: "Tomatoes on a Rope"
	quest.2D35837B42389FD6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: grow upward"
	quest.2D35837B42389FD6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tomato vines climb rope, so a single plant grows several blocks tall and fruits all the way up."
		"&eHow:&r craft rope from straw (check JEI), hang it above a tomato plant, and let the vine climb."
		"&eTip:&r rope also lets you climb down mineshafts; right-click a placed rope to extend it downward."
	]
	quest.726507D0921F20DA.title: "Harvest Festival"
	quest.726507D0921F20DA.quest_subtitle: "Optional: 128 crops of any kind"
	quest.726507D0921F20DA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a full harvest: any 128 items from the shared crops tag (wheat, carrots, potatoes, tomatoes, rice and more)."
		"&eHow:&r a large field, Hopper Botany Pots, or an MI Farmer all count. Carry them in one go."
		"&eTip:&r crop storage blocks (crates and bags) pack 9 crops each; you need the loose crops here."
	]
	quest.3890E7B5FA9CA044.title: "Hopper Botany Pots"
	quest.3890E7B5FA9CA044.quest_subtitle: "A farm in one block"
	quest.3890E7B5FA9CA044.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Hopper Botany Pots grow crops and push the harvest into the container below."
		"&eHow:&r place one on a chest, add soil (dirt) and a seed."
		"&eTip:&r Rich Soil or farmland grows faster than dirt, and Mystical Agriculture seeds work in pots too."
	]
	quest.1449CF00D49726FD.title: "Animal Husbandry"
	quest.1449CF00D49726FD.quest_subtitle: "Breeding, explained by Just Enough Breeding"
	quest.1449CF00D49726FD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r cows, sheep, pigs and chickens give food, leather, wool and eggs. Two adults fed their favourite food make a baby."
		"&eHow:&r lead two animals into a pen and feed them. Just Enough Breeding adds a JEI page per animal: look up any mob egg or food to see what it eats and what it drops."
		"&eTip:&r babies take about 20 minutes to grow; feeding them their breeding food speeds that up."
	]
	quest.797F266229BD1FB2.title: "Pet Food"
	quest.797F266229BD1FB2.quest_subtitle: "Optional: feed for horses and wolves"
	quest.797F266229BD1FB2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Horse Feed heals and speeds up horses; Dog Food heals tamed wolves and gives them buffs."
		"&eHow:&r both are Farmer's Delight crafting recipes (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a well-fed wolf is a decent bodyguard in the early Twilight Forest."
	]
	quest.383BB756C9C76954.title: "N, P and K"
	quest.383BB756C9C76954.quest_subtitle: "The three numbers on every fertiliser bag"
	quest.383BB756C9C76954.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r plants need nitrogen (N), phosphorus (P) and potassium (K) more than anything else from the soil. These three compounds deliver them."
		"&eChemistry:&r urea CO(NH₂)₂ is 46% nitrogen; diammonium phosphate (NH₄)₂HPO₄ carries N and P; potassium nitrate KNO₃ carries K and N."
		"&eHow:&r make all three in the Alchemistry Combiner (check JEI for the element recipe of each)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: why nitrogen is the hard one.&r"
		"Air is 78% nitrogen, but N₂ has a triple bond that plants can't break. Only some soil bacteria (and lightning) can 'fix' it."
		"In 1909 Fritz Haber found how to force N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃ with a metal catalyst, high pressure and heat; Carl Bosch scaled it up."
		"Today about half the nitrogen in your body passed through a Haber-Bosch plant. Ammonia is turned into urea, ammonium nitrate and phosphates."
		"You'll build that same reaction in the main quests (Haber-Bosch, HV tier). Phosphorus comes from mined phosphate rock, and potassium from potash salts like KCl."
	]
	quest.201E746EF18C024B.title: "NPK Fertilizer"
	quest.201E746EF18C024B.quest_subtitle: "Liquid fertiliser from the Chemical Reactor"
	quest.201E746EF18C024B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Extended Industrialization's NPK Fertilizer is a fluid the MI Farmer can spread to grow crops faster."
		"&eChemistry:&r bone meal is calcium phosphate; sulfuric acid frees phosphoric acid, H₃PO₄, just like the real 'wet process' for phosphate rock."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor, three steps (check JEI): bone meal + H₂SO₄ → phosphoric acid; potato/carrot/beetroot + water + HCl → potassium chloride, then KCl + H₂ + O₂ → potassium hydroxide; finally nitrogen + phosphoric acid + KOH → NPK Fertilizer."
		"&eTip:&r real NPK plants start from ammonia, not raw nitrogen. Here the recipe takes the shortcut."
	]
	quest.42489EAAE4800867.title: "The Steam Farmer"
	quest.42489EAAE4800867.quest_subtitle: "A multiblock that plants and harvests"
	quest.42489EAAE4800867.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Extended Industrialization's Farmer is a multiblock that tills, plants, harvests and (with fertiliser) speeds up a whole field."
		"&eHow:&r analog circuits, a motor, bronze plated bricks, a steel combine and a bronze pipe casing (check JEI). Its layout is in JEI and the MI guidebook."
		"&eTip:&r the Electric Farmer is the upgrade. JEI has a fertiliser page that shows which fluids speed up a Farmer."
	]
	quest.4388A334EC12570D.title: "Food Fight"
	quest.4388A334EC12570D.quest_subtitle: "Secret: ammunition, not dinner"
	quest.4388A334EC12570D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r you found a use for spoiled tomatoes: rotten tomatoes can be thrown."
		"&eChemistry:&r rotting is bacteria and fungi breaking sugars into acids, alcohols and gases. Don't eat it."
		"&eTip:&r they're also good compost material. Probably better than throwing them at the team."
	]
	chapter.1C9E9D35BDB125AE.title: "Mystical Agriculture"
	chapter.1C9E9D35BDB125AE.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Resource crops, within the rules of chemistry."
	]
	quest.7592FE8784DA7D0E.title: "Mystical Agriculture"
	quest.7592FE8784DA7D0E.quest_subtitle: "Resource crops, made on an altar"
	quest.7592FE8784DA7D0E.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember coaxing metal out of the ground like wheat. Some of that still works.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r resource crops grow essence that crafts into real materials. Seeds are made on the Infusion Altar with Infusion Pedestals around it."
		"&eHow:&r inferium ore gives inferium essence (mobs drop some too). The altar is gold, stone and red wool; pedestals are in JEI."
		"&eTip:&r &eTier 3/4/5 seeds need MI LV/MV/HV circuits&r, and crops for chemistry milestones can't be grown at all. Farming is a convenience here, not a shortcut."
	]
	quest.476972F4A69AE2B6.title: "Prosperity"
	quest.476972F4A69AE2B6.quest_subtitle: "Shards for seed bases and crystals"
	quest.476972F4A69AE2B6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r prosperity shards come from prosperity ore. They make seed bases (the core of every resource seed) and infusion crystals."
		"&eHow:&r mine prosperity ore; 4 shards around wheat seeds make a Prosperity Seed Base."
		"&eTip:&r Ultimine the veins; you'll want a lot of shards."
	]
	quest.53DFFD39635750E6.title: "Infusion Crystal"
	quest.53DFFD39635750E6.quest_subtitle: "The tool that upgrades essence"
	quest.53DFFD39635750E6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a crystal that combines lower essence into higher tiers. It wears out with use."
		"&eHow:&r a diamond, prosperity shards and inferium essence (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the Master Infusion Crystal never wears out; it comes much later, from supremium."
	]
	quest.05F6FABCA51A5D27.title: "Prudentium"
	quest.05F6FABCA51A5D27.quest_subtitle: "Tier 2 essence"
	quest.05F6FABCA51A5D27.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the second essence tier, for tier 2 seeds (JEI lists every crop and its tier)."
		"&eHow:&r 4 inferium essence around an infusion crystal make 1 prudentium (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r it uncrafts back to inferium if you overshoot (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.63BC9482303C7949.title: "Tertium: LV Seeds"
	quest.63BC9482303C7949.quest_subtitle: "Tier 3 seeds need an analog circuit"
	quest.63BC9482303C7949.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tier 3 seeds (iron, copper, redstone, nether quartz, tin, lead and more) need Tertium essence and an &eMI analog circuit&r."
		"&eChemistry:&r the analog circuit stands on steel, and steel stands on coke: coal baked without air until only carbon is left."
		"&eHow:&r 4 prudentium around an infusion crystal make 1 tertium. Each seed type costs its circuit once; planted seeds multiply."
	]
	quest.429B4A2ABF9C8710.title: "Imperium: MV Seeds"
	quest.429B4A2ABF9C8710.quest_subtitle: "Tier 4 seeds need an electronic circuit"
	quest.429B4A2ABF9C8710.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tier 4 seeds (gold, lapis, nickel, blaze, enderman and more) need Imperium essence and an &eMI electronic circuit&r."
		"&eChemistry:&r the electronic circuit needs aluminum, which only electrolysis can free from its oxide: 2Al₂O₃ → 4Al + 3O₂."
		"&eHow:&r 4 tertium around an infusion crystal make 1 imperium."
	]
	quest.329417D2B6B5EF41.title: "Supremium: HV Seeds"
	quest.329417D2B6B5EF41.quest_subtitle: "Tier 5 seeds need a digital circuit"
	quest.329417D2B6B5EF41.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember gardens that grew gold. These come close, and they still answer to chemistry.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r tier 5 seeds (diamond, emerald, netherite and more) need Supremium essence and an &eMI digital circuit&r."
		"&eChemistry:&r the digital circuit needs polyethylene: thousands of ethylene units, C₂H₄, linked into one chain."
		"&eHow:&r 4 imperium around an infusion crystal make 1 supremium."
	]
	quest.12AA4108F02395E9.title: "Growth Accelerators"
	quest.12AA4108F02395E9.quest_subtitle: "Optional: crops grow faster above them"
	quest.12AA4108F02395E9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r growth accelerators placed below farmland speed up the crops above them. Stack several for more effect."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for each tier's recipe."
		"&eTip:&r put them under the floor of your crop room so they're out of the way."
	]
	quest.4D32DDE3DA6B6767.title: "Awakening"
	quest.4D32DDE3DA6B6767.quest_subtitle: "Optional: beyond supremium"
	quest.4D32DDE3DA6B6767.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Awakening Altar turns supremium into awakened supremium for the strongest Mystical Agriculture gear."
		"&eHow:&r JEI shows the altar, its Awakening Pedestals, the Essence Vessels and the awakening recipe."
		"&eTip:&r awakened supremium makes the best Mystical Agriculture tools and armour."
	]
	quest.7B1B5EF67E8690E8.title: "Master Infusion Crystal"
	quest.7B1B5EF67E8690E8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a crystal that never breaks"
	quest.7B1B5EF67E8690E8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an infusion crystal with no durability, so essence upgrades stop costing crystals."
		"&eHow:&r a supremium gemstone, supremium essence and prosperity shards (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r worth it once you are mass-producing tertium and imperium for seeds."
	]
	quest.08D5A196E95B09AF.title: "Inferium Seeds"
	quest.08D5A196E95B09AF.quest_subtitle: "The crop that grows more essence"
	quest.08D5A196E95B09AF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Inferium Seeds grow inferium essence, the fuel for every higher tier. Any 4 Mystical Agriculture seeds complete this."
		"&eHow:&r 8 inferium essence around wheat seeds in a crafting grid (no altar needed). Plant them on farmland and replant the extra seeds."
		"&eTip:&r every other resource seed starts from a seed base on the altar, so build a big inferium field first."
	]
	quest.05CAB1D55ED3D024.title: "Essence Farmland"
	quest.05CAB1D55ED3D024.quest_subtitle: "Better soil for inferium crops"
	quest.05CAB1D55ED3D024.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r farmland infused with essence. Inferium crops drop more essence on higher-tier farmland."
		"&eHow:&r one inferium essence plus one farmland, shapeless (check JEI). Higher tiers use their own essence."
		"&eTip:&r upgrade the farmland under your inferium field as each new essence tier arrives."
	]
	quest.54A29771FF1DDF78.title: "Mystical Fertilizer"
	quest.54A29771FF1DDF78.quest_subtitle: "Optional: grow a crop instantly"
	quest.54A29771FF1DDF78.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r instantly grows a crop or sapling, including resource crops that bone meal can't push."
		"&eHow:&r bone meal, inferium essence and a diamond make 4 (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r save it for slow, expensive crops rather than wheat."
	]
	quest.5839B7784C096EED.title: "Agglomeratio"
	quest.5839B7784C096EED.quest_subtitle: "Optional: materials for crops with no single item"
	quest.5839B7784C096EED.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r some crops (nature, the four elements, dye, nether, coral and others) don't map to one item. Their seed recipes use an agglomeratio instead."
		"&eHow:&r Nature Agglomeratio is pumpkin, potato, cactus and sugar cane; JEI shows the rest."
		"&eTip:&r the elemental crops (air, earth, water, fire) feed many other recipes, so they're good early picks."
	]
	quest.24AE5486AE474342.title: "Why Chemistry Won't Grow"
	quest.24AE5486AE474342.quest_subtitle: "Some seeds were removed on purpose"
	quest.24AE5486AE474342.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r seeds for uranium, uraninite, osmium, fluorite, silicon, steel, aluminum, graphite, platinum, iridium, refined obsidian and refined glowstone don't exist in this pack. Click the checkmark when you've read why."
		"&eHow:&r if JEI shows no altar recipe for a crop, it's one of these. Get them from ore processing and the reactors in the main quests."
		"&eTip:&r iron, copper, tin, lead, gold and other everyday metals are still farmable, behind their circuit gates."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: why these metals?&r"
		"Each blocked resource is the reason a tier exists. Steel needs carbon from coke and an oxygen-controlled furnace; aluminum needs electrolysis of molten alumina (Hall-Héroult, 2Al₂O₃ → 4Al + 3O₂)."
		"Silicon is reduced from quartz with carbon at about 2000 °C (SiO₂ + 2C → Si + 2CO). Fluorite is the fluorine source for uranium enrichment; uranium and uraninite are the nuclear chain."
		"Platinum and iridium come from the PGM line: anode sludge, aqua regia, ammonium hexachloroplatinate, calcining. Graphite and osmium gate Mekanism and MI steps."
		"Growing them on a plant would skip the chemistry those tiers teach. Everything else stays farmable, so farming saves time without replacing a single reaction."
	]
	quest.31B95BF1B78FC771.title: "Watering Can"
	quest.31B95BF1B78FC771.quest_subtitle: "Water speeds up growth"
	quest.31B95BF1B78FC771.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r right-click to water crops in an area, which makes them grow faster while you hold it."
		"&eHow:&r iron ingots, a bowl and bone meal (check JEI). Fill it from any water source."
		"&eTip:&r stand in the middle of the field and hold right-click."
	]
	quest.2AE6F05324BA2C59.title: "Inferium Ingots"
	quest.2AE6F05324BA2C59.quest_subtitle: "The metal for Mystical Agriculture gear"
	quest.2AE6F05324BA2C59.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r essence-infused ingots for tools, armour and the better watering cans."
		"&eHow:&r a prosperity ingot plus 2 inferium essence (check JEI for the prosperity ingot)."
		"&eTip:&r each essence tier has its own ingot; JEI shows the upgrade path."
	]
	quest.3BC7002FEB68725F.title: "Inferium Watering Can"
	quest.3BC7002FEB68725F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a bigger watering area"
	quest.3BC7002FEB68725F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a tiered watering can covers a larger area and works faster."
		"&eHow:&r your watering can, inferium ingots and mystical fertilizer (check JEI). The higher tiers repeat the pattern."
		"&eTip:&r the can keeps its contents when upgraded."
	]
	quest.08F7E833C88C6704.title: "A Lucky Harvest"
	quest.08F7E833C88C6704.quest_subtitle: "Secret: a rare drop from the field"
	quest.08F7E833C88C6704.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r crops sometimes drop Fertilized Essence. You found one."
		"&eHow:&r it crafts into mystical fertilizer (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r more crops means more chances; a big inferium field pays for itself."
	]
	quest.1A6616EA3169DE4E.title: "Soulstone"
	quest.1A6616EA3169DE4E.quest_subtitle: "A Nether stone with something inside"
	quest.1A6616EA3169DE4E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r soulstone clusters generate in the Nether. A few of their blocks are soulium ore, the source of soulium dust."
		"&eHow:&r mine soulstone in the Nether and watch for soulium ore (check JEI for its drops)."
		"&eTip:&r a soulium ingot is a prosperity ingot plus 2 soulium dust; soul dust (for soul glass) comes from smelting smooth soulstone."
	]
	quest.0A1E76D6BAED16FB.title: "Soulium Dagger"
	quest.0A1E76D6BAED16FB.quest_subtitle: "A blade that collects souls"
	quest.0A1E76D6BAED16FB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r kills with this dagger capture the mob's soul into a Soul Jar in your inventory."
		"&eHow:&r a golden sword, soulium ingots and soulium dust (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r JEI's soul extraction page shows how many souls each mob gives."
	]
	quest.428E72DF157C0E84.title: "Soul Jars"
	quest.428E72DF157C0E84.quest_subtitle: "Glass that holds a mob's essence"
	quest.428E72DF157C0E84.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each jar stores souls of one mob type. Full jars are the material for mob seeds."
		"&eHow:&r soul glass (soul dust around glass) and a soulium ingot (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r carry one empty jar per mob type you're hunting."
	]
	quest.26B2F788E44A88FF.title: "Fill a Jar"
	quest.26B2F788E44A88FF.quest_subtitle: "Kill 20 zombies with the dagger"
	quest.26B2F788E44A88FF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fill a Soul Jar with zombie souls for zombie seeds (rotten flesh)."
		"&eHow:&r keep an empty Soul Jar in your inventory and kill zombies with the Soulium Dagger."
		"&eTip:&r the Soul Extractor can also pull souls out of mob drops like rotten flesh (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.7BF7865AB438BD4F.title: "Mob Seeds"
	quest.7BF7865AB438BD4F.quest_subtitle: "Grow mob drops without the mobs"
	quest.7BF7865AB438BD4F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r mob seeds start from a Soulium Seed Base and grow drops like rotten flesh, bones and string."
		"&eHow:&r a prosperity seed base plus 2 soulium dust. On the altar, put it in the middle and the full jars and essence on the pedestals (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r zombie, skeleton, spider and creeper are tier 3, so they also need an analog circuit."
	]
	quest.0D456A2E999CC4F8.title: "Machine Frame"
	quest.0D456A2E999CC4F8.quest_subtitle: "The base of Mystical Agriculture machines"
	quest.0D456A2E999CC4F8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the shared frame for the Harvester, Soul Extractor, Seed Reprocessor and other MA machines."
		"&eHow:&r iron, redstone and stone (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r MA machines run on Forge Energy, so they plug into any FE cable."
	]
	quest.4E7A8526103C06DE.title: "Harvester"
	quest.4E7A8526103C06DE.quest_subtitle: "Harvests and replants a field"
	quest.4E7A8526103C06DE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Harvester picks mature crops in an area in front of it and replants them, pushing drops into its inventory."
		"&eHow:&r machine frame, soulium ingots, iron and two diamond scythes (check JEI). Power it with FE."
		"&eTip:&r pipe its output into storage and the field runs itself."
	]
	quest.1AB94C1A78E23821.title: "Soul Extractor"
	quest.1AB94C1A78E23821.quest_subtitle: "Optional: souls from mob drops"
	quest.1AB94C1A78E23821.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fills Soul Jars from mob drops (rotten flesh, bones, string and more) instead of kills."
		"&eHow:&r machine frame, soulium ingots, iron and a soulium dagger (check JEI). Power it with FE."
		"&eTip:&r feed it drops from an HNN Simulation Chamber for a fully passive soul supply."
	]
	quest.2E34A7CBAE7C47D5.title: "A Pot Farm"
	quest.2E34A7CBAE7C47D5.quest_subtitle: "Eight hopper pots of resource crops"
	quest.2E34A7CBAE7C47D5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mystical Agriculture seeds grow in Hopper Botany Pots, which harvest by themselves into a chest below."
		"&eHow:&r put each pot on a hopper, pipe or chest, add dirt or farmland and a seed. Hold any MA seed in JEI to see its pot growth time."
		"&eTip:&r a column of pots over one shared item pipe is a compact essence farm for every tier."
	]
	chapter.58F2F526022035F5.title: "Quality of Life"
	chapter.58F2F526022035F5.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Small things that make a big difference."
	]
	quest.7861E90E0F778D26.title: "One Book to Rule Them All"
	quest.7861E90E0F778D26.quest_subtitle: "Every guidebook in one item"
	quest.7861E90E0F778D26.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember a library that held everything. A single book will have to do.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Akashic Tome merges every mod's guidebook into one item."
		"&eHow:&r craft it, then right-click it with other guidebooks to add them."
		"&eTip:&r right-click the tome to choose which book to open."
	]
	quest.24E1DFE3C86BAB94.title: "Find Anything"
	quest.24E1DFE3C86BAB94.quest_subtitle: "Compasses for biomes and structures"
	quest.24E1DFE3C86BAB94.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Nature's Compass finds biomes; Explorer's Compass finds structures (Nether Fortresses, Ancient Cities, villages)."
		"&eHow:&r craft both (check JEI), right-click to pick a target, then follow the needle."
		"&eTip:&r the Explorer's Compass is the fastest way to find an Ancient City for the Deeper and Darker quests."
	]
	quest.417C968CF0B6DB90.title: "No More Mob Spawns"
	quest.417C968CF0B6DB90.quest_subtitle: "One torch, a huge safe radius"
	quest.417C968CF0B6DB90.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Mega Torch stops hostile mobs spawning naturally in a huge radius."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the recipe and place it near the middle of your base."
		"&eTip:&r it blocks natural spawns only. Spawners and Simulation Chambers still work."
	]
	quest.2CDD3C38275B155C.title: "Graves"
	quest.2CDD3C38275B155C.quest_subtitle: "Your items wait where you fell"
	quest.2CDD3C38275B155C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r if you die, Corail Tombstone keeps your items in a grave where you fell."
		"&eHow:&r walk back and open the grave to recover everything. Click the checkmark once you've read this."
		"&eTip:&r JourneyMap drops a waypoint where you died, so the grave is easy to find."
	]
	quest.6DE92B29EF0F35A9.title: "Backups"
	quest.6DE92B29EF0F35A9.quest_subtitle: "Automatic world saves"
	quest.6DE92B29EF0F35A9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Simple Backups saves your world automatically."
		"&eHow:&r on a server, backups live in the server's backups folder. In single player, look in your instance folder."
		"&eTip:&r copy a backup somewhere else before trying risky reactor builds."
	]
	quest.604BDD9A6947B39B.title: "Dread Lamp"
	quest.604BDD9A6947B39B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the Mega Torch for Nether mobs"
	quest.604BDD9A6947B39B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Dread Lamp blocks Nether mob spawns in a large radius, the way the Mega Torch does for Overworld mobs."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Place it at your Nether base or portal hub."
		"&eTip:&r place it before building in the Nether so your base stays quiet."
	]
	quest.7B910D75AE5CB5BE.title: "Crafting on a Stick"
	quest.7B910D75AE5CB5BE.quest_subtitle: "A crafting table that fits in your pocket"
	quest.7B910D75AE5CB5BE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a crafting table you carry around. Right-click it to open a 3x3 grid anywhere: in a mine, out exploring, mid-build."
		"&eHow:&r craft it from a crafting table and a stick (check JEI). The same mod makes pocket versions of the stonecutter, smithing table, anvil, grindstone, loom and cartography table."
		"&eTip:&r it saves a hotbar slot over placing and breaking tables. The pocket stonecutter is great for building with Create Deco and Rechiseled blocks."
	]
	quest.0168A13FA2435F4D.title: "A Whole Workshop"
	quest.0168A13FA2435F4D.quest_subtitle: "Pocket stonecutter and smithing table"
	quest.0168A13FA2435F4D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r optional: the pocket stonecutter and smithing table."
		"&eHow:&r each one is its block plus a stick (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the smithing table is how netherite and Apotheosis upgrades are applied, so it's handy to carry."
	]
	quest.4BC3CD31C26ED641.title: "Backpack Upgrades"
	quest.4BC3CD31C26ED641.quest_subtitle: "Pickup and magnet upgrades"
	quest.4BC3CD31C26ED641.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r pickup and magnet upgrades pull items straight into your backpack."
		"&eHow:&r craft an Upgrade Base, then the upgrades (check JEI). Put them in the backpack's upgrade slots."
		"&eTip:&r set a filter on the pickup upgrade so it only grabs ores and drops you actually want."
	]
	quest.288CF747C2D939F7.title: "Iron Backpack"
	quest.288CF747C2D939F7.quest_subtitle: "More slots and more upgrade space"
	quest.288CF747C2D939F7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each backpack tier adds inventory rows and upgrade slots: iron, gold, diamond, netherite."
		"&eHow:&r surround your backpack with iron ingots (check JEI). It keeps everything inside."
		"&eTip:&r stack upgrades multiply how many items fit in each slot."
	]
	quest.087BBFFCDB2D5BBE.title: "Feeding Upgrade"
	quest.087BBFFCDB2D5BBE.quest_subtitle: "Optional: never stop to eat again"
	quest.087BBFFCDB2D5BBE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r eats food from the backpack automatically when you're hungry."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Farmer's Delight meals restore a lot per bite."
		"&eTip:&r set a filter so it doesn't eat your golden apples."
	]
	quest.667CA6C7D1391223.title: "Netherite Backpack"
	quest.667CA6C7D1391223.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the biggest backpack"
	quest.667CA6C7D1391223.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the top tier: the most inventory slots and upgrade space."
		"&eHow:&r ring the backpack with gold, then diamonds, then smith in a netherite ingot with a netherite upgrade template."
		"&eTip:&r a netherite backpack has room for several stack upgrades at once."
	]
	quest.5B094C907C8047AF.title: "Waystones"
	quest.5B094C907C8047AF.quest_subtitle: "Teleport between your places"
	quest.5B094C907C8047AF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r waystones are teleport points. Activate one by right-clicking it, then warp between any you've activated."
		"&eHow:&r found in villages, or craft one (check JEI). Place them at your base, mines and portals."
		"&eTip:&r warping costs a little XP depending on distance; check the config if it seems steep."
	]
	quest.491A989F2FB877C8.title: "Warp Scrolls"
	quest.491A989F2FB877C8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one-use trips to any waystone"
	quest.491A989F2FB877C8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a single-use warp to any activated waystone, handy before you can afford a Warp Stone."
		"&eHow:&r paper, an ender pearl, gold nuggets and an ink sac (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep one in your backpack for emergencies."
	]
	quest.17EB435344732ED5.title: "Maps"
	quest.17EB435344732ED5.quest_subtitle: "JourneyMap and FTB Chunks"
	quest.17EB435344732ED5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r JourneyMap draws a minimap and a full world map as you explore, with waypoints."
		"&eHow:&r press &eJ&r for the full JourneyMap. FTB Chunks has its own map for claims (check Controls for its key). Click the checkmark when you've tried them."
		"&eTip:&r drop a waypoint at every rich ore deposit you find. Deposits are rare, so note the depth too."
	]
	quest.7F227CA37B21D828.title: "Claim Your Land"
	quest.7F227CA37B21D828.quest_subtitle: "Protect your base with FTB Chunks"
	quest.7F227CA37B21D828.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember a whole world that answered to you. Start with a few chunks.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r claimed chunks are protected from other players and explosions (per your team settings). Force-loaded chunks keep machines running while you're away."
		"&eHow:&r open the FTB Chunks map and drag across chunks to claim them (the map's help shows the controls). Click the checkmark when done."
		"&eTip:&r force-load your main factory so chemical lines don't stall when you travel."
	]
	quest.697F3B912ADA9643.title: "Inventory Tricks"
	quest.697F3B912ADA9643.quest_subtitle: "Sorting, dragging and a trash slot"
	quest.697F3B912ADA9643.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r small mods that save hours: Mouse Tweaks (drag and scroll to move stacks), Inventory Tweaks (sorting) and TrashSlot (a trash can in your inventory)."
		"&eHow:&r try a scroll-wheel drag over stacks, the sort button, and the trash slot by your hotbar. Click the checkmark when done."
		"&eTip:&r Polymorph shows a button when two recipes share a grid; click it to pick the one you want."
	]
	quest.1F2CF66554D65C93.title: "Feral Flare Lantern"
	quest.1F2CF66554D65C93.quest_subtitle: "Optional: light a whole cave at once"
	quest.1F2CF66554D65C93.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the lantern places invisible light sources in the dark spots around it, so a cave or a big hall lights up without a single torch."
		"&eHow:&r gold ingots, glass and glowstone dust (check JEI). Place it in the middle of the room."
		"&eTip:&r great for a clean-looking factory floor. It still lets mobs spawn in spots it can't reach."
	]
	quest.5B9CAB5D9BAADF57.title: "Grave Tricks"
	quest.5B9CAB5D9BAADF57.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more from Corail Tombstone"
	quest.5B9CAB5D9BAADF57.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Corail Tombstone does more than store your items: it adds scrolls, tablets and the Ankh of Prayer, plus a book that makes items soulbound."
		"&eHow:&r search 'tombstone' in JEI to browse them. Click the checkmark when you've had a look."
		"&eTip:&r by default only you can open your grave, so a death on a server doesn't mean losing your gear to someone else."
	]
	quest.7A2E8D54084A7224.title: "Loot for Everyone"
	quest.7A2E8D54084A7224.quest_subtitle: "Optional: every player gets their own chest loot"
	quest.7A2E8D54084A7224.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r with Lootr, structure chests (dungeons, temples, villages, mineshafts) hold separate loot for each player."
		"&eHow:&r open any generated chest. You get your own roll; your friends still get theirs. Click the checkmark when you've seen one."
		"&eTip:&r on a server, nobody has to race to a dungeon first."
	]
	quest.014F5E0E68AA6574.title: "Stack Upgrade"
	quest.014F5E0E68AA6574.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more items per slot"
	quest.014F5E0E68AA6574.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a stack upgrade multiplies how many items each backpack slot holds. Higher tiers multiply more."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI; each tier is built from the one before it."
		"&eTip:&r stack upgrades make a backpack the best place to carry dust and ingots between machines."
	]
	quest.74B98B27BE564EAD.title: "Tool Swapper"
	quest.74B98B27BE564EAD.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the right tool, automatically"
	quest.74B98B27BE564EAD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r swaps the tool in your hand for the best one in your backpack when you start mining a block or hitting a mob."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI, then put it in an upgrade slot and fill the backpack with tools."
		"&eTip:&r pairs well with a paxel; it switches to shears or a sword only when needed."
	]
	quest.1572A9CFC13F6605.title: "Refill Upgrade"
	quest.1572A9CFC13F6605.quest_subtitle: "Optional: never run out of torches"
	quest.1572A9CFC13F6605.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r keeps chosen hotbar items topped up from the backpack: torches, blocks, food."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Set the items to refill in the upgrade's tab."
		"&eTip:&r refill building blocks while bridging and you'll never stop to open your inventory."
	]
	quest.32CFD45D94EE955E.title: "Pocket Anvil"
	quest.32CFD45D94EE955E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: repair and disenchant anywhere"
	quest.32CFD45D94EE955E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r pocket versions of the anvil and grindstone, opened with right-click."
		"&eHow:&r each one is its block plus a stick (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the pocket anvil wears down like a placed one, so carry a spare for long trips."
	]
	quest.295E46752750C4C1.title: "FTB Ultimine"
	quest.295E46752750C4C1.quest_subtitle: "Break a whole vein in one swing"
	quest.295E46752750C4C1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Ultimine breaks every connected matching block at once: a full ore vein, a tree, a strip of stone."
		"&eHow:&r hold the Ultimine key (default &e`&r, the key left of 1) and break a block. Arrow keys up and down change the shape. Click the checkmark when you've tried it."
		"&eTip:&r it can cost extra hunger, so eat first. Shapes include tunnels and flat planes for clearing space."
	]
	quest.24582FFEF0C9CA48.title: "Form a Team"
	quest.24582FFEF0C9CA48.quest_subtitle: "Share quests, claims and loot"
	quest.24582FFEF0C9CA48.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r FTB Teams groups players into a party. Teammates share quest progress and claimed chunks."
		"&eHow:&r open the Teams screen from the button on your inventory screen (or use /ftbteams) and create a party, then invite friends. Click the checkmark when done."
		"&eTip:&r playing alone? A solo party still lets you set chunk permissions for visitors."
	]
	quest.0A6808C7A052CA16.title: "Homes and /back"
	quest.0A6808C7A052CA16.quest_subtitle: "FTB Essentials teleport commands"
	quest.0A6808C7A052CA16.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r FTB Essentials adds /sethome and /home (one home by default), /back to return to where you died or last teleported, /spawn, and /tpa to ask to teleport to a friend."
		"&eHow:&r stand at your base and type /sethome, then try /home from somewhere else. Click the checkmark when done."
		"&eTip:&r each command has a short cooldown. /back after a death walks you straight to your grave."
	]
	quest.3419EC047902045A.title: "Just Zoom"
	quest.3419EC047902045A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a spyglass without the spyglass"
	quest.3419EC047902045A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Just Zoom lets you zoom in on the distance with a key, no item needed."
		"&eHow:&r find its key under Options → Controls, and hold it to zoom (its options are in the Mods menu). Click the checkmark when you've tried it."
		"&eTip:&r handy for spotting structures, meteorites and villages from a hilltop."
	]
	quest.213AD19CC7D30A37.title: "Ping Wheel"
	quest.213AD19CC7D30A37.quest_subtitle: "Optional: point things out to friends"
	quest.213AD19CC7D30A37.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Ping Wheel puts a marker on the spot you look at, visible to the other players nearby."
		"&eHow:&r find its keys under Options → Controls. Look at something and ping it. Click the checkmark when done."
		"&eTip:&r ping an ore deposit or a dangerous mob instead of typing coordinates."
	]
	quest.1E27CF7DD38A14C8.title: "Chat Heads"
	quest.1E27CF7DD38A14C8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: see who's talking"
	quest.1E27CF7DD38A14C8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Chat Heads shows each player's face next to their messages in chat."
		"&eHow:&r nothing to set up; it works as soon as someone talks. Click the checkmark when you've seen it."
		"&eTip:&r its options are in the Mods menu if you want to change how heads are shown."
	]
	quest.69F41022F3C27254.title: "Trade Cycling"
	quest.69F41022F3C27254.quest_subtitle: "Reroll a villager's offers"
	quest.69F41022F3C27254.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Trade Cycling adds a button to the villager trade screen that rerolls the offers of a villager nobody has traded with yet."
		"&eHow:&r give a villager a job block, open its trades and press the cycle button until the offer you want appears. Earn 16 emeralds by trading."
		"&eTip:&r once you trade, the offers lock. Cycle a librarian until it sells the enchanted book you need."
	]
	quest.370448FDEA00C30C.title: "Merchant Prince"
	quest.370448FDEA00C30C.quest_subtitle: "Secret: a demigod with a market stall"
	quest.370448FDEA00C30C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r four emerald blocks: 36 emeralds. The villagers have noticed you."
		"&eChemistry:&r emerald is beryl, Be₃Al₂Si₆O₁₈, coloured green by traces of chromium."
		"&eTip:&r every Warp Stone needs an emerald, so a good trading hall pays for your travel network."
	]
	quest.2570EB0A8AF93C47.title: "Tool Belt"
	quest.2570EB0A8AF93C47.quest_subtitle: "Optional: tools on a quick wheel"
	quest.2570EB0A8AF93C47.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Tool Belt holds tools outside your hotbar and opens as a radial menu so you can swap fast."
		"&eHow:&r leather and string (check JEI). Keep it in your inventory; find its key under Options → Controls."
		"&eTip:&r put the wrench, the config card and your paxel on the belt."
	]
	quest.7DAD39B76BA322EE.title: "Belt Pouches"
	quest.7DAD39B76BA322EE.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more slots on the belt"
	quest.7DAD39B76BA322EE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each pouch adds a slot to your tool belt."
		"&eHow:&r craft pouches, then craft them together with the belt (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a full belt keeps your hotbar free for blocks and food."
	]
	quest.7966EBF899C9AB72.title: "A Waystone Network"
	quest.7966EBF899C9AB72.quest_subtitle: "Optional: four more waystones"
	quest.7966EBF899C9AB72.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one waystone is a landmark; four make a network. Base, mine, Nether portal and a far-off biome."
		"&eHow:&r any four waystones of any style (check JEI for the variants), or bring back ones found in villages."
		"&eTip:&r name each one clearly ('Bauxite Mine -40') so the list stays readable."
	]
	quest.2367545F51E52EA0.title: "Warp Stone"
	quest.2367545F51E52EA0.quest_subtitle: "Optional: warp from anywhere"
	quest.2367545F51E52EA0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a reusable item that opens the waystone menu wherever you stand. It recharges after each use."
		"&eHow:&r amethyst shards, ender pearls and an emerald (check JEI). It's also in the Demigod Token shop."
		"&eTip:&r with a Warp Stone, warp scrolls become backup only."
	]
	quest.4C714AF8B234F7FB.title: "Waypoints"
	quest.4C714AF8B234F7FB.quest_subtitle: "Optional: never lose a deposit again"
	quest.4C714AF8B234F7FB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r JourneyMap waypoints mark places on the minimap and in the world, with distance shown on screen."
		"&eHow:&r open the full map (&eJ&r) and right-click a spot to add a waypoint, or use JourneyMap's waypoint key (see Controls). Click the checkmark when you've made one."
		"&eTip:&r JourneyMap makes a death waypoint for you; share waypoints with teammates in chat."
	]
	chapter.29A6965304E1D4DA.title: "The Demigod's Market"
	chapter.29A6965304E1D4DA.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Spend your Demigod Tokens: supplies and comforts, never shortcuts."
	]
	quest.7CD14A8D2BC590A9.title: "The Market"
	quest.7CD14A8D2BC590A9.quest_subtitle: "What Demigod Tokens are for"
	quest.7CD14A8D2BC590A9.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember offerings left at your altar. Now the world pays you in coins instead.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Demigod Tokens are the reward currency of this book. You trade them for supplies by crafting, with no shopkeeper and no server plugin."
		"&eHow:&r every shop trade is a shapeless crafting recipe: put tokens in a crafting grid and the item appears."
		"&eTip:&r this chapter explains the price bands, the exchange and what tokens will never buy."
	]
	quest.2B95087344F45A1D.title: "Where Tokens Come From"
	quest.2B95087344F45A1D.quest_subtitle: "Every quest pays"
	quest.2B95087344F45A1D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r almost every quest pays tokens, scaled by tier: 1 per quest at the start, 2 in the steam and Nether chapters, 3 at LV and MV, 4 at HV, 5 at EV, 8 in space."
		"&eHow:&r milestone quests (the big ones) pay double and also roll that tier's reward table. Optional side quests pay 1 or 2."
		"&eTip:&r on a team, rewards go to each player who claims them, so everyone builds their own purse."
	]
	quest.28AD4AEDE3D6AD2F.title: "Reading the Price List"
	quest.28AD4AEDE3D6AD2F.quest_subtitle: "The whole shop lives in JEI"
	quest.28AD4AEDE3D6AD2F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r there is no shop screen. The price list is JEI."
		"&eHow:&r search &eDemigod Token&r in JEI and press &eU&r (uses). Every trade shows as a crafting recipe. Do the same for the Greater Demigod Token."
		"&eTip:&r bookmark the trades you use most so they stay on screen."
	]
	quest.5452D2F4A6EBEED3.title: "What Tokens Never Buy"
	quest.5452D2F4A6EBEED3.quest_subtitle: "Convenience, not shortcuts"
	quest.5452D2F4A6EBEED3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the shop sells raw supplies and comforts. It never sells machines, circuits, alloys or anything that skips a tier."
		"&eChemistry:&r a bag of raw ore is not a refinery. Raw tin still needs your crusher, raw titanium still needs your blast furnace."
		"&eHow:&r use tokens to skip boring gathering (sand, gravel, string, torches), never to skip learning."
		"&eTip:&r if a trade seems missing, it was left out on purpose."
	]
	quest.730D392B8D2C31C6.title: "Small Band: 1 to 3 Tokens"
	quest.730D392B8D2C31C6.quest_subtitle: "Everyday supplies"
	quest.730D392B8D2C31C6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r cheap stacks of things you'd otherwise spend an afternoon gathering."
		"&eHow:&r 1 token: 32 torches, 16 bread, 8 bottles o' enchanting, 32 bone meal, 64 sand, 64 gravel or 32 clay balls."
		"&eHow:&r 2 tokens: 16 iron ingots, 16 coke, 16 rubber sheets, 16 fire clay dust, 32 salt dust, 16 string, 16 leather or a sleeping bag."
		"&eHow:&r 3 tokens: 8 osmium ingots, 2 backpack upgrade bases, 16 gunpowder, 16 slime balls, 32 redstone or 16 lapis."
		"&eTip:&r sand and gravel are the best early value: concrete, glass and silicon all start there."
	]
	quest.5927B0F6E131CD9E.title: "Medium Band: 4 to 8 Tokens"
	quest.5927B0F6E131CD9E.quest_subtitle: "Raw ores and mob drops"
	quest.5927B0F6E131CD9E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r raw ores (you still process them yourself) and drops you would otherwise farm."
		"&eHow:&r 4 tokens: a Warp Stone, 32 raw copper, 16 raw tin, 16 raw lead, 16 bauxite dust, 32 quartz or 32 glowstone dust."
		"&eHow:&r 5: 16 raw nickel, 8 ender pearls, 4 phantom membranes, 16 amethyst. 6: 8 blaze rods, 4 ghast tears, 16 certus quartz, 8 source gems."
		"&eHow:&r 7: 8 raw titanium or 2 name tags. 8: 8 raw tungsten or 32 prismarine shards."
		"&eTip:&r raw ore bought here is worth up to 5x once your Mekanism line is running. Buy late, process well."
	]
	quest.1A97B140379BA760.title: "Large Band: Greater Tokens"
	quest.1A97B140379BA760.quest_subtitle: "Rare comforts"
	quest.1A97B140379BA760.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the big trades cost Greater Demigod Tokens, not regular ones."
		"&eHow:&r 1 Greater: 4 golden apples, 4 diamonds, 16 emeralds or a saddle. 2: 2 shulker shells, a heart of the sea or a netherite scrap."
		"&eHow:&r 3 Greater: a totem of undying or 4 echo shards. 4 Greater: an enchanted golden apple."
		"&eTip:&r shulker shells mean shulker boxes. Many players find that the best trade in the shop."
	]
	quest.003F5C5CD886D522.title: "The Exchange"
	quest.003F5C5CD886D522.quest_subtitle: "Nine tokens make one Greater Token"
	quest.003F5C5CD886D522.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Greater Demigod Token is worth 9 Demigod Tokens, and the trade works both ways."
		"&eHow:&r 9 tokens in a crafting grid make 1 Greater Token. 1 Greater Token alone in the grid gives the 9 back."
		"&eTip:&r late-tier milestones and boss loot sometimes pay Greater Tokens directly."
	]
	quest.78DBBB51C5B3D742.title: "Market Day: Early"
	quest.78DBBB51C5B3D742.quest_subtitle: "Hold 10 tokens; pick a comfort"
	quest.78DBBB51C5B3D742.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a reward for saving. Hold 10 Demigod Tokens at once and choose one comfort: a sleeping bag, a Warp Stone, backpack upgrade bases or a saddle."
		"&eHow:&r the tokens are only checked, not taken. Spend them afterwards if you like."
		"&eTip:&r the Warp Stone is the pick if you explore a lot."
	]
	quest.410F8D5BAEFB395A.title: "Market Day: Industrial"
	quest.410F8D5BAEFB395A.quest_subtitle: "Hold 30 tokens; pick a feedstock"
	quest.410F8D5BAEFB395A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r hold 30 tokens and choose a stack of raw feedstock: tin, lead, nickel, bauxite or salt."
		"&eHow:&r tokens are checked, not taken."
		"&eTip:&r bauxite is the slow one to find, and aluminium is the gate to MV."
	]
	quest.4F2FD5E25FC1E6FB.title: "Market Day: Divine"
	quest.4F2FD5E25FC1E6FB.quest_subtitle: "Hold 64 tokens; pick a treasure"
	quest.4F2FD5E25FC1E6FB.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember when worshippers brought you treasures. Now you just keep a full stack.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r hold a full stack of 64 tokens and choose a treasure: a totem, shulker shells, a heart of the sea, an enchanted golden apple or 3 Greater Tokens."
		"&eHow:&r tokens are checked, not taken. Exchange Greater Tokens back if you need 64 loose ones."
		"&eTip:&r picking the Greater Tokens is the same as taking 27 regular tokens home."
	]
	quest.5D7536360603F09D.title: "A Dragon's Hoard"
	quest.5D7536360603F09D.quest_subtitle: "81 tokens' worth, unspent"
	quest.5D7536360603F09D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r hold nine Greater Demigod Tokens at once. That's 81 tokens you chose not to spend."
		"&eTip:&r the demigod approves of patience. The demigod also notes that totems exist."
	]
	chapter.452C93B72D978D1A.title: "Completionist"
	chapter.452C93B72D978D1A.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Collections for the thorough demigod. All optional."
	]
	quest.24914735614B7E05.title: "Sixteen Colours of Wool"
	quest.24914735614B7E05.quest_subtitle: "One block of every wool colour"
	quest.24914735614B7E05.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember making a world with every colour in it. Start small: sixteen.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a collection page. Nothing here is needed to progress; every quest is a bragging right with a small reward."
		"&eHow:&r shear sheep and dye white wool in a crafting grid (wool + dye). Sheep can also be dyed before shearing."
		"&eTip:&r dye a sheep once and it grows that colour back forever. A pen of sixteen sheep is a wool farm."
	]
	quest.3C3A4C35AF19917F.title: "The Dyer's Palette"
	quest.3C3A4C35AF19917F.quest_subtitle: "All sixteen dyes"
	quest.3C3A4C35AF19917F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every dye colour, from flowers, plants, minerals and mixing."
		"&eChemistry:&r real dyes are molecules that absorb some wavelengths of light. Lapis gets its blue from lazurite, a sodium aluminosilicate with sulfur ions trapped in its cage."
		"&eHow:&r flowers give most primaries; cocoa gives brown, cactus smelts into green, ink sacs give black. Mix the rest (JEI shows every recipe)."
		"&eTip:&r bone meal on grass and flowers gives you endless primaries."
	]
	quest.05CCE3C3E12A4F47.title: "Concrete Rainbow"
	quest.05CCE3C3E12A4F47.quest_subtitle: "All sixteen concretes"
	quest.05CCE3C3E12A4F47.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one block of every concrete colour."
		"&eChemistry:&r real concrete sets by hydration, not drying: water reacts with the calcium silicates in cement to grow a stiff mesh of calcium silicate hydrate."
		"&eHow:&r craft concrete powder (4 sand, 4 gravel, 1 dye), then place it in water or touch it with water to set it."
		"&eTip:&r place powder in front of a water stream and mine it with a good pickaxe: fast and repeatable."
	]
	quest.29FD9FD275EB8B42.title: "Every Vanilla Tree"
	quest.29FD9FD275EB8B42.quest_subtitle: "Ten saplings from the vanilla world"
	quest.29FD9FD275EB8B42.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one sapling from every vanilla tree, including the mangrove propagule and both azaleas."
		"&eChemistry:&r every tree builds itself from air and water: 6CO₂ + 6H₂O → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂, powered by sunlight."
		"&eHow:&r break leaves in each biome. Cherry groves sit on mountain meadows; azaleas grow above lush caves; propagules hang under mangrove leaves."
		"&eTip:&r a Nature's Compass finds the biome you need."
	]
	quest.3E6E555D15E5618C.title: "Trees of Distant Lands"
	quest.3E6E555D15E5618C.quest_subtitle: "Ten saplings from modded biomes"
	quest.3E6E555D15E5618C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r saplings from Biomes O' Plenty and Regions Unexplored trees."
		"&eHow:&r find the biome first: redwood and jacaranda groves, mystic groves (magic), tropics (palm), snowblossom groves; baobab savannas, eucalyptus forests, Joshua deserts, wisteria groves and rainforests."
		"&eTip:&r JEI shows each sapling's leaves. Botany Pots grow any of them without a forest."
	]
	quest.5CF80E20FAD6CF13.title: "The Creeper Collection"
	quest.5CF80E20FAD6CF13.quest_subtitle: "Twelve discs that creepers drop"
	quest.5CF80E20FAD6CF13.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the twelve classic discs. A creeper drops one when a skeleton (or stray or bogged) kills it."
		"&eHow:&r lure creepers into a skeleton's line of fire, or build a mob farm that lets skeletons do the shooting. Dungeon chests also hold a few."
		"&eTip:&r a skeleton spawner dungeon is perfect: trap the skeletons, then walk creepers past them."
	]
	quest.30EC54EB8A9DFD35.title: "Treasure Discs"
	quest.30EC54EB8A9DFD35.quest_subtitle: "Pigstep, otherside, Relic and 5"
	quest.30EC54EB8A9DFD35.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r four discs that only come from structures."
		"&eHow:&r Pigstep: bastion remnant chests. otherside: dungeon and stronghold chests (rare). Relic: brush suspicious gravel in trail ruins. 5: craft nine disc fragments found in ancient city chests."
		"&eTip:&r an Explorer's Compass points to the structure you need."
	]
	quest.064638080B9AC1F3.title: "Trial Discs"
	quest.064638080B9AC1F3.quest_subtitle: "Three discs from trial chambers"
	quest.064638080B9AC1F3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the discs added with trial chambers."
		"&eHow:&r Precipice comes from vaults opened with a trial key; Creator from ominous vaults (ominous trial key); Creator (Music Box) from decorated pots in the chambers."
		"&eTip:&r drink an ominous bottle before a trial spawner to turn it ominous. Bring food, a shield and fire resistance."
	]
	quest.76E6697544E0D8BF.title: "Overworld Trims"
	quest.76E6697544E0D8BF.quest_subtitle: "Seven templates from Overworld structures"
	quest.76E6697544E0D8BF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r armour trim templates decorate armour in a smithing table."
		"&eHow:&r coast: shipwrecks. dune: desert pyramids. wild: jungle temples. sentry: pillager outposts. vex: woodland mansions. tide: elder guardians in ocean monuments. eye: strongholds."
		"&eTip:&r copy a template with 7 diamonds and the block it's made of (check JEI) instead of hunting a second one."
	]
	quest.3A9524CD2B47B654.title: "Dug-Up Trims"
	quest.3A9524CD2B47B654.quest_subtitle: "Four templates from trail ruins"
	quest.3A9524CD2B47B654.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r four trims buried in trail ruins."
		"&eHow:&r brush suspicious gravel in trail ruins with a brush (feather, copper, stick). These are rare drops, so brush a lot."
		"&eTip:&r the same gravel holds pottery sherds and the Relic disc."
	]
	quest.71DF0C78D78D5E7B.title: "Trims of the Deep Dark"
	quest.71DF0C78D78D5E7B.quest_subtitle: "Ward and Silence"
	quest.71DF0C78D78D5E7B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the two ancient city trims. Silence is the rarest template in the game."
		"&eHow:&r loot ancient city chests. Sneak, wool on the floor, and don't let the shriekers call the Warden."
		"&eTip:&r a stack of wool carpets silences your footsteps on sculk sensors."
	]
	quest.476FD0DDC043D665.title: "Trims of Fire and Void"
	quest.476FD0DDC043D665.quest_subtitle: "Rib, Snout and Spire"
	quest.476FD0DDC043D665.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one trim each from Nether fortresses (rib), bastions (snout) and End cities (spire)."
		"&eHow:&r fortress chests, bastion chests and End city chests. Bring gold armour for the bastion."
		"&eTip:&r bastion treasure rooms also hold the netherite upgrade template."
	]
	quest.6E25BE0980F1ED98.title: "Trial Trims"
	quest.6E25BE0980F1ED98.quest_subtitle: "Flow and Bolt"
	quest.6E25BE0980F1ED98.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the two trial chamber trims."
		"&eHow:&r bolt comes from regular vaults (trial key); flow from ominous vaults (ominous trial key)."
		"&eTip:&r every player gets their own loot from each vault, so bring friends."
	]
	quest.3154336597FED77E.title: "Ore Cabinet: Overworld"
	quest.3154336597FED77E.quest_subtitle: "Every vanilla Overworld ore, as a block"
	quest.3154336597FED77E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one ore block of each vanilla Overworld ore (stone or deepslate both count)."
		"&eChemistry:&r real ores are minerals: iron as hematite (Fe₂O₃), copper as chalcopyrite (CuFeS₂), lapis as lazurite. Diamond is pure carbon."
		"&eHow:&r you need a &eSilk Touch&r pickaxe so the ore drops itself. Emerald only grows under mountains."
		"&eTip:&r place them in item frames as a display: a real geology cabinet."
	]
	quest.7AA71D0F3718C0F5.title: "Ore Cabinet: Nether"
	quest.7AA71D0F3718C0F5.quest_subtitle: "Three ores from the Nether"
	quest.7AA71D0F3718C0F5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Nether gold, Nether quartz and ancient debris."
		"&eChemistry:&r real quartz is silicon dioxide, SiO₂, the same thing as sand and the silicon you refine later."
		"&eHow:&r Silk Touch for the gold and quartz ores. Ancient debris always drops itself; mine around Y 15."
		"&eTip:&r beds explode in the Nether. That's a fast (and loud) way to find debris."
	]
	quest.17CB280131B353E2.title: "Ore Cabinet: Industrial"
	quest.17CB280131B353E2.quest_subtitle: "Eight Modern Industrialization ores"
	quest.17CB280131B353E2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one block of each common MI ore."
		"&eChemistry:&r bauxite is aluminium hydroxide; antimony is mined as stibnite (Sb₂S₃); monazite is a rare-earth phosphate, (Ce,La,Nd)PO₄, often with thorium."
		"&eHow:&r Silk Touch. Rich deposits sit at metal-specific depths: lead around Y −24 to 16, nickel lower at Y −32 to 8."
		"&eTip:&r Jade shows the ore name as you look at it, so you can tell tin from lead in the dark."
	]
	quest.56909AAC70A18B96.title: "Ore Cabinet: Deep and Rare"
	quest.56909AAC70A18B96.quest_subtitle: "Uranium, tungsten, osmium and fluorite"
	quest.56909AAC70A18B96.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the deep ores, as blocks."
		"&eChemistry:&r uranium ore is uraninite (UO₂); tungsten comes from wolframite and scheelite (CaWO₄); fluorite is calcium fluoride, CaF₂, the source of the hydrofluoric acid you'll need for uranium."
		"&eHow:&r Silk Touch. Uranium and tungsten deposits sit deep, around Y −56 to −24."
		"&eTip:&r Mekanism's radiation comes from its nuclear fluids and waste later on. Hazmat gear is in Tools and Comfort."
	]
	quest.65B54DE3A16529B1.title: "Ore Hoarder"
	quest.65B54DE3A16529B1.quest_subtitle: "256 ore blocks of any kind"
	quest.65B54DE3A16529B1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r four stacks of unprocessed ore blocks (anything tagged as an ore)."
		"&eHow:&r Silk Touch plus FTB Ultimine makes this quick. Keep them as blocks: Mekanism and MI process ore blocks too."
		"&eTip:&r ore blocks wait patiently. Store them until your 5x line is ready and every block is worth more."
	]
	quest.7C76F5D615A21CFD.title: "Circuit Collection"
	quest.7C76F5D615A21CFD.quest_subtitle: "LV, MV, HV and EV, side by side"
	quest.7C76F5D615A21CFD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one of each MI circuit tier you have built: analog, electronic, digital, processing unit."
		"&eChemistry:&r each tier stands on new chemistry: rubber, then aluminium, then polyethylene, then PVC and pure silicon."
		"&eHow:&r you made all of these on the main path. Keep one of each."
		"&eTip:&r frame them in order. It's a history of everything you've learned."
	]
	quest.2FD7F1F49B2C90E4.title: "Quantum Circuit"
	quest.2FD7F1F49B2C90E4.quest_subtitle: "The circuit beyond the main path"
	quest.2FD7F1F49B2C90E4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MI's top circuit. Nothing on the main path needs it, which makes it the perfect trophy."
		"&eHow:&r an Assembler: 4 processing units, 2 cooling cells, 2 qubits and a quantum circuit board. The board needs superconductor cable, plutonium batteries, iridium plates and helium-3 (check JEI for each)."
		"&eTip:&r iridium comes from the PGM residue line; plan the iridium before you start."
	]
	quest.46DBFE74EB369FB5.title: "Basic Factory"
	quest.46DBFE74EB369FB5.quest_subtitle: "Three items at once"
	quest.46DBFE74EB369FB5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Mekanism factory runs several copies of one machine in one block. Basic factories have 3 slots."
		"&eHow:&r right-click a placed Mekanism machine with a Basic Tier Installer, or craft the factory (check JEI). Any basic factory counts."
		"&eTip:&r a basic smelting factory with speed upgrades already beats a row of furnaces."
	]
	quest.246D14A3AF1EEC26.title: "Advanced Factory"
	quest.246D14A3AF1EEC26.quest_subtitle: "Five items at once"
	quest.246D14A3AF1EEC26.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r advanced factories have 5 slots."
		"&eHow:&r an Advanced Tier Installer on a basic factory. Its control circuit needs an MI electronic circuit (MV) and infused alloy."
		"&eTip:&r upgrade in place: the installer keeps the factory's contents and settings."
	]
	quest.0D793D529C26B98B.title: "Elite Factory"
	quest.0D793D529C26B98B.quest_subtitle: "Seven items at once"
	quest.0D793D529C26B98B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r elite factories have 7 slots."
		"&eHow:&r an Elite Tier Installer; its circuit needs an MI digital circuit (HV) and reinforced alloy."
		"&eTip:&r factories sort their own input slots if you turn on auto-sort in the GUI."
	]
	quest.1B2975F8496440C3.title: "Ultimate Factory"
	quest.1B2975F8496440C3.quest_subtitle: "Nine items at once"
	quest.1B2975F8496440C3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ultimate factories have 9 slots, the most Mekanism offers."
		"&eHow:&r an Ultimate Tier Installer; its circuit needs an MI processing unit (EV) and atomic alloy."
		"&eTip:&r one ultimate enriching factory can feed a whole 5x ore line's first step."
	]
	quest.1B30AE1DEF39A277.title: "The Full Line-Up"
	quest.1B30AE1DEF39A277.quest_subtitle: "All nine ultimate factories"
	quest.1B30AE1DEF39A277.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every factory type at ultimate tier: smelting, enriching, crushing, compressing, combining, purifying, injecting, infusing and sawing."
		"&eHow:&r build or upgrade one of each. Purifying and injecting are the 4x and 5x ore steps; infusing makes alloys."
		"&eTip:&r this is a lot of atomic alloy. Automate the refined obsidian first."
	]
	quest.4FE53067D8E11C2A.title: "The s-Block"
	quest.4FE53067D8E11C2A.quest_subtitle: "Groups 1 and 2, plus helium"
	quest.4FE53067D8E11C2A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every s-block element: the alkali metals, the alkaline earth metals, hydrogen and helium."
		"&eChemistry:&r their outermost electrons sit in an s orbital. One or two to give away, which makes them reactive metals (helium's full 1s² shell is the exception)."
		"&eHow:&r the Dissolver gives most of the light metals (helium needs fusion: H + H). Rubidium, cesium, francium and radium are rare: build them in the Fusion Chamber by adding proton numbers (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r francium is so unstable that no one has ever seen a visible amount of it."
	]
	quest.1E660F2BA4576CE8.title: "The p-Block: Light"
	quest.1E660F2BA4576CE8.quest_subtitle: "Periods 2 to 4 of groups 13–18"
	quest.1E660F2BA4576CE8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the lighter p-block elements: the non-metals of life and most of what you've refined so far."
		"&eChemistry:&r these elements fill p orbitals. Across a row they go from metals that lose electrons to halogens that grab them, ending at a noble gas."
		"&eHow:&r most come from the Dissolver. Neon, argon and krypton need the Fusion Chamber (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r carbon, nitrogen, oxygen and phosphorus are most of the mass of a living thing besides hydrogen."
	]
	quest.0F28C5F7ADC0D5D0.title: "The p-Block: Heavy"
	quest.0F28C5F7ADC0D5D0.quest_subtitle: "Periods 5 to 7, ending at element 118"
	quest.0F28C5F7ADC0D5D0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the heavy p-block, including the superheavy elements made only in particle accelerators."
		"&eChemistry:&r past lead, every element is radioactive. Bismuth's half-life is a billion times the age of the universe; oganesson's is under a millisecond."
		"&eHow:&r the Fusion and Fission Chambers. Pick pairs whose proton numbers add up (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r astatine is the rarest naturally occurring element: less than a gram exists in Earth's crust at any time."
	]
	quest.525A2965171EDB91.title: "The d-Block: Period 4"
	quest.525A2965171EDB91.quest_subtitle: "Scandium to zinc"
	quest.525A2965171EDB91.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the first row of transition metals, the workhorses of industry."
		"&eChemistry:&r transition metals fill d orbitals, which gives them colourful compounds, several oxidation states and catalytic tricks (iron in Haber-Bosch, platinum in Ostwald)."
		"&eHow:&r dissolve their ingots and dusts; build scandium and vanadium by fusion if you can't find a source (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r stainless steel is iron, chromium and nickel: three boxes in this row."
	]
	quest.0388D8B002BD2CC4.title: "The d-Block: Period 5"
	quest.0388D8B002BD2CC4.quest_subtitle: "Yttrium to cadmium"
	quest.0388D8B002BD2CC4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the second transition row, including three platinum-group metals."
		"&eChemistry:&r technetium (43) was the first element made artificially, in 1937. It has no stable isotope at all."
		"&eHow:&r ruthenium and rhodium come from your PGM residue; the rest by dissolving or fusion (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r rhodium is one of the most expensive metals on Earth, mostly used in car catalytic converters."
	]
	quest.40683E6E4778245E.title: "The d-Block: Period 6"
	quest.40683E6E4778245E.quest_subtitle: "Hafnium to mercury"
	quest.40683E6E4778245E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the heaviest stable transition metals: refractory tungsten, dense osmium, noble platinum and gold."
		"&eChemistry:&r osmium is the densest element (22.6 g/cm³). Gold is yellow and mercury is liquid because of relativity: their inner electrons move fast enough to change the orbitals' energies."
		"&eHow:&r the PGM line gives platinum, iridium and osmium; the rest by dissolving or fusion (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r tungsten has the highest melting point of any metal, 3422 °C."
	]
	quest.7509598E14623D37.title: "The d-Block: Period 7"
	quest.7509598E14623D37.quest_subtitle: "The transactinides"
	quest.7509598E14623D37.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the superheavy transition metals, 104 to 112."
		"&eChemistry:&r each was made a few atoms at a time by smashing nuclei together. Several are named after scientists: Rutherford, Seaborg, Bohr, Meitner, Röntgen, Copernicus."
		"&eHow:&r only the Fusion Chamber makes these. Check JEI for pairs that add up."
		"&eTip:&r seaborgium was named while Glenn Seaborg was alive, a rare honour."
	]
	quest.418512B7873C1A28.title: "The Lanthanides"
	quest.418512B7873C1A28.quest_subtitle: "All fifteen rare earths of the f-block"
	quest.418512B7873C1A28.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the whole lanthanide row, 57 to 71."
		"&eChemistry:&r they fill the 4f orbitals, which sit deep inside the atom, so their chemistry is almost identical. That's why separating them takes hundreds of extraction steps."
		"&eHow:&r press U on each element in JEI for Dissolver sources; fuse the rest in the Fusion Chamber. Promethium has no stable isotope."
		"&eTip:&r four of them are named after one Swedish village, Ytterby: yttrium, ytterbium, terbium, erbium."
	]
	quest.156884A7119394CC.title: "The Actinides"
	quest.156884A7119394CC.quest_subtitle: "All fifteen of the 5f row"
	quest.156884A7119394CC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the whole actinide row, 89 to 103. Every one is radioactive."
		"&eChemistry:&r only thorium and uranium last long enough to be found in quantity. Everything past uranium was first made in reactors or in the debris of bomb tests."
		"&eHow:&r dissolve uranium and thorium materials; fuse the heavier ones (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r americium is in most household smoke detectors."
	]
	quest.48916F4FA6905695.title: "Every Box Filled"
	quest.48916F4FA6905695.quest_subtitle: "All 118 elements, held in your hands"
	quest.48916F4FA6905695.quest_desc: [
		"&6Every element, in a chest. You remember when this was how you made worlds.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r you've collected every block of the periodic table."
		"&eHow:&r click to claim. Keep the chest; a periodic table wall of item frames is a fine way to show it off."
		"&eTip:&r the Combiner can now build almost any compound you can name."
	]
	quest.1DDE790728CC948C.title: "Tour: The Frozen North"
	quest.1DDE790728CC948C.quest_subtitle: "Seven cold Overworld biomes"
	quest.1DDE790728CC948C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r visit seven snowy biomes."
		"&eChemistry:&r ice floats because water expands about 9% when it freezes: hydrogen bonds lock the molecules into an open hexagonal lattice."
		"&eHow:&r walk in. A Nature's Compass finds each one."
		"&eTip:&r powder snow on frozen peaks swallows players. Leather boots let you walk on it."
	]
	quest.5F230391BCAF5E21.title: "Tour: Heat and Rain"
	quest.5F230391BCAF5E21.quest_subtitle: "Seven warm Overworld biomes"
	quest.5F230391BCAF5E21.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r visit seven warm biomes, from dry desert to jungle."
		"&eChemistry:&r badlands terracotta gets its reds and oranges from iron oxides, the same rust you can make in the Combiner."
		"&eHow:&r walk in. Badlands have gold at every height, so bring a pickaxe."
		"&eTip:&r jungle temples and desert pyramids hold trim templates for the trim quests."
	]
	quest.07A9CBB7D105660B.title: "Tour: Hidden Places"
	quest.07A9CBB7D105660B.quest_subtitle: "Six rare Overworld biomes"
	quest.07A9CBB7D105660B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the rare and underground biomes."
		"&eChemistry:&r dripstone forms when water with dissolved calcium bicarbonate drips and loses CO₂, leaving calcium carbonate behind: Ca(HCO₃)₂ → CaCO₃ + H₂O + CO₂."
		"&eHow:&r mushroom fields are islands far out at sea. Lush and dripstone caves sit under the surface; the deep dark sits below Y 0 under mountains."
		"&eTip:&r no hostile mobs spawn on mushroom fields. Safe camping."
	]
	quest.63AC8473D812F00F.title: "Tour: Strange Lands"
	quest.63AC8473D812F00F.quest_subtitle: "Seven biomes from the biome mods"
	quest.63AC8473D812F00F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r seven biomes from Biomes O' Plenty and Regions Unexplored."
		"&eHow:&r Nature's Compass lists modded biomes too. Prismachasm is a cave biome, so dig."
		"&eTip:&r volcanoes have lava at the top. Bring fire resistance."
	]
	quest.628CBA274F9C5F97.title: "Tour: The Five Fires"
	quest.628CBA274F9C5F97.quest_subtitle: "Every vanilla Nether biome"
	quest.628CBA274F9C5F97.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r visit all five vanilla Nether biomes."
		"&eChemistry:&r basalt is cooled lava, mostly silicates of iron and magnesium. Nether quartz is SiO₂."
		"&eHow:&r walk in. Warped forests are the safest place in the Nether: endermen only."
		"&eTip:&r ghasts hunt soul sand valleys. A shield blocks fireballs."
	]
	quest.086D64601C092565.title: "Tour: The Deeper Fires"
	quest.086D64601C092565.quest_subtitle: "Six modded Nether biomes"
	quest.086D64601C092565.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Nether biomes from Biomes O' Plenty and Regions Unexplored."
		"&eHow:&r Nature's Compass works in the Nether too. Withered abyss is a void: don't fall in."
		"&eTip:&r crystalline chasm's crystals are pretty and brittle. Mine with care."
	]
	quest.3D24912A6A30A85B.title: "Tour: The Void"
	quest.3D24912A6A30A85B.quest_subtitle: "Every vanilla End biome"
	quest.3D24912A6A30A85B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r visit the five End biomes, from the central island to the outer islands."
		"&eHow:&r after the dragon, throw an ender pearl into an end gateway to reach the outer islands."
		"&eTip:&r end cities sit in the highlands. Bring slow falling against shulkers."
	]
	quest.485ADC9463B35474.title: "Tour: Twilight Lowlands"
	quest.485ADC9463B35474.quest_subtitle: "Nine open Twilight Forest biomes"
	quest.485ADC9463B35474.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Twilight Forest biomes you can walk into from day one."
		"&eHow:&r walk in. The Magic Map shows biomes as you explore."
		"&eTip:&r enchanted forests hold rainbow oak and the odd quest ram."
	]
	quest.16F651F61CAD882E.title: "Tour: Twilight Frontier"
	quest.16F651F61CAD882E.quest_subtitle: "Nine biomes locked behind bosses"
	quest.16F651F61CAD882E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Twilight biomes that open as you beat its bosses."
		"&eHow:&r locked biomes hurt or block you until you beat the boss before them. Follow the Twilight boss order in Worlds."
		"&eTip:&r the final plateau is the last place in the Twilight Forest. Enjoy the view."
	]
	quest.48F10386696CBC9B.title: "Tour: The Undergarden"
	quest.48F10386696CBC9B.quest_subtitle: "Eight Undergarden biomes"
	quest.48F10386696CBC9B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r explore the Undergarden's biomes."
		"&eHow:&r walk in. Bring light: the Undergarden has no sun."
		"&eTip:&r smog spires and smogstem forests are where you'll find the strangest mobs."
	]
	quest.1973AAD62BAC2C46.title: "Tour: The Otherside"
	quest.1973AAD62BAC2C46.quest_subtitle: "Four biomes beyond the deep dark"
	quest.1973AAD62BAC2C46.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the four Otherside biomes from Deeper and Darker."
		"&eHow:&r walk in. Sculk listens here too: sneak."
		"&eTip:&r echo trees in the echoing forest give wood you can't get anywhere else."
	]
	quest.01CF0FA12664D89A.title: "Tour: The Solar System"
	quest.01CF0FA12664D89A.quest_subtitle: "Nine biomes on five worlds"
	quest.01CF0FA12664D89A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r stand in every planetary biome Ad Astra adds."
		"&eChemistry:&r Mars is red from iron(III) oxide dust; Venus's clouds are sulfuric acid droplets, the same H₂SO₄ you make in the Contact Process."
		"&eHow:&r fly to the Moon, Mars, Venus, Mercury and Glacio. Wear the right suit: Venus and Mercury need heat protection."
		"&eTip:&r martian polar caps are frozen CO₂ and water in real life; in game, bring an oxygen supply."
	]
	quest.2AA63CC0780D5E5A.title: "Element 5, Track 5"
	quest.2AA63CC0780D5E5A.quest_subtitle: "A very specific pun"
	quest.2AA63CC0780D5E5A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r disc 5 and five boron. Boron is element 5."
		"&eChemistry:&r boron is in borosilicate glass, which barely expands when heated. That's why lab glassware survives a flame."
		"&eTip:&r the demigod finds this funnier than anyone else will."
	]
	quest.57F252721837BC8A.title: "An Egg from the Past"
	quest.57F252721837BC8A.quest_subtitle: "Something older than you"
	quest.57F252721837BC8A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a sniffer egg, brushed out of warm ocean ruins."
		"&eHow:&r place it on moss to hatch it faster. Adult sniffers dig up ancient seeds."
		"&eTip:&r torchflowers and pitcher plants only come from sniffers."
	]
	quest.12F7DBB03E253B15.title: "The Only One"
	quest.12F7DBB03E253B15.quest_subtitle: "There is exactly one per world"
	quest.12F7DBB03E253B15.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the dragon egg. It teleports when you hit it."
		"&eHow:&r push it off the portal with a piston, or let it fall onto a torch, then pick it up."
		"&eTip:&r you'll need it for the Seed of a New World. Don't drop it in the void."
	]
